bout our university and campuses. Anticipated Salary Range The anticipated starting salary is $42,900, commensurate with experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our interactive too l to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://jobs.fsu.edu. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select \u201cyes\u201d to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for eligibility information and required documentation , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Eligible for on-call pay additives This position is being re-advertised. Previous applicants need not apply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63090&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Retail Sales Associate (Part-Time/OPS)", "description": "Job Title Retail Sales Associate (Part-Time/OPS) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63090 Location Sarasota, FL Full/Part Time Part-Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The John & Mable Ringling Museum of Art is located in Sarasota, Florida, and is a department of Florida State University . Responsibilities Primary responsibilities for this role include: Provide excellent, enthusiastic customer service to visitors. Proactively seek out and assist visitors in greeting and product selections. Learning the store's products and the story behind the product. Answering general visitor inquiries in person or via the phone. Processing sales at the register. Additional responsibilities include: Processing shipping orders and returns. Helping maintain the store's appearance, including dusting, straightening, restocking, and other duties as assigned. Qualifications High school diploma or equivalent Ability to stand for extended periods of time, climb a small step ladder, stock products on high and low shelves, and often lift up to 25 lbs. Preferred Qualifications Previous retail experience Ability to learn a computer based point-of-sale system Contact Info For more information or technical assistance, please contact Ringling Human Resources via email or by calling 941-358-2771. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range $15.45 (24 hours a week) How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an OPS/temporary job. Based on the duties, this position may require completion of a criminal history background check . Work Location: Sarasota, FL Employees are required to adhere to the business dress standards. If selected for an interview, a work sample will be administered. This position is being readvertised. Previous applicants need not reapply. Working Hours Shift typically starts at 9:30 AM, three days a week, but varies based on the needs of The Ringling. Please note this role's hours include weekends, days, evenings, and holidays. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63695&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Administrative Associate to Dean\u2019s Suite", "description": "Job Title Administrative Associate to Dean\u2019s Suite Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63695 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department College of Law Responsibilities This position provides administrative support to faculty and staff in the College of Law (COL) Dean\u2019s Office, with day-to-day operations. Processes involve sensitive and confidential matters that require a high level of professionalism. Responsibilities Greets visitors to the Dean's office and answers phone calls. Performs general duties assigned to Dean's office staff, to include organization and cleanliness of Dean's office, Dean's office kitchen and Dean's conference room, checking mail, maintenance and repair requests, monitoring and stocking office supplies. Provides other Administrative support as needed especially to supervisor and to the Assistant to the Dean. Maintains the conference room calendar. Ensures the Dean's office files are complete and organized, including paper and computer based. Assists with candidate searches and provides support, including scheduling meetings as needed, arranging travel for candidates, processing travel authorization and travel expense reimbursements. Will assist with travel planning, organization and processing of travel authorizations and travel expense reimbursements for the Dean, Associate Dean and other Deans as needed. Will assist the Law-UBA department in the tracking of position descriptions for FSU compliance. Will work with the Law-UBA department in monitoring FACET reporting acknowledgements, assisting in making corrections as needed. May assist with Assignments of Responsibility and the distribution of faculty evaluations. Assist the Law-UBA department in tracking required evaluation trainings and with recruitment of permanent staff. Prepares materials for faculty meetings and presentations, drafts routine correspondence, and assists with organizing orientation sessions. Provides backup and assistance if needed for Dean, Associate Deans and/or Assistant Deans. Qualifications HS diploma or equivalency and three years experience or a combination of post high school education and experience equal to three years. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select \u201cyes\u201d to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for Veterans\u2019 Preference eligibility requirements and Veterans\u2019 Preference required documentation (PDF) , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63696&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Carpenter (Open Rank-Multiple Hires)", "description": "Job Title Carpenter (Open Rank-Multiple Hires) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63696 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Maintenance Department Responsibilities Builds, erects, installs, and repairs forms, structures, and other fixtures made from wood and other materials as needed to assist with various types of construction projects. Installs and/or repairs kitchen cabinets, vanities and shelving units along with other general carpentry duties. Repairs furniture tables, chairs, etc. Repairs and/or installs new doors and hardware. Utilizes various hand and power tools to securely build assigned projects. Assists other trades as needed, such as locksmith, plasterer and painters. Operates vehicles to carry supplies and travel campus wide to perform various skilled maintenance. Loads and unloads necessary equipment and materials. Reviews plans and work orders to ensure correct completion of scope of work. Documents work performed and orders materials on appropriate departmental forms. Follows established safety rules and regulations and maintains a safe and clean environment. Moves necessary materials around job-site. Cleans up work site debris. Responsible for security, safety and maintenance of all equipment, supplies and vehicles. Maintains tools and equipment ensuring all hand and power tools are in proper working condition and reports maintenance problems to the supervisor. Organizes and cleans assigned shop areas. Prepares requests for materials and supplies. Performs additional maintenance and supervises helpers as required to include minor plaster, sheet rock repairs and replacement of floor tiles, ceramic tiles, and damaged carpet campus wide. Qualifications High school diploma or equivalency and two years of experience or a combination of post high school education and experience equal to two years. Technical or vocational degree may substitute for experience. A valid State of Florida or Georgia Driver\u2019s License or the ability to obtain prior to hire. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select \u201cyes\u201d to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for Veterans\u2019 Preference eligibility requirements and Veterans\u2019 Preference required documentation (PDF) , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Appropriate rank will be determined at time of appointment. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63630&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "FAMU-FSU College of Engineering, Senior Grants Specialist", "description": "Job Title FAMU-FSU College of Engineering, Senior Grants Specialist Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63630 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department FAMU-FSU College of Engineering Responsibilities Responsible for managing contract and grant (C&G) budgets and project compliance from both FSU and FAMU within assigned departments, including Industrial & Manufacturing Engineering and Material Science & Engineering. Performs specialized C&G budgetary services, accounting services, and activities related to C&G budgetary reports, long-range budget planning, allocation of funds, and monitoring of financial reports for designated C&G budgets. Serves as a liaison between the Department, College, funding agencies, Research Foundation, Sponsored Research, and other relevant organizations. Responsible for post-award financial and administrative management of assigned C&G portfolios at both FAMU and FSU. Monitors and reconciles awards monthly; tracks expenditures, encumbrances, salary commitments, subawards, and other planned costs; and maintains forward-looking projections of available balances through project end dates. Meets regularly with PIs to review financial status, burn rate, projected balances, and required actions. Processes and supports rebudgets, budget amendments, procurement, travel, FACET (effort reporting)-related C&G questions, financial reporting, records management, and project closeout. Proactively identifies projected deficits, unspent balances, expiring funds, and other financial or compliance concerns and works with PIs and appropriate University offices to resolve them. Responsible for pre-award support for assigned faculty and units. Reviews solicitations and sponsor guidelines for eligibility, budget caps, cost-sharing obligations, F&A limitations, and submission requirements, and advises PIs accordingly. Develops and analyzes complex proposal budgets, including multi-year, cost-share, and subaward budgets, and drafts corresponding budget justifications. Applies federal, state, University, and sponsor regulations in budget construction. Collects and verifies subrecipient commitment documentation. Prepares and routes proposals in RAMP system and coordinates with Sponsored Research at FSU and FAMU to meet internal and sponsor deadlines. Serves as a departmental resource for grants administration and interprets applicable University, sponsor, and regulatory requirements for faculty and staff. Monitors assigned portfolios for financial and compliance risks, communicates concerns promptly to PIs and appropriate leadership, and recommends corrective actions. Supports consistent College grants-management procedures, timelines, internal controls, and process improvements in coordination with Research Office leadership and central University offices. Improves grants administration processes through data analysis, reporting, and development of procedures and training materials. Participates in Sponsored Research training and communicates procedural changes to assigned departments. Supports grants-related special projects and other sponsored research duties as assigned. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and three-years of experience; or high school diploma/equivalent and experience equal to seven years. (Note: post-high school education can substitute for experience at the equivalent rate.) This position requires successful completion of the eSPEAR Certification or ability to obtain the certification within 6 months of hire. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63629&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "FAMU-FSU College of Engineering, Senior Grants Specialist", "description": "Job Title FAMU-FSU College of Engineering, Senior Grants Specialist Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63629 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department FAMU-FSU College of Engineering Responsibilities Responsible for managing contract and grant (C&G) budgets and project compliance from both FSU and FAMU within assigned college departments, including Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering and Electrical & Computer Engineering. Performs specialized C&G budgetary services, accounting services, and activities related to C&G budgetary reports, long-range budget planning, allocation of funds, and monitoring of financial reports for designated C&G budgets. Serves as a liaison between the Department, College, funding agencies, Research Foundation, Sponsored Research, and other relevant organizations. Responsible for post-award financial and administrative management of assigned C&G portfolios at both FAMU and FSU. Monitors and reconciles awards monthly; tracks expenditures, encumbrances, salary commitments, subawards, and other planned costs; and maintains forward-looking projections of available balances through project end dates. Meets regularly with (Principal Investigators) PIs to review financial status, burn rate, projected balances, and required actions. Processes and supports rebudgets, budget amendments, procurement, travel, FACET (effort reporting)-related C&G questions, financial reporting, records management, and project closeout. Proactively identifies projected deficits, unspent balances, expiring funds, and other financial or compliance concerns and works with PIs and appropriate University offices to resolve them. Responsible for pre-award support for assigned faculty and units. Reviews solicitations and sponsor guidelines for eligibility, budget caps, cost-sharing obligations, finance and administration limitations, and submission requirements, and advises PIs accordingly. Develops and analyzes complex proposal budgets, including multi-year, cost-share, and subaward budgets, and drafts corresponding budget justifications. Applies federal, state, University, and sponsor regulations in budget construction. Collects and verifies subrecipient commitment documentation. Prepares and routes proposals in RAMP system and coordinates with Sponsored Research at FSU and FAMU to meet internal and sponsor deadlines. Serves as a departmental resource for grants administration and interprets applicable University, sponsor, and regulatory requirements for faculty and staff. Monitors assigned portfolios for financial and compliance risks, communicates concerns promptly to PIs and appropriate leadership, and recommends corrective actions. Supports consistent College grants-management procedures, timelines, internal controls, and process improvements in coordination with Research Office leadership and central University offices. Improves grants administration processes through data analysis, reporting, and development of procedures and training materials. Participates in Sponsored Research training and communicates procedural changes to assigned departments. Supports grants-related special projects and other sponsored research duties as assigned. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and three-years of experience; or high school diploma/equivalent and experience equal to seven years. (Note: post-high school education can substitute for experience at the equivalent rate.) This position requires successful completion of the eSPEAR Certification or ability to obtain the certification within 6 months of hire. Preferred Qualifications Knowledge of Uniform Guidance. Knowledge of and ability to apply Generally Accepted Accounting Principles (GAAP). Knowledge of federal, state, and private sources for contract and grant funds. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63496&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "General Maintenance Technician (Levels 1-2)", "description": "Job Title General Maintenance Technician (Levels 1-2) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63496 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Facilities - Central Utilities Plant Responsibilities Ensures the plant\u2019s utilities are properly functioning to receive steam, chilled water, hot water, compressed air, electricity, and gas. Inspects, repairs, and maintains boilers, steam turbines, emergency generators, water pumps, fuel oil pumps, compressors, chillers, buildings, fuel oil storage tanks, and all support equipment and piping systems at the Central Utilities and Satellite Plants. Removes and/or replaces pumps, fans, and electric motors. Repairs/rebuilds pumps, fans, and electric motors for system modifications, to be reinstalled and returned to service. Packs pumps, glands, valves, and lubrication equipment to reduce product loss and to ensure safe and efficient operation. Performs diagnostic tests for corrective, preventive, and predictive maintenance on all related equipment. Performs routine inspections of water distribution systems, rotary equipment, and related components. Troubleshoots and calibrates flow meters. Performs vibration analysis. Maintains related records and CUP logs. Operates University vehicle as necessary. Installs electrical apparatus, hangers, and brackets to support electrical products, fixtures, switches, circuit breaker panels, relays, and other electrical control and distribution equipment. Installs safety and distribution components, pneumatic solenoid valves, switches, photo eyes, control panels etc. Inspects circuit breakers and other electrical components for faults. Performs maintenance procedures to keep wiring, lighting, and control systems in good working order. Prepares proper mechanical joints through precise cutting, welding, brazing, threading, cementing, and caulking. Devises and fabricates special jigs and fixtures to perform required tasks. Complies with state, and federal laws, policies, and regulations, and adheres to quality assurance programs and safety standards. Performs related duties as assigned. Completes all assigned training related to boilers, chillers, pumps, motors, and steam boiler compliance. Qualifications High school diploma or equivalent and two years' experience, or a relevant Technical or vocational degree may substitute for experience. A valid State of Florida or Georgia Driver\u2019s License or ability to obtain upon hire. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select \u201cyes\u201d to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for Veterans\u2019 Preference eligibility requirements and Veterans\u2019 Preference required documentation (PDF) , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being re-advertised. Previous applicants need not apply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63237&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Groundskeeper (Multiple Vacancies)", "description": "Job Title Groundskeeper (Multiple Vacancies) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63237 Location Sarasota, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The John & Mable Ringling Museum of Art is located in Sarasota, Florida, and is a department of Florida State University . Responsibilities Performs campus groundskeeping tasks such as edging, raking, mulching, power blowing, light pruning, trimming spent blooms and watering plants. Identifies and removes weeds from flowerbeds, gardens, planting areas, and pathways, ensuring the removal of roots to prevent regrowth. This includes hand weeding and the use of tools like hoes or weed pullers. Transplants plant/flower materials, assists with minor landscape renovations, to include soil excavation and removal. Responsible for debris removal, leaf removal, trash pickup and other tasks to keep grounds clean and presentable. Maintains areas by spreading landscape materials such as shell, bark, or rocks. Performs other duties and projects as assigned that support museum operations and provides general assistance for the Facilities department at the museum as needed. Qualifications Completion of 9th grade or higher Please note that due to the need to use golf carts on The Ringling grounds, applicants must be 18 years of age or older. Valid Florida Driver's license or the ability to obtain one prior to hire. Driver's permits are not acceptable. Ability to meet physical requirements as determined by position, including the ability to lift 50 pounds, walk long distances, work from heights, and work in extreme weather conditions. Contact Info For more information or technical assistance, please contact Ringling Human Resources via email or by calling 941-358-2773. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Rate of pay will be commensurate with the selected candidate's education, skills, and experience. Find out more about our comprehensive benefits package under the \"FSU Total Rewards\" section. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select \u201cyes\u201d to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for Veterans\u2019 Preference eligibility requirements and Veterans\u2019 Preference required documentation (PDF) , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is based in Sarasota, FL. Employees are required to wear the standard issue uniform while at work. This role is designated as essential and may be required to work before, during, or after an emergency museum closure. This advertisement is to fill multiple vacancies. This position is being readvertised. Previous applicants need not reapply. Working Hours Monday - Friday from 6:30 AM to 3:00 PM with a half hour meal period. Weekends, evenings, and holidays may be required per the needs of the Ringling. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=61380&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "HVAC Operator", "description": "Job Title HVAC Operator Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 61380 Location Sarasota, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The John & Mable Ringling Museum of Art is located in Sarasota, Florida, and is a department of Florida State University . Learn more about The Ringling at https://www.ringling.org/about-ringling/careers/. Responsibilities This position serves as an HVAC Operator and assists the Facilities Supervisor for Ringling Buildings Maintenance. Monitors operation of computerized heating, ventilation and air conditioning system (Chilled Water Plant). Maintains appropriate operational logs and analyzes trends in system. Makes appropriate system adjustments to maintain consistent system production and efficient energy consumption. Works together with Facilities Supervisor and HVAC Support Worker on determining daily assignments. Makes suggestions and provides guidance on plant operations. Develops and carries out preventative maintenance program for plant operation with guidance from the Facilities Supervisor. Troubleshoots and identifies chilled water pipe problems. Performs repairs on heating and/or air conditioning equipment. Uses motorized vehicle to transport tools and materials. Assists with emergency and or special Facilities' maintenance projects as needed. Remains on-call during designated periods outside normal working hours as needed to monitor and remotely make necessary adjustments for the chiller plant. While on-call, the incumbent may be required to return to the work site to respond to maintenance emergencies. Generates and responds to emails and work orders via online work order system. Updates work order system once per day regarding progress and/or upon completion of assignment. Performs a variety of work to maintain all buildings on campus such as pressure washing, painting, plumbing, filter changes, inspecting buildings/equipment to ensure good and safe operating conditions. Performs other duties and projects as assigned that support museum operations, including performing grounds work or general assistance for the Facilities department at the museum. Qualifications High school diploma and two years' experience. Relevant Technical or Vocational degree may substitute for experience. Ability to meet physical requirements as determined by position including the ability to lift and carry 50 pounds, climb ladders, and work in small spaces. Valid Florida driver's license or the ability to obtain prior to hire. Preferred Qualifications Technical or vocational degree or certification in HVAC. Steam boiler and Alerton and Tracer Summit experience. Familiar with Commercial/Industrial centralized HVAC systems. Direct Digital Controls (DDC) systems experience. Knowledge of: The practices and the ability to perform skilled carpentry, painting, plumbing, electrical, HVAC, or other related trades work. Identifying safety hazards and taking necessary safety precautions to establish a safe work environment. Ability to: Safely operate machinery, tools, equipment and materials used in area of work. Utilize technical skills in identifying air conditioning/heating/ventilation problems and repair. Communicate effectively verbally and in writing. Understand and follow written and oral instructions. Utilize problem solving skills. Establish and maintain effective working relationships. Prioritize, organize and perform multiple work assignments simultaneously. Contact Info For more information, technical assistance, or should you require accommodations for the application or interview processes, please contact Ringling Human Resources at 941-358-2773 or employment@ringling.org. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. Anticipated Salary Range This position has a starting salary range of $41,000 + with final offer amount based on the education, skills, and experience of the selected applicant. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our interactive too l to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://jobs.fsu.edu. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select \u201cyes\u201d to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for eligibility information and required documentation , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Work Location: Sarasota, FL This position is being readvertised. Previous applicants need not reapply. This role is designated as essential and may be required to work before, during, or after an emergency museum closure. Working Hours The primary working hours for this position are between 6:30 AM and 3:00 PM (with a 30 minute meal period) Monday - Friday. This role may be required to work a flexible schedule including nights, weekends and special events based on the needs of The Ringling. This position is eligible to receive on-call pay. The position incumbent is required to be accessible and available to return to work during off-duty hours as scheduled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=61379&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "HVAC Support Worker", "description": "Job Title HVAC Support Worker Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 61379 Location Sarasota, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The John & Mable Ringling Museum of Art is located in Sarasota, Florida, and is a department of Florida State University . Learn more about The Ringling at https://www.ringling.org/about-ringling/careers/ . Responsibilities The HVAC Support Worker provides preventative maintenance of HVAC systems and supports Facilities maintenance for The Ringling. Performs routine servicing of HVAC systems as part of the preventative maintenance program. Maintenance and repair of boilers, generators, air compressors, water pumps, fuel oil pumps, fans, and chillers. Completes other repairs as directed or assigned. Responds to issues that may arise which require emergency attention. Drives golf cart to various locations on campus. Operates boilers and chillers in accordance with schedules and procedures. Checks all meters and gauges to ensure the safe and efficient operation of boilers and chilled water equipment. Maintains chiller and boiler logs. Performs a variety of work to maintain all buildings on campus such as pressure washing, painting, plumbing, filter changes, inspecting buildings/equipment to ensure good and safe operating conditions. Generates and responds to emails and work orders via online work order system. Updates work order system once per day regarding progress and/or upon completion of assignment. Assists with emergency and or special Facilities maintenance projects as needed. Remains on-call during designated periods outside normal working hours as needed. While on-call, the incumbent may be required to return to the work site to respond to maintenance emergencies. Completes water quality tests to determine and correct improper chemical balance for boiler and chiller operations. Performs other duties and projects as assigned that support museum operations and provides general assistance for the Facilities department at the museum, which may include supporting events, performing grounds work, and general assistance as needed. Must be able to obtain a lift certification and be physically able and willing to operate a areal lift, forklift. Qualifications High school diploma and two years of experience. Relevant technical or vocational degree may substitute for experience. Ability to lift and carry 50 pounds, climb ladders, and work in small spaces. Valid Florida driver's license or the ability to obtain prior to hire. Preferred Qualifications Technical or vocational degree or certification in HVAC. Experience with: Steam boiler and Alerton and Tracer Summit experience. Commercial/Industrial centralized HVAC systems. Direct Digital Controls (DDC) systems. Knowledge of: The practices and the ability to perform HVAC work. Applicable computer applications and basic computer functions. Ability to: Perform skilled carpentry, painting, plumbing, electrical, or other related trades work. Understand and follow written and oral instructions. Prioritize, organize and perform multiple work assignments simultaneously. Troubleshoot, diagnose, maintain and repair a variety of equipment and machinery used in area of work. Identify safety hazards and necessary safety precautions to establish a safe work environment. communicate effectively verbally and in writing. Utilize problem solving skills. Establish and maintain effective working relationships. Contact Info For more information, technical assistance, or should you require accommodations for the application or interview processes, please contact Ringling Human Resources at 941-358-2773 or employment@ringling.org. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. Anticipated Salary Range This position has a starting salary range of $40,000 + with final offer amount based on the education, skills, and experience of the selected applicant. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our interactive too l to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State 