ent is required to be accessible and available to return to work during off-duty hours on a rotating schedule. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=62329&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "HVAC/R Technician", "description": "Job Title HVAC/R Technician Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 62329 Location Sarasota, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The John & Mable Ringling Museum of Art is located in Sarasota, Florida, and is a department of Florida State University . Learn more about The Ringling at https://www.ringling.org/about-ringling/careers/ . Responsibilities This role is responsible for the maintenance and repair of The Ringling's HVAC and chilled water loop systems. Troubleshoots, diagnoses, maintains, and repairs HVAC equipment. Monitors operation of computerized heating ventilation and air conditioning system (Chilled Water Plant). Maintains appropriate operational logs. Makes appropriate system adjustments to maintain consistent system production and efficient energy consumption. May make emergency decisions affecting system operation and/or shutdown. Troubleshoots and identifies chilled water pipe problems. Performs installs of new or repairs heating and/or air conditioning equipment, including compressors, condensers, and pumps. Recharges air conditioner units with refrigerant as needed. Inspects and maintains low pressure gas fired boilers. Generates and responds to emails and work orders via online work order system. Updates work order system once per day regarding progress and/or upon completion of assignment. Assists the Maintenance Supervisor in monitoring work orders and overseeing daily work projects assigned to the team. Works to ensure project quality, identifies deficiencies and reports to supervisor. Uses motorized vehicles to travel campus. Assists with emergency and or special Facilities' maintenance projects, as assigned, that support museum operations and provides general assistance for the Facilities department. This position serves as lead worker for the Ringling Facilities Building Maintenance Team and, in the absence of the Maintenance Supervisor, ensures assignments are carried out by staff. Qualifications High school diploma and two years' experience; or a relevant Technical or vocational degree may substitute for experience. Valid Florida driver's license or the ability to obtain one prior to hire. Ability to lift up to 50 lbs, climb ladders, and work in small spaces/heights. Preferred Qualifications Previous experience with computerized heating ventilation and air conditioning systems and low pressure gas fired boilers. Knowledge of and ability to: Safely operate machinery, tools, equipment and materials. Perform skilled carpentry, painting, plumbing, electrical, HVAC, or other related trades work. Use a computer-based work order system (FacilityDude). Contact Info For more information, technical assistance, or should you require accommodations for the application or interview processes, please contact Ringling Human Resources at 941-358-2773 or employment@ringling.org . University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. Anticipated Salary Range Commensurate with the education, skills, and experience of the selected applicant. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our interactive too l to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://jobs.fsu.edu. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select \u201cyes\u201d to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for eligibility information and required documentation , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Employees are required to wear the standard issue uniform while at work. This role is designated as essential and may be required to work before, during, or after an emergency museum closure. Remains on-call during designated periods outside normal working hours, as needed, to monitor and remotely make necessary adjustments for the chiller plant. While on-call, the incumbent may be required to return to the work site to respond to maintenance emergencies. This position is being readvertised. Previous applicants need not reapply. Working Hours While the primary working hours for this position are Monday - Friday from 6:30 AM to 3:00 PM with a half hour for lunch, the incumbent may be required to work a flexible schedule including nights, weekends, and/or special events. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63293&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Horticulturalist", "description": "Job Title Horticulturalist Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63293 Location Sarasota, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The John & Mable Ringling Museum of Art is located in Sarasota, Florida, and is a department of Florida State University . Responsibilities Under the direction of the Associate Director of Facilities and Grounds, this position is responsible for performing hands-on garden work, managing, maintaining, and developing The Ringling's gardens. Provide expert advice on the care, maintenance, and propagation of the museum's gardens. Manage, maintain, and enhance the health and aesthetics of The Ringling's living collections and garden spaces. Performs planting, weeding, pruning, trimming, and other activities to ensure gardens are attractive and well-kept. Utilizes pertinent management reports to schedule, evaluate, and improve plant health and general appearance of campus gardens. Generates and responds to emails and work orders via online work order system. Updates work orders in Facilities Dude regarding progress or completion of work order assignments. Assists as needed in reviewing project costing, monitoring supplies inventory and maintenance, and makes recommendations for long-range planning of grounds and gardens preventative maintenance. Serves as point of contact for gardens' volunteers, community service workers, and interns. Collaborates with the Grounds Supervisor for Groundskeeper support in the maintenance of garden spaces. Organizes, monitors, and inspects special garden projects to evaluate progress and ensure project quality. Supervises work performed by staff and volunteers in the gardens and provides assistance in the proper care of trees, shrubs, ground covers, and plants. Oversees gardens' spray program and pest management including the application of integrated pest management practices. Monitors for the presence of pest and takes appropriate measures to treat issues as they arise. Safely operates company vehicles, mowers, and power tools and grounds keeping equipment. Ensure maintenance equipment is operating safely and returned clean to shop at end of each work day. Perform routing and preventative maintenance and cleaning of all tools. Serves as the subject matter expert on the campus grounds and gardens. Collaborates interdepartmentally to develop programming and promote gardens and grounds. Provides gardens and grounds based programming and educational workshops. Participates in community outreach initiatives to cultivate relations, increase awareness of the gardens, and increase volunteer support from outside groups such as local garden clubs, universities, and horticulture facilities. Answers visitor questions regarding the gardens. Develops signage for the gardens. Assists as needed with grounds projects and grounds maintenance. May cover areas of responsibility for other grounds staff. Responds to and assists with emergency grounds needs. Performs other duties as assigned that support the Facilities department and operations of the museum. Qualifications Bachelor's degree in agronomy, arboriculture, horticulture, landscaping, landscape design, or landscape technology or a high school degree and four years of appropriate experience. Ability to meet physical requirements as determined by position including lift up to 25 lbs., walk long distances, and work in extreme weather conditions. Valid Florida driver's license or the ability to obtain prior to hire. Preferred Qualifications Skill in public speaking. Ability to: Perform groundskeeping work to include the transplanting, cultivation, pruning, and trimming of plants, shrubs, and trees. Effectively train and direct the work of others. Establish and maintain effective working relationships. Prioritize, organize and perform multiple work assignments simultaneously. Perform assigned responsibilities with minimal to moderate supervision. Knowledge of and ability to: Applicable computer applications and basic computer functions such as Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel, PowerPoint, & Outlook), along with the ability to use the TreeKeeper software suite and the ability to maintain computerized records. Identify safety hazards and necessary safety precautions to establish a safe work environment. Safely operate machinery, tools, equipment and materials used in area of work. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Rate of pay will be commensurate with the selected candidate's education, skills, and experience. Find out more about our comprehensive benefits package under the \"FSU Total Rewards\" section. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Your application is not considered complete without attaching a position-relevant cover letter and resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select \u201cyes\u201d to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for Veterans\u2019 Preference eligibility requirements and Veterans\u2019 Preference required documentation (PDF) , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check. Work Location: Sarasota, FL Employees are required to wear the standard issue uniform while at work. This role is designated as essential and may be required to work before, during, or after an emergency museum closure. This position is being readvertised. Previous applicants need not reapply. Working Hours Monday - Friday from 6:30 AM and 3:00 PM with a 30 minute meal period. Weekends, evenings, and holidays may be required per the needs of the Ringling. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=61349&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Irrigation Technician", "description": "Job Title Irrigation Technician Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 61349 Location Sarasota, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The John & Mable Ringling Museum of Art is located in Sarasota, Florida, and is a department of Florida State University . Learn more about The Ringling at https://www.ringling.org/about-ringling/careers/ . Responsibilities This position is responsible for pump repairs and maintenance, skill in working with variable frequency drives (VFDs), and hands-on experience with irrigation systems and troubleshooting. Monitors, adjusts, and repairs irrigation systems throughout campus for optimal performance. Reports issues to the Associate Director of Facilities & Grounds and makes recommendations for corrective measures. Performs preventive maintenance on irrigation systems. Diagnoses and troubleshoots system issues, including leaks, electrical faults, and pump malfunctions. Identifies and resolves problems with irrigation controls, wiring, piping, and sprinkler heads. Repairs, overhauls, and replaces defective parts on irrigation systems. Establish and monitor irrigation schedules to meet landscaping needs while prioritizing water conservation using equipment related to the trade including variable frequency drives (VFDs). Maintains tools and equipment to keep in clean, proper working order. Operates and maintains power tools, hand tools, and trenching equipment. Operates, maintains, manipulates, and extracts data from central irrigation system. Conduct regular inspections to ensure system efficiency and compliance with local water regulations. Completes work orders and submits paperwork in a timely manner. Maintains accurate records of irrigation schedules, repairs, water usage, and inventory. Orders parts and supplies for irrigation system maintenance and repairs. Maintains an accurate inventory of irrigation parts. Prepares water usage/consumption reports. Collaborates with the groundskeeping team to support plant health, landscape aesthetics, and grounds maintenance. Works with and trains grounds employees in irrigation system repair, modification procedures, and techniques. Maintains trees, plants, shrubs, flowers, and grass through pruning, mowing, trimming, planting, watering, leaf blowing, raking, and mulching. Fertilizes plants, shrubs, trees, and grass on a seasonal basis. Plants and transplants plants, trees, shrubs, and flowers. Monitors for disease, insect damage, and weeds; reports and treats as directed. Operates landscaping equipment (string trimmers, hedge trimmers, mowers, edgers, sod cutters, chainsaws). Designs and installs irrigation systems. Plans and installs manual and automatic irrigation systems (battery-operated, hydraulic, electrical). Performs trenching, backfilling, and other excavation activities required for irrigation installation. Provides information about the plants to visitors and responds to questions. Drives motorized vehicles to traverse campus. Performs other duties and projects as assigned that support museum operations, including performing grounds work or general assistance for the Facilities department at the museum. Qualifications High school diploma and two years' experience. Relevant Technical or Vocational degree may substitute for experience. Ability to meet physical requirements as determined by position including the ability to lift 50 pounds, walk long distances, and work in extreme weather conditions. Valid Florida driver's license or the ability to obtain prior to hire. Preferred Qualifications Knowledge of: Pump repairs and maintenance, skill in working with variable frequency drives (VFDs), and hands-on experience with irrigation systems and troubleshooting. The practices and the ability to perform skilled carpentry, painting, plumbing, electrical, HVAC, or other related trades work. Landscaping and groundskeeping techniques. Ability to: Perform groundskeeping work to include the transplanting, cultivation, pruning, and trimming of plants, shrubs, and trees. Safely operate machinery, tools, equipment and various types of motorized vehicles including but not limited to dump trucks, tractors, forklifts, pallet trucks, front-end loaders, and golf-carts. Identify safety hazards and take necessary safety precautions to establish a safe work environment Establish and maintain effective working relationships. Perform assigned responsibilities with minimal to moderate supervision. Understand and follow written and oral instructions. Prioritize, organize and perform multiple work assignments simultaneously Troubleshoot, diagnose, maintain and repair a variety of equipment and machinery used in area of work. Contact Info For more information, technical assistance, or should you require accommodations for the application or interview processes, please contact Ringling Human Resources at 941-358-2773 or employment@ringling.org. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. Anticipated Salary Range This position has a salary range beginning at $40,000 + with final offer amount based on the education, skills, and experience of the selected applicant. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our interactive too l to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://jobs.fsu.edu. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select \u201cyes\u201d to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for eligibility information and required documentation , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Work Location: Sarasota, FL This position is being readvertised. Previous applicants need not reapply. This role is designated as essential and may be required to work before, during, or after an emergency museum closure. Working Hours The primary working hours for this position are between 6:30 AM and 3:00 PM (with a 30 minute meal period) Monday - Friday. This role may be required to work a flexible schedule including nights, weekends and special events based on the needs of The Ringling. This position is eligible to receive on-call pay. The position incumbent is required to be accessible and available to return to work during off-duty hours as scheduled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63691&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Museum Custodian", "description": "Job Title Museum Custodian Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63691 Location Sarasota, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The John & Mable Ringling Museum of Art is located in Sarasota, Florida, and is a department of Florida State University . Responsibilities This role serves as a member of the General Museum Housekeeping Team, performing custodial tasks such as floor maintenance, public restrooms cleaning and stocking, mopping, dusting, etc. Cleans and sanitizes all public spaces and restrooms throughout the Sarasota Campus Complex during the day. Restocks tissue, towels, and hand soap supplies. Completes assigned daily tasks in campus venue to include prepare the campus to open, cleaning glass, dusting, sweeping, mopping, and emptying wastebaskets. Respond to service calls. Clean special event areas as needed: clearing refuse and using appropriate tools to remove stains and scrub hard surfaces. Complete assigned work orders and stock custodial closets according to supply request sheets or as needed. Drives custodial golf carts to traverse the 66 acre campus to deliver supplies and carry equipment. Clear trash from Sarasota Campus Complex grounds and clean exterior surfaces. Empty and transport recycling. Performs custodial maintenance projects. Completes other duties and projects as assigned that support museum operations and provides general assistance for the Facilities department at the museum, which may include supporting events and general assistance as needed. Qualifications Valid Florida driver's license or the ability to obtain prior to hire Due to the need to drive golf carts in this role, applicants must be 18 years of age or older. 9th-grade education or higher Ability to meet physical requirements as determined by position, to include moving objects up to 45lbs, working with chemicals, climbing and descending stairs, standing and walking for extended periods. Preferred Qualifications Demonstrated attention to detail and commitment to maintaining high standards of cleanliness and organization. Ability to: Communicate effectively, both verbally and in writing. Understand and follow written and verbal instructions. Work independently while contributing positively to a team environment. Recognize workplace safety hazards and implement appropriate safety precautions. Knowledge of the safe operation of custodial equipment, machinery, tools, and cleaning materials. Problem-solving skills with the ability to identify issues and take appropriate corrective action. Verbal fluency in additional language(s) besides English. Contact Info For more information or technical assistance, please contact Ringling Human Resources via email or by calling 941-358-2773. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range $33,408 or higher annually. Final offer amount will be determined based on the education, skills, and experience of the selected applicant. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select \u201cyes\u201d to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for Veterans\u2019 Preference eligibility requirements and Veterans\u2019 Preference required documentation (PDF) , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check. This position is based in Sarasota, FL. Employees are required to wear the standard issue uniform while at work. This role is designated as essential and may be required to work before, during, or after an emergency museum closure. Working Hours Friday to Tuesday from 10:00 AM to 6:30 PM with a half hour meal period. Weekends, weekdays, evenings, and holidays may be required per the needs of the Ringling. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63694&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "OPS Postdoctoral Scholar - Webster", "description": "Job Title OPS Postdoctoral Scholar - Webster Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63694 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Postdoctoral Researcher in Genetics, Genomics, and Bioinformatics The Webster Lab in the Department of Biological Science at Florida State University invites applications for a postdoctoral researcher. Our lab investigates individual variation: we seek to understand why genetically identical individuals in a shared environment vary for both molecular and organismal phenotypes, and we then determine how genotype and environment can regulate this variation. We combine computational genomics, molecular biology, and experiments in Caenorhabditis elegans to address these questions. The successful candidate will help shape a project aligned with their interests and career goals. Projects may be fully computational or may combine bioinformatics with laboratory experiments. Funding for the position will be provided through either our lab's NSF CAREER award or startup funds, depending on the planned project. Responsibilities The postdoctoral researcher will analyze large genomic datasets, develop reproducible analysis pipelines, contribute to manuscripts and presentations, and collaborate with other members of the lab. The position requires thoughtful and efficient use of modern coding assistants as part of computational work, together with careful validation, documentation, and version control. Depending on the project and the candidate\u2019s interests, responsibilities may also include designing and conducting experiments with C. elegans, mentoring junior researchers, and contributing to grant proposals. The position may be fully computational, or may be a split between computational and wetlab work; in either case, proficiency with bioinformatic analysis is a must. Qualifications A Ph.D. completed by the position\u2019s start date in genetics, genomics, bioinformatics, molecular biology, evolutionary biology, or a closely related field Experience analyzing high-throughput sequencing data using bioinformatics Proficiency in at least one relevant programming language, such as R or Python Ability to work independently and collaboratively and to communicate research effectively Preferred Qualifications Experience working with C. elegans Experience with transcriptomic, epigenomic, or population-genomic sequencing data Experience developing reproducible computational workflows Interest in combining computational analysis with molecular or organismal experiments Helpful The lab is committed to supportive, individualized mentoring. The postdoctoral researcher and principal investigator will establish a mentoring plan and revisit it regularly through one-on-one meetings. Mentoring will include support for research independence, publishing, conference participation, fellowship and grant applications. Postdoctoral scholars have access to career-development programs, networking, travel awards, and other resources through FSU\u2019s Office of Postdoctoral Affairs . They may participate in the FSU Postdoctoral Association . Candidates interested in teaching may also pursue opportunities to serve as an instructor of record for a course, subject to departmental need and approval. Contact Info Questions may be directed to Amy Webster . Additional information about the lab is available here . University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Compensation, mentoring, and professional development Salary will be commensurate with relevant postdoctoral experience and aligned with the current NIH NRSA postdoctoral stipend scale . The position also includes applicable FSU employee benefits. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Applicants should submit (1) a cover letter describing their research experience, interests, and career goals; (2) a curriculum vitae; and (3) contact information for two references. Review of applications will begin October 26 and continue until the position is filled. The anticipated start date is flexible, but ideally will be between January and July 2027. Considerations This is an OPS/temporary job. Based on the duties, this position may require completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63646&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Technician OPS", "description": "Job Title Technician OPS Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63646 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The FAMU-FSU College of Engineering is pleased to announce the acceptance of qualified applications for the Computer Technician (OPS) position within Information Technology Services (ITS) . Responsibilities Providing excellent, responsive service to our college customers (faculty, staff and students) when they contact our office (walk in or call in); Handle simple technical issues; Assist more senior teammates with various projects, including personal computer and classroom technology support. Qualifications A high school diploma or equivalency and some experience with customer service roles and supporting personal computers. Good basic knowledge of Microsoft Windows and Microsoft Office. Commitment to providing excellent customer service. Good communications skills. Prepared to work well in a team-oriented environment. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an OPS/temporary job. Based on the duties, this position may require completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63678&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Accounting Specialist - UBA/College of Music", "description": "Job Title Accounting Specialist - UBA/College of Music Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63678 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department University Business Administrators - College of Music Responsibilities Responsible for performing professional fiscal activities at the College of Music (CoM), including travel, purchasing, and deposit accounting, with an emphasis on student-facing financial functions, including student group travel and tours, student travel grants, scholarships, course-enhancement initiatives, tuition waivers, and student finance communications. Responsible for day-to-day origination of travel authorizations, cash advances, and expense reports for student travel, including individual, small group, and large group trips/tours. Provides recommendations to support the travel initiatives developed to enhance and enrich the CoM student experience. Creates and maintains CoM-specific travel training guides, travel resources, and post-travel forms. Proactively communicates with International Travel, Safety, and Risk, and the University Clery Compliance Officer prior to CoM group travel. Routes student travel waivers prior to departure for all college-sanctioned student group travel. Reviews travel card transactions for accuracy and policy compliance. Maintains appropriate travel logs and regularly updates interested parties on the status of their upcoming travel and post-travel expense reports. Tracks and monitors purchasing activities at the CoM to ensure a sound environment of internal controls and compliance. Interprets and communicates policies to faculty, staff, and students. Makes recommendations regarding purchasing processes and advises on alternatives as needed, in particular to accommodate requests for purchase of course materials or in support of student entrepreneurial initiatives. Prepares and utilizes college-wide reports for tracking requisitions and purchase orders to ensure adherence to area budget allocations as well as timely transaction entry and payment processing. Communicates with internal stakeholders as necessary and ensures compliance with University policies and procedures. Serves as primary PCard holder for CoM Fiscal Office requests. Serves as backup to Sr. Accounting Specialist for faculty, staff, professional development, recruitment, and guest artist travel. Serves as backup PCard Proxy for the CoM, assisting with auditing and coding of departmental purchase card payments as needed. Serves as secondary liaison between College cardholders and FSU Procurement/PCard Admin. Enters and reconciles all foundation scholarship awards in FS4U. Collaborates with Sr. Accounting Specialist and Assistant Deans for Admissions & Recruitment and Finance & Administration, as well as the Associate Dean for Academic Affairs, Graduate Academic Program Specialist, and Assistant Dean for Undergraduate Programs to process and reconcile all academic year awards. Participates in unencumbered payment activities at the (CoM) to include origination of non-travel reimbursements in FSU Systems, payments to vendors via ePRF, and the PCard program. Identifies process enhancements in existing operations to improve efficiency and delegation throughout the the CoM Fiscal Office. Regularly reviews and takes necessary actions on PCard transactions, outstanding T-Card transactions, and aging travel requests, monitoring financial transactions and ensuring compliance with University policy and procedures. Serves as a key point of contact for College of Music (CoM) student inquiries pertaining to student financials, including account balances, award disbursements, tuition waivers, insurance subsidies, fee liability, scholarship status, tax liability, payment plans, and adjustments. Serves as a liaison among the CoM Fiscal Office, Office of Student Success, FSU Financial Aid, Student Finance, The Graduate School, and Payroll. Qualifications A Bachelor's degree and two years of experience; or a high school diploma or equivalent and six years of experience. (Note: a combination of post high school education and experience equal to six years.) Preferred Qualifications The preferred candidate should have the following skill and/or experience. Collaborative attitude and the ability to thrive working with faculty, students, guests, and staff. Excellent attention to detail, communication skills, and the ability to work independently. Ability to successfully prioritize, organize and perform multiple work assignments simultaneously. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63473&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Admissions & Workflows Analyst", "description": "Job Title Admissions & Workflows Analyst Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63473 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The Division of Enrollment Management - Technology Operations Unit Responsibilities The Division of Enrollment Management is comprised of four distinct units: Office of Admissions, Office of the University Registrar , Office of Financial Aid , and Technology Operations. Enrollment Management\u2019s integrated services provide distinctive support throughout the students\u2019 development and progression in their academic experience \u2013 from recruitment through commencement. Through collaboration, communication, and commitment, all units within Enrollment Management achieve the highest level of student-centered service to current and prospective students and families as well as to campus partners across the University. The Technology Operations Unit within Enrollment Management provides technology support, technology-based solutions, systems configuration, identity and data management, and analysis across the division. The unit works closely with subject matter experts in Admissions, Registrar, and Financial Aid to meet the operational and reporting needs of various stockholders across campus. Works collaboratively with Admissions staff and campus stakeholders to develop scalable solutions that improve data integrity, application processing, communication delivery, and student experience. Develops and maintains Slate workflows, forms, queries, rules, communications, and related system functionality. Analyzes business processes and operational requirements to identify opportunities for automation, efficiency, and process improvement through Slate. Develops and maintains advanced reporting tools to guide decision-making and improve recruitment effectiveness. Stays current on Slate capabilities and best practices and actively engages with peer institutions to share ideas and improve processes. Evaluates new feature requests and assesses their potential impact and feasibility. Serves as liaison and Slate support resource for designated talent-based admissions programs and populations, including but not limited to Music, Dance, Theatre, Studio Art, and Film. Collaborates with program staff and campus partners to develop and maintain application and review processes that support program objectives. Coordinates with departmental stakeholders to reconcile data, identify process issues, send communications to prospective students, and improve applicant experiences. Supports the day-to-day operations of the undergraduate Slate system by maintaining documentation, ensuring data integrity, and providing responsive support to internal and external users. Contributes to the Admissions knowledgebase and delivers training to new users to promote consistent and effective use of Slate. Participates in special events hosted by the Office of Admissions. Assists other sections during peak times in support of the goals of Enrollment Management. Qualifications A Bachelor's degree and two years of experience; or a high school diploma or equivalent and six years of experience. (Note: a combination of post high school education and experience equal to six years.) Preferred Qualifications The ability to prioritize and organize multiple work assignments simultaneously. Experience with data management as well as using Microsoft Word, Excel, and Outlook or comparable software. Demonstrable technical experience to include handling configuration changes, modifications, enhancements and/or workarounds related to an application. Applicants should be able to establish and maintain effective working relationships and be able to communicate effectively verbally and in writing. Preferred applicants should have a strong understanding of University admissions and recruitment processes. Previous work experience with admissions CRMs (Slate). Candidates with a strong sense of initiative and the demonstrated ability to manage multiple responsibilities concurrently are preferred. The ability to make sound judgments while working in a deadline-driven environment is essential. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range $47,660, commensurate with education and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being re-advertised. Previous applicants need not reapply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63066&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Event Logistics Assistant (OPS/Part-Time)", "description": "Job Title Event Logistics Assistant (OPS/Part-Time) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63066 Location Sarasota, FL Full/Part Time Part-Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The John & Mable Ringling Museum of Art is located in Sarasota, Florida, and is a department of Florida State University . Responsibilities This role provides logistical setup of venues for events, both large and small. Responsibilities include: Carrying & moving tables, chairs, lighting, and other event-related equipment around the Ringling's 66-acre campus. Setting up and operating A/V equipment. Ensuring logistical setups are completed prior to event start time and cleared promptly at the close of the event. Assisting with oversight of vendor load-ins and load-outs. Interfacing with clients, vendors, guests, and Museum staff with a focus on customer service. Enforcing established rules and policies for sound, guests, and vendor conduct. Maintaining the safety of property, in conjunction with the security department. Attending weekly planning meetings and maintaining event equipment and supplies. Qualifications High school diploma or equivalent Valid Florida driver\u2019s license or the ability to obtain prior to hire. Ability to lift up to 50 lbs. Preferred Qualifications Experience with: Event logistics A/V equipment Customer service Ability to: Respond calmly to urgent situations Effectively communicate and problem-solve Contact Info For more information or technical assistance, please contact Ringling Human Resources via email or by calling 941-358-2771. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range $16.22 per hour (20 hours per week) How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an OPS/temporary job. Based on the duties, this position may require completion of a criminal history background check . Work Location: Sarasota, FL Employees are required to adhere to the business dress standards. This position is being readvertised. Previous applicants need not reapply. Working Hours This role has a dynamic schedule that is determined by planned events at The Ringling. Events are scheduled at a minimum of 2 weeks in advance of an event. Events are scheduled at various times, including days, evenings (as late as 1:00 AM), weekends, and holidays. Additional support is often needed during high season each year between October and May. Weekends, days, evenings, or holidays may be required as needed by Ringling. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63690&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Media Specialist- Public Affairs (National High Magnetic Field Lab)", "description": "Job Title Media Specialist- Public Affairs (National High Magnetic Field Lab) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63690 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department National High Magnetic Field Laboratory Join the world-renowned National High Magnetic Field Laboratory at Florida State University (FSU). FSU was recently recognized as one of America\u2019s Best-in-State Employers for its strong workplace culture and employee-centered values. Responsibilities This position supports the National High Magnetic Field Laboratory\u2019s public affairs and outreach efforts through the creation of digital, print, and multimedia communications. The position develops content and visual materials that promote the Lab's research, education, events, and community engagement initiatives, while supporting communications across web, social media, print, and other outreach channels for audiences at all three MagLab sites. Key Responsibilities: Conceptualize, design, and produce visually compelling print and digital marketing collateral, including brochures, reports, infographics, newsletters, promotional items, and other communication materials. Ensure consistency with MagLab branding and visual identity standards across communication products and platforms. Collaborate with the Public Affairs team to write, edit, and produce content that reaches and engages the Lab's audience map. Coordinate the Public Affairs team's community outreach portfolio, including Science Nights at the Library. Develop new hands-on experiences, cultivate and manage community partnerships, and expand outreach opportunities. Play a strong role in organizing, developing, and executing new visitor and community engagement experiences at MagLab Open House and other public-facing events. Implement creative communication strategies that advance the Lab's goals, strengthen stakeholder relationships, and build deeper trust with internal and external audiences. Support the Public Affairs Director and broader Public Affairs team with departmental initiatives, including proofreading, editing, Open House planning and execution, tours, special projects, and other communications needs as assigned. Support internal communication efforts through strategic and timely contributions to channels including the MagBLAB newsletter and the MagNET intranet. Qualifications A Bachelor's degree and two years of experience; or a high school diploma or equivalent and six years of experience. (Note: post-high school education may substitute for experience at the equivalent rate.) Preferred Qualifications Experience in graphic design & brand management Experience in email campaign marketing Experience in content creation Adobe Creative Suite proficiency, including Photoshop, Illustrator, and InDesign. Helpful What You Gain at FSU Opportunity to work at a world-renowned national research laboratory. Meaningful contributions to scientific discovery and student learning. A collaborative environment that values your expertise and invests in your growth. Contact Info For additional information, please contact Caroline McNiel . University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63665&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Program Director, Academic and Student Services", "description": "Job Title Program Director, Academic and Student Services Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63665 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Institute for Governance and Civics Florida State University Responsibilities Leads CLS program design, strategy, and policy in consultation with leadership. Manages project timelines, budgets, and process improvements. Oversees admissions goals, enrollment projections, student issues, curriculum updates, and required reporting. Drives CLS recruitment, marketing, and communications. Promotes programs at local, regional, and national events while producing updated collateral. Advises prospective students to align their interests with appropriate degree pathways. Directs CLS student services, managing admissions liaison, application reviews, and records. Leads advising and retention efforts (SAP, academic recovery), guides at-risk students to resources, and analyzes student success data to inform program decisions. Serves as the CLS expert on degree requirements and transfer articulation. Evaluates external transcripts, processes approved faculty exceptions, maintains curricular prerequisites and leveling standards, and ensures accurate credit posting in the SIS. Develop and implement database applications, spreadsheets, document templates and other technology solutions to automate and streamline office tasks. Build and maintain an alumni database. Manage internship activities. Evaluate and articulate transfer credits from other institutions. Analyze applicant, admission, registration benchmarks and graduation data for the CLS program. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and six years experience or a combination of post high school education and experience equal to ten years. Contact Info Lila Seagle - ls24bf@fsu.edu https://igc.fsu.edu/ University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63685&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Training Specialist, SLP - Florida Center for Interactive Media", "description": "Job Title Training Specialist, SLP - Florida Center for Interactive Media Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63685 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Florida Center for Interactive Media Responsibilities Produce and/or review technical assistance materials that support the development and implementation of quality services for students. Maintain current knowledge on appropriate practices related to speech/langauge impaired, deaf/hard of hearing, and visually impaired. Utilize available resources to provide assistance in other areas related to students. Research, analyze, and recommend guidance, policies and procedures related to federal and state requirements, curriculum, and instruction for students. Provide technical assistance through workshops, presentations, meetings, etc. to FDOE and constituents to support quality services for students. Perform other duties assigned related to the development and implementation of quality services for students. Qualifications A Bachelor's degree and two years of experience; or a high school diploma or equivalent and six years of experience. (Note: a combination of post high school education and experience equal to six years.) University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position requires the successful completion of a Level 2 Background Check by the Florida Department of Education. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63664&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Assistant/Associate in Research, 12 Month Salaried (Statistics)", "description": "Job Title Assistant/Associate in Research, 12 Month Salaried (Statistics) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63664 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Statistics | College of Arts and Sciences Responsibilities The Department of Statistics at Florida State University (FSU) invites applications for a 12-month, non-tenure-track Assistant in Research or Associate in Research faculty position in Biostatistics. The successful candidate will join one of the nation\u2019s oldest and most reputable statistics departments and contribute to an established, growing biostatistics research program through collaborative biomedical, clinical, translational, and population health research across a comprehensive research university. The successful candidate will: Collaborate with investigators from FSU Health, the College of Medicine, and other interdisciplinary research programs and centers across FSU on the study design, conduct, analysis, and interpretation of research findings. Provide statistical expertise in the application of appropriate modern statistical and computational methods. Contribute to preparing and participating in grant applications, research protocols, manuscripts, presentations, and other scholarly products. Communicate statistical methods and findings effectively to collaborators from diverse scientific and clinical backgrounds. Promote rigorous and reproducible research through appropriate statistical research collaboration. Contribute to the Department\u2019s interdisciplinary research initiatives and broader scholarly and research mission. Qualifications A doctoral degree from an accredited institution in Biostatistics, Statistics, or a closely related quantitative field is required by the time of appointment. Candidates should demonstrate: Strong training in statistical methodology, data analysis, and proficiency in statistical programming software such as R, SAS, Python, or equivalent platforms. Demonstrated potential for effective collaboration in biomedical, clinical, translational, public health, or other interdisciplinary research settings. Strong written and oral communication skills, including the ability to explain statistical concepts to collaborators from other disciplines. Ability to manage multiple collaborative research projects and work effectively both independently and as part of interdisciplinary teams. Experience communicating and collaborating effectively with investigators from non-statistical disciplines. Contact Info For questions about our hiring process, please contact Pamela McGhee . University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Please apply by January 15, 2027. This position requires that you submit a statement on research and have at least three confidential professional letters of recommendation submitted on your behalf. Follow the steps below to request these letters through our system: 1) After submitting your application, click the Careers link; 2) Click the My References link; 3) Click the Send/View Reference Request button next to the appropriate position; and 4) Follow the steps on that page to send your references a system generated email requesting they submit a letter of recommendation on your behalf. You may also return to the My References link and click on \"Send/View Reference Request\" to see if your references have responded, add additional references, or resend requests. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=61633&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Carpenter 3", "description": "Job Title Carpenter 3 Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 61633 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Facilities - Maintenance Responsibilities Performs repairs and replacement of floor tiles, ceramic tiles, and damaged carpet campus wide. Field measure, build and install, and or repair kitchen cabinets, vanities, and shelving units, along with general carpentry. Repair furniture tables, chairs, etc. Repair and or install new doors and hardware. Assist other trades as needed, ie, Locksmith, plasterer, and painters. Use vehicles to carry supplies and travel campus wide to perform various skilled maintenance. Performs minor plaster and sheet rock repairs, including maintenance, but not limited to such tasks as doors, furniture, painting, and lock hardware. Documents work performed and orders materials on appropriate departmental forms. Maintains tools and equipment, organizes and cleans assigned shop areas as required, and performs related work as assigned by supervisor. Performs additional maintenance and supervises helpers as required. Qualifications High school diploma or equivalency and ten years external professional experience. Must have a Builder's License. A valid State of Florida or Georgia Driver\u2019s License or the ability to obtain upon hire. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. Anticipated Salary Range The anticipated starting salary is $49,400, commensurate with experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our interactive too l to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://jobs.fsu.edu. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select \u201cyes\u201d to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for eligibility information and required documentation , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . The work schedule is 8:00am to 4:30pm with 30-minute break. This position is being re-opened. Previous applicants need not apply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63652&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Classroom Support Specialist - Information Technology Services", "description": "Job Title Classroom Support Specialist - Information Technology Services Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63652 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Information Technology Services Responsibilities Responsible for providing technical customer support for internal desktop systems, software, hardware, and network infrastructure. Installs, configures, and troubleshoots desktop systems, workstations, printers, servers, and network issues. Serves as a principal point of contact to answer inquiries and initiate resolution of problems. Communication may be on-site, electronic, or by phone. May respond to requests from the help desk to support end-users on various desktop systems issues and assess assigned priority levels. This position is part of ITS Classroom Support, which is the first line of support for instructors in over 250 classrooms around FSU. It is a very active, fast-paced environment, and the employee must learn about numerous new technologies. Qualifications High school diploma or equivalent and two years' experience or a combination of post high school education and experience equal to two years. A valid Florida or Georgia driver's license, class E or the ability to obtain one upon hire. Preferred Qualifications Thoroughly familiar with Windows 10 and/or 11 Customer support experience University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select \u201cyes\u201d to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for Veterans\u2019 Preference eligibility requirements and Veterans\u2019 Preference required documentation (PDF) , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . The schedule for this position is variable, but the usual hours are from 12:30PM to 9:30PM. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=62710&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Control Technician (Levels 1-2)", "description": "Job Title Control Technician (Levels 1-2) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 62710 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Facilities - Maintenance Responsibilities Perform advanced troubleshooting tasks for complex building systems such as variable speed drive replacement, machine-specific controllers repair or replacement, air compressors controls, boiler controls, heat exchangers, fume hoods, lab controls, and chiller controls. Perform network diagnostics for FLN and BLN Ethernet and other communication systems. Must be able to set up TECs on BACNet, P1, ModBus, KNX, and other networks used in the control systems. Perform all tasks as described in the Maintenance Technician position description, including basic mechanical, electrical, control, and plumbing tasks. Perform calibrations for sensors, controllers, flow meters, and other measurement devices. Coordinate with the Siemens on-site support technician to identify and repair components causing system faults. Coordinate with the energy engineer and other FSU team members to resolve complex system problems. Completes required safety training and complies with all safety standards, including, but not limited to: lock out-tag out, safe handling of refrigerant, confined space safety, safe handling of hazardous chemicals, participation in campus safety teams, and wearing required personal protective equipment (PPE). Reports complex and/or unusual problems to the supervisor and coordinates with other Maintenance staff as required to complete complex tasks. Operates mobile equipment and/or campus vehicles, including trucks, golf carts, personnel lifts, and forklifts, and maintains licensure and completes required training. Strives to provide excellent service to campus areas as measured by the 5-star program. Demonstrate proficient use of AiM mobile devices to complete work orders. Other duties as needed, including back-up plant operator duties in Utilities, and assisting other specialists or maintenance technicians. Qualifications High school diploma or equivalent and two years' experience, or a relevant Technical or vocational degree may substitute for experience. A valid State of Florida or Georgia Driver\u2019s License or ability to obtain upon hire. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. Anticipated Salary Range The anticipated starting salary is $37,000, commensurate with experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our interactive too l to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://jobs.fsu.edu. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select \u201cyes\u201d to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for eligibility information and required documentation , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being re-advertised. Previous applicants need not apply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63609&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Digital Humanities Librarian, 12 Month Salaried", "description": "Job Title Digital Humanities Librarian, 12 Month Salaried Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63609 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Florida State University Libraries Responsibilities The Digital Humanities Librarian serves as the advanced technical lead for CreateFSU, the Libraries' academic web-hosting service, providing expert consultation and technical support for faculty and student digital scholarship initiatives. This position collaborates closely with the DRS team, the AI and Data Lab, and campus partners to advance digital research methodologies, expand access to emerging technologies, and support the university's mission of research excellence and student success. The successful candidate will help empower researchers and students to explore, create, and share new forms of scholarship while contributing to a vibrant and growing digital humanities community at FSU. Support Digital Scholarship and Research Innovation Serve as the advanced technical lead for CreateFSU and related web-hosting platforms, providing consultation, troubleshooting, and support for complex digital scholarship projects. Assist faculty, graduate students, and researchers in developing and sustaining digital humanities projects using a variety of publishing and web-based platforms. Develop and maintain technical documentation, tutorials, and user guides that support digital research and publishing initiatives. Advance Student Learning and Research Skills Collaborate with DRS colleagues to design and deliver workshops, instructional programming, and technical training through initiatives such as the Digital Research Incubator. Provide instruction in digital research methods, programming, data analysis, and related technologies, helping students and researchers build practical skills that support academic and professional success. Partner with faculty to integrate digital humanities tools, methodologies, and assignments into undergraduate and graduate curricula. Build Campus Partnerships Consult with faculty, students, and staff on digital research projects, scholarly communication, and emerging technologies. Foster collaborative relationships with partner units, including the Research Computing Center and the Interdisciplinary Data Humanities Initiative. Serve as a resource for campus digital scholarship efforts and contribute to strategic initiatives that enhance research capabilities across disciplines. Contribute to Professional Excellence Engage in ongoing professional development and scholarly activities related to digital humanities, digital scholarship, and academic librarianship. Participate in library, university, and professional service activities. Stay informed of emerging trends, technologies, and best practices that advance digital research and scholarship. Qualifications Master's degree from an ALA-accredited library and information science program; or Master's degree in a humanities discipline, digital humanities, or a closely related field with relevant technical experience. Demonstrated ability to independently learn and apply new technologies, software applications, programming languages, and web-based tools. Understanding of current research trends, emerging technologies, and methodological shifts in the digital humanities. Strong interpersonal and communication skills, with a commitment to public service and user-centered support. Strong collaborative mindset and adaptability in a fast-paced, evolving organizational environment. Preferred Qualifications Experience providing technical support, debugging, or administration for web-hosting platforms (e.g., WordPress, Reclaim Hosting). Proficiency in programming languages common to humanistic research, such as Python or R. Familiarity with web development technologies (HTML, CSS, JavaScript) for site customization and troubleshooting. Demonstrated experience designing and delivering technical instruction, workshops, or academic presentations. Ph.D. in a humanities or related digital studies field. Other Information University Libraries seeks a collaborative and technically skilled Digital Humanities Librarian to help shape the future of digital scholarship, research innovation, and student learning. Located within the Office of Digital Research and Scholarship (DRS), this position provides an exciting opportunity to partner with faculty, researchers, and students on innovative digital humanities projects while helping develop technical skills and research capabilities that support academic success. Join us in advancing discovery, scholarship, and student success through the power of digital humanities and emerging technologies. At FSU Libraries, you will have the opportunity to: Collaborate with innovative faculty, researchers, and students on impactful digital scholarship projects. Help prepare students with the digital research and analytical skills needed for academic and career success. Work in a collaborative environment that values creativity, innovation, continuous learning, and professional growth. Contact Info Dr. Aaron Rodriguez , Director of Digital Research and Scholarship University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Starting at $60,000, commensurate with education and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63666&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Enrollment Management Specialist (Student Affairs/Admissions - College of Medicine)", "description": "Job Title Enrollment Management Specialist (Student Affairs/Admissions - College of Medicine) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63666 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Student Affairs/Admissions - College of Medicine Responsibilities Manages academic and administrative processes for enrollment within the Division of Student Affairs and Admissions (DSAA) at the College of Medicine. Manages all aspects of the electronic student files to include maintaining the security of student records, uploading all applicable documentation, processing acceptance documents, tracking enrollment requirements and posting all final degrees to the official student record. Acts as primary point of contact for all admitted students and enrolled students in the Bridge, MD, and PA degree programs. Counsels and corresponds with all incoming and currently enrolled students, providing information on guidelines and policies for University and college enrollment requirements. Manages scheduling courses and registration for all Bridge, MD, and PA courses each semester. Supports enrollment responsibilities as needed for Genetic Counseling degree program. Assists with managing student information and different academic calendars for all the cohorts for MD and PA. Assists Enrollment Manager with tasks related to graduation, degree certifications, licensure requirements, data reporting, and related tasks. Assists the division staff with student functions such as Orientation, Graduation, White Coat ceremony, actively participating as part of the DSAA team. Requires driving to transport sensitive documents on campus. Qualifications Bachelor's degree or higher and two years of experience. Valid Florida or Georgia Driver's License, or the ability to obtain prior to hire. Contact Info Melinda McDaniel Program Manager Enrollment Services University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Starting salary: mid $40,000's, commensurate with education and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . May require occasional evening and weekend hours. This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63657&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Open Rank Teaching Faculty I, 12 Month Salaried (Department of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering-Florida A&M University \u2013 Florida State University College of Engineering)", "description": "Job Title Open Rank Teaching Faculty I, 12 Month Salaried (Department of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering-Florida A&M University \u2013 Florida State University College of Engineering) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63657 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The Department of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering at the Florida A&M University-Florida State University College of Engineering is pleased to invite applications from highly qualified individuals for teaching faculty positions in the field of Aerospace and Mechanical Engineering in Tallahassee, Florida. Responsibilities The successful candidate is expected to have a strong commitment to teaching excellence in graduate courses and participate in college and professional service. Qualifications Candidates must possess an earned Ph.D. in Mechanical or Aerospace Engineering or a closely related discipline, demonstrate the ability to teach graduate-level classes (in-person and online), and have a strong interest in using technology in engineering education. Helpful The MAE Department currently has about 36 faculty, 200+ graduate students, ~1000 undergraduate students, and annual research expenditures exceeding $27M. We are starting our graduate programs (MS-Aero and MS-Mechanical) at the FSU Panama City (PC) campus. We expect the candidates to be part of our faculty at the FSU PC campus and to collaborate with our existing faculty at the Tallahassee campus. Potential applicants seeking more information are encouraged to visit our website Department of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering The FAMU-FSU College of Engineering is the nexus of two major public universities, each with a distinct mission but focused on world-class engineering education and research. Created by the Florida Legislature in 1982, the joint university is the College of Engineering for both Florida A&M and Florida State universities. This unique combination of focus, resources, and mission from our parent university has created on our campus a truly innovative atmosphere that leverages the benefits of the traditional HBCU model with the innovations of an R-1 public research university. After completing pre-requisites at their home university, FAMU and FSU students learn, study and research together at our independent campus with joint-appointed faculty and staff. Students graduate from their enrolling university and from the FAMU-FSU College of Engineering. Both FAMU and FSU are part of the State University System of Florida and are accredited by the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools Commission on Colleges. Additionally, all seven of the college\u2019s eligible undergraduate degree programs are accredited by the Engineering Accreditation Commission of ABET . Contact Info Any questions about the position should be directed to Dr. Unnikrishnan Sasidharan Nair, Search Committee Chairperson, usasidharannair@eng.famu.fsu.edu . University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include the following documents: A cover letter A full curriculum vitae A 2-page teaching statement. This statement should clearly indicate how the proposed teaching plan will connect with existing courses in the department and universities. A 1-page research statement (optional) Two selected publications for review (optional) The names and contact information of four potential references Faculty Information We are interested in candidates with backgrounds in Mechanical & Aerospace engineering who can teach graduate-level courses, including but not limited to Aerodynamics, Fluid Dynamics, Aerospace Propulsion, Aerospace Structures, Dynamics & Controls, and Mechanics & Materials. Other areas of Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering will also be considered, particularly if they complement the department's existing strengths. The positions are at the Teaching Faculty I level, but well-qualified candidates will be considered for a higher rank. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Application review will begin on January 4, 2027. Acceptance and review of applications will continue until the position is filled. The appointment is anticipated to begin in August 2027. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63361&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Travel Assistant (Herbert Wertheim College of Business)", "description": "Job Title Travel Assistant (Herbert Wertheim College of Business) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63361 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Herbert Wertheim College of Business Responsibilities Originates travel requests, cash advances, travel, and expense reimbursements to Wertheim College of Business students through Concur. Works directly with students traveling on behalf of the Wertheim College for student professional development opportunities, including travel requests, expense reports, and other methods that adhere to University policies and procedures. Holds a Travel Card. Responsible for reconciling monthly financial statements for Wertheim College travel and student professional funds. Works with the Senior Travel Administrator to monitor area travel budgets and report to the Dean\u2019s office. Ensures that expense reports are flowing correctly and check payments have been reconciled or redistributed as needed. Communicates and interprets University policies and procedures with the appropriate directors, department chairs, faculty, staff, and students. Assists the Assistant Director for Finance and Administration and Assistant Dean for Finance and Administration to develop controls to ensure compliance with the University policies and procedures. Partners with Wertheim College Business Analyst to support and maintain reporting system for students with eligible professional development funds. Partners with the Wertheim College\u2019s Student Engagement team and Business Career Services office to promote professional development opportunities to students. Educates students on proper utilization of funds. Assists the Senior Travel Administrator in processing other travel transactions during peak periods. Other duties as assigned. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and two years of experience; or a high school diploma/equivalent and six years of relevant experience. (Note: a combination of post high school education and experience equal to six years.) Contact Info Nicole Folkert Senior Travel Administrator University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being re-advertised. Previous applicants need not reapply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63579&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Warren and Margot Coville Photography Internship - Spring 2027 (Part-Time/OPS)", "description": "Job Title Warren and Margot Coville Photography Internship - Spring 2027 (Part-Time/OPS) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63579 Location Sarasota, FL Full/Part Time Part-Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The John & Mable Ringling Museum of Art is located in Sarasota, Florida, and is a department of Florida State University. Responsibilities The Warren and Margot Coville Photography Intern will: Work with the Curator of Photography and New Media to research objects in The Ringling's photography collection in order to update or correct catalog records. Assist in research and create bibliographies and summary reports on selected artists and/or photographs. Locates applicable resources onsite in the Ringling Museum's Art Library or identifies potential loans from other institutions. Assist the curator with the weekly survey of the paper storage vault on-site to view, assess, and research photographs. Assist in the planning and research for upcoming exhibitions. Qualifications Applicant must be currently enrolled in an undergraduate program at a college. Knowledge and skill using Microsoft Office Suite/Microsoft 365. Ability to lift boxes or books up to 15lbs. Preferred Qualifications Robust organizational and time management skills. Proficiency in Adobe Acrobat. Skill in online and library-based research. Ability to take direction and work independently. Experience compiling bibliographies in Chicago or MLA style. Students majoring or minoring in art, art history, or the humanities, especially with an interest in photography or the history of photography. Helpful Learning Outcomes Develop art history research skills Gain a better understanding of the history of photography Understand best practices for safe handling, care, and storage of photographic objects Develop skills in curatorship within a professional museum environment Length of Internship The internship will be during the Spring 2027 semester. The start date is flexible beginning January/early February 2027 and ending early May 2027 (maximum of 16 weeks). Contact Info For more information or technical assistance, please contact Ringling Human Resources via email or by calling 941-358-2771. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range $15.45 per hour (8 to 10 hours per week) How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Your application is not considered complete without the following items attached: Cover Letter Resume Unofficial Transcripts Considerations This is an OPS/Part-Time job This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check. Work Location: Sarasota, FL Please note this will be an in-person internship experience, not remote. Employees are required to adhere to the business dress standards. Working Hours 8 to 10 hours per week on weekdays, with a flexible schedule. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63667&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Custodial Worker (Multiple Vacancies)", "description": "Job Title Custodial Worker (Multiple Vacancies) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63667 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department FSU Custodial Services Responsibilities Cleans blinds, baseboards, windowsills in parlor and office; dusts, polishes furniture and vacuum carpet. Cleans all bathroom areas by scrubbing and disinfecting toilets, showers and lavatories, empties and cleans sanitary cans, tissues boxes and waste baskets; cleans student kitchens; sweeps entrance walks and building entrances. Dust mops floors and stairwells; cleans trash chute rooms; dust walls, doors, ceiling, baseboards and transoms in entire building. Collects trash from trash barrels on each floor to be picked up by the city collectors. Mops, waxes, and buffs floors in areas assigned. Checks reports and replace light bulbs that need replacing and cleans trash containers regularly. Apply disinfectants, deodorizes and other chemicals by spray method for sanitation purposes; performs other duties as assigned by supervisor. Qualifications 9th Grade Education Preferred Qualifications Preferred experience in custodial work. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select \u201cyes\u201d to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for Veterans\u2019 Preference eligibility requirements and Veterans\u2019 Preference required documentation (PDF) , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63660&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Immigration Advisor", "description": "Job Title Immigration Advisor Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63660 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The Center for Global Engagement Responsibilities This position will provide immigration-related services and advise international students enrolled in F-1 status. Serve as a Department of Homeland Security Designated School Official regularly submitting updates to the federal immigration (SEVIS) database to comply with regulatory reporting responsibilities and to authorize or recommend immigration benefits. Interpret and apply federal immigration regulations to support students in their maintenance of lawful F-1 status. Effectively use the Sunapsis database to ensure accurate immigration-related records. Assist and guide students with solving problems and identifying resources. Work closely with academic departments, university Human Resources, and other units throughout FSU. Engage in extensive and frequent communication by phone, Teams/Zoom, email and in-person with enrolled international students in F-1 status, other CGE team members, FSU faculty and staff, community, employers, and representatives of government agencies on issues related to federal F-1 immigration regulations (e.g. enrollment, graduation, transfer/change of level, employment authorization, extension of stay, etc.), general immigration laws that impact students in F-1 status (e.g. registration documentation, address reporting, international travel, change of status, etc.), and other state and federal policies. Help create supportive environment for international students. Work closely with academic departments, Admissions, Registrar, Student Finance, Division of Student Affairs departments, and other partners across campus. Hold multiple roles in FSU databases, with access to input and change visa codes, place and remove holds, view basic admissions information, student account information, student addresses, and student enrollment information, etc. Participate in the development and testing of new electronic forms developed by the Program Director for Data and Compliance, recommend updates to current forms and form communication, and provide feedback on data feed and data extract issues. Access daily the federal government immigration (SEVIS) database and Sunapsis to enter determinations regarding continuing eligibility for F-1 status, process employment authorizations (Curricular Practical Training) or recommendations (Optional Practical Training), update academic program changes, transfer immigration records to other U.S. institutions, and submit other required updates within regulatory reporting periods. Maintain accurate background information and documentation in Sunapsis to support the submitted SEVIS updates as required by regulations. Monitor daily auto-assigned cases in Sunapsis to identify immigration status issues and to review and process submitted electronic forms. Use Sunapsis communication tools to contact students regarding their cases to ensure consistent advising. Deliver regular Optional Practical Training workshops in person and via Zoom in rotation with other CGE advisors. Participate in new international student orientations each semester by giving presentations, checking students in, and/or guiding short tours. Play a role in the semesterly ACIREMA interactive simulation activity for the university community. Assist with developing and providing additional presentations and workshops for international students and the FSU community. Attend trainings offered by Undergraduate Advising, Human Resources, Research Compliance, and other areas. Contribute to CGE assessment efforts as needed. Participate in major CGE events and programs. Serve on DSA and/or CGE committees as needed. Provide back-up support to other advisors and to front desk. Participate in professional associations for international educators. Other duties as assigned. Qualifications A Bachelor's degree and two years of experience; or a high school diploma or equivalent and six years of experience. (Note: a combination of post high school education and experience equal to six years.) Applicant must be a U.S. citizen or permanent resident due to federal SEVIS database requirements. Preferred Qualifications Master\u2019s degree in international affairs, higher education, or closely related field. Experience as a Designated School Official and/or Alternate Responsible Officer using SEVIS regularly. Experience using Sunapsis, Terra Dotta, or other case management software. Ability to manage competing priorities while maintaining a high level of accuracy and efficiency. Experience presenting information in one-on-one, small group, and large group settings both in-person and online. Evidence of strong professional writing skills and ability to analyze complex information. Experience living, studying, or working abroad and knowledge of a second language. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Starting in the high $40,000\u2019s to low $50,000\u2019s, commensurate with education and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Applicants must upload a cover letter when completing the online application. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. Review of applicants will begin on October 16, 2026. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=61585&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Teaching Faculty I, 9 Month Salaried (Department of Business Analytics, Information Systems & Supply Chain, College of Business)", "description": "Job Title Teaching Faculty I, 9 Month Salaried (Department of Business Analytics, Information Systems & Supply Chain, College of Business) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 61585 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Business Analytics, Information Systems & Supply Chain | College of Business Responsibilities The Department of Business Analytics, Information Systems, and Supply Chain (BAISSC) at Florida State University\u2019s Herbert Wertheim College of Business invites applications for a teaching faculty position (non-tenured track, 9 months salaried). The start date is August 2027. Responsibilities include teaching undergraduate courses in the areas of Business Analytics and Information Systems. Possible graduate level and/or additional course offerings may be available depending on qualifications. Qualifications An earned doctorate or other terminal degree from an accredited institution in a field closely related to Business Analytics or Information Systems is required. Preferred Qualifications Preference will be given to candidates with teaching experience in areas such as Operations Management, Business Analytics, and/or Management Information Systems. Contact Info For inquiries regarding this position, please contact: Dr. Noyan Ilk Department Chair Department of Business Analytics, Information Systems & Supply Chain University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://hr.fsu.edu/facultyjobs. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Application materials include: 1) A letter of interest 2) Curriculum vitae 3) Three letters of reference This position requires that you have three confidential professional letters of recommendation submitted on your behalf. Follow the steps below to request these letters through our system: 1) After submitting your application, click the Explore Jobs link; 2) Click the My References link; 3) Click the Send/View Reference Request button next to the appropriate position; and 4) Follow the steps on that page to send your references a system generated email requesting they submit a letter of recommendation on your behalf. You may also return to the My References link and click on \"Send/View Reference Request\" to see if your references have responded, add additional references, or resend requests. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position will remain open until January 15, 2027. For priority consideration, please submit all application materials by November 15, 2026, when application reviews will begin. Applications received after this date will be reviewed on a rolling basis until the position is filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63650&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Open Rank Associate Dean for Academic Affairs, 12 Month Salaried - The Graduate School", "description": "Job Title Open Rank Associate Dean for Academic Affairs, 12 Month Salaried - The Graduate School Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63650 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The Graduate School Responsibilities The Associate Dean for Academic Affairs serves as a member of the Graduate School's senior leadership team and provides strategic leadership for graduate academic affairs, policy development, academic quality, student success initiatives, and graduate program administration. The Associate Dean works collaboratively with the Dean, Graduate Program Directors, college leadership, faculty, students, and university stakeholders to advance the academic mission of the Graduate School and support excellence in graduate education. The Associate Dean supervises one full-time professional staff member and serves as a primary resource for graduate academic policy interpretation, implementation, and assessment across the university. Academic Policy Leadership Provide leadership for the development, implementation, interpretation, and periodic review of graduate academic policies, procedures, and standards. Direct and advise Dean on graduate student appeals and exceptions processes including, admissions appeals, enrolled student appeals, time extensions, and other exception requests. Recommend policy revisions to support student success, academic excellence, and regulatory compliance. Collaborate with university leadership, colleges, and departments to ensure consistent application of graduate policies. Monitor emerging issues, best practices, and national trends in graduate education and recommend appropriate responses. Graduate Academic Programs and Quality Assurance Provide oversight for graduate academic program review processes and continuous improvement efforts. Support academic units in the development of new graduate degrees, certificates, concentrations, and program modifications. Coordinate review of graduate curriculum proposals and academic program changes. Promote innovation and excellence in graduate education through evidence-based practices and strategic initiatives. Graduate Student Success and Academic Progress Lead policy initiatives that promote graduate student retention, progression, completion, and professional development. Guide university-wide policy approaches to graduate academic support and student success. Review complex academic issues involving graduate students and recommend resolutions consistent with university policy. Collaborate with faculty, advisors, and administrative units to ensure student success. Leadership and University Collaboration Serve as a member of the Graduate School senior leadership team. Represent the Graduate School on university committees, work groups, task forces, and external organizations. Foster productive relationships with Graduate Program Directors, department chairs, deans, faculty, and student groups. Provide and maintain Graduate Program Director resources, including GPD Orientation, the GPD Handbook and the Graduate Student Handbook. Collaborate with other Graduate School leaders on strategic planning, assessment, accreditation, and institutional initiatives. Supervision and Administrative Management Supervise, mentor, and evaluate one full-time professional staff member. Establish goals, priorities, and performance expectations for supervised personnel. Support the efficient administration of academic affairs functions within the Graduate School. Monitor workflows and implement process improvements. Other Duties as Assigned Undertake special projects and initiatives assigned by the Dean. Serve on university committees or represent the Graduate School at institutional and professional events. Perform other duties consistent with the responsibilities of an Associate Dean. Qualifications Academic master's degree or highest-level terminal degree from an accredited institution in an appropriate field of specialization or equivalent qualifications based on professional experience. Preferred Qualifications Earned doctorate or terminal degree in an appropriate discipline from an accredited institution. Tenured faculty member at the rank of Associate Professor or Professor. Record of scholarly achievement and professional accomplishment sufficient to maintain graduate faculty status. Demonstrated experience in graduate education administration, academic leadership, program leadership, or related responsibilities. Knowledge of graduate academic policies, curriculum development, and academic program administration. Experience working collaboratively with faculty, academic administrators, and students. Demonstrated commitment to student success and academic excellence. Strong analytical, organizational, and problem-solving skills. Excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. Demonstrated ability to supervise, mentor, and support professional staff. Ability to interpret and apply university policies, procedures, and regulations. Academic administrative experience as a department chair, associate chair, graduate program director, assistant/associate dean, or similar leadership role. Experience with graduate student success, admissions, retention, and completion strategies. Experience developing or revising academic policies and procedures. Experience working with faculty governance structures and university committees. Demonstrated ability to build collaborative relationships across academic and administrative units. Record of leading major projects or managing complex organizational initiatives. Contact Info Brian Barton , Search Committee Chair University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Please submit a cover letter outlining your interest in the position, leadership experience, and qualifications relevant to the responsibilities of the Associate Dean role. This position requires that you have three confidential professional letters of recommendation submitted on your behalf. Follow the steps below to request these letters through our system: After submitting your application, click the Careers link Click the My References link Click the Send/View Reference Request button next to the appropriate position Follow the steps on that page to send your references a system generated email requesting they submit a letter of recommendation on your behalf. You may also return to the My References link and click on \"Send/View Reference Request\" to see if your references have responded, add additional references, or resend requests. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Appropriate rank associated with the appointment will be determined based on the selected candidate\u2019s qualifications and experience. The distribution of effort between the administrative assignment within the Graduate School and teaching, research, service, and/or other faculty responsibilities in an academic department will be determined based on the selected candidate's qualifications and experience. Financial Disclosure may be required. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63647&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Program Associate - Educational Psychology & Learning Systems - Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences", "description": "Job Title Program Associate - Educational Psychology & Learning Systems - Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63647 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Educational Psychology & Learning Systems | Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences Responsibilities Coordinates and maintains student files and all related components for the Sport Psychology program (Master's and doctoral levels) from initial contact as applicants, through their graduation from the program, and beyond. Admission tasks, which occur on an annual cycle for Fall admission, include but are not limited to: preparing and regularly updating standard communication letters for applicants to be uploaded to Slate, communicating with applicants by e-mail and phone; calculating GPAs for faculty review; alerting faculty about strong completed applicant files for fellowship consideration; sending related admissions paperwork to OASIS for processing and serves as liaison with that office. Maintaining and evaluating admission statistics for the Sport Psychology program, including GRE score tracking, GPA tracking, and related information; reporting on admissions activities to the Sport Psychology faculty. Converts admissions files into permanent student files and maintains updated and accurate inventories of these files. Communicates graduation lists to Sport Psychology coordinators. Recommends policies and procedures related to admissions activities in Sport Psychology. Assists with academic advising activities of the Sport Psychology program. Processes travel for the Educational Psychology and Learning Systems department. Travel tasks include but are not limited to: entering T-auths and Expense reports for approval in Concur; collecting back-up receipts and other required documentation for travel processing; maintaining accurate records of all travel T-auths and Expense reports. Communicates with travelers regarding necessary documentation. Requires knowledge of various budgets related to travel (E&G, Auxiliary, C&G, Foundation), several of which are outside the department. Processes non-travel reimbursements in Concur as required. Creates and maintains the Course Schedule Master (CSM) each semester for entire EPLS department, working with faculty program coordinators and Associate Chair to gather accurate and complete data for CSM building. Processes Drop/Add slips, DIS, preliminary exams, dissertation hours, defenses, and similar coursework for all students in the Counselor Education and Combined PhD in Counseling and School Psychology programs. Advises students on policies and procedures related to coursework, Drop/Add, defenses, deadlines, timelines, signatures, programs of study, and all other registration and academically related matters. Processes departmental textbook orders each semester in conjunction with CSM building. Assists Senior Administrative Specialist with tuition waiver entry and tracking, FACET and AOR activities, Promotion and Tenure activities and serves as secondary attendance and leave representative. Serves as P-card proxy for the department, reconciles weekly charges against receipts and submits monthly reconciliation report with back-up to the Purchasing Department. Qualifications High school diploma or equivalent and four years of experience. (Note: post high-school education and/or experience may substitute at a comparable rate.) Preferred Qualifications Experience providing administrative support in a higher education or academic environment. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships. Ability to interpret academic program requirements and provide advice. Ability to communicate effectively verbally and in writing. Experience processing travel, reimbursements, purchasing, or other financial transactions. Contact Info Bryan Richards , Search Committee Chair/Department Manager University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select \u201cyes\u201d to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for Veterans\u2019 Preference eligibility requirements and Veterans\u2019 Preference required documentation (PDF) , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=62604&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Teaching Faculty - DNP Core Coordinator, 12 Month Salaried", "description": "Job Title Teaching Faculty - DNP Core Coordinator, 12 Month Salaried Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 62604 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department College of Nursing Responsibilities The FSU College of Nursing is seeking to hire a collaborative Doctor of Nursing Practice (DNP) Core Course Coordinator responsible for coordination of one or more courses within the DNP core curriculum, based in Tallahassee, Florida (FL). Responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Provide leadership and oversight for assigned DNP core course(s), including maintenance of the master syllabi and course structure. Ensure alignment of course objectives, assignments, and evaluations with DNP Program Outcomes and AACN Essentials (2021) competencies. Coordinate course implementation across multiple sections and faculty instructors, ensuring consistency in expectations and grading standards. Collaborate with program leadership to support sequencing and scaffolding of scholarly deliverables across the DNP curriculum. Support development of competencies related to evidence-based practice, systems leadership, quality improvement, and practice change initiatives. Provide guidance and support to faculty of record and adjunct instructors teaching the course. Monitor course outcomes, student performance trends, and evaluation data to support continuous curriculum improvement. Contribute to program evaluation, accreditation documentation, and curriculum planning activities as needed. Performs other duties as assigned. This role focuses on high-quality didactic instruction in the graduate nursing program and supports the college\u2019s mission to prepare practice-ready, compassionate nurse leaders. Faculty are expected to be actively engaged in teaching, student mentorship, and academic service in a collaborative, on-campus environment. For more information about our academic programs, please visit the following link: Academics | College of Nursing . Qualifications An academic doctorate (PhD, DNP) or highest-level terminal degree in nursing from an accredited institution is required, with eligibility for graduate faculty status. Non-nurse trained candidates will not be considered. Active FL Registered Nurse (RN) or Advanced Practice Registered Nurse (APRN) license; or licensed in another state with eligibility to obtain FL licensure within 30 days of hire. Three to five years of teaching experience in graduate nursing education. Preferred Qualifications Knowledge of DNP education standards and AACN Essentials (2021) Experience with curriculum development, course coordination, or program evaluation Strong written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. Demonstrated ability to work well with students, faculty, and staff at all levels within a collaborative environment. Experience with Microsoft Word, Excel and Outlook or equivalent software. Experience supervising and training employees. Experience meeting project deadlines. Other Information This is a full-time, in-person position, and the level is commensurate with experience. Successful candidates must relocate to Tallahassee, Florida. Up to three official teaching evaluations from your most recent teaching experiences may be requested later in the recruiting process. Contact Info Inquiries about the positions may be directed to Dr. Susan A Baker , Associate Dean for Faculty Affairs. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our interactive too l to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://hr.fsu.edu/facultyjobs. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. In your application, please include the following documents: Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae (CV) including a listing of courses developed and taught Teaching Philosophy, not to exceed two pages Do not include reference letters in your application; they will be collected later in the recruiting process. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being readvertised as opened until filled. Previous applicants need not reapply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=62755&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Teaching Faculty - FNP Coordinator, 12 Months Salaried - College of Nursing", "description": "Job Title Teaching Faculty - FNP Coordinator, 12 Months Salaried - College of Nursing Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 62755 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department College of Nursing Join a nationally recognized leader in nursing education, known for research distinction and educational innovation. With simulation space in a brand new $126 million FSU Health building, $12 million to design a new building, and a transformative $10 million gift, the FSU College of Nursing is hiring additional faculty for strategic growth. Responsibilities The FSU College of Nursing is seeking to hire a collaborative educator to teach in our graduate program, based in Tallahassee, Florida (FL). Responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Actively work with the Assistant Dean for Graduate Program to develop and revise Graduate Curriculum. Assume an active role in recruiting prospective graduate students to the FNP (Family Nurse Practitioner) major; Review potential plans of study with prospective students. Maintain pertinent professional organization membership and assume leadership roles in professional organizations that support FNP practice and education. Teach Core Doctor of Nursing Practice (DNP) or FNP courses as assigned; assume lead responsibility for practicum courses within program. Conduct DNP and certificate FNP Program orientation activities. Oversee Objective Structured Clinical Evaluation (OSCE) within track. Work with Clinical Coordinator to recruit high-quality clinical preceptors. Manage student clinical rotations in conjunction with assigned clinical faculty. Work with the Assistant Dean for Graduate Program to forecast student enrollments in track courses. Work with Clinical Coordinator to execute PEPs, or preceptor forms/letters as needed. Review and verify clinical logs of DNP and certificate FNP students, providing student and faculty feedback, as appropriate. Review and monitor clinical hours for graduate students. Track certification requirements and results for Graduate Program. Evaluate transfer credits for FNP students in conjunction with the Assistant Dean. Complete and conduct FNP student annual review (May - June) and guide students through admission, matriculation and completion of major related courses. Complete education verification forms for certification. Other duties as assigned in the coordination of track-related activities as the lead faculty program track faculty member, such as but not limited to: supporting new faculty teaching in both didactic and practicum courses (orient to course syllabus, set up Simple syllabus as needed, orient students and relevant faculty to the track, track courses, and track-related activities) This role focuses on high-quality instruction in the graduate nursing program and supports the college\u2019s mission to prepare practice-ready, compassionate nurse leaders. Faculty are expected to be actively engaged in teaching, student mentorship and academic service in a collaborative environment. For more information about our academic programs, visit our Academics page . Qualifications An academic doctorate (PhD, DNP) or highest-level terminal degree in nursing from an accredited institution is required, with eligibility for graduate faculty status. Non-nurse trained candidates will not be considered. Active FL Registered Nurse (RN) or Advanced Practice Registered Nurse (APRN) license; or licensed in another state with eligibility to obtain FL licensure within 30 days of hire. Two to three years of teaching experience in graduate nursing education. Preferred Qualifications Knowledge of DNP education standards and AACN Essentials (2021). Experience with curriculum development, course coordination, or program evaluation Strong written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. Demonstrated ability to work well with students, faculty, and staff at all levels within a collaborative environment. Experience with Microsoft Word, Excel and Outlook or equivalent software. Experience supervising and training employees. Experience meeting project deadlines. Other Information This is a full-time, in-person position, and the level is commensurate with experience. Successful candidates must relocate to Tallahassee, Florida. Up to three official teaching evaluations from your most recent teaching experiences may be requested later in the recruiting process. Contact Info Inquiries about the positions may be directed to Dr. Susan A Baker , Associate Dean for Faculty Affairs. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our interactive too l to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://hr.fsu.edu/facultyjobs. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. In your application, please include the following documents: Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae (CV) including a listing of courses developed and taught Teaching Philosophy, not to exceed two pages Please do not include reference letters in your application; they will be collected later in the recruiting process. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This is a full-time, in-person position, and the level is commensurate with experience. Successful candidates must relocate to Tallahassee, Florida. Up to three official teaching evaluations from your most recent teaching experiences may be requested later in the recruiting process. This position is being readvertised as open until filled. Previous applicants need not reapply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63642&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Teaching Faculty I, 12 Month Salaried (Meteorology)", "description": "Job Title Teaching Faculty I, 12 Month Salaried (Meteorology) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63642 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Earth, Ocean and Atmospheric Science I College of Arts & Sciences Responsibilities The Department of Earth, Ocean, and Atmospheric Sciences (EOAS) at Florida State University (FSU) invites applications for a full-time, non-tenure track, 12-month Teaching Faculty I position beginning Fall 2027 to teach undergraduate meteorology courses for majors and non-majors. We are particularly interested in candidates who can teach synoptic and broadcast meteorology. A full-time specialized faculty member in the Teaching Track (Teaching Faculty I, II, III) shall normally be assigned not less than 75% teaching responsibility and not more than 5% research responsibility, averaged over any academic year. This typically is represented as approximately eight 3-credit courses a year, with course reduction possible for substantial service roles such as academic advising or the TV Meteorology Program studio manager. Qualifications A Ph.D. or highest-level terminal degree from an accredited institution in Meteorology or Atmospheric Science or equivalent qualifications based on professional experience is required, with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching. M.S. applicants with substantial teaching or broadcast meteorology experience post-degree are encouraged to apply. Other Information EOAS has 37 tenured/tenure-earning faculty, 3 teaching faculty, about 350 undergraduate students, about 100 graduate students, a student population, and grants undergraduate and/or graduate degrees in Geology, Meteorology, Oceanography, and Environmental Sciences. For additional information on EOAS research and FSU\u2019s facilities and resources, please visit our website . The undergraduate meteorology degree program is large (typically 30 students each year) with a long and distinguished history dating back over 75 years. Contact Info Inquiries may be addressed to the chair of the search committee, Prof. Robert Hart . University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applications should include a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching interest/philosophy, and contact information for three references who can provide letters of recommendation. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Review of applications will begin immediately. The deadline for receipt of applications is November 13, 2026. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63476&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Administrative Specialist - UBA/Herbert Wertheim College of Business", "description": "Job Title Administrative Specialist - UBA/Herbert Wertheim College of Business Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63476 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department University Business Administrators \u2013 Herbert Wertheim College of Business Responsibilities This position is responsible for managing administrative functions with a primary focus on faculty and a shared focus on USPS and A&P employees within the Herbert Wertheim College of Business (HWCOB), respective schools, departments, programs, and institutes. Faculty Personnel Administration Serves as the primary administrator for faculty personnel processes within the HWCOB, liaising between the college and its campus partners. Coordinates in consultation with the Assistant Director on faculty recruitment, RAMP screening, work authorization processes, appointments, reappointments, onboarding, assignments of responsibilities (AOR), FACET reporting, annual evaluations, promotion and tenure, post-tenure review, sabbaticals, leave requests, overloads, and other faculty employment actions. Interprets University policies and provides recommendations based on knowledge of the organization's business administrative objectives and activities. Ensures compliance with university regulations, collective bargaining agreements, policies, procedures, and deadlines. Maintains faculty personnel records and prepares required documentation and reports. Serves as a resource to college staff, faculty, and administrators regarding faculty personnel procedures. Staff Personnel Administration Provides shared transactional support for USPS and A&P personnel actions across the HWCOB. Collaborates with departmental team members to coordinate recruitment, hiring, onboarding, personnel transactions, evaluations, leave administration, funding changes, position updates, separation processes, and related duties. Provides guidance to supervisors, interpreting and applying university HR policies and procedures. Refers complex policy interpretation issues to the Assistant Director as appropriate. Ensures personnel documentation is processed accurately and timely. Provides backup support for faculty personnel administration functions. Records, Reporting, and Compliance Maintains departmental personnel records and tracking systems, monitors personnel deadlines, and prepares reports and documentation. Tracks departmental HR transactions throughout the workflow cycle, providing timely status updates and advising staff and supervisors on required actions, next steps, and appropriate procedures. Serves as a key resource and quality control checkpoint for departmental HR transactions initiated by supervisors, ensuring accuracy, policy alignment, and adherence to established standards. Utilizes myFSU Business Intelligence (BI) to generate cyclical HR Actives and cost center reports, reconciling appointments, compensation levels, and funding distributions to maintain data integrity. Prepares payroll certification documentation and HR Actives reports for leadership review, providing critical support in validating payroll accuracy and ensuring compliance with internal controls and audit requirements. Process Improvement and Administrative Support Identifies, recommends, and implements departmental HR process improvement initiatives. Contributes to special projects, communications, and operational support activities. Provides cross-training and backup support for other departmental HR functions as needed to ensure continuity of operations and customer service. Other duties as assigned for the HWCOB. Qualifications A Bachelor's degree and two years of experience; or a high school diploma or equivalent and six years of experience. (Note: a combination of post high school education and experience equal to six years.) Preferred Qualifications Experience supporting human resources functions in a higher education environment Experience coordinating faculty personnel processes or academic employment actions Strong organizational, communication, and customer service skills University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being re-advertised. Previous applicants need not reapply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63516&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Vocal Coaching, 9 Month Salaried - College of Music", "description": "Job Title Assistant Professor of Vocal Coaching, 9 Month Salaried - College of Music Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63516 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department College of Music - Voice & Opera Area Responsibilities The qualified candidate will coach graduate voice majors in preparation for degree recitals and opera productions and will be expected to demonstrate a strong commitment to mentoring students. The candidate will also teach appropriate vocal-related courses in undergraduate and graduate sequences, including diction and song literature. Musical collaboration for faculty recitals will be expected. Additional responsibilities may include instructing graduate collaborative piano students; serving as Music Director of Opera Workshop; mentoring Opera Graduate Assistants; and contributing to other instructional and artistic activities appropriate to the candidate\u2019s experience and expertise. Qualifications Candidate will have completed a doctoral degree in collaborative piano or a master's degree with equivalent professional experience with a record of achievement as an actively performing, collaborative artist. Knowledge of and experience in working as a vocal coach with professional proficiency in English, French, German and Italian lyric diction is required. Candidate must have experience coaching opera and vocal repertoire, across all major historical periods, at the post-secondary and/or professional level. The ideal candidate must be open to a range of musical styles and approaches to learning and teaching, recruitment, creative activity, and service. Preferred Qualifications Experience in Spanish, Russian and/or Czech is desired. The qualified candidate should demonstrate extensive experience performing and collaborating with vocal artists at the collegiate and/or professional levels. Excellent interpersonal and communication skills and demonstrated ability/interest in working in a collegial and mutually supportive environment is expected. Other Information FSU Opera encompasses three fully staged opera productions each year with orchestra; up to two outreach opera productions; curricular Opera Workshop and Opera Literature courses; MM programs in opera coaching and opera stage direction; and fully staged opera scenes programs. The qualified candidate will be an experienced and proficient opera coach and rehearsal accompanist and will contribute as a member of the FSU Opera team. Additional opportunities and responsibilities may be available depending on the candidate\u2019s experience and expertise. The College of Music at Florida State University: is the largest such college in the Southeast and the third largest university-based music program in the nation. With over 90 faculty and 40 support staff, the College offers a range of degrees in music, baccalaureate through the doctorate. We are home to approximately 700 undergraduate and 400 graduate students, who represent nearly every state in the nation and 20 foreign countries. Contact Info For technical assistance applying to this position, please contact Eden Wahlquist Other inquiries may be directed to the search committee chair as follows: Dr. Marc\u00eda Porter , Committee Chair University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Application Materials: Cover letter, one to two pages CV Names and contact information for five references Links to performances of operatic and art song repertoire in a variety of languages, 20 to 30 minutes Vocal coaching video of the candidate coaching singer(s) from the piano, 20 to 30 minutes All videos and recordings must be from the last five years Confidential letters of recommendation from at least three references will also need to be submitted on your behalf. Letters may be solicited through our system or directed to CM-HiringDocs@fsu.edu Follow the steps below to request these letters through our system: 1) After submitting your application, click the Careers link; 2) Click the My References link; 3) Click the Send/View Reference Request button next to the appropriate position; and 4) Follow the steps on that page to send your references a system generated email requesting they submit a letter of recommendation on your behalf. You may also return to the My References link and click on \"Send/View Reference Request\" to see if your references have responded, add additional references, or resend requests. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. However, for priority consideration, please complete all application materials by November 15, 2026. Review of applications will begin immediately and will remain ongoing until the position is filled. Appointment will begin August 9, 2027. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63616&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Interior Design, 9 Month Salaried - School of Design", "description": "Job Title Assistant/Associate Professor of Interior Design, 9 Month Salaried - School of Design Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63616 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department School of Design Responsibilities Florida State University invites applications for a full-time, nine-month, tenure-track faculty position in Interior Design program at the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor. We seek a collaborative educator and scholar who will contribute to undergraduate and graduate education through innovative teaching, research and/or creative scholarship, and student mentorship. The successful candidate will advance human-centered design, evidence-based inquiry, and creative and critical thinking while preparing students to address complex challenges in the built environment. Candidates should demonstrate expertise that complements and expands the program\u2019s strengths and the ability to connect design inquiries with professional practice. We welcome contributions to interdisciplinary teaching and scholarship, graduate education, and the thoughtful integration of emerging technologies into design. Teach undergraduate and graduate studio, lecture, and/or seminar courses in interior design. Contribute expertise in Construction Documents, Construction Systems, Commercial Office and Hospitality Design, with flexibility to support other areas of the curriculum. Develop and sustain a program of research and/or creative scholarship, disseminate work through appropriate peer-reviewed or juried outlets, and pursue external funding opportunities. Mentor undergraduate and graduate students; advise graduate research and creative work; and chair or serve on thesis committees. Participate in curriculum development, assessment, and accreditation activities. Contribute to interdisciplinary collaboration and the integration of research, creative inquiry, and professional practice into teaching. Provide service to the academic unit, College, University, community, and profession, as appropriate to rank and assignment. Participate in relevant academic and/or professional organizations. Qualifications An earned master\u2019s or doctoral degree in interior design, interior architecture, architecture, or a closely related field with substantial working experience Demonstrated teaching experience with Adobe Creative Cloud and Autodesk products, and familiarity with rendering & 3D visualization software (e.g., Enscape). Demonstrated ability to teach interior design studios and related courses effectively. Demonstrated ability to develop a sustained program of research and/or creative scholarship. Proficiency in design communication and the application of relevant design technologies in teaching, practice, and/or scholarship. Effective oral, written, and visual communication skills. Ability to collaborate with colleagues and support student learning and development. Candidates for appointment at the Assistant Professor rank should demonstrate promise in teaching, research and/or creative scholarship, and service. Candidates for appointment at the Associate Professor rank should demonstrate a sustained record of teaching effectiveness, research and/or creative achievement, and service commensurate with appointment at that rank at Florida State University. Preferred Qualifications An MFA, M. Arch, PhD, or equivalent terminal degree in interior design, interior architecture, architecture, or a closely related field, completed by the appointment start date. Expertise in emerging design technologies (e.g., AI, VR, AR, etc.) and their thoughtful application to design education and inquiry (research/creative components). NCIDQ certification, architectural licensure or NCARB certification, and/or other relevant professional credentials. Teaching experience at the undergraduate and/or graduate level. Professional practice experience in interior design, interior architecture, architecture, or related areas. Experience mentoring graduate students and supporting their thesis research or creative scholarship. Experience with interdisciplinary teaching, research, or collaborative design practice. Evidence of external funding activity or potential to develop externally supported projects. Familiarity with Council for Interior Design Accreditation standards and accreditation processes. Other Information The Interior Design Program in the School of Design at Florida State University emphasizes human-centered design, evidence-based design processes, and creative and critical thinking. The program prepares students to contribute to human health, safety, and well-being through the environments and experiences they design. Situated within the College of Fine Arts, the program offers opportunities to connect design education with broader artistic, scholarly, and interdisciplinary inquiry. The successful candidate will contribute to the continued development of undergraduate and graduate education and help strengthen the program\u2019s research and creative contributions. The College of Fine Arts at Florida State University is dedicated to fostering artistic excellence, creative exploration, and scholarly inquiry across a variety of disciplines. Our renowned faculty and staff educate and empower students to become visionary performers, artists, educators, art historians, designers, curators, art therapists, researchers, and arts administrators who shape the future of the visual arts, healing arts, performing arts, and design. Through passionate teaching, community engagement, innovative research, and artistic practice we enrich lives, elevate artistic expression, and inspire positive change and well-being in society. Contact Info Questions may be directed to Search committee chair, Daejin Kim , Ph.D., Associate Professor University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. A letter of interest addressing qualifications, teaching expertise, and anticipated contributions to the program. A curriculum vitae. A teaching statement of one to two pages. A research and/or creative scholarship statement of one to two pages. A PDF portfolio containing 10\u201320 examples of research, creative, professional, and/or teaching-related work. Identify the applicant\u2019s role in collaborative projects and distinguish student work from the applicant\u2019s own work. Confidential Letters of Reference: This position requires that you have three confidential professional letters of recommendation submitted on your behalf. Follow the steps below to request these letters through our system: 1) After submitting your application, click the Explore Jobs link; 2) Click the My References link; 3) Click the Send/View Reference Request button next to the appropriate position; and 4) Follow the steps on that page to send your references a system generated email requesting they submit a letter of recommendation on your behalf. You may also return to the My References link and click on \"Send/View Reference Request\" to see if your references have responded, add additional references, or resend requests. Candidates who currently hold tenure and are seeking appointment with tenure at Florida State University will need to submit the materials for evaluation if selected. These materials are required to support the tenure review process at the time of hire. Finalists may be asked to provide the below additional documentation as part of the evaluation. Examples of excellence in research or creative activity or excellence in teaching. CV One-page statement of their accomplishments over the last five years. Discussion of their teaching, research and service (no longer than six pages). Three outside letters of recommendation directed specifically to Florida State University. No professional relationships should exist between the candidate and the external reviewer. Relationships include, but are not limited to, student- teacher (including dissertation committee chairs and members), colleagues in graduate school, former departmental colleagues, collaborators, and co-authors. These letters should be sent to MiKayla Jackson, Administrative Specialist, directly from the external reviewer. mjj22e@fsu.edu Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled and will begin Fall 2027. Review of applications will begin on December 15 and continue until the position is filled. The faculty rank associated with the appointment will be determined based on the selected candidate\u2019s qualifications and experience. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63645&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Brand Graphic Designer", "description": "Job Title Brand Graphic Designer Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63645 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department University Marketing Responsibilities The Brand Graphic Designer creates self-service toolkits, templates, and brand asset libraries that help colleges, departments, and sub-brands produce compliant communications while allowing the central creative team to focus on strategic and executive priorities. Design, launch, and manage a comprehensive library of self-service templates (via Canva for Enterprise, Adobe Express, or similar platforms) for use by campus communicators. Work with campus partners to identify areas of need and future template expansions. Develop standardized, plug-and-play toolkits for recurring campus needs, including event flyers, digital signage, social media avatars, and presentation decks. Provide brand consultations and training sessions for internal marketing and communications personnel across campus, teaching them how to effectively utilize the design systems. Gather feedback and improve training offerings. Assist in evaluating brand identity requests from various campus groups, ensuring clarity between academic, institutional, and marketplace sub-brands. Serves as representative to the director of branding when needed. Provide art direction and design support for major, university-wide strategic initiatives, internal marketing and communications conferences, and high-visibility institutional campaigns. Collaborate closely with fellow University Marketing graphic designers to ensure brand cohesion at all levels of university activity. Commit to continuous learning by staying abreast of industry trends and emerging marketing technologies. Foster a culture of continuous learning within the team. Mentor team members on branding principles, ensuring ongoing skill development through on-the-job training and staying updated with industry publications and training. Qualifications Bachelor\u2019s degree and three years of experience or a combination of post high school education and experience equal to seven years. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63644&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Laboratory Assistant - Kopania (OPS)", "description": "Job Title Laboratory Assistant - Kopania (OPS) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63644 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Dr. Emily Kopania's laboratory in the Department of Biological Scienc e at Florida State University (https://ekopania.github.io/ and https://www.bio.fsu.edu/). Our lab seeks to understand how selective pressures interact with developmental and functional constraints. We primarily do this by studying two different biological systems: (1) The evolution of vision in fish and (2) The evolution of reproduction in rodents. Our work integrates cutting-edge genomics and transcriptomics techniques with phylogenetic comparative approaches to understand molecular and trait evolution. Responsibilities The primary duties of this role include, but are not limited to, the following: Helping to set up a molecular genomics laboratory and fish husbandry facility. Performing molecular laboratory experiments. Examples include DNA and RNA extraction and library preparation, immunohistochemistry, and microscopy. General lab upkeep and organization, such as ordering supplies, scheduling, and maintaining supplies and equipment. Managing a fish (trout) facility through tasks such as regular feedings, health checks, and water quality monitoring. Mentoring and training others in laboratory techniques. Qualifications B.S. or B.A. degree (or higher) in the life sciences or related field. Exceptions may be made for students with laboratory research experience who are finishing their degrees this year. At least one year of experience in a biology laboratory. Proficiency with Microsoft Suite (Excel, Word, Teams) and Google Docs. A strong interest in evolutionary biology and genomics. Excellent time management, communication, and problem-solving skills. Strong ability to work with a team of students and researchers Preferred Qualifications Previous experience with molecular biology laboratory techniques. Previous experience working with animals in research settings, especially fish. Anticipated Salary Range Competitive salary commensurate with experience. Fringe benefits included. Ideal start date would be in October 2026 but is flexible based on candidate availability. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Please send your CV, a one-page statement describing your past research experience and interest in the position, and contact information for at least two references to Dr. Emily Kopania . Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis, and the position will remain open until filled. Considerations This is an OPS/temporary job. Based on the duties, this position may require completion of a criminal history background check . A full-time (40 hours/week), in-person research assistant position. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63643&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Professional Development Trainer/Bootcamp Instructor, ASCENT (Panama City Campus) (Multiple Vacancies) (Part-time, OPS)", "description": "Job Title Professional Development Trainer/Bootcamp Instructor, ASCENT (Panama City Campus) (Multiple Vacancies) (Part-time, OPS) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63643 Location Panama City, FL Full/Part Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department ASCENT - Office of Professional Engagement and Learning (OPEL) Florida State University is one of the nation\u2019s top 25 public universities and FSU Panama City amplifies the university\u2019s efforts to preserve, expand and disseminate knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and human services professions. FSU Panama City is located 100 miles west of Tallahassee on the beautiful North St. Andrews Bay and is only three miles from the sparkling waters of the Gulf. FSU PC currently houses 20 bachelor's programs, 9 master's programs, 1 doctoral program, and boasts a small faculty-to-student ratio, which gives students a more personalized academic experience. Please visit https://pc.fsu.edu/promise for information about our FSU PC Promise to students and https://pc.fsu.edu/ for more information about our campus. FSU Panama City also recently opened a brand new, residential housing complex on campus and right on the water. This new apartment-style complex at FSU PC houses both undergraduate and graduate students. For more information about our on-campus housing, visit https://seminolelandingfsu.com/ Responsibilities Providing classroom, online, or hybrid instruction in professional development and bootcamp formats. Fulfilling all contractual obligations during the term. Delivering training sessions aligned with pre-approved curricula and industry standards. Preparing thoroughly for each session and adhering to schedules. Leveraging modern teaching technologies, including learning management systems (LMS) and web-conferencing tools. Engaging learners actively, providing timely responses to questions and offering support or referrals when necessary. Collaborating with ASCENT staff to ensure seamless delivery and high-quality learner experiences. Assisting in the development and refinement of training content, as needed. Maintaining accurate records of attendance, grades, and evaluations, as applicable. Completing annual compliance training and adhering to university policies. Performing additional duties as assigned by the OPEL Program Manager. Qualifications High school diploma or equivalent. Relevant industry certifications, coupled with two or more years of field experience. Preferred Qualifications Proven expertise in the subject areas being taught (e.g., technology, business, healthcare, etc.). Certifications in relevant tools or technologies (e.g., cybersecurity, IT, programming languages, project management, etc.). Post-secondary teaching or training experience preferred. Evidence of ongoing professional development through education, certifications, or other activities. Proficiency with teaching technologies, including LMS platforms, lecture-capture tools, and synchronous online engagement software. Strong communication and interpersonal skills with demonstrated ability to engage others. Contact Info Heidi Gentry University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an OPS/temporary job. Based on the duties, this position may require completion of a criminal history background check . The position is anticipated to begin in Fall 2026. This position requires a flexible schedule for trainings and occasional classes that start outside normal business hours. This position may be on location at any of the eight counties of the panhandle region. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63612&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Registered Nurse - FSUS", "description": "Job Title Registered Nurse - FSUS Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63612 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Florida State University School (FSUS) Responsibilities Develop and deliver engaging lessons aligned with State curriculum standards. Teach nursing assistant and allied health competencies through classroom, laboratory, and clinical instruction. Supervise students during clinical rotations and hands-on learning experiences. Evaluate student performance using assessments, skills checklists, projects, and industry standards. Prepare students for industry certifications such as CNA or related healthcare credentials. Maintain accurate attendance, grades, clinical records, and student competency documentation. Promote professionalism, communication, teamwork, and ethical behavior in the healthcare settings. Ensure compliance with OSHA, HIPAA, infection control, and school safety regulations. Coordinate with healthcare partners for clinical placements and career experiences. Participate in faculty meetings, professional development, advisory committees, and school activities. Maintain current nursing licensure as required. Qualifications Associates degree in nursing or related healthcare field and two years of clinical nursing experience. Current unrestricted Registered Nurse (RN) or equivalent license. Preferred Qualifications Experience working with adolescents or teaching/training adults. Knowledge of healthcare industry standards and clinical procedures. Stong training, communication, and organizational skills. Ability to integrate technology into instruction. Experience with simulation labs and clinical instruction. Ability to build partnerships with healthcare facilities and community organizations. Commitment to student success, career readiniess, and workforce development. Other Information We proudly serve as a laboratory K-12 school, blending the rigors of academic achievement with a commitment to educational research and innovation. We draw upon the resources of a world-class university, bringing cutting-edge practices and insights directly into our classrooms. This dynamic approach ensures that our students benefit from the latest advancements in pedagogy and fosters an environment where curiosity and exploration are celebrated. Florida State University Schools is not just a place of learning; it's a community dedicated to empowering the leaders of tomorrow. We invite you to explore the possibilities at FSUS and join us on a journey of academic excellence, personal growth, and a commitment to making a positive impact on the world. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select \u201cyes\u201d to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for Veterans\u2019 Preference eligibility requirements and Veterans\u2019 Preference required documentation (PDF) , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check , including a fingerprint-based screening via AHCA\u2019s Clearinghouse pursuant to Section 1012, Florida Statutes, for positions in a FSU Developmental Research School or Section 409.175, Florida Statutes, for positions in a Childcare or Summer Camp position. Visit the AHCA Clearinghouse Screenings webpage for more information. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63593&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Assistant State Climatologist, 12 Month Salaried (Florida Climate Center)", "description": "Job Title Assistant State Climatologist, 12 Month Salaried (Florida Climate Center) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63593 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Part-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Florida Climate Center | Center for Ocean-Atmospheric Predication Studies (COAPS) | College of Arts & Sciences Responsibilities The selected candidate will be involved in the day-to-day operations of the Florida Climate Center, especially as it pertains to outreach and communication. This position will serve as a key member of the Center for Ocean-Atmospheric Prediction Studies (COAPS) outreach team and help identify, plan, and participate in a variety of events and opportunities. Limited travel to outreach events and workshops may be required. Responsibilities include: Providing climate data and services to citizens, private businesses, and government agencies in the State of Florida. Duties involve responding to inquiries about climate and weather via phone and email. Independently utilizing all resources available to answer questions and formulate data, products, and reports to meet the needs of the customer. Developing and disseminating regular climate products and reports, and maintaining a suite of web-based climate data products in response to needs and gaps. Serving as a liaison between the Florida Climate Center and our partners in climate services at the National Centers for Environmental information, Southeast Regional Climate Center, other state climate offices, and the National Weather Service. Performing research-related tasks as opportunities arise or as driven by public demand and in support of other projects/grants in place at COAPS. This could include independent research projects assigned by the Director of the Florida Climate Center, as well as providing data and technical support for research projects from undergraduate students, graduate students, summer interns, and faculty. Leading outreach/educational presentations and experiments related to climate and weather information in classroom as well as informal settings. Creating, editing, and distributing routine climate reports and newsletters. Managing and providing content to social media accounts for the Florida Climate Center. Qualifications A master's degree from an accredited institution in the field of Meteorology or a related science is required. A bachelor\u2019s degree in Meteorology or related field with a minimum of two years of experience in the field of Meteorology/Climatology/Climate Services or in Science Education/Outreach/Communication may also be considered. This position will be hired at the rank of Assistant in Research. The selected candidate must also possess: A friendly and helpful professional demeanor and be able to work well independently as well as with a variety of groups including other scientists, the general public, and stakeholder groups, such as educators, practitioners, school-aged children, etc. Ability to prepare publication-quality graphics and maps, have basic web and programming skills, strong organizational skills, good oral and written communication, and the ability to write on technical subjects and make them understandable for non-scientists. Experience with data analysis, including basic knowledge of and/or the ability to learn computer programming and statistical analysis software, such as Python, R, HTML, SASS, GIS, or Matlab, as well as some research experience, is preferred. Contact Info For more details, please contact Dr. Emily Powell . University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This is a state funded part-time position (0.50 FTE, 20 hours per week). Subject to the availability of future grant funding, the position may increase up to full-time (1.0 FTE). Applications review will begin November 13, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63641&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Director (Rural Health Transformation Program - College of Medicine)", "description": "Job Title Director (Rural Health Transformation Program - College of Medicine) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63641 Location Hybrid Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Rural Health Transformation Program - College of Medicine Florida State University\u2019s College of Medicine has been awarded more than $19 million through the Rural Health Transformation Program to strengthen healthcare access and outcomes in rural Florida. The funding will support six new projects focused on critical needs including behavioral health, preventive care, food insecurity, telehealth, at-home care and healthcare workforce development. Through partnerships with communities and healthcare organizations across Northwest and Southwest Florida, FSU is working to bring innovative, practical solutions directly to rural communities and help close longstanding gaps in care. Responsibilities Provides strategic leadership, direction, and administrative oversight for the Rural Health Transformation (RHT) portfolio of six programs. For the overall RHT program at FSU, oversees the planning, development, implementation, review, and evaluation of program goals, objectives, policies, and procedures to support successful achievement of funding priorities, organizational objectives, and community health outcomes. Directs activities supporting the growth, sustainability, and long-term advancement of Rural Health Transformation initiatives. Identifies opportunities to expand programmatic impact through new partnerships, innovative initiatives, funding opportunities, and collaborative endeavors that support the University's rural health mission. Directs the establishment of operational frameworks, policies, procedures, and performance standards that promote alignment and consistency across Rural Health Transformation initiatives. Ensures program activities are conducted in accordance with University, state, federal, and funding agency requirements. Provides strategic leadership for relationships with key external partners including healthcare organizations, governmental agencies, academic institutions, community stakeholders, and other partners that support Rural Health Transformation objectives. Serves as a representative of the University in collaborative initiatives that advance rural health priorities throughout the state. Works with program evaluator, optimize program performance data impact through communication and dissemination activities publicly. Utilizes performance data and stakeholder input with Rural Health Transformation portfolio to measure program effectiveness, identify opportunities for improvement, and demonstrate organizational impact. Utilizes data and outcomes to guide decision-making, strategic planning, and future program development. Leads development of overall RHT program website, social media and other key dissemination and communication outlets. Serves as a resource to University leadership, program personnel, and stakeholders regarding Rural Health Transformation initiatives and priorities. Participates in and may lead committees, advisory groups, and collaborative efforts that advance program objectives and support the University's health and human services mission. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and six years of experience related to administrative services; or a high school diploma/equivalent and experience equal to ten years. (Note: post-high school education can substitute for experience at the equivalent rate.) Valid Florida or Georgia Driver's license or the ability to obtain prior to hire. This position requires successful completion of the eSPEAR Certification or ability to obtain the certification within 6 months of hire. Contact Info Georgia Arnold University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position requires regular travel in support of program activities and responsibilities. Travel may occur within the employee\u2019s assigned region and throughout the State of Florida, as needed. The frequency and location of travel may vary based on programmatic and operational needs. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63634&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Animal Care Assistant (Part-time, OPS)", "description": "Job Title Animal Care Assistant (Part-time, OPS) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63634 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Laboratory Animal Resources (LAR ) is looking to fill the role of Animal Care Assistant (Part-time, OPS) Responsibilities This position performs routine duties associated with cage sanitation and preparation for reuse in a research setting, including cage maintenance, preventive maintenance of equipment, monitoring equipment for proper function, and maintaining sanitary conditions. Operates mechanical washers and ensures that cage washing and related equipment are in proper working order. Operates autoclaves to sterilize or decontaminate caging and equipment. Assists in receiving and storing materials, food, and supplies. Transports animals, caging, and supplies between animal rooms and facilities. Maintains the sanitary condition of cage wash facilities and other ancillary areas, including corridors and storage rooms. Takes necessary precautions to adhere to OSHA standards, other applicable federal and state regulations, and LAR standard operating procedures when working with hazardous agents, animals, and power equipment. They will provide diligent and responsible animal care. Feeds and waters animals. Changes and clean cages. Sanitizes equipment and facilities. Records and reports animal abnormalities, including altered eating, drinking, waste elimination, behavior, superficial lesions, and/or death. Assists with technical procedures, including record keeping, animal identification, breeding, sexing, specimen collection, preparing diets, and euthanasia. Records and reports any environmental abnormalities. Provides routine physical maintenance of assigned areas. Performs other duties as assigned. Qualifications High School diploma and one year of work experience. A valid State of Florida or Georgia Driver\u2019s License or the ability to obtain one prior to hire. Ability to perform physical tasks, such as standing, gripping, reaching, bending, and the ability to regularly lift up to 50 pounds. Preferred Qualifications Experience working with animals or in research. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an OPS/temporary job. Based on the duties, this position may require completion of a criminal history background check . The desired schedule is 20 hours per week, Monday - Friday, between 07:30 am and 5:30 pm, as determined by the candidate and supervisor. Scheduled shifts would be a minimum of 4 hours. This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63628&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Assistant or Associate Professor, 9 Month Salaried - Reading Education or Special Education", "description": "Job Title Assistant or Associate Professor, 9 Month Salaried - Reading Education or Special Education Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63628 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department School of Teacher Education in the Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences and the Florida Center for Reading Research Responsibilities Candidates will be expected to maintain a rigorous grant writing and research program, teach undergraduate and graduate level courses in their program, train doctoral students, and participate in university governance commensurate with rank. Qualifications Ph.D. in Reading Education, Special Education, or related field Demonstrated evidence of rigorous research productivity Demonstrated commitment to undergraduate and graduate teaching and training Demonstrated commitment to continued grant-funded research and scholarly productivity Preferred Qualifications Demonstrated commitment to and evidence of developing doctoral students Demonstrated evidence of (or potential for) an externally funded, independent research program A quality program of research related to reading and/or writing development, assessment, instruction, intervention, or related topic areas (emerging at the assistant rank, established at the associate rank) Teaching experience in preschool through grade 12 settings Other Information The School of Teacher Education (STE) in the Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences (Anne\u2019s College) and the Florida Center for Reading Research (FCRR) at the Florida State University invite applications for a nine-month, tenured or tenure-earning assistant or associate professor of Reading Education or Special Education. The position will involve teaching, research, and service within STE, and will include a joint appointment with FCRR. The position carries a reduced teaching assignment with correspondingly high expectations for research productivity. The successful candidate will have a tenure home in one of two majors within STE: Reading Education or Special Education. These majors work closely together in STE and FCRR, so a collaborative orientation is desired. The candidate will be expected to maintain a rigorous grant writing and research program, including competitive externally funded research grants. The candidate will also teach undergraduate, masters, and/or doctoral level classes within their program, and train doctoral students through active participation in their research program. The candidate will also be expected to participate in university governance in the department, college, and FCRR, at a level that is commensurate with their rank. The candidate will join an interdisciplinary group of colleagues and students at STE, Anne\u2019s College, and FCRR. Drawing from multiple disciplines, FCRR investigates all aspects of reading and reading-related skills across the lifespan. Through rigorous and robust research, innovation, and engagement, FCRR advances the science of reading to improve learning and achievement from birth through adulthood. Meanwhile, Anne\u2019s College advances society and enriches our community through support and education, while enhancing the quality of life of all our students, faculty and staff. Through meaningful collaborations, commitment to public scholarship, and integration of research, practice and policy, Anne\u2019s College addresses America\u2019s urgent education challenges in the innovative manner characteristic of FSU. The roots of FSU\u2019s Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences date back to the university\u2019s establishment, and it is the oldest college of its kind in Florida. The College is home to six academic departments united through a common goal to maximize human potential. In total, the College includes the Department of Educational Leadership & Policy Studies, Department of Educational Psychology & Learning Systems, Department of Human Development & Family Sciences, Department of Health, Nutrition & Food Sciences, Department of Sport Management, School of Teacher Education, numerous research centers, and three laboratory schools (Florida State University School, FSU Pembroke Pines Charter School, and The Collegiate School at FSU Panama City). Anne\u2019s College serves over 4,000 students via approximately 200 full-time faculty and nearly 80 full-time staff. Contact Info Sonia Cabell , Ph.D., Sigmon Endowed Professor and Search Committee Chair University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applicants should also include a CV, a cover letter detailing how they meet the required and preferred qualifications, a sample publication, names of three references with contact information, and a statement of research interests. Transcripts, work samples (such as teaching artifacts or manuscripts), and three letters of recommendation will be required of candidates selected for an interview. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. Review of candidates will begin 10/26/2026 and will continue until filled. We urge interested candidates to submit materials as soon as possible. The anticipated start date is August 2027. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63604&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Director, FSU Real Estate Center - Herbert Wertheim College of Business", "description": "Job Title Director, FSU Real Estate Center - Herbert Wertheim College of Business Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63604 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Risk Management/Insurance, Real Estate and Legal Studies - Herbert Wertheim College of Business Responsibilities Strategic Leadership and Advisory Board Management The Director leads the development and implementation of the objectives and strategic goals of the FSU Real Estate Center. Acts as the highly visible, senior external-facing leader and chief liaison to real estate industry personnel, employers, and alumni. Leverages an established industry network to expand opportunities for the Center. Manages the Center\u2019s Executive Advisory Board, including directing Board communications and meetings, identifying and cultivating prominent industry leaders for new membership, assisting Board subcommittees, and reporting to the Board at its biannual meetings. Industry Engagement and Professional Events Provides the framework, strategic vision, and guidance for the Center\u2019s professional events and activities, ensuring they serve as premier networking and talent pipeline opportunities. Oversees the annual TRENDS conference, the FSU-Kislak Market Strategy Forums, the Evan Jennings Speaker Series, the Real Deal & Entrepreneurs Series, and any future forums designed to advance the preeminence of the real estate program. Collaborates with faculty and external stakeholders to ensure programming reflects current industry trends, technologies, and market opportunities. Student Success and Career Pathways Responsible for connecting students in the real estate program with internships, mentorships, industry projects, and full-time career pathways through strategic employer partnerships. Coordinates the Center\u2019s support of student activities, including the FSU Real Estate Society. Directs the Center\u2019s program manager and other staff in the awarding of fellowships, travel grants, and administrative assistance for student participation in corporate tours, case competitions, networking opportunities, mentoring, and other experiential learning activities. Center Administration and Operation s Supervises Center staff and oversees the Center\u2019s day-to-day administrative and financial operations. Coordinates Center communications with alumni, Executive Board members, sponsors, employers, students, and faculty. Ensures compliance with applicable University and State of Florida policies and requirements. Program Advocacy and Brand Management Serves as the primary external face of the Real Estate Center to industry leaders and professional organizations to articulate the successes and objectives of the Program, its faculty, and its students. Works with the College\u2019s PR & marketing team to develop branding and messaging that elevates the Center\u2019s national reputation. Assures that the FSUREC brand, mission, products, and services are consistently presented in a strong, positive image to relevant stakeholders. Donor Stewardship and Development Collaboration Acts as a subject-matter expert and strategic partner to the College\u2019s development, engagement, business development, and career services teams to support fundraising, sponsorship, employer, executive education, and alumni/donor engagement efforts. Identifies and develops corporate sponsorship opportunities for Center programs and activities. Accompanies gift officers on strategic visits to provide programmatic vision, assisting in the cultivation and stewardship of employer and donor partners to enhance student, faculty, and Center resources. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and six years of experience related to administrative services; or a high school diploma/equivalent and ten years of experience related to administrative services? (Note: post-high school education may substitute for experience at the equivalent rate.) Preferred Qualifications A demonstrated record of strategic leadership and partnership development, supported by a robust, existing network of commercial real estate professionals, employers, and industry leaders. Experience managing complex, multi-stakeholder initiatives, professional events, and program budgets. An advanced degree in business, real estate, finance, planning, or a related field is highly desired. Six or more years of professional experience in commercial real estate development, commercial brokerage, investment, or related financial services. Experience working with students, faculty, and staff in a higher education setting. Professional credentials in real estate, planning, or finance are strongly advantageous. Contact Info J. Bradley Karl , PhD Chair, Department of Risk Management/Insurance, Real Estate and Legal Studies Dr. William T. Hold/The Alliance's Program in Risk Management and Insurance University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=62364&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Law Enforcement Officer (Panama City Campus)", "description": "Job Title Law Enforcement Officer (Panama City Campus) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 62364 Location Panama City, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Panama City Campus Police & Public Safety Responsibilities The Law Enforcement Officer is responsible for the protection of life and property, prevention of crime, misconduct, traffic and crowd control, criminal and traffic law enforcement, criminal and traffic accident investigation, community service and providing information regarding laws, University policy, and distribution of information to the community. Patrols the FSU campus for the primary purposes of seeking out and apprehending violators of Florida statutes, identifying and reporting safety hazards and providing a visible presence throughout campus to deter crime. Responds to fire and burglar alarms, traffic accidents and other incidents that may be reported. Interacts with other law enforcement agencies to assist and cooperate in their efforts and to secure their assistance with preventing and responding to situations on campus. Protects the safety of drivers, bikers and pedestrians through traffic control and direction in the event of collisions, construction work or other mitigating circumstances. Provides non-emergency assistance to members of the University community, such as unlocking buildings and car doors as needed, helping with dormitory move-in and providing directions. Acts as a first responder when necessary, providing CPR and first aid. These responsibilities apply to the campuses of Florida State University Panama City and the Gulf Coast State College. Conducts Investigations in the resolution of open investigations by securing crime scenes, assisting with evidence collection, taking witness statements and conducting interviews with victims, witnesses and suspects. These responsibilities apply to the campuses of Florida State University Panama City and the Gulf Coast State College. Writes and submits reports with all pertinent details related to cases of lost, stolen or damaged property, incidents in which harm has been threatened or inflected on any person, and other miscellaneous incidents on campus with a bearing on safety and security. These responsibilities apply to the campuses of Florida State University Panama City and the Gulf Coast State College. Provides security services for scheduled events occurring both indoors and outdoors on campus, in partnership with other law enforcement agencies and security officers. Prevents crime and apprehends those in violation of the law through scheduled crime suppression details. These responsibilities apply to the campuses of Florida State University Panama City and the Gulf Coast State College. Supports Crime Prevention activities by participating in formal crime prevention programs, such as the RAD (Rape Aggression Defense) program, Click-It-Or-Ticket, and Bicycle Safety programs. Prevents crime through informal contact with students, faculty and staff to raise awareness of safety issues on campus and to encourage safe behavior and wise decision-making. These responsibilities apply to the campuses of Florida State University Panama City and the Gulf Coast State College. Other duties as assigned to support the mission of the Department and the University. Qualifications High school diploma or equivalent. Must be at least 19 years of age. Must be a citizen of the United States. Must meet the requirements of Section 943.13, Florida Statutes, and the ability to pass the state certification exam for Law Enforcement Officers within six months of being hired. A valid State of Florida or Georgia driver's license or the ability to obtain prior to hire. Preferred Qualifications Applicants may qualify for employment with the FSU Police Department through the Equivalency of Training (EOT) process if they meet one of the following: Out-of-State or Federal Officers: 1+ year full-time sworn experience Comparable training to Florida\u2019s basic recruit academy No more than 8-year break in service Special Operations Forces Members: 5+ years of service No more than 4-year break in service Previously Certified Florida Officers: Fully certified in Florida 4\u20138-year break in service Contact Info Malia Brown - (850) 644-1239 - mbrown10@fsu.edu University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our interactive too l to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://jobs.fsu.edu. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select \u201cyes\u201d to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for eligibility information and required documentation , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . All applicants must successfully complete a Physical Standards Test (PST) as part of the selection process. Successful completion of the assessment is mandatory for employment consideration. Law enforcement officers assigned to the Patrol Division will work 12-hour shifts (6:30pm - 6:30am or 6:30am - 6:30pm), 80 hours bi-weekly. Additionally, the position may be required to assist during home football games, holidays, and during state, national or University emergencies. Special assignments as directed by law enforcement chain of command. This position requires completion of a supplemental employment questionnaire and a post-offer employment physical exam, drug screening, psychological evaluation, police background check, and Federal Bureau of Investigations (FBI)/Florida Department of Law Enforcement (FDLE) fingerprinting. This position qualifies for special risk benefits and classification under applicable retirement or insurance programs. Final approval for special risk benefits is subject to Florida Retirement System review and approval. This position is located in Panama City, FL. This position is being re-advertised. Previous applicants need not reapply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63635&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Senior Grants Specialist", "description": "Job Title Senior Grants Specialist Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63635 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department ICON-Health within the Office of Research seeks to fill the Senior Grants Specialist position. Responsibilities This position is responsible for the comprehensive pre- and post-award administration of sponsored projects, ensuring absolute accuracy and compliance with university (FSU), division, center, and agency policies and regulations. This includes developing, reviewing, and analyzing sponsored project documents for accuracy and compliance. Assist Principal Investigators (PIs) with long-term planning, budget development, analysis, forecasting, amendments, and grant closeout. Serve as the local subject matter expert on federal, institutional, and funding agency policies; interpret guidelines for grantees and advise faculty on allowable expenditures (materials, supplies, services). Prepare, review, and audit budget reports and amendments in a timely manner, monitoring all project activities to ensure fiscal compliance. Act as the primary liaison between faculty, Sponsored Research Administration (SRA), University central offices, the Office of Research, and the College of Medicine throughout the grant lifecycle from submission to closeout. This position reviews and analyzes fiscal transactions and reconciliation reports on a monthly basis, provides monthly budget summary to PIs. Makes corrections as needed. Audits and ensures completion of all post award transactional grant activities including appointments, purchases, travel corrections such as DOLs, eRDFs, etc. Advises PIs on fund utilization in order to maximize budget allocations. This position approves travel and procurement actions to ensure alignment with PIs request, overall fund management strategy, and compliance with Federal, State, University and Agency regulations, laws, policies and guidelines. Trains new staff and recommends policies, procedures, and guidelines related to grants activities. This position organizes and communicates personnel appointments and verifies effort certification is accurately reflected for PIs and personnel employed on assigned projects. Coordinates mass appointment data each semester for sponsored project funded graduate students and faculty. Approves personnel appointments to ensure alignment with fund management. Identifies funding opportunities, conducts research, and interprets advanced technical information for grantees. Additional duties as assigned as it relates to the grant management, business operations and overall success of ICON-Health. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and three years experience or a combination of post high school education and experience equal to seven years. This position requires successful completion of the eSPEAR Certification series within the first six months from start date. Preferred Qualifications Experience in pre \u2013 and post-award Research Administration Contact Info Averi Allbritton at adeering@fsu.edu University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63502&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Jazz Trumpet, 9 Month Salaried - College of Music", "description": "Job Title Assistant Professor of Jazz Trumpet, 9 Month Salaried - College of Music Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63502 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department College of Music Responsibilities Teach undergraduate and graduate-level jazz trumpet students, and supervise graduate teaching assistants. Recruit and maintain a successful teaching studio Serve on doctoral and master\u2019s committees and juries. Maintain a professional career as a performing artist. Participate in university and professional service activities nationally and internationally as appropriate. Additional responsibilities may include teaching courses in the candidate\u2019s area of expertise. Qualifications A doctoral degree in a related field or a master\u2019s degree with equivalent professional experience is required at the time of appointment. The successful candidate will: Hold a record of successful university-level teaching experience and proven artistry as a professional performer. Demonstrate strong commitment to the recruitment of outstanding students. Other Information The College of Music at Florida State University: is the largest such college in the Southeast and the third largest university-based music program in the nation. With over 90 faculty and 40 support staff, the College offers a range of degrees in music, baccalaureate through the doctorate. We are home to approximately 700 undergraduate and 400 graduate students, who represent nearly every state in the nation and 20 foreign countries. Contact Info For technical assistance applying to this position, please contact Eden Wahlquist For questions regarding the position, please contact Rodney Jordan , Professor of Jazz Bass and Coordinator of Jazz and Music Industry University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Application Materials: Cover Letter, CV, List of Links, etc. Confidential letters of recommendation from at least three references will also need to be submitted on your behalf. Letters may be solicited through our system or directed to CM-HiringDocs@fsu.edu Follow the steps below to request these letters through our system: 1) After submitting your application, click the Careers link; 2) Click the My References link; 3) Click the Send/View Reference Request button next to the appropriate position; and 4) Follow the steps on that page to send your references a system generated email requesting they submit a letter of recommendation on your behalf. You may also return to the My References link and click on \"Send/View Reference Request\" to see if your references have responded, add additional references, or resend requests. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. However, for priority consideration, please complete all application materials by November 1st, 2026. Review of applications will begin immediately and will remain ongoing until the position is filled. Appointment will begin August 9th, 2027. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63500&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Music Therapy, 9 Month Salaried - College of Music", "description": "Job Title Assistant Professor of Music Therapy, 9 Month Salaried - College of Music Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63500 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department College of Music Responsibilities Teaches undergraduate and graduate-level courses in Music Therapy or related areas. Courses will be selected from current area offerings and/or implemented in the candidate's area of expertise. Supervises clinical music therapy experiences. Directs doctoral and master's-level committees. Conducts research and scholarly activities related to their interests and areas of expertise. Engage in recruitment of outstanding students. Develop and maintain community partnerships. Participates in university and professional service activities appropriate to rank. Qualifications Academic doctorate or highest-level terminal degree from an accredited institution in Music Therapy or related area. Credentialing through the Certification Board for Music Therapists (MT-BC) is required. Minimum of five years of full time (or equivalent) clinical experience as an MT-BC is also required. A record of successful university-level teaching experience. Demonstrated excellence in clinical musicianship as a practicing professional. Experience as a clinical supervisor. Preferred Qualifications Preference will be given to candidates with substantial clinical and supervision experience, and who hold the NICU-MT and/or other specializations. A record of ongoing research/scholarly activity is also preferred. Other Information The College of Music at Florida State University is the largest such college in the Southeast and the third largest university-based music program in the nation. With over 90 faculty and 40 support staff, the College offers a range of degrees in music, baccalaureate through the doctorate. We are home to approximately 700 undergraduate and 400 graduate students, who represent nearly every state in the nation and 20 foreign countries. Contact Info For technical assistance applying to this position, please contact Eden Wahlquist Other inquiries may be directed to the search committee chair as follows: Dr. Lori Gooding , Associate Professor of Music Therapy and Co-Coordinator of Music Education & Music Therapy University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Each item below should be uploaded as a PDF to the Additional Documents section of the online application: One to two-page cover letter Curriculum vitae A copy of scholarly writing that clearly reflects your research focus and direction such as a refereed published article, an in-press article, or a doctoral-level scholarly paper Link to a 20-minute video of the applicant teaching Confidential letters of recommendation from at least three references will also need to be submitted on your behalf. Letters may be solicited through our system or directed to CM-HiringDocs@fsu.edu Follow the steps below to request these letters through our system: 1) After submitting your application, click the Careers link 2) Click the My References link 3) Click the Send/View Reference Request button next to the appropriate position 4) Follow the steps on that page to send your references a system generated email requesting they submit a letter of recommendation on your behalf. You may also return to the My References link and click on \"Send/View Reference Request\" to see if your references have responded, add additional references, or resend requests. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. However, for priority consideration, please complete all application materials by October 20th, 2026. Review of applications will begin immediately and will remain ongoing until the position is filled. Appointment will begin August 9th, 2027. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63621&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Executive Assistant to the Dean (Senior Administrative Specialist) - Herbert Wertheim College of Business", "description": "Job Title Executive Assistant to the Dean (Senior Administrative Specialist) - Herbert Wertheim College of Business Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63621 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Herbert Wertheim College of Business Responsibilities Reports to the Dean of the Herbert Wertheim College of Business and provides high-level, confidential administrative and operational support to the Office of the Dean. Serves as the primary coordinator for Dean\u2019s Suite operations, stakeholder service, executive meetings, travel and expense processes, correspondence, records, events, and special projects. Ensures a professional, responsive, and well-organized executive office through sound judgment, discretion, accurate documentation, and timely follow-through on established priorities. Dean\u2019s Suite Operations Manages daily Dean\u2019s Suite operations, maintaining a professional, welcoming, responsive, and organized environment for university leaders, faculty, staff, students, alumni, donors, partners, and visitors. Serves as primary contact; screens, routes, and resolves inquiries and administrative matters; and promptly elevates sensitive, urgent, or complex issues. Recruits, trains, schedules, and supervises OPS student employees, setting clear expectations for professionalism, service, confidentiality, responsiveness, and issue escalation. Oversees office procedures, coverage, digital workspaces, records, supplies, mail, conference rooms, and a visitor-ready environment. Coordinates authorized use, training, scheduling, documentation, service, and maintenance of college vehicles in compliance with university policy. Maintains templates, checklists, procedures, and documentation for recurring work and improves processes to strengthen service, accuracy, efficiency, continuity, and stewardship. Travel, Expense, and Procurement Coordination Coordinates travel, expense, and procurement for the Dean and Associate and Assistant Deans, including itineraries, reservations, schedules, and logistics for approved business needs. Prepares and monitors travel authorizations, reimbursements, receipts, and supporting records; resolves routine issues; and coordinates with the UBA team to ensure timely reconciliation and compliance. Uses an assigned university purchasing card for approved Dean\u2019s Suite purchases and maintains documentation, approvals, reconciliations, and records consistent with university policies and financial controls. Maintains templates, checklists, recurring-request tools, and approved workflows that improve process accuracy, timeliness, consistency, and efficiency. Meeting Administration and Action Tracking Coordinates executive, governance, faculty, staff, board, committee, and Dean-assigned meetings and initiatives, including the Executive Committee, faculty meetings, staff town halls, Board of Governors, and Student Investment Fund Board. Supports annual faculty and staff award processes. Coordinates schedules, agendas, materials, participant communications, logistics, and complex calendar alignment involving the Dean and senior college or university leaders. Attends designated meetings and uses approved tools to capture discussions and prepare accurate minutes, action summaries, and related documents for review and distribution. Maintains action logs and follow-up systems documenting commitments, owners, deadlines, and status; issues reminders and escalates unresolved matters. Organizes source materials, committee and membership records, award documentation, and digital files for accuracy, traceability, access, and updating. Digital Correspondence and Document Production Produces, proofreads, formats, and quality-checks executive correspondence, announcements, speeches, reports, spreadsheets, presentations, briefings, and other materials requiring accuracy, professionalism, and audience awareness. Maintains secure digital workflows and records using approved collaboration, forms, survey, document-management, and AI-enabled tools, with appropriate review, confidentiality, accessibility, version control, records retention, and responsible use. Reviews final materials for accuracy, clarity, consistent formatting, accessibility, audience suitability, version control, and alignment with approved sources and college or university standards. Special Projects and Events Coordinates special and annual projects, processes, and events assigned by the Dean, providing confidential, organized, and timely administrative support. Manages annual performance reviews for Associate and Assistant Deans, department chairs, and directors, including schedules, materials, and required submissions. Oversees the Dean\u2019s List communication process. Coordinates AACSB accreditation-visit documentation, travel, meeting schedules, room reservations, and leadership support. Plans Dean\u2019s Suite events, including welcome activities and holiday gatherings, and supports major college events such as board meetings, town halls, receptions, and other high-profile engagements. Coordinates administrative, operational, and analytical projects, including the college directory, textbook compliance, commencement logistics, and recurring initiatives. Maintains accurate records, clear communications, organized timelines, and timely completion of assigned work. Qualifications Bachelor\u2019s degree and four years of relevant professional experience in executive support, administration, operations, hospitality, or a related field; or a high school diploma or equivalent and eight years of experience in relevant professional experience in executive support, administration, operations, hospitality, or a related field. (Note: post-high school education may substitute for experience at the equivalent rate.) Preferred Qualifications Experience providing confidential administrative support to a dean, senior executive, board, executive committee, or comparable leadership office, preferably in higher education, government, public service, or another complex organization. Strong organizational judgment, discretion, prioritization, routing, escalation, and follow-through. Exceptional interpersonal, written, and verbal communication skills and the professional presence to work effectively with internal and external stakeholders. Experience coordinating complex calendars, meetings, travel, expenses, purchasing, records, and recurring administrative processes. Experience preparing executive-level correspondence, briefings, reports, presentations, meeting records, and decision summaries. Advanced proficiency with Microsoft Office or comparable productivity and collaboration platforms. Experience with enterprise travel, procurement, finance, human resources, and customer relationship management systems, such as Concur, Workday, PeopleSoft, and Salesforce. Experience supervising, training, or scheduling student, temporary, or administrative staff. Familiarity with approved AI-enabled tools, workflow automation, digital forms, task-tracking, document-management, dashboards, and data-visualization tools. Ability to safeguard sensitive information and comply with applicable records, accessibility, information-security, and financial-control requirements. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63587&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Export Control Officer", "description": "Job Title Export Control Officer Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63587 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Research, Integrity, Security & Ethics within the Division of Research seeks to fill the role of Export Control Officer. Responsibilities This role will develop, implement, and maintain the university's export control compliance program. Interpret and apply federal regulations including ITAR, EAR, OFAC, and related research security requirements. Develop policies, procedures, guidance documents, and internal controls to ensure institutional compliance and minimize regulatory risk. Monitor regulatory and agency changes and recommend program modifications as necessary. Review research proposals, contracts, grants, agreements, disclosures, international collaborations, shipments, and activities for export control implications. Evaluate foreign national participation, controlled technologies, technical data, and restricted research requirements. Provide recommendations and compliance determinations to faculty, staff, and leadership. Will develop, implement, and monitor Technology Control Plans (TCPs) and related security measures for export-controlled research and controlled unclassified information. Conduct risk assessments, compliance reviews, and monitoring activities to ensure adherence to institutional and regulatory requirements. Oversee restricted party screening and international compliance review processes. Evaluate international visitors, collaborators, vendors, sponsors, and research partners for sanctions or export control concerns. Document determinations and maintain required records. Develop and deliver training, educational programs, and compliance resources related to export controls, research security, international collaborations, foreign influence, and related regulatory requirements. Promote awareness and compliance across the research community. Prepare license applications and regulatory submissions when required. Serve as the university liaison with federal regulatory agencies. Investigate potential compliance concerns, recommend corrective actions, maintain required records, and prepare reports for institutional leadership. Qualifications Bachelor's degree with six years of professional experience. Four years of experience will need to be in research compliance, export controls, regulatory compliance, research administration, or a related field. Preferred Qualifications Our Ideal candidate would have experience within a higher education setting, developing and implementing compliance programs and plans, and hold current certifications of ITAR, EAR, and OFAC. Contact Info Cassidy Cooksey at rsch-workforce@fsu.edu University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=62416&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Program Director & Open Rank Professor, 12 Months Salaried (Ascension Bay Internal Medicine) College of Medicine", "description": "Job Title Program Director & Open Rank Professor, 12 Months Salaried (Ascension Bay Internal Medicine) College of Medicine Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 62416 Location Panama City, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department College of Medicine, COM Residency Program Administration Responsibilities The Program Director oversees the Internal Medicine Residency Program (\u201cIM Program\u201d or \u201cProgram\u201d) under the guidance of the Designated Institutional Official (DIO). The Program Director handles the general management, curriculum development, hiring, and teaching and mentoring of the Program. The Program Director sets the strategic vision of the Program and ensures its standards, quality, and reputation. The Program Director is expected to support the collaboration of the IM Program with physician practices and hospital clinical services in a way that improves value and quality, and that fosters a positive environment for professional practice and medical education. The Program Director will also work in collaboration with the program leadership to ensure outstanding educational offerings within Ascension Sacred Heart Bay Hospital. Clinical Teaching and Supervision of Residents Core Program Clinical Teaching Clinical Practice in Internal Medicine or applicable Subspecialty General Administration Graduate Medical Education (GME) Committees/Meetings GME Lecturing/Teaching Conferences GME Recruiting/Interviewing GME Research/Scholarly Activity Resident Evaluation/Monitoring Program Evaluation Qualifications Doctoral degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Valid FL medical license, or licensed in another state with the ability to obtain FL licensure. Must be board certified in Internal Medicine by the American Board of Internal Medicine (ABIM). Must have a minimum of three years of faculty and administrative experience in an ACGME accredited internal medicine residency program. Preferred Qualifications Effective professional management skills, including the ability to plan, organize and schedule work in an efficient and productive manner, focusing on key priorities and meeting deadlines. Outstanding interpersonal, leadership, mentoring and teaching skills. A strong work ethic and desire to participate in a team-oriented, performance-driven health system. Ability to communicate with others in a clear, understandable, and professional manner in person, on the phone, electronically, and in writing. Ability to build and lead high-performing teams; must be able to provide clear and accurate direction and guidance. Strong administrative and team building skills. Other Information Ascension Sacred Heart Bay \u2013 Panama City, FL As part of Ascension, the largest non-profit health system in the U.S. and the world\u2019s largest Catholic health system: Sacred Heart was founded by the Daughters of Charity in 1915. While our technology has improved dramatically, and the buildings have grown and expanded, our commitment to the mission remains steadfast: to provide excellent health care to all people, with special attention to the poor and vulnerable. Sacred Heart Health System includes hospital campuses in Pensacola, Miramar Beach, Panama City, and Port St. Joe, Florida, as well as The Studer Family Children\u2019s Hospital at Sacred Heart, Northwest Florida\u2019s only children\u2019s hospital and Sacred Heart Medical Group, the largest network of primary care and specialty physicians in Northwest Florida. The 47-million-dollar renovation of Bay Medical after Hurricane Michael is in process and aims to create a facility with 200 private rooms. The improvements include major upgrades to information technology and creation of new space for physician offices and other services, including the laboratory, imaging and pharmacy. Bay offers an accredited Stroke Center, a Level II Trauma Center, which provides 24-hour emergency care for life-threatening injuries and illnesses, and emergency services located at the main hospital as well as a freestanding emergency center on Panama City Beach. Helpful The successful candidate will have the opportunity to shape the program in their vision and recruit core faculty. Candidates with recent scholarly activity such as peer reviewed funding, publication of original research or review articles in peer-reviewed journals, chapters in textbooks, publication or presentation of case reports or clinical series at scientific society meetings, or participation in national committees or educational organizations are highly encouraged to apply. Contact Info Jessee Graham: jjgraham@fsu.edu University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our interactive too l to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://hr.fsu.edu/facultyjobs. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Faculty Information This faculty position is jointly affiliated with Florida State University (FSU) and Ascension Sacred Heart. Appointment is contingent upon the successful completion of all onboarding and employment requirements of both institutions. These requirements include, but are not limited to: a comprehensive credentialing process through Ascension Sacred Heart Medical Staff Office, background screening, professional reference checks, drug screening, and submission of a self-query report from the National Practitioner Data Bank (NPDB). Please note that Ascension Sacred Heart credentialing process may take up to 90 days from the date the offer is accepted. Final appointment and the ability to initiate clinical responsibilities are contingent upon the approval of medical staff membership and clinical privileges by Ascension Sacred Heart. Further details regarding onboarding and credentialing processes will be provided during the interview and offer stages. Additional list of Ascension Sacred Heart Program Director Requirements . Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This is a clinical/non-tenure earning role, and rank is commensurate with experience. This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63607&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried (Chemical Oceanography/Aquatic Chemistry)", "description": "Job Title Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried (Chemical Oceanography/Aquatic Chemistry) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63607 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Earth, Ocean and Atmospheric Science l College of Arts & Sciences Responsibilities The Department of Earth, Ocean and Atmospheric Science (EOAS) at Florida State University (FSU) invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Chemical Oceanography / Aquatic Chemistry. We seek candidates whose research centers on aquatic chemical processes and biogeochemical cycling. Research areas of interest include, but are not limited to, the inorganic carbon system, ocean gas exchange, isotope geochemistry, nutrient cycling, chemical tracers of ocean circulation, aquatic / marine pollution, and modeling of chemical and biogeochemical processes in aquatic / marine systems. The appointee is expected to contribute to undergraduate and graduate teaching in Oceanography and Environmental Science, as well as to supervise and mentor undergraduate and graduate students in research and creative activities. The faculty member would support core instruction in chemical oceanography while developing advanced courses in specialized areas such as biogeochemical cycles, aquatic geochemistry, isotope geochemistry, and aquatic / marine pollution. The successful candidate would develop a vigorous externally funded research program focused on aquatic / marine chemical processes and biogeochemical cycling. Qualifications Candidates must hold a Doctoral degree or the highest degree appropriate in Oceanography / Environmental Science or a related discipline. Other Information EOAS is housed in a recent building (2020) with state-of-the-art facilities and laboratories, has approximately 35 tenure-track faculty and 100 graduate students, and offers undergraduate and/or graduate degrees in Geology, Meteorology, Oceanography, and Environmental Sciences. In addition to collaborations with other faculty within EOAS, the appointee can expect collaborations with colleagues at the Center for Ocean-Atmosphere Prediction Studies and the National High Magnetic Field Laboratory. For additional information on EOAS and FSU\u2019s resources, please check our website . Contact Info For any inquiries, please, reach out to search committee chair Dr. Robert Spencer . University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Required application materials include: Cover letter Curriculum vitae Statements on research and teaching interests Contact information for three references to provide letters of recommendation Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Application review will begin November 2, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63326&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Monographic Cataloging Librarian, 12 Months Salaried", "description": "Job Title Monographic Cataloging Librarian, 12 Months Salaried Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63326 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department University Libraries Responsibilities Leads monographic cataloging operations, including the creation, editing, analysis, and quality control of metadata for monographic and foreign language resources. Develops, implements, and improves cataloging and metadata workflows and coordinates the identification and remediation of metadata quality issues. Applies established cataloging and authority control standards and works with local and statewide colleagues on cataloging practices and system-wide changes. Supervises two full-time cataloging staff and provides training, guidance, and documentation related to monographic and foreign language cataloging. Contributes to the work of FSU Libraries and the profession through collaborative projects, committees, research, professional organizations, conferences, and continuing education. Qualifications MLS/MLIS degree from a program accredited by the American Library Association (or international equivalent), or a master's degree in a specialized area directly relevant to the position. At least one year of cataloging experience using MARC 21 and experience applying established cataloging standards and guidelines such as RDA, NACO, LCC, and PCC. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to take initiative, learn new technologies and technical skills quickly, and adapt to changing priorities. Ability to plan and coordinate projects and workflows, provide clear guidance and documentation, and work both independently and collaboratively. Strong communication and interpersonal skills and the ability to work effectively with colleagues in a collaborative environment. Preferred Qualifications The following qualifications are welcomed but are not required. Candidates are encouraged to apply even if they do not have experience in every area listed below. Experience with or interest in cataloging resources in non-Roman alphabets, particularly Chinese, Japanese, and/or Korean, or a background in linguistics or language studies. Familiarity with library systems and tools used for cataloging and authority control, such as Ex Libris Alma, OCLC Connexion, NACO, ORCID, or ISNI. Experience in supervision, project management, and/or providing instruction and training in an academic or research library environment. Helpful FSU Libraries seeks an innovative and resourceful librarian to lead and help shape its monographic cataloging program. This is an exciting opportunity for an early- to mid-career librarian who is eager to build their expertise while solving complex problems, improving workflows, and exploring how emerging technologies can support the future of resource description and discovery. This position will lead cataloging operations for monographic resources in all languages, including materials in non-Roman scripts, and will work with colleagues to re-envision monographic and foreign language cataloging procedures at FSU. A particularly exciting area of exploration will be the use of AI-assisted approaches to support the translation and transliteration of materials in non-Roman alphabets, particularly Chinese, Japanese, and Korean, while maintaining the accuracy and quality essential to library metadata. This faculty librarian will supervise two full-time catalogers and will combine hands-on cataloging expertise with workflow development, staff training, quality control, and collaborative problem solving. The position offers opportunities to build specialized expertise, contribute to professional service and research, and grow as part of a team of enthusiastic learners. Contact Info Alex Chisum , Head of Cataloging and Metadata University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range $60,000 - $75,00, commensurate with education and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63605&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Associate Dean for Academic Affairs \u2013 Associate/Full Professor or Teaching Faculty II/III Rank - Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences", "description": "Job Title Associate Dean for Academic Affairs \u2013 Associate/Full Professor or Teaching Faculty II/III Rank - Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63605 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences Responsibilities The Associate Dean for Academic Affairs serves in a leadership position, overseeing the operations of the Office of Academic Services and Intern Support (OASIS) in the College. Leadership & Oversight Supervising, assigning areas of responsibility, and evaluating all faculty and staff within the Academic Affairs unit (approximately 17 faculty and staff). Overseeing the unit\u2019s financial planning and budgeting activities. Student Affairs Serving as the Academic Dean for all student-related processes, which includes, but is not limited to: Advising students, faculty, and chairs regarding Grade Appeals and General Grievance processes. Advising the College Student Leadership Committee (SLC). Academic Affairs Serving as the Academic Dean and the College liaison for University-level entities, including the Office of Accreditation and Quality Assurance, the Office of Institutional Performance and Assessment, the Office of Faculty Development and Advancement, Undergraduate Studies and the Graduate School. Serving on multiple committees as the College representative for academic affairs. Maintaining the College Degree Program Inventory (DPI) and Certificate Program Inventory (CPI) with FSU IR. Assisting academic programs with new degree, major, and certificate proposals. Working closely with chairs, faculty, academic staff, and students regarding the College and FSU graduate and undergraduate policies and procedures. Overseeing the College curriculum committee and associated curriculum proposal process. Approving all Graduate Faculty Status, Graduate Teaching Status, and Co-Directive applications. Recruitment, Admissions, & Enrollment Management Data Overseeing all College academic affairs data processes, including analysis and reporting. Coordinating annual student Program Satisfaction Surveys. Assisting with design and maintenance of the College Data SharePoint site. Accreditation & State Program Approval (Office of Quality Assurance) Serving as FSU\u2019s Florida Department of Education Liaison for all educator preparation programs (Anne\u2019s College, Panama City, Fine Arts, and Music). Maintaining curriculum, policies, and procedures for all FLDOE approved educator preparation programs. Working with nationally accredited programs through assisting in the design and full implementation of student learning outcome assessment systems. Working Environment Promoting methods for communicating policies and procedures to faculty and academic staff; Supports department academic staff in all areas of academic affairs. Maintaining a congenial and collaborative relationship with all departments and academic support units within the College. Teaching Department responsibilities are limited to teaching and advising doctoral students. Teaching responsibilities equivalent to one course per academic year in the fall or spring semester for tenure-track candidates or two courses per academic year for specialized faculty candidates. Qualifications Earned doctoral degree in a discipline related to one of the academic units in the College. Demonstrated success in research and/or teaching, depending on the type of faculty line (tenured/tenure-earning or specialized teaching) sought. Prior experience in academic leadership at the program, center, institute, department, or college level. Ability to analyze data and make data-informed decisions. Preferred Qualifications Prior experience working with state-approved and/or nationally accredited academic programs. Prior experience developing new academic degree programs. Other Information The Office of the Dean in the Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences at Florida State University invites applications for an Associate Dean for Academic Affairs position to start in July or August of 2027. For external candidates, the faculty rank (tenure-track associate/full professor or specialized teaching faculty II/III) associated with the appointment will be determined based on the selected candidate\u2019s qualifications and experience. The Office of Academic Services and Intern Support (OASIS) is the representative office for the academic dean of the Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences. OASIS strives to provide students, staff, and faculty, with the tools and support needed for student success. OASIS serves as the central repository for all student records, monitors required academic milestones, provides academic advising and support for undergraduate students, collaborates with academic departments to provide academic support for graduate students, and serves as the primary liaison between current students and the Office of the Registrar, the Division of Undergraduate Studies, and The Graduate School. OASIS directly manages the undergraduate admission process and provides support to academic departments in the admission of graduate students. Additionally, OASIS works with educator preparation programs throughout the university to coordinate internship placements and field-based experiences with PK-12 schools and students. The roots of FSU\u2019s Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences date back to the university\u2019s establishment, and it is the oldest college of its kind in Florida. The College is home to six academic departments united through a common goal to maximize human potential. In total, the College includes the Department of Educational Leadership & Policy Studies, Department of Educational Psychology & Learning Systems, Department of Human Development & Family Sciences, Department of Health, Nutrition & Food Sciences, Department of Sport Management, School of Teacher Education, numerous research centers, and three laboratory schools (Florida State University School, FSU Pembroke Pines Charter School, and The Collegiate School at FSU Panama City). Anne\u2019s College serves over 4,000 students via approximately 200 full-time faculty and nearly 80 full-time staff. Contact Info Toby Park-Gaghan , Search Committee Chair University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applicants should also include a letter of application, names of three references with contact information, and a statement of academic affairs leadership philosophy. Transcripts, work samples (such as journal articles or teaching artifacts), and three letters of recommendation will be required of candidates selected for an interview. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . The faculty rank associated with the appointment will be determined based on the selected candidate\u2019s qualifications and experience. A 9-month versus 12-month appointment will be dependent on the selected candidate's rank and program. Review of candidates will begin November 13, 2026, and will continue until filled. We urge interested candidates to submit materials as soon as possible. This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63592&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Open Rank Professor, 9 Month Salaried - School of Dance", "description": "Job Title Open Rank Professor, 9 Month Salaried - School of Dance Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63592 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department School of Dance Responsibilities The Florida State University School of Dance invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track Open Rank Faculty in Dance with expertise in Dance Science, Dancer Health and Wellness, and evidence-informed approaches to dancer training. We seek a collaborative scholar, educator, and mentor whose work bridges scientific inquiry, embodied practice, and creative exploration in ways that advance the preparation and well-being of dancers. Situated within our nationally recognized Dancer Training Program, this position offers a distinctive opportunity for an individual whose expertise may span areas such as applied science, performance research, pedagogy, somatic practices, rehabilitation, conditioning, creative scholarship, or interdisciplinary inquiry, while maintaining a clear commitment to optimizing dancer development through research-informed practice. The successful candidate will join a dynamic community of faculty, staff, and students dedicated to innovation, excellence, and the evolving future of dancer training. Teaching The successful candidate will contribute to the School's nationally recognized Dancer Training Program through teaching that reflects expertise in dance science, dancer health and wellness, and evidence-informed approaches to training. Teaching courses such as Dance Conditioning, Dance Kinesiology, Science of Dance Training, Dance Coaching, Research in the Dance Sciences, and related topics. Contributing specialized instruction in areas aligned with the candidate's expertise, such as Pilates, Gyrotonic, Yoga, Strength and Conditioning, Somatic Practices, Motor Learning, Injury Risk Management, Rehabilitation-Informed Training, Dance Technique, and other movement-based practices. Developing innovative courses and learning experiences that integrate scientific inquiry, embodied practice, creative exploration, and emerging approaches to dancer development. Research and Creative Scholarship The successful candidate will maintain an active research and/or creative scholarship agenda that advances the preparation, performance, health, and well-being of dancers. Conducting research related to dancer health, wellness, performance optimization, conditioning, pedagogy, injury risk management, motor learning, and related areas in the dance sciences. Disseminating scholarship through peer-reviewed publications, presentations, and other professional activities and venues with national and international reach. Engaging in applied, practice-based, and creative forms of inquiry that connect research with studio, classroom, laboratory, rehearsal, or performance settings. Contributing to the continued evolution of the dance sciences through interdisciplinary, collaborative, and innovative approaches to research and artistic practice. Service The successful candidate will contribute to the shared governance and mission of the School of Dance through service to the program, university, and profession. Serving on the Dance Conditioning and Wellness Committee and supporting initiatives within the School's Movement Training Laboratory. Contributing expertise to programs and initiatives that promote dancer health, wellness, and performance excellence. Participating in School, College, and University governance through committee work and other service assignments determined through faculty governance processes and in consultation with the Chair. Engaging in professional service activities that support the broader fields of dance science, dancer training, and higher education. Mentoring and Student Development The successful candidate will mentor undergraduate and graduate students as artists, scholars, researchers, and movement practitioners. Advising students pursuing interests in the dance sciences, dancer health and wellness, movement training, performance coaching, or related fields. Mentoring student research, creative scholarship, and practice-based inquiry. Guiding students in the application of evidence-informed approaches to performance preparation, training, recovery, and injury-risk reduction. Supporting students' professional development and preparation for careers in academic, artistic, clinical, research, or interdisciplinary settings. Contributing to an environment of student success through mentoring that extends across teaching, scholarship, service, and community engagement. Qualifications Doctoral degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization from an accredited institution in one of the dance sciences or a related field with an emphasis on working with dancers. Evidence of scholarly, creative, or applied research activity related to dancer development, health and wellness, performance optimization, pedagogy, movement training, or closely related areas. Demonstrated ability to contribute to a collaborative academic environment and to work effectively with faculty, staff, and students in advancing initiatives related to dancer training, health, and wellness. Demonstrated commitment to evidence-informed practice and the integration of research, embodied knowledge, and teaching. Preferred Qualifications Experience teaching courses related to the dance sciences, dancer health and wellness, movement training, conditioning, kinesiology, performance preparation, pedagogy, coaching, or related fields. Experience teaching, coaching, training, or facilitating movement-based practices such as Pilates, Gyrotonic, Yoga, Strength and Conditioning, Somatics, Motor Learning, Injury Risk Management, Rehabilitation-Informed Training, Dance Technique, or other approaches that support dancer development and well-being. Active research, creative scholarship, or applied professional practice that advances understanding of healthy and effective dancer training. Experience mentoring undergraduate and/or graduate students in research, creative inquiry, professional practice, or career pathways related to dance science, dancer health and wellness, and movement training. Demonstrated ability to bridge scientific inquiry, embodied practice, and artistic exploration in teaching, scholarship, or professional work. Familiarity with quantitative, qualitative, mixed-methods, and/or practice-based research approaches relevant to dancer training and performance, including experience with small-N and within-subject research designs. Other Information The College of Fine Arts at Florida State University is dedicated to fostering artistic excellence, creative exploration, and scholarly inquiry across a variety of disciplines. Our renowned faculty and staff educate and empower students to become visionary performers, artists, educators, art historians, designers, curators, art therapists, researchers, and arts administrators who shape the future of the visual arts, healing arts, performing arts, and design. Through passionate teaching, community engagement, innovative research, and artistic practice we enrich lives, elevate artistic expression, and inspire positive change and well-being in society. Montgomery Hall is one of the best developed dancer training facilities in the nation. The Maggie Allesee National Center for Choreography (MANCC) is an internationally recognized dance choreographic research center and part of the School of Dance. This unique and visionary institute brings a steady stream of prominent and emerging dance artists to campus to create and develop the work that the rest of the world will experience in years to come. Add to this mix an esteemed faculty and talented, highly motivated students, and it is easy to see why we are excited for what is to come. Contact Info Search Committee Chair: Professor Gwen Welliver University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applicants are required to submit: Examples of excellence in research or creative activity or excellence in teaching. CV One-page statement of their accomplishments over the last five years. Discussion of their teaching, research and service (no longer than six pages). Names, addresses, telephone numbers, and email addresses of three references. Confidential Letters of Reference: This position requires that you have three confidential professional letters of recommendation submitted on your behalf. Follow the steps below to request these letters through our system: 1) After submitting your application, click the Explore Jobs link; 2) Click the My References link; 3) Click the Send/View Reference Request button next to the appropriate position; and 4) Follow the steps on that page to send your references a system generated email requesting they submit a letter of recommendation on your behalf. You may also return to the My References link and click on \"Send/View Reference Request\" to see if your references have responded, add additional references, or resend requests. Candidates who currently hold tenure and are seeking appointment with tenure at Florida State University will need to submit the materials for evaluation if selected. These materials are required to support the tenure review process at the time of hire. Finalists may be asked to provide the below additional documentation as part of the evaluation. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. Review of applicants will begin on December 1, 2026. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63081&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Postdoctoral Research Associate in Ultrafast XUV Spectroscopy in High Magnetic Fields (OPS)", "description": "Job Title Postdoctoral Research Associate in Ultrafast XUV Spectroscopy in High Magnetic Fields (OPS) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63081 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The National High Magnetic Field Laboratory , headquartered at Florida State University, a top-tier research-intensive university, seeks highly qualified applicants to join our program in optical spectroscopy of condensed matter, with an emphasis on ultrafast optical techniques. The NHMFL is the world\u2019s largest and highest-powered magnet laboratory. It is home to several world-record-breaking magnets, including the 45 T Hybrid and the 25 T Split-Florida Helix. Research spans physics, chemistry, materials science, biochemistry, instrumentation, and related fields. The NHMFL hosts one of the world's largest communities of scientists working in high magnetic fields and provides a highly collaborative environment with extensive technical and scientific support. The post-doctoral associate being sought will work with a team to develop and use instrumentation to produce, deliver, and measure extreme ultraviolet (XUV) light to samples placed in the 25 T Split-Florida Helix magnet. Responsibilities The successful candidate will contribute to the development of a novel experimental platform combining ultrafast extreme ultraviolet spectroscopy with high magnetic fields to investigate emergent phenomena in quantum materials and other condensed matter systems. The candidate will work closely with DC Magnetic Field staff, external project co-PIs, MagLab users, graduate students, and postdoctoral fellows; contribute to collaborative and independent research projects; publish manuscripts; and participate in the development of external grant proposals. Postdoctoral applicants must have completed a Ph.D. in a STEM field and demonstrate strong scholarly potential in the ultrafast spectroscopy of condensed matter, chemistry, biochemistry, or related subject matter. Qualifications PhD in Physics, Chemistry, or a related area Applicants should have demonstrated expertise in ultrafast optical spectroscopy including (but not limited to) sample preparation, data acquisition, experiment design and construction. Experience with high-harmonic generation, XUV spectroscopy, or related ultrafast nonlinear optical techniques is highly desirable. Familiarity with cryogenic and vacuum technologies for low-temperature measurements. The ability to bring innovative methods, technology development, or collaborative opportunities will be considered a significant strength. Other Information Please include: Curriculum vitae Cover letter describing research experience and future interests Contact information for at least three references (letters submitted through the application system) Contact Info For inquiries about this position, please contact Dr. Stephen McGill . University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://jobs.fsu.edu. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an OPS/temporary job. Based on the duties, this position may require completion of a criminal history background check. The position is full-time and includes health benefits. This position is being re-advertised. Previous applicants need not reapply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63596&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Professor & Director, 9 Month Salaried - School of Teacher Education - Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences", "description": "Job Title Professor & Director, 9 Month Salaried - School of Teacher Education - Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63596 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department School of Teacher Education - Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences Responsibilities Provide leadership and strategic direction for all academic programs in the School Lead and enhance the School\u2019s strategic efforts for research productivity and excellence Lead the effort for identifying the major priorities of the School, including the combined BS/MS pathways in teacher education, and other graduate programs (e.g., PhD and master\u2019s) Align the School\u2019s strategic planning goals with the strategic plans of the University and the College Manage budgetary, personnel, and other departmental resources Foster and maintain a supportive environment for all faculty, staff, and students in the School Provide leadership and direction for creating an environment of transparency and open communication within the School Enhance the rigor and quality of research in the School, as well as the opportunities for PhD students Collaborate with the Director of the Florida Center for Reading Research and the Learning Systems Institute to continue developing productive research partnerships that promote the work of faculty in the department Lead efforts to build relationships within and outside the University that lead to the betterment of the College, and the well-being of the community and the region Qualifications Earned doctorate from one of the educational disciplines found within the School, or a closely-related field. A record of scholarly accomplishments consistent with the rank of full professor with tenure; exceptionally qualified candidates may also be considered for the Mack and Effie Campbell Distinguished Professorship. Preferred Qualifications Previous experience in academic leadership, including budgetary oversight and management Broad research knowledge and experience at Research 1 universities\u2014to understand, guide, and communicate with faculty working in different fields within various paradigms and methodologies Experience as a leader for faculty members\u2019 professional development and growth. Experience with building and maintaining relationships with K-12 and community agency field partners and field-placement management Demonstrated commitment to faculty development and advancement Other Information The Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences at Florida State University invites applications for a Professor and Director of the School of Teacher Education. The College encourages applications from visionary leaders committed to education and its role in maximizing human potential. Reporting to the Dean of the College, the Director is responsible for the overall success of the School, its students, and its faculty and staff. The School of Teacher Education is committed to high quality personnel preparation programs; service to the state of Florida; and high-quality scholarly research in elementary education, early childhood education, reading/language arts, second language education, special education, blindness and low vision, science education, math education, social science education, English education, and related areas. The School strives to provide undergraduate and graduate students with world-class training in teaching, research, and professional development. Through the guidance and mentorship of faculty, students graduate to serve as educational leaders who will contribute to the betterment of a pluralistic, global society in the context of the state of Florida's needs for an educated, global-minded citizenry. In addition to mentoring and preparing the next generation of educators, faculty engage in a wide range of research activities. Faculty work routinely appears in prestigious publications and is cited by peers. Furthermore, faculty receive support from a robust Office of Research to pursue research opportunities, professional awards, and more. The roots of FSU\u2019s Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences date back to the university\u2019s establishment, and it is the oldest college of its kind in Florida. The College is home to six academic departments united through a common goal to maximize human potential. In total, the College includes the Department of Educational Leadership & Policy Studies, Department of Educational Psychology & Learning Systems, Department of Human Development & Family Sciences, Department of Health, Nutrition & Food Sciences, Department of Sport Management, School of Teacher Education, numerous research centers, and three laboratory schools (Florida State University School, FSU Pembroke Pines Charter School, and The Collegiate School at FSU Panama City). Anne\u2019s College serves over 4,000 students via approximately 200 full-time faculty and nearly 80 full-time staff. Contact Info Dr. Alysia Roehrig , Search Committee Chair Questions regarding the application submission system and process should be directed to the application coordinator: Jania Kadar , Sr. Administrative Specialist University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applicants should also include contact information for three professional references (references will not be contacted prior to notifying applicants), and a cover letter of no more than four pages that articulates the candidate\u2019s experience and vision for the School as related to: (1) leadership, innovation, and strategic partnerships; (2) research; and (3) teaching. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. Review of candidates will begin October 31, 2026 and will continue until filled. We urge interested candidates to submit materials as soon as possible. This position has a proposed start date of July 1, 2027. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=62745&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Research Engineer, Level II-IV (Magnet Science & Technology - National High Magnetic Field Laboratory)", "description": "Job Title Research Engineer, Level II-IV (Magnet Science & Technology - National High Magnetic Field Laboratory) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 62745 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department National High Magnetic Field Laboratory Join the world-renowned National High Magnetic Field Laboratory at Florida State University (FSU) and support groundbreaking scientific discovery in a collaborative, high-tech environment. FSU was recently recognized as one of America\u2019s Best-in-State Employers for its strong workplace culture and employee-centered values. Responsibilities Responsible for mechanical design applying standard engineering practices, procedures, and criteria in designing complex high field magnet assemblies at the National High Magnetic Field Laboratory. Engineering Design & Analysis Responsible for selecting standard engineering techniques, procedures, and criteria in designing complex magnets. Evaluate requirements and constraints of magnets, designed to meet scientific or research needs, and create mechanical designs to accommodate them according to their applied loads. Perform structural analyses to designed hardware and fasteners. Read and understand technical drawings including geometric dimensioning and tolerancing. System Design & Development Directs conceptual design, detailed system design, and preparation of engineering drawings/documents of magnet systems using 3D CAD and may also include software such as Autodesk Inventor, Solid Works, Pro-Engineer, etc. Design from engineering prototype to final system using technology development, fabrication process development, preparation of engineering documentation, and supply chain management. Testing, Fabrication & Quality Develop tooling and assist in building mechanical assemblies while applying quality controls and adhering to safe practices. Responsible for preparing, testing, and evaluating plans and specifications of magnets designed to meet scientific or research needs. Ensures the product quality meets the researchers needs. Develops unique methods and processes for technical tasks such as system assembly, performance testing and analysis of results. Project Coordination & Collaboration Interacts and coordinates with external users, researchers, and scientists in the development and implementation of projects. Assists group leaders in directing individual project/programs. In absence of group leaders may need to provide leadership decision making concerning acquisitions, staff and technical project details. Attend team meetings to discuss project testing needs and report test results. Conduct background research to help develop and define engineering requirements. Interact with other professional staff for test method development, and the design and construction of magnet systems. Laboratory Operations Perform general laboratory duties such as creating purchase requests, maintaining tools and equipment, and organizing and maintaining inventory. Research, Publications & Outreach Publish and/or present the results designs, testing, or other works in journals or conferences when appropriate. Participate in outreach activities and interact with numerous technical visitors from domestic and international laboratories and industries. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and three years of experience; or a high school diploma and seven years of experience. (Note: post high-school education and/or experience may substitute at a comparable rate.) Additional experience qualifies candidates for higher-level consideration (III\u2013VI). Each level requires three additional years of experience. Helpful What you Gain at FSU Opportunity to work at a world-renowned national research laboratory. Meaningful contributions to scientific discovery and student learning. A collaborative environment that values your expertise and invests in your growth. Contact Info Please contact Kayla West if you have questions. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. Anticipated Salary Range Level II \u2013 Mid $60,000\u2019s, commensurate with education and experience. Level III \u2013 Mid $70,000\u2019s, commensurate with education and experience. Level IV \u2013 Mid $80,000\u2019s, commensurate with education and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our interactive too l to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://jobs.fsu.edu. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being re-advertised. Previous applicants need not reapply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63538&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Associate Dean for Research, 9 Month Salaried - Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences", "description": "Job Title Associate Dean for Research, 9 Month Salaried - Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63538 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Office of the Dean in the Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences Responsibilities The Associate Dean for Research serves in a leadership position, overseeing the operations of the Office of Research in the College. Operations Supervising, assigning areas of responsibility, and evaluating faculty, clinical and administrative staff within the Office of Research unit (approximately 15 faculty and staff), as appropriate Overseeing the Office of Research (OoR) operations, including but not limited to: Identifying and implementing effective grant development activities and proposal tracking systems for efficient operation within the OoR Supervising the administration of all grants related activities effectively and with a commitment to the highest quality of customer service for faculty and staff Creating and implementing innovative programs expanding research activities Tracking and supporting grant activity, using a variety of analytical tools (e.g., Academic Analytics) to analyze proposal submissions, grant awards, journal article publications, journal article citations, and honorific awards Maintaining fiscal responsibility for the OoR budget, external fund sources affiliated with the OoR, and OoR SRAD funds Collaborating with, PIs, OoR senior editor(s), and methodologist in the conceptualization and design phases of grant proposals and other research projects Managing administrative facility requests, including, but not limited to Office of Research space allocation requests/usage and activities associated with research amplification Supporting Faculty Meeting with prospective faculty members to communicate college expectations related to all aspects of Anne\u2019s College research enterprise, including expectations for faculty grant submission, programs aligned to successful proposal development and awards, and direct Office of Research (OoR) support in grant development, including faculty research agenda development, administration, and amplification Assisting faculty in applying for and obtaining external funding including, but not limited to, differentiating various support mechanisms managed by the OoR Evaluating faculty candidate readiness to engage in grant activities and high-impact research (e.g., proposal preparation skills, likelihood of obtaining funding to support research interests, working on grant projects, publishing in high-impact journals) Communicating with College leadership faculty candidate readiness to undertake a robust and impactful research agenda Collaborating with new faculty, in conjunction with appropriate OoR personnel, to discern research interest, develop research agenda, identify funding opportunities, and develop supportive plans to apply and obtain funding across various institution specific opportunities (e.g., FYAP program) Developing and implementing all programs and activities related to internal research catalyst funding Liaising with the Office of Research Development and Sponsored Research Administration to elevate and expand Anne\u2019s College research footprint in campus-wide interdisciplinary research programs, including facilitating the management of internal grant applications, mock review panels, and faculty research profiles intra-institutionally Coordinating all research amplification activities, including targeted social media posts, facilitating the College\u2019s Open Access Publishing program, and enhancing programs related to indexed journal article publishing Leadership Serving as a visible member of the Dean\u2019s Cabinet Ensuring alignment of OoR activities with College strategic plans and policies Providing the Dean and the College leadership team with data analysis to support and inform research-related strategic planning and resource allocation decisions Chairing Strategic Planning Committee\u2019s Academic Quality Subcommittee Administering the annual Dean\u2019s Circle Catalyst Grant Program Leading the Academy of Scholars program and helping to coordinate all related activities throughout the year Ensuring the successful planning and implementation of College research events Coordinating all research partnerships with the Florida Department of Education Advising the College\u2019s department chairs on the potential impact grant activities might have on faculty workload and SRAD distribution Working with the OoR Program Director and at the discretion of the Dean to provide administrative support and oversight to Florida State University Schools, FSU Pembroke Pines, and the Collegiate School at Panama City External Relations Attending, and serving as spokesperson at, College grant-related research meetings Establishing strategic professional relationships with key individuals within various funding agencies (e.g., IES, NSF, NIH, Spencer Foundation, W.T. Grant Foundation) Developing and maintaining effective collaborative relationships with all relevant individuals and groups (e.g., FSU VP for Research, other Associate Deans for Research, Director of the Office of Research Development, FSU Office of Research, LSI, FCRR) Serving as a member of the Council of Associate Deans for Research (CADR) Serving as the College\u2019s representative member of the LEARN Coalition Representing the Dean or College/University interests at regional, national, or international conferences, convenings, or events at the discretion of the Dean Teaching Department responsibilities are limited to teaching and advising doctoral students Teaching responsibilities equivalent to one course per academic year in the fall or spring semester. Qualifications Earned doctoral degree in a discipline related to one of the academic units in the College. Demonstrated success in research that would warrant tenure in a discipline within the College Prior experience in academic leadership at the program, center, institute, department, or college level. Ability to analyze data and make data-informed decisions. Preferred Qualifications Prior experience in navigating and establishing strategic professional relationships with key individuals within an institutional structure as well as governmental or private extramural funding agencies. Prior experience in developing and maintaining effective and collaborative college and campus relationships with individuals and groups relevant to the portfolio of responsibilities for the position. Prior experience developing programs to support faculty research and elevate institutional profile. Prior experience in supervision of organizational structures comparable to the Anne\u2019s College Office of Research. Other Information The Office of the Dean in the Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences at Florida State University invites applications for an Associate Dean for Research position to start in July or August of 2027. For external candidates, the faculty rank associated with the tenure-track appointment will be determined based on the selected candidate\u2019s qualifications and experience. The mission of the Office of Research (OoR) is to provide excellent service to the Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences faculty in the development, administration, and amplification of research efforts. The roots of FSU\u2019s Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences date back to the university\u2019s establishment, and it is the oldest college of its kind in Florida. The College is home to six academic departments united through a common goal to maximize human potential. In total, the College includes the Department of Educational Leadership & Policy Studies, Department of Educational Psychology & Learning Systems, Department of Human Development & Family Sciences, Department of Health, Nutrition & Food Sciences, Department of Sport Management, School of Teacher Education, numerous research centers, and three laboratory schools (Florida State University School, FSU Pembroke Pines Charter School, and The Collegiate School at FSU Panama City). Anne\u2019s College serves over 4,000 students via approximately 200 full-time faculty and nearly 80 full-time staff. Contact Info Bob Eklund , Search Committee Chair University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applicants should also include a letter of application, names of three references with contact information, and a statement of research leadership philosophy. Transcripts, work samples (such as journal articles or teaching artifacts), and three letters of recommendation will be required of candidates selected for an interview. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . The faculty rank associated with the appointment will be determined based on the selected candidate\u2019s qualifications and experience. This is a 9-month faculty position with a guaranteed summer appointment for the administrative role. Review of candidates will begin November 13, 2026, and will continue until filled. We urge interested candidates to submit materials as soon as possible This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=62366&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Talent Engagement Specialist", "description": "Job Title Talent Engagement Specialist Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 62366 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Office of Human Resources - Talent Acquisition Responsibilities About This Role Florida State University - recognized as a Forbes Best-In-State Employer - is a place where meaningful work and organizational impact intersect every day. The Talent Engagement Specialist strengthens FSU\u2019s ability to compete for top talent by enhancing outreach, guiding hiring leaders with consultative support, and improving how candidates experience FSU at every stage of the recruitment journey. This role meets immediate workforce needs while steadily building the pipelines that keep the university positioned for long-term success. This position is dedicated to advancing strategic recruitment partnerships and initiatives across the university, with a specialized focus on our Facilities teams. Through talent intelligence, sourcing expertise, and relationship-driven outreach, the Talent Engagement Specialist helps ensure FSU is positioned to meet highly technical, operational, and mission-critical staffing needs across a large and evolving campus environment. Why This Role Matters Talent Acquisition at FSU supports an evolving proactive, insight-driven model that aligns recruitment with the university\u2019s long-range strategic priorities. This role is central to that progression, strengthening our ability to anticipate workforce needs, activate talent pipelines early, and support hiring leaders with guided strategies that keep FSU competitive in a dynamic talent landscape. In this role, you\u2019ll help FSU attract and engage talent for critical operational, technical, and leadership positions, with a primary focus on Facilities. Your work will directly support the teams who maintain and enhance the physical environments where students learn, researchers innovate, and campus life thrives. What You\u2019ll Do Strategic Sourcing & Talent Research Develop targeted sourcing strategies to identify passive talent for specialized, technical, and leadership roles, with a primary focus on Facilities staffing needs. Conduct talent mapping, market research, and advanced searches to build high-quality candidate pools. Leverage digital platforms, AI-enabled tools, and sourcing technology to expand reach and accelerate candidate engagement. Candidate Engagement & Pipeline Development Build and maintain talent pipelines for key workforce areas, including operations, skilled trades, technical specialists, and Facilities leadership. Create targeted outreach campaigns and refine messaging based on candidate engagement and response data. Represent FSU\u2019s employment brand through professional, responsive, and engaging candidate interactions. Recruitment Partnership & Strategy Partner with Facilities leadership, HR Representatives, and hiring managers to understand current and future workforce needs. Provide market insights, talent availability data, and sourcing recommendations to support recruitment decisions. Align sourcing efforts with FSU\u2019s Talent Acquisition strategy and broader university priorities. Technology, Analytics & Continuous Improvement Use CRM, ATS, LinkedIn, Indeed, and other digital recruitment platforms to execute and manage sourcing campaigns. Organize and segment prospective candidates for current and future opportunities. Track outreach, engagement, and conversion metrics and provide regular updates to Talent Acquisition leadership and Facilities partners. Continuously improve sourcing strategies based on recruitment data, workforce trends, and stakeholder feedback. Qualifications Bachelor\u2019s degree in Human Resources, Business, Communications, Marketing, or a related field and two years of experience in strategic sourcing, senior level recruiting, or talent acquisition; or a high school diploma or equivalent and the same experience equal to six years. Preferred Qualifications Demonstrated ability to source, engage, and cultivate relationships with passive candidates across niche, technical, and leadership talent markets. Familiarity with ATS and CRM platforms. Proficiency with CRM platforms such as Avature, Beamery, or Yello. Certifications such as AIRS, LinkedIn Certified Recruiter, or SHRM-CP. Advanced sourcing methodologies Talent mapping and market research CRM/ATS proficiency Helpful Working at Florida State University At FSU, you\u2019ll be part of a vibrant academic and professional community where ideas matter, collaboration fuels progress, and meaningful work shapes the future. The Talent Acquisition team plays a critical role in supporting the people who make FSU exceptional \u2014 ensuring the university can attract and retain the talent needed to advance our mission. Love What YOU DO at FSU! Your future begins here. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. Anticipated Salary Range Starting at $50,000, commensurate with education and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our interactive too l to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://jobs.fsu.edu. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. This position is being re-advertised. Previous applicants need not reapply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63573&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "UGS Academic Advisor Pool - Fall 2026 (Multiple Vacancies)", "description": "Job Title UGS Academic Advisor Pool - Fall 2026 (Multiple Vacancies) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63573 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Advising First \u2013 Division of Undergraduate Studies Responsibilities Responsible for advising undergraduate students in the development of academic schedules appropriate for stated education goals. Takes a proactive approach to academic advising, seeking out contact with students and staff, and providing advising services on request. Works with academic departments and other units within Undergraduate Studies to develop advising programs. Engages, helps plan, and participates in special projects for Advising First/UGST. Recommends changes and additions in existing policies and procedures that positively implement a successful advising program. Performs special projects as assigned by Undergraduate Studies. Qualifications Bachelor\u2019s degree and two years of experience; or a high school diploma or equivalent and six years of experience. (Note: a combination of post high school education and experience equal to six years.) Preferred Qualifications Knowledge of University rules and regulations. Prior customer service experience and /or experience working with students in an educational setting. Ability to extract complex academic information from various sources and maintain confidentiality. Experience and/or working knowledge of student advising, counseling, or working one-on-one with people in a professional or academic setting. Creative problem-solving skills. Master\u2019s degree is preferred. Computer skills to include experience with Microsoft Office and web-based applications. Ability to interpret and explain policies, procedures, goals, and objectives to students, parents, faculty, and staff. Ability to prioritize, organize, and perform multiple work assignments simultaneously with minimal to moderate supervision. Ability to deal with people in a calm, confident manner and with complete objectivity. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with students, parents, supervisors, and interdepartmental personnel. Attention to detail with a high standard of integrity. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Starting at $44,184, commensurate with education and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63492&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Musicology, 9 Month Salaried - College of Music", "description": "Job Title Assistant Professor of Musicology, 9 Month Salaried - College of Music Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63492 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department College of Music Responsibilities Maintain an active program of research and creative/scholarly activity leading toward tenure; teach undergraduate and graduate courses in Early Music, Musicology, and additional areas of expertise; mentor graduate students in the Musicology Area; contribute to the intellectual and artistic life of the College of Music; and participate in appropriate service. The successful candidate will also contribute to FSU's Early Music Program through historically informed performance, which may include coaching, directing, performing with, or otherwise supporting Early Music ensembles and related activities. Qualifications Completed doctorate or highest degree appropriate in Musicology, Historical Musicology, Ethnomusicology, or a closely related field by the time of appointment. Evidence of a developing record of excellence in research and teaching appropriate to a tenure-earning appointment. Scholarly expertise in Early Music (broadly defined) and demonstrated knowledge of historically informed performance practice. Preferred Qualifications Preference will be given to candidates whose scholarship and teaching engage substantially with performance and performance practice and who can contribute actively to FSU's Early Music Program. Demonstrated experience performing, coaching, directing, or otherwise working with historically informed vocal and/or instrumental performance is especially desirable. Additional areas of scholarly expertise are open. Other Information The Musicology Area seeks a scholar specializing in Early Music whose work integrates historical research with historically informed performance. The successful candidate will contribute to FSU's longstanding strengths in Early Music and its integration of musicological study, performance practice, and ensemble participation. The College of Music at Florida State University: is the largest such college in the Southeast and the third largest university-based music program in the nation. With over 90 faculty and 40 support staff, the College offers a range of degrees in music, baccalaureate through the doctorate. We are home to approximately 700 undergraduate and 400 graduate students, who represent nearly every state in the nation and 20 foreign countries. Contact Info Eden Wahlquist , Sr. Administrative Specialist (for technical assistance applying to this position) Dr. Frank Gunderson , Professor of Musicology (for inquiries for the search committee chair) University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Supplemental Application Materials: Please submit as individual PDFs a current CV and a cover letter. Three confidential letters of recommendation are required prior to the time of hire. Please be prepared to facilitate this process upon request. Additionally, we may request a writing sample and recording samples at a later date. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. However, for priority consideration, please complete all application materials by October 15th, 2026. Review of applications will begin immediately and will remain ongoing until the position is filled. Appointment will begin August 9th, 2027. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63501&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Trumpet, 9 Month Salaried - College of Music", "description": "Job Title Assistant Professor of Trumpet, 9 Month Salaried - College of Music Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63501 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department College of Music Responsibilities Teach undergraduate- and graduate-level trumpet, coordinate with large ensemble conductors and other cohorts, and supervise graduate teaching assistants. Recruit and maintain a successful teaching studio. Serve on doctoral and master\u2019s committees and juries. Maintain a professional career as a performing artist. Participate in university and professional service activities nationally and internationally as appropriate. Additional responsibilities may include teaching courses in the candidate\u2019s area of expertise. Qualifications The successful candidate will: Have completed a doctoral degree at the time of appointment or demonstrate a record of equivalent performance and teaching experience. Hold a record of successful university-level teaching experience and proven artistry as a professional performer of solo, chamber music, and orchestral music. Demonstrate strong commitment to the recruitment of outstanding students. Demonstrate a proven commitment to creating an environment which contributes to the vibrancy, and economy of the university community and engages students and citizens from different backgrounds and walks of life. Other Information Seeking new knowledge and deeper understanding of music in interdisciplinary contexts through innovative research, music performance, and creative activity, The College of Music at Florida State University is the largest such college in the Southeast and one of the largest university-based music programs in the nation. With over 90 faculty and 40 support staff, the College offers a range of degrees in music, baccalaureate through the doctorate. We are home to approximately 700 undergraduate and 400 graduate students, who represent nearly every state in the nation and 20 foreign countries. Contact Info For inquiries related to specifications of this position, please contact Professor Jeff Keesecker , Search Committee Chair For technical assistance applying to this position, please contact Eden Wahlquist , Sr. Administrative Specialist For all other inquiries, please contact Erica Francis , Dean\u2019s Executive Assistant University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. It is necessary to fully complete the online application for consideration. Please also upload a cover letter, curriculum vitae, links to representative recordings of solo playing (live recordings preferred), links to video recordings of teaching, and three letters of reference. PDF format is preferred. If the representative recordings PDFs include YouTube links, please ensure that privacy settings are set to \u201cpublic\u201d or \u201cunlisted,\u201d but not \u201cprivate.\u201d Video recordings of teaching must be no more than 20 minutes in length total and should include one undergraduate applied student and one graduate applied student. Playing recordings should be no more than 30 minutes in length total, and live recordings are preferred. Letters of Reference: This position requires that you have three confidential professional letters of recommendation submitted on your behalf. Follow the steps below to request these letters through our system: 1) After submitting your application, click the Careers link; 2) Click the My References link; 3) Click the Send/View Reference Request button next to the appropriate position; and 4) Follow the steps on that page to send your references a system generated email requesting they submit a letter of recommendation on your behalf. You may also return to the My References link and click on \"Send/View Reference Request\" to see if your references have responded, add additional references, or resend requests. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled; however, for priority consideration, please complete all application materials by November 1st, 2026. Review of applications will begin immediately and will remain ongoing until the position is filled. Appointment will begin August 2027. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63555&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Assistant/Associate Professor in Sport Management, 9 Month Salaried - Department of Sport Management - Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences", "description": "Job Title Assistant/Associate Professor in Sport Management, 9 Month Salaried - Department of Sport Management - Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63555 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Sport Management - Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences Responsibilities The individual hired will be required to maintain an active research agenda, possess strong knowledge of quantitative and/or qualitative research methods for the effective mentoring of master\u2019s and doctoral student research, teach undergraduate and graduate courses (including teaching online courses), seek external funding, aid in developing external partnerships, and contribute to department and university growth through appropriate service activities. Qualifications Minimum qualifications for the position include earned doctorate degree in Sport Management or related field; college/university teaching experience; mentoring experience; evidence of scholarly productivity; experience procuring external funding, or evidence of ability to procure external funding. An individual\u2019s program of research should align with one of the department\u2019s core content areas. Preferred Qualifications Preference will be given to individuals with a research interest aligned with business-related content (e.g., marketing, finance, economics, management). Preference will also be given to individuals with a record of procuring external funding. Other Information Candidates are being sought for a tenure-track Assistant/Associate Professor position in the Department Sport Management in the Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences. The department has thematic pillar areas which provide the broad context from which our research and course offerings are derived: Legal and Policy Issues in Sport, Management of Sport, Sport Economics/Finance, Sport Marketing, and Sport Media and Culture Studies. Contact Info Dr. Timothy Kellison , Search Committee Chair Katherine Maddox , Sr. Administrative Specialist (for questions regarding the application submission system and process) University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applicants should also include: Current curriculum vitae Letter of interest highlighting their qualifications for the position Names and contact information of three references Statement of research Statement of teaching philosophy. Transcripts and three letters of recommendation will be required of candidates selected for an interview. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Review of applications will begin November 13, 2026. We urge interested candidates to submit materials as soon as possible. This position will begin Fall 2027. This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63562&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Education and Social Sciences Librarian,12 Months Salaried", "description": "Job Title Education and Social Sciences Librarian,12 Months Salaried Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63562 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department University Libraries Responsibilities Serve as a library liaison to the Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences and assigned social science departments, building relationships with faculty, students, and staff. Design and deliver engaging library instruction, workshops, research guides, and other learning opportunities in both online and in-person environments. Help students and faculty navigate the research process through consultations and referrals to relevant library resources, services, and expertise. Support the development and assessment of library collections and resources for assigned subject areas. Collaborate with colleagues across FSU Libraries and engage with emerging approaches and technologies, including AI, that support teaching, learning, and research. Qualifications Master\u2019s degree from an ALA-accredited library and information science program (or international equivalent) or expected completion of the degree prior to beginning employment. Teaching or instructional experience and an interest in supporting student learning. Strong communication and interpersonal skills and an interest in building collaborative relationships with students, faculty, and colleagues. Interest in education, health, human or social sciences and enthusiasm for developing subject expertise in these areas. Demonstrated interest in emerging technologies, including AI, and their applications to teaching, learning, research, or libraries. Preferred Qualifications Familiarity with education, health and human sciences, and/or social science research resources, including databases and systematic or evidence synthesis review methods. Exposure to or interest in collection development in an academic or research library setting. Familiarity with instructional technologies and tools used to support teaching and learning in online and in-person environments. Helpful FSU Libraries is seeking an early-career librarian who is excited to grow as an educator, research partner, and member of a collaborative academic library. As the library liaison to the Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences and other social science departments, you will work directly with students and faculty to support teaching, learning, and research. You will provide library instruction, help students develop research and information literacy skills, connect faculty and students with resources and services, and help build collections that support their academic and research needs. You will also have opportunities to explore how emerging technologies, including AI, are changing teaching, research, and librarianship. We are looking for someone who is curious about these developments and excited to learn, experiment, and contribute as FSU Libraries continues to expand its work in this area. This position is designed to provide opportunities to learn and grow. You do not need to arrive knowing every aspect of academic librarianship. We are looking for someone with a strong foundation, an eagerness and ability to learn, an interest in teaching and research support, and enthusiasm for developing their skills alongside experienced colleagues. Contact Info Kelly Grove , STEM Program Director | GIS and Earth Sciences Librarian University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Starting salary is $60,000. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63554&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Director of Parent and Family Philanthropy & Engagement", "description": "Job Title Director of Parent and Family Philanthropy & Engagement Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63554 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department FSU Division of University Advancement Florida State University is currently in the leadership phase of a comprehensive campaign. As the leadership phase of the campaign begins, the Division of University Advancement is accelerating the hiring of additional development officers\u2019 campus-wide and is excited to build out its team. For Advancement professionals who are interested in being a part of a comprehensive campaign from the beginning for their career development, the timing is ideal to join our team. Responsibilities The Director of Parent & Family Philanthropy & Engagement is a strategic advancement leader responsible for designing and executing a comprehensive parent and family giving program. This role integrates annual giving, leadership annual giving, and major gift development to build a sustainable donor pipeline. The Director demonstrates expertise across philanthropy, alumni and constituent engagement, leadership, and data-informed decision-making. The Director oversees all parent and family giving efforts while managing a portfolio of prospects and donors, and supervises one staff member. Philanthropy Develop, execute and analyze a comprehensive parent and family philanthropy and engagement strategy. Manage a portfolio of 25\u201350 parent and family prospects; qualify, cultivate, solicit, and steward donors; collaborate with major gift colleagues on strategies that align with their unit priorities. Create compelling, donor-centered solicitations aligned with institutional priorities. Oversee an omni-channel solicitation calendar that is produced in collaboration with other internal stakeholders to ensure messaging is donor-centric, impact-driven, and aligned with institutional brand and priorities. Constituent Engagement & Donor Relations Oversee stewardship and engagement strategies that deepen parent and family connection and philanthropic participation. Build a multi-year donor pipeline that transitions parents from first-time donors to leadership and major gift levels. Oversee volunteer structures and events (e.g., Parent & Family Advancement Council and philanthropic/engagement events). Partner with campus stakeholders to integrate philanthropy into the full parent lifecycle. Partner with volunteer engagement and alumni engagement teams to maximize regional outreach. Travel frequently and work outside of normal business hours for donor engagement. Leadership & Talent Management Supervise and mentor one staff member, setting clear performance goals and supporting professional growth. Foster a collaborative and high-performing team aligned with advancement best practices. Provide strategic leadership for parent philanthropy initiatives across the division; foster collaborative relations across campus to amplify the role of family philanthropy in advancing the university\u2019s academic mission. Data, Research & Analytics Cultivate relationships with campus partners, including the Division of Student Affairs, Office of Graduation, Admissions, Colleges/Schools/Unit, and others. Leverage CRM systems and analytics to manage donor pipelines, track engagement, and measure fundraising performance. Analyze participation, retention, and giving trends to inform strategy and optimize results. Utilize data to segment audiences and tailor solicitation strategies. Ethics, Policy & Professional Practice (5%) Adhere to ethical standards and best practices as outlined by CASE and advancement industry guidelines. Maintain confidentiality and ensure responsible use of donor data. Promote an environment of integrity, accountability, and transparency in all fundraising activities. Qualifications Bachelor\u2019s degree and six years of experience related to the job duties or in an advancement field; or a high school diploma/equivalent and ten years of experience related to the job duties or in an advancement field. (Note: post-high school education may substitute for experience at the equivalent rate.) Valid Florida or Georgia driver's license or the ability to obtain upon hire date University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. This role requires driving and travel. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63519&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Grants Coordinator", "description": "Job Title Grants Coordinator Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63519 Location Sarasota, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The John & Mable Ringling Museum of Art is located in Sarasota, Florida, and is a department of Florida State University. Responsibilities This role coordinates institutional grants for The Ringling, including overseeing end-to-end grant processing, grant data preparation, Research Administration Management Portal (RAMP) routing, proposal submissions, fiscal coordination with Accounting, reporting, solicitation tracking, and communications to support for grant-funded projects. Manages a portfolio of local, state and national grant opportunities; researches and tracks solicitations and deadlines; maintains the annual grants calendar. Prepares and submits letters of inquiry and intent, grant applications, sponsorship proposals, and acknowledgment letters. Maintains all grant reporting files, including government and foundation grants. Oversees end-to-end grant processing, including gathering required institutional and project data, coordinating approvals, and routing submissions through the Research Administration Management Portal (RAMP) or other required systems. Ensures timely proposal submissions, approval process, and reporting. Works closely with Ringling Accounting, FSU Sponsored Research Administration, and other appropriate offices to monitor back-end/fiscal grant responsibilities. Collects data and metrics for reporting and analysis per grant application and reporting requirements; assists with monitoring expenditures and activities. Completes grant reporting and closeout activities. Meets with representatives from foundations and corporations to cultivate interest in supporting museum initiatives through grant funding and establishes ongoing relationships with constituents that provide grant support to the museum. Coordinates with Marketing and Communications to support features, acknowledgments, and public-facing content related to grant-funded projects; may provide copy editing for grant-related communications and other marketing communications as needed. Collaborates with the Development Team to coordinate corporate and foundation grant applications, reduce request redundancy, and ensure relevant records are in the FSU Foundation CRM donor database. Performs other duties, as assigned, that support departmental and organizational projects and goals. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and one year of experience or a combination of post-high-school education and experience equal to five years. This position requires successful completion of the eSPEAR Certification or ability to obtain the certification within 6 months of hire. Preferred Qualifications Excellent written and verbal communication skills, including professional business writing Robust interpersonal skills and ability to collaborate with internal and external partners Demonstrated problem-solving skills and ability to work independently with minimal supervision Certified Grant Writer (CGW) or Grant Professional Certification (GPC) Advanced: Project management and organizational skills, with the ability to manage multiple deadlines Attention to detail and accuracy in documentation and data management Skill in Microsoft Office Suite, particularly Excel, Word, and Outlook Experience with: Coordinating grant applications, awards, and reporting requirements Preparing, reviewing, or monitoring budgets and financial reports Grant management software, databases, or CRM systems Experience coordinating meetings, maintaining records, and tracking deliverables Previous experience in grant administration, sponsored research, development, fundraising, or nonprofit operations Knowledge of: Grant compliance, regulations, and funding agency guidelines Nonprofit, higher education, government, or museum funding environments Ability to: Research and identify funding opportunities Analyze data and prepare reports for stakeholders and funding agencies Maintain confidentiality and handle sensitive information Contact Info For more information or technical assistance, please contact Ringling Human Resources via email or by calling 941-358-2773. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Commensurate with the education, skills, and experience of the selected applicant. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Your application is not considered complete without attaching the following items: Cover Letter Resume Contact information (phone/email) for three or more references Considerations This is an A&P position. This role: Is based in Sarasota, FL. Is required to adhere to the business dress standards. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check. Working Hours Monday \u2013 Friday from 8:00 AM to 5:00 PM with a one-hour meal period. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63017&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Program Manager, Media & Communications (Office of Strategic Outreach & Recruitment, Anne's College)", "description": "Job Title Program Manager, Media & Communications (Office of Strategic Outreach & Recruitment, Anne's College) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63017 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Office of Strategic Outreach & Recruitment | Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences Responsibilities Lead the development and execution of the college's communications and marketing strategy across print, digital, web, social media, photography, video, and other multimedia platforms. Oversee the creation and distribution of marketing, recruitment, and communications materials, including news stories, newsletters, promotional content, and digital media. Manage and enhance the college website by ensuring timely, engaging, and accurate content while monitoring website performance and search engine optimization (SEO). Develop and implement communications strategies to support college events, student recruitment initiatives, and strategic priorities in collaboration with internal stakeholders. Manage communications and recruitment projects by coordinating timelines, facilitating stakeholder collaboration, and ensuring successful project completion. Build and maintain collaborative relationships with university partners to promote college programs, events, and initiatives. Supervise communications staff, interns, and student employees while fostering a collaborative and creative work environment. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and four years of experience related to media, communications, and/or marketing services; or a high school diploma/equivalent and eight years of related experience. (Note: a combination of post high school education and experience equal to eight years.) Preferred Qualifications Strong writing, editing, and verbal communication skills. Experience in communication, recruitment, and event management. Strong working knowledge of Adobe Creative Suite (Photoshop, Illustrator, InDesign) and photo/video editing tools. Experience supervising staff and/or student employees. Experience managing social media accounts for an organization. Experience with web content management systems and SEO best practices. Contact Info Melissa Powell Director, Office of Strategic Outreach & Recruitment University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range The anticipated starting salary for this position is in the $50,000s, commensurate with education and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63557&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Service Desk Fall Pool", "description": "Job Title Service Desk Fall Pool Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63557 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Information Technology Services (ITS) The ITS Service Desk is the first point of contact for students, faculty, staff, and constituents of the University when associated with requesting and receiving support for technologies provided by ITS. Responsibilities This position helps ensure that ITS support and service requests are properly managed by ITS service providers and their staff. Answer inbound calls, resolve basic IT issues using Case Management Guidelines. Qualifications High school diploma or equivalent. Preferred Qualifications Customer Service experience and Time Management Skills. Helpful Who is an ideal candidate for this position? Self-starter, ability to follow instructions; ability to work in a structured work environment. Exceptional customer service and time management skills. What is a typical day in this position? Answer inbound calls via a call center environment, manage Cases to resolution and be a team player. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an OPS/temporary job. Based on the duties, this position may require completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63545&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried (Cognitive Neuroscience)", "description": "Job Title Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried (Cognitive Neuroscience) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63545 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Psychology | College of Arts and Sciences Responsibilities Responsibilities include teaching and mentoring undergraduate and graduate students, conducting and publishing research in cognitive neuroscience, and providing service to the department through work on committees. Qualifications PhD in Psychology, Neuroscience, Cognitive Science or related disciplines. Candidates must have a strong research program with a high likelihood of obtaining extramural funding and the potential for excellent teaching and mentorship. Preferred Qualifications Expertise in network-based functional magnetic resonance imaging (fMRI). Examination of the brain and cognition across the lifespan. Other Information The Psychology Department faculty is very active in research, with Ph.D. programs in cognition and cognitive neuroscience, neuroscience, social, clinical, and developmental psychology. FSU has a state-of-the-art research-dedicated MRI center featuring a 3T Siemens Prisma scanner, an MR-compatible high-density EEG system, MR- compatible TMS and tES systems, and peripheral equipment. Florida State ranks in the top 25 of National Public Universities (U. S. News & World Report). Contact Info Inquiries about the position may be directed to Derek Nee , search chair. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Application review will begin on September 30, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63544&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried (Clinical Psychology)", "description": "Job Title Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried (Clinical Psychology) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63544 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Psychology | College of Arts and Sciences Responsibilities The Department of Psychology at Florida State University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor in Clinical Psychology with a start date in August 2027. Area of specialization and research is open. Responsibilities will include conducting and publishing research in Clinical Psychology, teaching and mentoring undergraduate and graduate students, and providing service to the department through work on committees. Qualifications A doctoral degree in Clinical Psychology or closely related field is required. The successful candidate will demonstrate a strong research program, high likelihood of obtaining extramural funding, potential for excellence in teaching undergraduate and graduate students, and the ability to train graduate students in our APA-accredited Clinical Psychology program. Candidates with lines of research in any area of Clinical Psychology are encouraged to apply. Other Information FSU is classified as a Carnegie R1 (Very High Research Activity) institution and ranks in the top 25 of National Public Universities (U.S. News & World Report). The Department of Psychology faculty pursue active programs of research, producing high-impact findings and mentoring students in Ph.D. programs in clinical, social, and developmental psychology, as well as cognition/cognitive neuroscience and neuroscience. The department has an outstanding research infrastructure, with each faculty member having a dedicated laboratory suite, and a fully-staffed electronics and machine shop. FSU has a state-of-the-art research-dedicated MRI center featuring a 3T Siemens Prisma scanner, an MR-compatible high-density EEG system, MR-compatible TMS and tES systems, as well as peripheral equipment. Faculty have access to core equipment and resources (e.g., a confocal microscope and common-use histology/molecular laboratory in the building and numerous other shared resources across the department and campus). The department has a highly favorable teaching load and a collegial atmosphere. FSU is located in beautiful Tallahassee, the capital of Florida where it offers an exceptional quality of life with the amenities of a vibrant college town and the friendliness and accessibility of a close-knit community. The city combines affordable housing and highly regarded schools with short commute times and minimal traffic. Tallahassee also has a vibrant scene, with live music throughout the city and nationally recognized performers and productions brought to the community through Florida State University\u2019s Opening Nights and the Adderley Amphitheater at Cascades Park. Residents also have access to an abundance of regional springs, lakes, and rivers, an extensive trail system, and pristine beaches in the Gulf. Contact Info Inquiries about this position may be directed to Rick Macatee , Search Chair. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Please submit the following: (1) cover letter (2-page maximum), (2) curriculum vitae, (3) research statement (3-page maximum), (4) teaching statement (3-page maximum), (5) up to four peer-reviewed papers, and (6) names and contact information for 3 letters of recommendation. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Application review will begin on October 20, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63540&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried (Neuroscience)", "description": "Job Title Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried (Neuroscience) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63540 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Psychology | College of Arts and Sciences Responsibilities The Department of Psychology at Florida State University seeks to hire a tenure-track Assistant Professor in Behavioral/Systems/Computational Neuroscience, with a start date in August 2027. Responsibilities will include conducting and publishing research in Neuroscience, teaching and mentoring undergraduate and graduate students, and providing service to the department through work on committees. Qualifications Ph.D. or the highest degree appropriate from an accredited institution in Neuroscience or a related field. In addition, candidates must have a strong research program with a high likelihood of obtaining extramural funding and the potential for excellent teaching and mentoring. Candidates with lines of laboratory research in any area of Neuroscience are encouraged to apply. Preference will be given to applicants whose research programs synergize with existing departmental strengths in chemosensation, learning and memory, social behavior, neuroendocrinology, and the neurobiology of motivated behavior. Helpful For more information about our department visit the Psychology website, and for the Neuroscience program visit the Neuroscience website. Contact Info Inquiries about the position may be directed to Adam Dewan , Search Chair. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. The following are required with the application: Cover letter Curriculum vitae Research statement (maximum 2 pages) Teaching statement (maximum 1 page) List (with online access links) highlighting up to four peer-reviewed papers Names and contact information for three references who can provide letters of recommendation Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Application review will begin on October 30, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63484&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried (Statistics)", "description": "Job Title Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried (Statistics) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63484 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Statistics | College of Arts and Sciences Responsibilities The Department of Statistics at Florida State University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position starting in August 2027. The position provides an opportunity for engagement with our large undergraduate program and vibrant M.S. and Ph.D. programs in Biostatistics, Data Science, and Statistics. The successful candidate will join a faculty with research expertise including machine learning, high dimensional data, network analysis, survival and longitudinal analysis, Bayesian analysis, shape/object data analysis, causality and data privacy, to name a few ( our website ), in a collaborative environment at a comprehensive, Carnegie R1 University. Responsibilities include teaching graduate and undergraduate courses, conducting research, and student mentoring. Qualifications A Doctoral degree from an accredited institution in Biostatistics, Data Science, Statistics, or a related field with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching and academic research is required. Candidates with research areas in Biostatistics, Data Science, Statistics or related fields are encouraged to apply. Contact Info For questions about our hiring process, please contact Pamela McGhee . University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. This position requires that you submit statements on research and on teaching and have at least three confidential professional letters of recommendation submitted on your behalf. Follow the steps below to request these letters through our system: 1) After submitting your application, click the Careers link; 2) Click the My References link; 3) Click the Send/View Reference Request button next to the appropriate position; and 4) Follow the steps on that page to send your references a system generated email requesting they submit a letter of recommendation on your behalf. You may also return to the My References link and click on \"Send/View Reference Request\" to see if your references have responded, add additional references, or resend requests. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . The deadline for applications is November 13, 2026. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=60308&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "OPS Laboratory Assistant (Medicine Biomedical Sciences) Medicine", "description": "Job Title OPS Laboratory Assistant (Medicine Biomedical Sciences) Medicine Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 60308 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department College of Medicine, Medicine Biomedical Sciences Responsibilities Responsible for performing scientific experiments under the direction of the principal investigator related to immunology, infectious diseases, biochemistry, and structural biology. Instructs lab members in procedures and operation of laboratory equipment and lab safety. Responsible for performing independent laboratory research, to include designing and performing biochemical and immunological assays at the bench, taking detailed notes of experimental procedures, analyzing experimental data, writing research reports and manuscripts, and helping the PI prepare research proposals for grant applications. Analyzes existing methodologies, formulates hypotheses and develops new protocols. Responsible for maintaining accurate and complete laboratory notebooks and research reports, managing the PI\u2019s grant accounts, ordering supplies and reagents, generating monthly expense reports on personnel and lab purchases, and assisting in the general management of the lab including routine cleaning and maintenance of all lab equipment, training new personnel, and supervising lab members assigned by the PI. Manages the day to day lab environment, including individual lab member duties. Qualifications A bachelor\u2019s degree or higher (Ph.D., M.D., ScD., D.V.M., etc.) in an appropriate field is required. Preferred Qualifications Excellent scientific writing ability and strong oral communication skills. The ability to work effectively and collegially with colleagues. Two years of experience working in a laboratory environment. Prior experience working with rodent animal models. Contact Info Dr. Jarrod Mousa University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://jobs.fsu.edu. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an OPS/temporary job. This position is being readvertised. Previous applicants need not reapply. Based on the duties, this position may require completion of a criminal history background check . This is a full-time role, listed as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=62817&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "OPS Testing Center Support, Office of Accessibility Services - Fall 2026", "description": "Job Title OPS Testing Center Support, Office of Accessibility Services - Fall 2026 Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 62817 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Office of Accessibility Services | Department of Student Support & Transitions Responsibilities The responsibilities include directing visitors, answering and managing incoming calls, handling inquiries, and providing administrative support to various departments. The position will be primarily testing and transportation support. Qualifications High school diploma/equivalent. Preferred Qualifications This role requires a professional and courteous demeanor, excellent communications skills, and the ability to manage multiple tasks efficiently. Preference for graduate students. Contact Info Amber Wagner Director of the Office of Accessibility Services / Assistant Dean of Students 850-644-9566 DOS_OAS_Admin@fsu.edu University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an OPS/temporary job. Based on the duties, this position may require completion of a criminal history background check . This position's schedule is M-F, 8 AM - 5 PM. This position is being re-advertised. Previous applicants need not reapply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=62316&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Research Engineer, Level II-VI - (Machine Shop - National High Magnetic Field Laboratory)", "description": "Job Title Research Engineer, Level II-VI - (Machine Shop - National High Magnetic Field Laboratory) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 62316 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department National High Magnetic Field Laboratory Join the world-renowned National High Magnetic Field Laboratory at Florida State University (FSU) and support groundbreaking scientific discovery in a collaborative, high-tech environment. FSU was recently recognized as one of America\u2019s Best-in-State Employers for its strong workplace culture and employee-centered values. Responsibilities This position supervises the daily operations of the MagLab\u2019s prototype machine shop that works in close collaboration with designers, engineers, and technical staff to develop advanced, one of a kind mechanical components and assemblies. The role leads the integration of machining, prototyping, and design iteration to enable innovative research tools and push the boundaries of what is possible in support of laboratory scientists and users. Machining & Prototype Fabrication Leadership Lead machining and prototype fabrication activities to ensure quality, precision, and safety. Manage fabrication requests and ensure compliance with engineering and documentation standards. Support CNC programming, troubleshooting, testing, and custom prototype development. Collaborate with researchers and stakeholders to deliver fabrication solutions. Operations, Equipment & Resource Management Oversee shop operations, scheduling, resource allocation, and long-term planning. Manage equipment, tooling, inventory, maintenance, and procurement activities. Maintain budgets, job priorities, and operational records. Ensure fabrication technologies and practices align with industry standards. Team Leadership & Workforce Development Supervise, coach, and evaluate machinists to promote safety and performance. Manage work assignments, productivity, quality, and compliance. Provide technical guidance for complex projects and initiatives. Foster collaboration and support organizational values. Engineering Collaboration & Project Coordination Serve as the liaison between machinists, engineers, researchers, and project teams. Coordinate project schedules, communication, and execution. Review designs for machinability, safety, quality, and compliance. Strengthen integration between design, engineering, and fabrication functions. Training, Safety & Continuous Improvement Lead training programs on machining, equipment operation, and safe work practices. Develop and maintain technical and safety training for laboratory personnel. Support and advance laboratory safety initiatives and programs. Promote continuous learning, innovation, and process improvement. Research Support & External Engagement Support scientific research through advanced fabrication and engineering solutions. Collaborate with external users, visiting scientists, and research partners. Contribute to outreach efforts that advance the laboratory's mission and impact. Qualifications A Bachelor's degree and three years of experience; or a high school diploma or equivalent and seven years of experience. (Note: post-high school education may substitute for experience at the equivalent rate.) Additional experience qualifies candidates for higher-level consideration (III\u2013VI). Each level requires three additional years of experience. Helpful What You Gain at FSU Opportunity to work at a world-renowned national research laboratory. Meaningful contributions to scientific discovery and student learning. A collaborative environment that values your expertise and invests in your growth. Contact Info For additional information, please contact Kayla West . University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. Anticipated Salary Range Level II \u2013 Mid $60,000\u2019s, commensurate with education and experience. Level III \u2013 Mid $70,000\u2019s, commensurate with education and experience. Level IV \u2013 Mid $80,000\u2019s, commensurate with education and experience. Level V \u2013 High $90,000\u2019s, commensurate with education and experience. Level VI \u2013 Low $110,000\u2019s, commensurate with education and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our interactive too l to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://jobs.fsu.edu. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position is being advertised as open until filled. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63535&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried (Paleobiology/Geobiology)", "description": "Job Title Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried (Paleobiology/Geobiology) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63535 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Earth, Ocean & Atmospheric Science l College of Arts & Sciences Responsibilities The Department of Earth, Ocean & Atmospheric Science (EOAS) at Florida State University (FSU) seeks a full-time tenure-track faculty member in the field of Paleobiology/Geobiology at the Assistant Professor level. Successful candidates will investigate the coevolution of life and environment with implications for planetary habitability of Earth and exoplanets, biosignatures for life (radiations and extinctions), and modern implications. Some of the research areas of interest include but are not limited to: paleobiology, geobiology, extinction dynamics, paleoecology, paleontology, biotic responses to global change, and biogeochemistry. The appointee is expected to develop and maintain a vigorous externally funded research program and contribute to the undergraduate and graduate programs by teaching Earth History and Paleontology and providing experiential learning experiences. Qualifications Candidates must hold a Doctoral degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in Earth Science or a related field with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Other Information EOAS is housed in a recent building (2020) with state-of-the-art facilities and laboratories, has approximately 35 faculty members and 110 graduate students, and offers undergraduate and/or graduate degrees in Geology, Meteorology, Oceanography, and Environmental Sciences. Please visit the EOAS website for additional information. Contact Info Inquiries may be addressed to the Search Committee or the Search Committee Chair, Dr. Seth Young . University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applicants should submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statements of research and teaching interests, and contact information for at least three references. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Review of applications will begin November 2, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63474&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Open Rank Professor, 9 Month Salaried (Department of Chemical & Biomedical Engineering Florida A&M University\u2013Florida State University College of Engineering)", "description": "Job Title Open Rank Professor, 9 Month Salaried (Department of Chemical & Biomedical Engineering Florida A&M University\u2013Florida State University College of Engineering) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63474 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The Department of Chemical & Biomedical Engineering (CBE) at the Florida A&M University (FAMU)\u2013Florida State University (FSU) College of Engineering invites applications from highly qualified individuals for a tenure track faculty position in biomedical engineering, in the city of Tallahassee, Florida. Responsibilities Successful candidates are expected to develop research programs that are internationally recognized with significant and sustained funding, incorporate interdisciplinary collaboration with researchers across campus, and demonstrate a strong commitment to excellence in education. Teaching undergraduate and graduate courses and supervising undergraduate, graduate, and post-doctoral researchers are expected. Qualifications Candidates must possess an earned Ph.D. in biomedical engineering, chemical engineering, or a related discipline, and demonstrate documented potential for outstanding research. Although all applications will be reviewed, priority will be given to candidates that complement and build upon our research in polymeric biomaterials, regenerative medicine, and 3D bioprinting with a goal of aligning with the new FSU Health Initiative. Areas of particular interest include stem cell engineering, nanoparticle engineering, gene editing, immunomodulation, biomaterials, and biomedical imaging. Helpful The FAMU-FSU College of Engineering is the nexus of two major public universities, each with a distinct mission but focused on world-class engineering education and research. Created by the Florida Legislature in 1982, the joint organization is the college of engineering for both Florida A&M and Florida State universities. This unique combination of focus, resources and mission from our parent university has created on our campus a truly innovative atmosphere that leverages the benefits of the traditional HBCU model with the innovations of an R1 public research university. The College fosters interdisciplinary research and collaboration across engineering, science, medicine, and other fields, while providing faculty, researchers, and students access to the complementary expertise and resources of both universities. All seven of the college\u2019s eligible undergraduate degree programs are accredited by the Engineering Accreditation Commission of ABET . Contact Info Questions about the position should be directed to Dr. Tristan Driscoll, Search Committee Chair, at tdriscoll2@eng.famu.fsu.edu. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include the following documents: A cover letter A full curriculum vitae A 2 to 3-page research statement. This statement should clearly indicate how the proposed research efforts will connect to other efforts in the Department and universities. A one-page teaching statement No more than four selected publications for review The names and contact information of four potential references Faculty Information CBE has a dynamic group of faculty members actively involved in research encompassing various areas of chemical engineering, materials science and engineering, and biomedical engineering. The department has seen major expansion in the graduate and undergraduate biomedical and chemical engineering education and research activities since the establishment of an undergraduate BME degree in 2019 through the hiring of 15 new faculty members and approximately doubling of the graduate and undergraduate enrollment. The expanding college of engineering has increased research expenditures by 195% over the last 5 years ($87.6M in FY2025) and is continuing to grow its faculty and campus. A new research facility (the Interdisciplinary Research and Commercialization Building) was completed in Spring of 2025, and an additional engineering building was recently funded by the state legislature. Our nationally recognized and award-winning faculty members have access to state-of-the-art laboratories for research in biomedical and chemical engineering and the two programs are closely integrated in research and education. In addition to present faculty at the FAMU-FSU College of Engineering and its associated research centers, successful candidates will have many opportunities to interact and collaborate at both universities (including the FSU College of Medicine, the National High Magnetic Field Laboratory, and the FAMU College of Pharmacy). Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Application review will begin on November 1, 2026. Acceptance and review of applications will continue until the position is filled. The appointment is anticipated to begin in August 2027. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63542&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Research Faculty - 12 Month Salaried (Open Rank) - Bioinformatics and Proteomics Software Development (NHMFL)", "description": "Job Title Research Faculty - 12 Month Salaried (Open Rank) - Bioinformatics and Proteomics Software Development (NHMFL) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63542 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Ion Cyclotron Resonance (ICR) Program, National High Magnetic Field Laboratory (NHMFL). The NHMFL is operated for the National Science Foundation by a collaboration of institutions comprising Florida State University, the University of Florida, and Los Alamos National Laboratory and houses the world\u2019s premier ICR laboratory, with state-of-the-art FT-ICR mass spectrometers that operate at 21 T, 14.5 T, 9.4 T, and 9.4 T, for research in chemistry, materials science, engineering, geochemistry, biochemistry, and biology. Current areas include natural organic matter, emerging environmental contaminants, biofuels, top-down proteomics, lipidomics, metabolomics, and mass spectrometry imaging. Responsibilities The ICR Program seeks a research faculty member with expertise in bioinformatics, computational mass spectrometry, and scientific software development. The successful candidate will collaborate with researchers in the ICR Program to develop, implement, and validate novel algorithms for the analysis of high-resolution mass spectrometry data, with particular emphasis on top-down proteomics, de novo sequencing, proteoform characterization, and related applications in metabolomics and lipidomics. The candidate will contribute to the design of software tools and computational workflows for processing data generated by state-of-the-art FT-ICR and Orbitrap mass spectrometers. The candidate is expected to collaborate with NHMFL staff, graduate students, postdoctoral fellows, and external users; publish manuscripts; present at scientific conferences; and contribute to applications for external research funding. Additional responsibilities include maintaining software resources, supporting users with computational aspects of their projects, and helping to establish robust and reproducible data analysis pipelines for the ICR user community. Qualifications Candidates are expected to have a Ph.D. in Bioinformatics, Computer Science, Computational Biology, Analytical Chemistry, Data Science, or a closely related STEM field, along with experience conducting interdisciplinary research in a collaborative environment. For the Research Faculty I level, 2-5 years of additional experience in these areas is required. For the rank of Research Faculty II or III, 6-9 or 10+ years, respectively, of additional experience is required. The successful candidate must have demonstrated expertise in software development and scientific programming in Python, including the ability to independently design, implement, test, and maintain research software, scientific algorithms, and computational workflows. Candidates should have a record of scholarly achievement through peer-reviewed publications, software development, or other research accomplishments and experience analyzing large, complex biological datasets. Applicants must demonstrate experience developing computational tools through peer-reviewed software publications, publicly available software packages, GitHub repositories, or equivalent evidence of software development. Preferred Qualifications Desired qualifications include experience with mass spectrometry-based proteomics, metabolomics, lipidomics, or related omics disciplines; development of algorithms and software for scientific data analysis; database searching and identification workflows for proteins, peptides, metabolites, or other biomolecules; and quantitative analysis of biological datasets. Experience applying artificial intelligence, machine learning, graph-based methods, pattern recognition, or statistical modeling to biological data is highly desirable. Additional experience with de novo sequencing, computational mass spectrometry, high-performance computing, and open-source software development is preferred. Familiarity with mass spectrometry data formats, computational workflows for high-resolution mass spectrometry, and the development of reproducible and well-documented software tools is desirable. Contact Info Kristina Hakansson , ICR Director, khakansson@magnet.fsu.edu Kayla West , NHMFL HR Director University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63506&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Head Coach - Middle School Girls Basketball (Part-time, OPS)", "description": "Job Title Head Coach - Middle School Girls Basketball (Part-time, OPS) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63506 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Florida State University Schools Responsibilities Florida State University Schools (Florida High) is seeking a dedicated and student-centered Middle School Girls Basketball Head Coach to lead and grow our middle school Girls Basketball program. The MS Girls Basketball Head Coach will be responsible for fostering a positive, competitive, and developmentally appropriate environment that emphasizes sportsmanship, academic accountability, and athletic excellence. This position reports directly to the Athletic Director and is expected to uphold all FSUS, FHSAA, and FSU policies and procedures while supporting the mission and values of Florida High Athletics. Lead and supervise all aspects of the MS Girls Basketball program Plan and conduct practices, conditioning sessions, and skill development activities Develop training plans that promote athlete safety, technical development, and competitive growth Schedule contests in accordance with guidelines and school policies Monitor and support student-athlete academic progress and eligibility Establish effective communication with student-athletes, parents, administration, and staff Coordinate game logistics, transportation, and supervision in alignment with FSUS policies Promote the program through school communication, social media, and community engagement Organize team events, awards, and end-of-season recognition Manage equipment, uniforms, filed needs, and program inventory Ensure compliance with rules, district regulations, and FSUS clearance procedures Assist with off-season development, camps, clinics, and program growth initiatives Collaborate with youth and feeder programs to strengthen the long-term success of the MS Girls Basketball program Qualifications High School Diploma or equivalent Valid State of Florida Coaching Certificate (or ability to obtain) Current certifications in CPR, First Aid, Concussion in Sports, and Sudden Cardiac Arrest (required prior to season) Experience working with children and young adults in an educational or athletic setting Strong organizational, leadership, and communication skills Preferred Qualifications Previous basketball coaching experience at the middle school, high school, club, or collegiate level Knowledge of rules and interscholastic athletics Playing experience at the high school, collegiate, or professional level College coursework or degree in Education, Kinesiology, Sports Management, or a related field Experience with player development, team management, and program building Other Information We proudly serve as a laboratory K-12 school, blending the rigors of academic achievement with a commitment to educational research and innovation. We draw upon the resources of a world-class university, bringing cutting-edge practices and insights directly into our classrooms. This dynamic approach ensures that our students benefit from the latest advancements in pedagogy and fosters an environment were curiosity and exploration are celebrated. Florida State University Schools is not just a place of learning; it's a community dedicated to empowering the leaders of tomorrow. We invite you to explore the possibilities at FSUS and join us on a journey of academic excellence, personal growth, and a commitment to making a positive impact on the world. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an OPS/Temporary job. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check , including a fingerprint-based screening via AHCA\u2019s Clearinghouse pursuant to Section 1012, Florida Statutes, for positions in a FSU Developmental Research School or Section 409.175, Florida Statutes, for positions in a Childcare or Summer Camp position. Visit the AHCA Clearinghouse Screenings webpage for more information. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63490&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried (Data Science & AI)", "description": "Job Title Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried (Data Science & AI) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63490 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Computer Science | College of Arts & Sciences Responsibilities The Department of Computer Science at the Florida State University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position to begin in August 2027. This position is 9-month, full-time, and benefits eligible. We seek strong candidates in the theory, applications, or systems of AI and Data Science. We will also consider outstanding candidates in related areas. Outstanding applicants in other areas will also be considered. Responsibilities will include teaching, research, and service activities. Qualifications Applicants should hold a Doctoral degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of Computer Science or closely related field and have a demonstrated record of scholarly accomplishments. Other Information The department currently has 31 tenure-track and 7 specialized faculty members and offers BS, MS, and PhD degrees, including an AI Concentration, a new MS in CyberAI, and a new BS in AI. The department is an NSA/DHS Center of Academic Excellence in Cyber Defense Education (CAE/CDE) and Research (CAE-R). FSU is classified as a Carnegie R1: Doctoral Universities \u2013 Very High Research Activity and is ranked No. 17 among public universities in TIME\u2019S America\u2019s Best Colleges list. Its primary role is to serve as a center for advanced graduate and professional studies, with an emphasis on research and excellence in undergraduate education. Contact Info Questions can be emailed to Prof. Xiuwen Liu , Faculty Search Committee Chair. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Please include a curriculum vitae and statements of teaching and research philosophy with the online application. This position requires that you have three confidential professional letters of recommendation submitted on your behalf. Follow the steps below to request these letters through our system: 1) After submitting your application, click the Careers link; 2) Click the My References link; 3) Click the Send/View Reference Request button next to the appropriate position; and 4) Follow the steps on that page to send your references a system generated email requesting they submit a letter of recommendation on your behalf Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. Application review will begin on December 15, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63482&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Director of Development, College of Medicine", "description": "Job Title Director of Development, College of Medicine Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63482 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department FSU Division of University Advancement Florida State University is currently in the leadership phase of a comprehensive campaign. As the leadership phase of the campaign begins, the Division of University Advancement is accelerating the hiring of additional development officers\u2019 campus-wide and is excited to build out its team. For Advancement professionals who are interested in being a part of a comprehensive campaign from the beginning for their career development, the timing is ideal to join our team. Responsibilities The Director of Development will strategically execute a personal solicitation program resulting in philanthropic support by maximizing the identification, cultivation, solicitation and stewardship of prospects for gifts at the $100,000 and up level for College of Medicine. This individual will secure, on an annual basis, private support at the major and principal gift level and will be responsible for identification of potential major and principal gift prospects. The Director of Development will be expected to uphold and exemplify the operating practices of the Division of University Advancement while raising philanthropic dollars in support of the mission of Florida State University. Works with the Dean, and the other members of the College of Medicine development, communication and alumni team to develop and execute strategic fundraising initiatives on behalf of the College and the university. Develops, coordinates, and executes an annual major gift plan, implementing fund-raising activities designed to meet an established monetary goal while also hitting a set suite of metrics. Establishes new relationships resulting in philanthropic investment, maintains existing relationships, which may generate new philanthropic investments, and provides prospect/donor-related assessments and feedback for the College and the Division of University Advancement. Identifies, qualifies and sustains a donor prospect portfolio with individuals who have a giving capacity of $500,000 or more. Travels frequently, and secures gifts and pledges from alumni, parents, faculty, staff, and friends of FSU. Exhibits and promotes a comprehensive understanding of the philanthropic priorities of the College, effectively matching the specific interests of prospects to those needs. Plans for and initiates direct activities with prospects that are designed to enhance the affiliation between the prospect and FSU. Effectively communicates FSU\u2019s mission and represents FSU\u2019s culture to external stakeholders. Central Development Collaboration Coordinates with the Division of University Advancement colleagues to identify prospects for planned giving, corporate and foundation giving in partnership with the Office of University Research, and principal giving in partnership with the Principal Gifts Team. Protects confidential information. Perform other related duties as required and assigned. Administrative/Events Assists in the facilitation of meetings, communications, informational exchanges and project / philanthropic coordination with the faculty and faculty chairs. Prepares proposals and gift agreements as required for proper gift documentation. Prepares correspondence with prospects and documents communications, solicitation activity and gift information in compliance with the FSU Foundation\u2019s reporting guidelines. Creates, inspires, and maintains donor loyalty, interest and enthusiasm through stewardship communication and activities designed to express recognition, appreciation and the impact of their gift(s). Implementation of such a stewardship plan may include but should not be limited to letters, communication of unit or university initiatives, invitations to appropriate activities, meetings, events, student engagement or the facilitation of campus visits. Board/Volunteer Management Assists in the management of all volunteer boards associated with the College of Medicine. Qualifications Master's degree and four years of experience in a related advancement field or a Bachelor's degree and six years of related experience. Higher education can substitute for experience at a comparable rate. A valid Florida Driver's License or the ability to obtain upon hire. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. This role requires driving and travel. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63491&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Open Rank Professor, 9 Month Salaried (Data Science & AI)", "description": "Job Title Open Rank Professor, 9 Month Salaried (Data Science & AI) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63491 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Computer Science | College of Arts & Sciences Responsibilities The Department of Computer Science at Florida State University invites applications for a tenure-track open rank Professor position to begin in August 2027. The position is 9-month, full-time, and eligible for benefits. Focus areas include Machine Learning Systems, Foundation Models, and Multi-Agent Systems, as well as supporting domains for AI, such as Big Data Engineering, Edge Computing and Sensor Networks, High-Performance Computing, and Human-Computer Interaction. We will also consider outstanding candidates in related areas. Qualifications A doctoral degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in Computer Science or closely related field with demonstrated record of achievement in teaching and academic research is required. Candidates with outstanding academic credentials commensurate with tenured Associate or Full Professors are encouraged. Candidates at this level will be expected to have the experience and expertise to lead a cutting-edge research group. Other Information The department currently has 31 tenure-track and 7 specialized faculty members and offers BS, MS, and PhD degrees, including an AI Concentration, a new MS in CyberAI, and a new BS in AI. The department is an NSA/DHS Center of Academic Excellence in Cyber Defense Education (CAE/CDE) and Research (CAE-R). FSU is classified as a Carnegie R1: Doctoral Universities \u2013 Very High Research Activity and is ranked No. 17 among public universities in TIME\u2019S America\u2019s Best Colleges list. Its primary role is to serve as a center for advanced graduate and professional studies, with an emphasis on research and excellence in undergraduate education. Contact Info Questions can be emailed to Prof. Xiuwen Liu , Faculty Search Committee Chair. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Please include a curriculum vitae and statements of teaching and research philosophy with the online application. This position requires that you have three confidential professional letters of recommendation submitted on your behalf. Follow the steps below to request these letters through our system: 1) After submitting your application, click the Careers link; 2) Click the My References link; 3) Click the Send/View Reference Request button next to the appropriate position; and 4) Follow the steps on that page to send your references a system generated email requesting they submit a letter of recommendation on your behalf Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. Application review will begin on December 15, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63480&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried (Latin American History)", "description": "Job Title Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried (Latin American History) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63480 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of History | College of Arts & Sciences Responsibilities The Department of History at Florida State University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in the history of Latin America to begin August 2027. The area and period of specialization are open. The successful candidate will be expected to work with the department\u2019s undergraduate and graduate students, supervise PhD candidates, and teach two courses per semester. Qualifications Doctoral degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization required. Contact Info Any questions about the position should be directed to Dr. Anasa Hicks . University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applicants must include a cover letter and curriculum vitae. The application deadline is November 2, 2026. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Please note that semifinalists will be required to arrange for three confidential letters of recommendation and to submit a writing sample, (e.g. chapter, article, etc.). Only completed applications will be considered. Semifinalists will be interviewed via Zoom. Finalists will be invited to campus to present their research. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63505&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "OPS-Office Support (Full-Time)- FIN", "description": "Job Title OPS-Office Support (Full-Time)- FIN Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63505 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Through FIN , the FSU Learning Systems Institute collaborates with districts and schools to provide customized services and supports ensuring that all students with disabilities have the same educational, social, and future opportunities as their peers. FIN services and resources include (1) district capacity-building, (2) school-based planning, implementation, and support, (3) on-demand, web-based resources and products, and (4) family support and information. Responsibilities Serves as Office Support Specialist to FIN at Learning Systems Institute for students with disabilities (SWD) Staff: Provides coordination of travel activities for all team members to meet the needs of educational stakeholders across the State of Florida. Serves as one of the travel representatives for the team, processes and submits all travel requests, gathers documentation and submits travel reimbursement. Makes all necessary travel arrangements to include hotels, flights, car rentals as needed for faculty and staff in accordance with FSU policies and procedures. Ensures travel arrangements and reimbursements are processed in a timely manner. Responsible for assisting in the purchasing, shipping and distribution of supplies. Qualifications High school diploma/equivalency and two years experience; or a combination of post-high school education and experience equal to four years. Preferred Qualifications Experience communicating effectively verbally and in writing. Experience establishing and maintaining effective working relationships. Experience gathering, interpreting, reporting, and/or editing information. Experience performing basic mathematical calculations. Experience prioritizing, organizing, and performing multiple work assignments simultaneously. Knowledge of applicable computer applications and basic computer functions. Contact Info FIN Network Email- lsi-finadmin@fsu.edu University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range This position pays $19.00/hr. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an OPS/temporary job. Based on the duties, this position may require completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63477&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar (OPS) - Experimental, Modeling and Simulations of Magnetic Separations of Critical Materials (NHMFL)", "description": "Job Title Postdoctoral Scholar (OPS) - Experimental, Modeling and Simulations of Magnetic Separations of Critical Materials (NHMFL) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63477 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department National High Magnetic Field Laboratory Responsibilities A postdoctoral position is available for highly motivated candidates to join a multi-disciplinary group of chemical engineers, physicists, chemists, and geochemists at the Florida State University (FSU) and the National High Magnetic Field Laboratory (NHMFL). The project will involve experiments, modeling and simulations of critical metals fluids under influence of magnetic fields. The candidate selected is expected to conduct research on the experiments and modeling of a range of separation strategies for recovery of critical materials from industrial waste. The initial appointment will be for one year, with renewal for up to two additional years conditional upon performance and availability of funding. Qualifications PhD in Engineering and/or Physics or relevant discipline. Experience in computational fluid dynamics, magnet design and actuation, experimental micro/macro fluidics, colloidal science, and separation processes. Experience with instrument design and/or automation experience. Team player with leadership, communication, and presentation skills. A track record of quality publications with excellent writing skills is essential. Applicants should hold a PhD in chemical engineering, mechanical engineering, physics, or related fields, and have a strong background in chemical physics, experiments, flow visualizations, X-ray florescence, fluid dynamics, modeling, and simulations with COMSOL or other CFD platforms. Contact Info For information about this position, please contact Hadi Mohammadigoushki . University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Please include: CV A statement of research interests The names and contact information of three references Considerations This is an OPS/temporary job. Based on the duties, this position may require completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63504&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Teaching Faculty I, 9 Month Salaried (College of Social Work)", "description": "Job Title Teaching Faculty I, 9 Month Salaried (College of Social Work) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63504 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department College of Social Work Responsibilities The College of Social Work offers a collegial environment committed to maintaining a broad and supportive faculty community, supporting high quality and rigorous scholarship, and delivering high quality instruction. We invite applications for a 9-month, full-time, non-tenure track faculty position with opportunities for promotion and multi-year contracts. This position is fully on campus and in-person. Primary responsibilities include: Teaching and providing support to students in the BSW and MSW programs. Teaching a 4\u20134 course load (four courses in the Fall and four in the Spring), with opportunities to teach additional courses during the Summer term, depending on the need of the college. Engaging in college service and committee work as appropriate. Qualifications Master of Social Work from a CSWE-accredited program and two years of post-MSW clinical experience are required. Preferred Qualifications Preference will be given to candidates with teaching experience and Clinical Social Work (LCSW) licensure or an equivalent credential. Additional preference will be given to candidates who demonstrate the ability to build strong community relationships and teach across the social work curriculum. Candidates with a doctoral degree are encouraged to apply Contact Info Lisa Jackson, PhD, LCSW Faculty Search Committee College of Social Work lisa.a.jackson@fsu.edu University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applicants should submit (a) cover letter describing interest in social work field education, related experiences, and teaching philosophy (b) current curriculum vitae; (c) evidence of teaching effectiveness (including copies of teaching evaluations with date); and (d) three names and contact information of people willing to provide letters of reference. Letters of reference will be requested from top applicants at a later date. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is open until filled Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63459&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Beach Volleyball Head Coach (Part-time, OPS)", "description": "Job Title Beach Volleyball Head Coach (Part-time, OPS) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63459 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Part-Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Florida State University School Responsibilities Florida State University Schools (Florida High) is seeking a dedicated and student-centered Beach Volleyball Head Coach to lead and grow our middle school and high school beach volleyball program. The Beach Volleyball Head Coach will be responsible for fostering a positive, competitive, and developmentally appropriate environment that emphasizes sportsmanship, academic accountability, and athletic excellence. This position reports directly to the Athletic Director and is expected to uphold all FSUS, FHSAA, and FSU policies and procedures while supporting the mission and values of Florida High Athletics. Lead and supervise all aspects of the Beach Volleyball program (Middle School, JV, and Varsity Levels) Plan and conduct practices, conditioning sessions, and skill development activities Develop training plans that promote athlete safety, technical development, and competitive growth Schedule contests in accordance with guidelines and school policies Monitor and support student-athlete academic progress and eligibility Establish effective communication with student-athletes, parents, administration, and staff Coordinate game logistics, transportation, and supervision in alignment with FSUS policies Promote the program through school communication, social media, and community engagement Organize team events, awards, and end-of-season recognition Manage equipment, uniforms, field needs, and program inventory Ensure compliance with rules, district regulations, and FSUS clearance procedures Assist with off-season development, camps, clinics, and program growth initiatives Collaborate with youth and feeder programs to strengthen the long-term success of the beach volleyball program Qualifications High School Diploma or equivalent Valid State of Florida Coaching Certificate (or ability to obtain) Current certifications in CPR, First Aid, Concussion in Sports, and Sudden Cardiac Arrest (required prior to season) Experience working with children and young adults in an educational or athletic setting Strong organizational, leadership, and communication skills Preferred Qualifications Previous beach volleyball coaching experience at the middle school, high school, club, or collegiate level Knowledge of rules and interscholastic athletics Playing experience at the high school, collegiate, or professional level College coursework or degree in Education, Kinesiology, Sports Management, or a related field Experience with player development, team management, and program building Other Information We proudly serve as a laboratory K-12 school, blending the rigors of academic achievement with a commitment to educational research and innovation. We draw upon the resources of a world-class university, bringing cutting-edge practices and insights directly into our classrooms. This dynamic approach ensures that our students benefit from the latest advancements in pedagogy and fosters an environment where curiosity and exploration are celebrated. Florida State University Schools is not just a place of learning; it's a community dedicated to empowering the leaders of tomorrow. We invite you to explore the possibilities at FSUS and join us on a journey of academic excellence, personal growth, and a commitment to making a positive impact on the world. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an OPS/Temporary job. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check , including a fingerprint-based screening via AHCA\u2019s Clearinghouse pursuant to Section 1012, Florida Statutes, for positions in a FSU Developmental Research School or Section 409.175, Florida Statutes, for positions in a Childcare or Summer Camp position. Visit the AHCA Clearinghouse Screenings webpage for more information. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=62714&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Teaching Faculty - Undergrad Clinical-focused, 12 Month Salaried (multiple vacancies) - College of Nursing", "description": "Job Title Teaching Faculty - Undergrad Clinical-focused, 12 Month Salaried (multiple vacancies) - College of Nursing Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 62714 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department College of Nursing Join a nationally recognized leader in nursing education, known for research distinction and educational innovation. With simulation space in a brand new $126 million FSU Health building, $12 million to design a new building, and a transformative $10 million gift, the FSU College of Nursing is hiring additional faculty for strategic growth. Responsibilities The FSU College of Nursing is seeking to hire collaborative educators to teach in our in-person, on-campus undergraduate clinical-focused program, based in Tallahassee, Florida (FL). Responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Provide clinical nursing instruction in community health, pediatrics, or mental health. Promote student success through highly engaged teaching. Participate in planning, organizing, and developing curriculum. Supervise, evaluate, and mentor students. Appropriately document student progress in clinical sessions. Participate in and meaningfully contribute to departmental and team meetings. Provide academic service and educational excellence through courteous, informed, accessible, and professional engagement. Other duties as assigned. These roles focus on high-quality clinical instruction in the undergraduate nursing program and support the college\u2019s mission to prepare practice-ready, compassionate nurse leaders. Faculty are expected to be actively engaged in teaching, student mentorship and academic service in a collaborative, on-campus environment. For more information about our academic programs, visit our Academics page . Qualifications A Master's degree in nursing from an accredited institution. Active FL Registered Nurse (RN) or Advanced Practice Registered Nurse (APRN) license; or licensed in another state with eligibility to obtain FL licensure within 30 days of hire. Candidates must have relevant teaching experience in pediatrics, mental health, or community health. Preferred Qualifications Strong written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. Demonstrated ability to work well with students, faculty, and staff at all levels within a collaborative environment. Experience with Microsoft Word, Excel and Outlook or equivalent software. Experience supervising and training employees. Experience meeting project deadlines. PhD preferred. Contact Info Dr. Susan Baker , Associate Dean for Faculty Affairs University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our interactive too l to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://hr.fsu.edu/facultyjobs. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Please include the following documents in your application: Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae (CV) including a listing of courses developed and taught Teaching Philosophy, not to exceed two pages Samples of recent teaching evaluations, if applicable Please do not include reference letters with your application; they will be collected later in the recruiting process. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . These are full-time, in-person positions, and the level is commensurate with experience. Successful candidates must relocate to Tallahassee, Florida. Candidates must be willing to work a flexible schedule at multiple local sites. This position is being readvertised as open until filled. Previous applicants need not reapply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=59278&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Teaching Faculty I Adjunct - College of Nursing", "description": "Job Title Teaching Faculty I Adjunct - College of Nursing Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 59278 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department FSU College of Nursing Responsibilities Applicants must be able to work in all clinical settings of the program. Provide instruction, service and support in accordance with college policies and procedures. Be able to lead a group of 8-12 nursing students in a hospital setting, focusing on teaching and facilitating learning in accordance with course outcomes. Facilitate teaching and learning of nursing skills such as critical thinking, clinical judgment, assessments, interventions, and evaluations. Qualifications Minimum degree requirements include completion of a Master's Degree in Nursing or related discipline. Must have an active, unencumbered, RN license in the state of Florida or Georgia (multi-state compact license preferred). University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://hr.fsu.edu/facultyjobs. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Considerations This is an OPS/temporary job. Based on the duties, this position may require completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being readvertised. Previous applicants need not reapply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=62911&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "HR Specialist, Benefits (Retirement)", "description": "Job Title HR Specialist, Benefits (Retirement) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 62911 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Human Resources - Benefits Responsibilities This position is responsible for the administration of authorized retirement plans offered at the University including employee enrollments, changes and terminations of approved products. Responsible for the administration of the Florida Retirement System Pension and Investment Plans, the FICA Alternative Program, the Optional Retirement Program and tax-sheltered annuities. Includes but is not limited to enrollments, terminations, counseling, payroll queries, any employee/vendor inquiries and providing assistance to the Insurance team as needed. Responsible for coordinating and analyzing all queries, reports and files in preparation for each pay cycle. Assists with the coordination of leave payouts with the appropriate HR teams. Works with employees that are retiring and guides them on how to continue their benefits, such as retiree insurance. Responsible for working with the families of deceased employees. Includes but not limited to final pay and continuing benefits. Performs other related duties and responsibilities as required, such as but not limited to, assisting with the Benefits and Wellness Fair, Retirement Planning Seminar, New Faculty Orientation, the HR- Retirement Inbox, and maintaining compliance with F.S. 119 as required by the FRS. Provides assistance to the Insurance team as coverage and situation require. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and two years of experience in human resources or a related field or a high school diploma/equivalency and six years of the same experience. (Note: post high-school education and/or experience may substitute at a comparable rate.) Helpful The ideal candidate for this position is someone who has excellent customer service skills and the ability to communicate retirement options to new employees. The individual should also be a good problem-solver and remain calm under pressure. The ability to operate strategically and understand the small details that impact business operations is a plus. During the first 60-90 days, time will be spent getting up to speed on the State of Florida and FSU retirement plans and procedures. You will also engage with other key HR staff members and begin meeting retirement vendor representatives. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Starting in the mid $45,000s, commensurate with education and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. This position is being re-advertised. Previous applicants need not reapply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63464&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Research Faculty - Institute for Governance and Civics - 12 Month Salaried (Open Rank, Multiple Vacancies)", "description": "Job Title Research Faculty - Institute for Governance and Civics - 12 Month Salaried (Open Rank, Multiple Vacancies) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63464 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Institute for Governance and Civics Florida State University http://igc.fsu.edu Responsibilities The Institute for Governance and Civics at Florida State University seeks candidates for up to five Research Faculty positions (at any rank) whose work addresses the topic of constitutional, economic, conscience, or educational liberty, broadly defined. We are particularly interested in candidates who will help us build what we are calling America's Liberty Lab. The Liberty Lab is a distinctive program that sets the IGC apart nationally. It uses the methods of the hard sciences and social sciences to study liberty itself. Just as traditional labs test hypotheses through experimentation and data, the Liberty Lab will investigate where and how liberty thrives-and where it does not. The Lab will serve as a hub for: data collection and empirical analysis across our four pillars of liberty (constitutional liberty, economic liberty, conscience liberty, and educational liberty); original survey research and public opinion polling; field and natural experiments on policy and institutional design; and evaluation of real-world laws and regulations. We are particularly interested in researchers whose work addresses real policy outcomes. We expect research faculty to publish in academic outlets as well as write white papers and other work read by policy makers. The goal is to link topflight academic research with nonpartisan public policy discussions. We see candidates from a broad array of academic backgrounds, including (but not limited to): political science, psychology, economics, communications, public policy, history, religion, and more. The successful candidate will be expected to show a commitment to the mission of enhancing civic awareness as well as a readiness to contribute to the intellectual life and programmatic development of the IGC. Experience with cognitive experimental methods is not required but is a plus. Qualifications Completed Ph.D. by the date of hire. Research interests that contribute to the study of liberty and American civics. Potential for high impact publications. Commitment to the mission of enhancing civic awareness as well as a readiness to contribute to the intellectual life and programmatic development of the Institute for Governance and Civics. Contact Info Dr. Eric Olson, Economic Liberty Branch Head Institute for Governance and Civics Florida State University eo26c@fsu.edu University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Considerations This is a Faculty position. The position is being advertised as open rank and open until filled. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63466&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Teaching Faculty - Institute for Governance and Civics - 9 Month Salaried - (Open Rank, Multiple Vacancies)", "description": "Job Title Teaching Faculty - Institute for Governance and Civics - 9 Month Salaried - (Open Rank, Multiple Vacancies) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63466 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Institute for Governance and Civics Florida State University https://igc.fsu.edu Responsibilities The Institute for Governance and Civics at Florida State University seeks candidates for up to five Teaching Faculty positions (at any rank) to teach courses in our newly created Civics and Liberty Studies degree program. Our approach is what we are calling a renewed civic pragmatism. This interdisciplinary degree program consists of two parts. One part examines civic formation through the liberal arts. The other part focuses on social science. The program integrates classical and modern texts, empirical social science, legal analysis, and rhetorical training to develop thoughtful, data-informed, and ethically grounded civic leaders. We seek candidates from a broad array of academic backgrounds, including (but not limited to): political science, psychology, economics, communications, public policy, history, religion, philosophy, and more. The successful candidate will be expected to show a commitment to the mission of enhancing civic awareness as well as readiness to contribute to the intellectual life and programmatic development of the IGC. Qualifications Completed JD or Ph.D. by the date of hire. Research interests that contribute to the study of liberty and American civics. Potential for high impact publications. Commitment to the mission of enhancing civic awareness as well as a readiness to contribute to the intellectual life and programmatic development of the IGC. Contact Info Dr. Phillip Pinell, Teaching Faculty Institute for Governance and Civics Florida State University pp25n@fsu.edu University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position is being advertised as open until filled. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63467&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Open Rank Professor, 9 Month Salaried - School of Dance", "description": "Job Title Open Rank Professor, 9 Month Salaried - School of Dance Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63467 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department School of Dance Responsibilities Teaching and Student Mentorship Teach undergraduate and graduate courses in lighting design, visual design, projection design, stage technology, and related areas of expertise. Develop and teach elective courses aligned with the candidate's specialized knowledge and creative practice. Mentor undergraduate and graduate students in coursework, production assignments, portfolio development, and professional preparation. Serve on graduate thesis and dissertation committees and support student research and creative activity. Supervise and guide student lighting and visual designers through all phases of production. Creative Activity and Production Design Serve as the resident lighting designer for School of Dance productions. Design lighting and visual elements for departmental performances, concerts, and special events. Collaborate with faculty choreographers, guest artists, and production personnel to create cohesive artistic experiences. Integrate lighting, projection, digital media, and emerging technologies into performance environments as appropriate. Maintain an active record of creative and/or scholarly achievement consistent with tenure-track expectations. Director of Production Provide leadership for the planning and execution of the School's annual production season. Coordinate the production calendar, including rehearsals, technical rehearsals, performances, and special events. Work closely with the Production Manager, Production Assistant, faculty, staff, and guest artists to ensure effective production operations. Supervise technical production personnel, student employees, and production crews. Manage production-related budgets, equipment inventories, and resource allocation. Oversee the maintenance and safe operation of lighting, projection, and production equipment. Ensure compliance with university and industry safety standards and best practices. Service and Leadership Participate in School, College, and University governance through committee service and other assigned responsibilities. Contribute to recruitment, retention, and student success initiatives. Engage in professional service at the regional, national, and/or international levels. Support the School's mission through collaborative leadership and active participation in institutional initiatives. Qualifications Terminal degree (M.F.A. or equivalent) in Lighting Design, Theatrical Design, Dance Production, Theatre, Dance, or a closely related field from an accredited institution. Minimum of five years of professional experience in lighting design, with significant experience designing for dance performance. Demonstrated expertise in lighting design processes, technologies, and production practices. Evidence of achievement in creative and/or scholarly work. Demonstrated commitment to teaching, mentoring, and collaborative artistic practice. Strong organizational, leadership, and project management skills. Preferred Qualifications Successful university-level teaching experience. Experience supervising production operations, technical staff, and production budgets. Experience with Qlab, Vectorworks software, LightWright, Eos systems, Dante software, and Paradigm. Expertise in one or more complementary areas such as: Projection or media design, Costume design, Scenic design, Filmmaking or digital media production, Musical composition or sound design, Dance technology, Related movement or dance practices Experience working across interdisciplinary artistic environments. Demonstrated commitment to excellence and student-centered learning. Other Information The Florida State University School of Dance seeks a dynamic, collaborative leader to fill an Open Rank faculty position in Lighting and Visual Design while serving as Director of Production. This hybrid faculty-administrative position combines teaching, creative research, student mentorship, production design, and oversight of the School's production operations. The successful candidate will maintain an active program of creative and/or scholarly activity, teach undergraduate and graduate courses in lighting and visual design, mentor student artists and designers, and provide leadership for the planning, coordination, and execution of all School of Dance productions. The College of Fine Arts at Florida State University is dedicated to fostering artistic excellence, creative exploration, and scholarly inquiry across a variety of disciplines. Our renowned faculty and staff educate and empower students to become visionary performers, artists, educators, art historians, designers, curators, art therapists, researchers, and arts administrators who shape the future of the visual arts, healing arts, performing arts, and design. Through passionate teaching, community engagement, innovative research, and artistic practice we enrich lives, elevate artistic expression, and inspire positive change and well-being in society. Dance has been included in Florida State University\u2019s offerings for over 90 years, with a major degree program for more than sixty of those years. It has been recognized as a leader among college dance programs. Graduates of our programs include dancers, teachers, scholars, and leaders in companies, schools, universities, and art organizations in the United States and abroad. Montgomery Hall is one of the best dance facilities in the nation. The Maggie Allesee National Center for Choreography (MANCC) is an internationally recognized dance research center and part of the School of Dance. This unique and visionary institute brings a steady stream of prominent and emerging dance artists to campus to create and develop the work that the rest of the world will experience in years to come. Add to this mix an esteemed faculty and talented students, and it is easy to see why we are excited for what is to come. Contact Info Associate Professor Daniel Smith , Search Committee Chair University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applicants are required to submit: Examples of excellence in research or creative activity or excellence in teaching. CV One-page statement of their accomplishments over the last five years. Discussion of their teaching, research and service (no longer than six pages). Names, addresses, telephone numbers, and email addresses of three references. Confidential Letters of Reference: This position requires that you have three confidential professional letters of recommendation submitted on your behalf. Follow the steps below to request these letters through our system: 1) After submitting your application, click the Explore Jobs link; 2) Click the My References link; 3) Click the Send/View Reference Request button next to the appropriate position; and 4) Follow the steps on that page to send your references a system generated email requesting they submit a letter of recommendation on your behalf. You may also return to the My References link and click on \"Send/View Reference Request\" to see if your references have responded, add additional references, or resend requests. Candidates who currently hold tenure and are seeking appointment with tenure at Florida State University will need to submit the materials for evaluation if selected. These materials are required to support the tenure review process at the time of hire. Finalists may be asked to provide the below additional documentation as part of the evaluation. Examples of excellence in research or creative activity or excellence in teaching. CV One-page statement of their accomplishments over the last five years. Discussion of their teaching, research and service (no longer than six pages). Three outside letters of recommendation directed specifically to Florida State University. No professional relationships should exist between the candidate and the external reviewer. Relationships include, but are not limited to, student- teacher (including dissertation committee chairs and members), colleagues in graduate school, former departmental colleagues, collaborators, and co-authors. These letters should be sent to Ian Williams , Senior Administrative Specialist, directly from the external reviewer. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. Review of candidates will begin on November 20th 2026, and will continue until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63436&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Assistant Professor in Educational Leadership and Policy, 9 Month Salaried - Educational Leadership and Policy Studies - Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences", "description": "Job Title Assistant Professor in Educational Leadership and Policy, 9 Month Salaried - Educational Leadership and Policy Studies - Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63436 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Educational Leadership & Policy Studies in the Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences Responsibilities Engaging in a well-defined scholarship agenda with clear connections to K-12 educational policy and/or transitions to higher education. Teaching graduate courses in our online EdD program related to educational policy and/or research methods; Advising graduate students in the online EdD program and other programs as requested; Serving on student graduate committees, including chairing EdD student dissertations; Providing service to the university, the department, the college, and the profession; Developing and submitting grant proposals to funding agencies. Qualifications Earned doctorate in educational leadership, educational policy, or related education and/or social science disciplines; Evidence of high-quality scholarship (e.g., recent publications in peer-reviewed journals, working papers, recent presentations at national or international conferences); Commitment to and experience working with students of various backgrounds; Ability to teach educational leadership and policy courses and/or research methods courses; Strong organizational and interpersonal skills. Preferred Qualifications Expertise in qualitative research methods Experience with mentorship, in preparation for chairing EdD student dissertations; Experience with online teaching at the undergraduate or graduate level. Experience with teaching or training in research design courses (literature review, prospectus development, applied qualitative methods, etc.); Potential for success in garnering external funding for research. Other Information The Department of Educational Leadership & Policy Studies (ELPS) in the Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences at Florida State University invites applications for a nine-month, tenure-earning assistant professor position. We seek a colleague committed to research, mentorship, teaching, and advising. The successful candidate will be expected to participate in ongoing research in well-defined scholarship areas with clear connections to K-12 educational policy, advise professional doctoral students in our online EdD program, chair EdD dissertation committees, contribute to academic service, and apply for external funding to support new research projects. ELPS strives to develop a deep understanding of, and respect for, our students and colleagues. The Department enrolls a sizable population of students in online EdD and master\u2019s/specialist degree programs, in-person PhD and master\u2019s programs, and hosts a program evaluation certificate program. We seek a colleague who is committed to and capable of effectively educating students across multiple programs, with a particular focus on advising EdD students. For more information about the Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences, visit: https://annescollege.fsu.edu/. For more information about the Department of Educational Leadership and Policy Studies, visit: https://annescollege.fsu.edu/elps . The roots of FSU\u2019s Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences date back to the university\u2019s establishment, and it is the oldest college of its kind in Florida. The College is home to six academic departments united through a common goal to maximize human potential. In total, the College includes the Department of Educational Leadership & Policy Studies, Department of Educational Psychology & Learning Systems, Department of Human Development & Family Sciences, Department of Health, Nutrition & Food Sciences, Department of Sport Management, School of Teacher Education, numerous research centers, and three laboratory schools (Florida State University School, FSU Pembroke Pines Charter School, and The Collegiate School at FSU Panama City). Anne\u2019s College serves over 4,000 students via approximately 200 full-time faculty and nearly 80 full-time staff. For more information about the Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences visit: https://annescollege.fsu.edu/ . Contact Info Search Committee Co-chairs: Erica Harbatkin and Eric Ludwig University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applicants should also include a letter of application, names of three references with contact information, and a statement of teaching interests. Transcripts, work samples (such as teaching artifacts or manuscripts), and three letters of recommendation will be required of candidates selected for an interview. Review of candidates will begin October 9, 2026 and will continue until filled. We urge interested candidates to submit materials as soon as possible. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63441&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Assistant or Associate Professor in Clinical Exercise Physiology, 9 Month Salaried - Health, Nutrition, and Food Sciences - Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, Human Sciences", "description": "Job Title Assistant or Associate Professor in Clinical Exercise Physiology, 9 Month Salaried - Health, Nutrition, and Food Sciences - Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, Human Sciences Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63441 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Health, Nutrition, and Food Science in the Anne Spencer Daves College Education, Health, and Human Sciences Responsibilities Develop and maintain a nationally and internationally recognized, extramurally funded research program in clinical exercise physiology, preventive medicine, chronic disease management/prevention, cardiometabolic health, rehabilitation, exercise interventions, healthy aging, metabolism, and related areas. Recruit, mentor, and guide graduate students through their academic and research endeavors, fostering their professional growth. Conduct high-impact research that reinforces and expands current departmental strengths in cardiometabolic health, skeletal muscle biology, gut microbiome, and immunity. Establish collaborative research partnerships with healthcare providers and investigators across FSU Health, affiliated clinical systems, and interdisciplinary teams to expand the scope and reach of the department\u2019s research initiatives. Contribute to the department\u2019s teaching efforts at both the undergraduate and graduate levels, designing and delivering courses aligned with your area of expertise. Develop innovative curricula and strategies to enhance student engagement and learning outcomes. Participate in departmental, college, and university service, including committee work, and engage in professional outreach activities. Engage in community and public outreach that promotes health, nutrition, and exercise science education (e.g., Exercise is Medicine). Qualifications Ph.D. in Exercise Physiology or a related field. Demonstrated success in teaching, research, and service commensurate with rank (Assistant or Associate Professor). Record of extramural funding to support research initiatives (Associate Professor) or evidence for the likelihood of obtaining extramural support (Assistant Professor). Strong scholarly productivity with peer-reviewed publications. Excellent communication skills and ability to work collaboratively within interdisciplinary teams. Appropriate Postdoctoral Training. ACSM Clinical Exercise Physiologist certification, or be willing to obtain this certification upon hire. Preferred Qualifications Priority will be given to those with established or emerging expertise and leadership in research related to clinical exercise physiology. Proven success with securing external research funding. Federally funded research program Experience with interdisciplinary research teams or collaborations. Evidence of effective teaching Other Information The Department of Health, Nutrition, and Food Sciences (HNFS) in the Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences at Florida State University invites applications for a nine-month, tenure-earning assistant/associate professor position. We seek candidates whose research programs focus on the role of exercise in health, disease prevention, clinical care, rehabilitation, and/or healthy aging, and who can leverage emerging opportunities within FSU Health and its affiliated clinical partners. The ideal applicant is committed to research, mentorship, teaching, and academic service. The successful candidate will be expected to develop an extramurally funded research program that integrates exercise physiology within healthcare settings, contributes to improving patient outcomes, and supports graduate and postdoctoral trainees. For more information about HNFS, visit: https://annescollege.fsu.edu/hnfs The roots of FSU\u2019s Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences date back to the university\u2019s establishment, and it is the oldest college of its kind in Florida. The College is home to six academic departments united through a common goal to maximize human potential. In total, the College includes the Department of Educational Leadership & Policy Studies, Department of Educational Psychology & Learning Systems, Department of Human Development & Family Sciences, Department of Health, Nutrition & Food Sciences, Department of Sport Management, School of Teacher Education, numerous research centers, and three laboratory schools (Florida State University School, FSU Pembroke Pines Charter School, and The Collegiate School at FSU Panama City). Anne\u2019s College serves over 4,000 students via approximately 200 full-time faculty and nearly 80 full-time staff. For more information about the Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences visit: https://annescollege.fsu.edu/ Contact Info Michael J. Ormsbee, PhD University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applicants should also include: Cover letter Curriculum Vitae Statement of current/future research plans Statement of teaching interests Contact information of at least three professional references. Three letters of recommendation will be required of candidates selected for an interview. Review of candidates will begin 10/15/2026 and will continue until filled. We urge interested candidates to submit materials as soon as possible. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63440&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Assistant/Associate Professor in Clinical Nutrition, 9 Month Salaried - Department of Health, Nutrition, and Food Sciences - Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences", "description": "Job Title Assistant/Associate Professor in Clinical Nutrition, 9 Month Salaried - Department of Health, Nutrition, and Food Sciences - Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63440 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Health, Nutrition, and Food Science in the Anne Spencer Daves College Education, Health, and Human Sciences Responsibilities Maintain a nationally recognized (and internationally recognized for Associate Professor applicants), extramurally funded research program in clinical and translational nutrition that advances the department's research mission. Conduct high-impact research that complements and expands departmental strengths in clinical and translational nutrition, metabolism, cardiovascular health, dietary nutrients and bioactive compounds, microbiome science, exercise and nutritional physiology, skeletal muscle biology, immunity, and healthy aging. Recruit, mentor, and supervise graduate students, postdoctoral scholars, and other research trainees. Develop collaborative research partnerships across FSU Health, Tallahassee Memorial HealthCare (TMH), and affiliated clinical and community-based organizations, including opportunities within the FSU Health Research and Collaboration Building. Teach undergraduate and graduate courses in areas aligned with disciplinary expertise. Contribute to curriculum development and innovation to enhance student learning and workforce readiness. Participate in departmental, college, university, and professional service activities. Engage in community outreach and translational activities that promote nutrition, health, and disease prevention and/or management. Qualifications Ph.D. in Nutrition, Physiology, or a closely related field. Appropriate postdoctoral training or equivalent research experience. Demonstrated success in teaching, research, and service commensurate with rank. Evidence of the potential to obtain extramural funding (Assistant Professor) or a demonstrated record of extramural funding to support an independent research program (Associate Professor). Strong record of scholarly productivity, including peer-reviewed publications. Excellent communication skills and the ability to work collaboratively within interdisciplinary teams. Experience conducting human clinical research and/or experience working in healthcare or community-engaged research relevant to clinical and translational science. Preferred Qualifications Priority will be given to candidates with established or emerging expertise and leadership in clinical and translational nutrition research related to dietary patterns, phytochemicals and nutrients, precision nutrition, metabolism and metabolomics, nutritional physiology and pharmacology, cardiometabolic and gastrointestinal health, body composition, nutrition-related chronic disease, and/or eating and ingestive behavior. Evidence of a successful externally funded research program, with preference given to candidates with current or prior federal funding. Experience working within interdisciplinary research teams and collaborative research environments. Registered Dietitian Nutritionist (RDN) credential preferred. Evidence of effective teaching and mentoring. Experience in healthcare settings and/or community-engaged research relevant to clinical and translational science. Other Information Florida State University invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position in Clinical Nutrition at the Assistant or Associate Professor level. We seek scholars with strong research programs that complement the department's strengths in nutrition, metabolism, exercise physiology, food science, cardiovascular health, gut microbiome, skeletal muscle biology, immunity, and healthy aging. Candidates with expertise in clinical and translational nutrition are particularly encouraged to apply. Areas of interest include precision nutrition, dietary patterns, bioactive compounds and nutrients, nutrition-related chronic disease, metabolism and metabolomics, nutritional physiology and pharmacology, cardiometabolic and gastrointestinal health, body composition, and eating/ingestive behavior. We welcome scholars whose research integrates nutrition with human physiology, biomedical sciences, behavior, physical activity, and/or clinical and translational research, and who can contribute to the expanding FSU Health research enterprise. The successful candidate will have opportunities to collaborate with investigators and healthcare providers across FSU Health and affiliated clinical practices. The position offers access to state-of-the-art research facilities, interdisciplinary partnerships, and a dynamic academic environment committed to advancing nutrition, exercise physiology, food science, and health-related research. The Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences supports faculty success through opportunities for professional development, research growth, and leadership. The roots of FSU\u2019s Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences date back to the university\u2019s establishment, and it is the oldest college of its kind in Florida. The College is home to six academic departments united through a common goal to maximize human potential. In total, the College includes the Department of Educational Leadership & Policy Studies, Department of Educational Psychology & Learning Systems, Department of Human Development & Family Sciences, Department of Health, Nutrition & Food Sciences, Department of Sport Management, School of Teacher Education, numerous research centers, and three laboratory schools (Florida State University School, FSU Pembroke Pines Charter School, and The Collegiate School at FSU Panama City). Anne\u2019s College serves over 4,000 students via approximately 200 full-time faculty and nearly 80 full-time staff. For more information about the Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences visit: https://annescollege.fsu.edu/ . Contact Info Sarah A. Johnson , PhD, RDN, FASN, Search Committee Chair University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applicants should submit a letter of application, a statement of teaching interests, and the names and contact information of three professional references. Candidates selected for an interview will be required to provide transcripts and work samples (e.g., teaching materials or manuscripts). Letters of recommendation may be requested from finalists. Review of applications will begin September 15, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. Interested candidates are encouraged to apply as soon as possible. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63439&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Teaching Faculty I/II in Nutrition and Food Science, 9 Month Salaried - Department of Health, Nutrition, and Food Sciences - Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences", "description": "Job Title Teaching Faculty I/II in Nutrition and Food Science, 9 Month Salaried - Department of Health, Nutrition, and Food Sciences - Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63439 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Health, Nutrition, and Food Science in the Anne Spencer Daves College Education, Health, and Human Sciences Responsibilities Teaching undergraduate and graduate courses within the Nutrition and Food Science program. Serving as the primary academic advisor and mentor for undergraduate and graduate students pursuing Food Science. Providing leadership and coordination for Food Science curriculum, assessment, and student success initiatives. Collaborating with faculty, staff, and students to strengthen and advance Food Science education within the Nutrition and Food Science program. Engaging in service that supports the department, college, university, community, and profession. Qualifications Doctorate in Food Science or a closely related field from an accredited institution. Demonstrated experience teaching Food Science or related courses at the undergraduate and/or graduate level. Relevant professional, industry, regulatory, extension, or applied experience in Food Science or a related field. Evidence of effective communication, collaboration, and student mentoring. Evidence of professional, university, and/or community service. Preferred Qualifications Experience coordinating academic programs, advising students, or providing curriculum leadership. Demonstrated commitment to student success through advising, mentoring, and experiential learning opportunities. Other Information The Department of Health, Nutrition, and Food Sciences in the Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences at Florida State University invites applications for a nine-month Specialized Teaching Faculty position. We seek a colleague with expertise in Food Science who is committed to excellence in teaching, student mentoring, academic advising, and program leadership. The successful candidate will serve as the primary teaching faculty member supporting Food Science education within the Nutrition and Food Science program. Responsibilities include teaching undergraduate and graduate courses in Food Science and related areas of the curriculum, providing academic advising and mentoring to Food Science students, and contributing to the continued growth, coordination, and advancement of Food Science education within the department. The Department of Health, Nutrition, and Food Sciences at Florida State University is a dynamic academic unit serving approximately 1,000 undergraduate and 120 graduate students. The department offers undergraduate degree programs in Nutrition and Food Science, Dietetics, Exercise Physiology, and Athletic Training. Graduate programs include master's degrees in Nutrition and Food Science, Sports Nutrition, Exercise Physiology, and Sports Sciences, as well as doctoral degrees in Nutrition and Food Science and Exercise Physiology. The department also offers an accredited Dietetic Internship that prepares graduates for credentialing and professional practice as Registered Dietitian Nutritionists. Faculty in the department are engaged in nationally and internationally recognized research and scholarship spanning nutrition, food science, exercise physiology, and related health sciences. Areas of expertise include basic, applied, clinical, and translational research focused on nutrition, metabolism, cardiovascular health, physical activity, food systems, human performance, and healthy aging. The department is committed to excellence in teaching, research, student mentorship, and interdisciplinary collaboration to advance health and well-being across the lifespan. The roots of FSU\u2019s Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences date back to the university\u2019s establishment, and it is the oldest college of its kind in Florida. The College is home to six academic departments united through a common goal to maximize human potential. In total, the College includes the Department of Educational Leadership & Policy Studies, Department of Educational Psychology & Learning Systems, Department of Human Development & Family Sciences, Department of Health, Nutrition & Food Sciences, Department of Sport Management, School of Teacher Education, numerous research centers, and three laboratory schools (Florida State University School, FSU Pembroke Pines Charter School, and The Collegiate School at FSU Panama City). Anne\u2019s College serves over 4,000 students via approximately 200 full-time faculty and nearly 80 full-time staff. For more information about the Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences visit: https://annescollege.fsu.edu / Contact Info Jennifer Farrell , Search Committee Chair University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applicants should also include a letter of application, names of three references with contact information, and a statement of teaching interests. Three letters of recommendation will be required of candidates selected for an interview. Review of candidates will begin immediately and will continue until filled. We urge interested candidates to submit materials as soon as possible. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63437&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried - Human Development and Family Science - Department of Human Development and Family Science - Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences", "description": "Job Title Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried - Human Development and Family Science - Department of Human Development and Family Science - Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63437 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Human Development and Family Science - Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences Responsibilities Conduct quality research in the broad domain of human development and family science. Provide guidance, leadership, and mentorship to graduate students. Provide quality teaching to undergraduate and graduate students. Support the service needs of the Department, College, and University. Collaborate with and support Departmental Centers and Institutes, such as the Family Institute and the Center for Couples and Family Therapy. Qualifications Earned doctorate in a relevant area of study (e.g., family studies/science, human development, or psychology). A record of research accomplishments with the potential for extramural funding. Evidence of college-level teaching excellence. Preferred Qualifications Experience with or secured extramural funding. Experience at Research 1 universities. Ability to teach online, hybrid, and traditional modes. Demonstrated success working with all student populations. Other Information The Department of Human Development and Family Science (HDFS) in the Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences at Florida State University invites applications for a nine-month, tenure-earning assistant professor position. We seek a colleague committed to research, mentorship, teaching, and advising. The successful candidate will be expected to participate in ongoing research in a well-defined scholarship area within the broad domain of human development and family science, with clear connections to human development (child, adolescent, adult or old age), family processes, family policy/programs, and/or relationship interventions. They will advise and mentor graduate students in the MS and Ph.D. programs, chair doctoral dissertation committees, contribute to academic service for the Department, College, and University, and apply for external funding to support and advance their research projects. The Department of Human Development and Family Science is committed to making a difference in the lives of people. Our programs focus on human development, family processes, and empirically supported relationship interventions. Specifically, our research, teaching, and service activities reflect our three program foci: Relational development and enhancement of children adolescents, young adults, couples, older adults, and families; distressed families and relational interventions; and the link between parenting and peer processes and relational and mental health outcomes. The Department also has a focus on health and well-being across the lifespan. The Department strives to provide undergraduate and graduate students with outstanding academic experiences in teaching, research, and professional development. For more information about the Department of Human Development and Family Science, visit: https://annescollege.fsu.edu/hdfs . The roots of FSU\u2019s Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences date back to the university\u2019s establishment, and it is the oldest college of its kind in Florida. The College is home to six academic departments united through a common goal to maximize human potential. In total, the College includes the Department of Educational Leadership & Policy Studies, Department of Educational Psychology & Learning Systems, Department of Human Development & Family Sciences, Department of Health, Nutrition & Food Sciences, Department of Sport Management, School of Teacher Education, numerous research centers, and three laboratory schools (Florida State University School, FSU Pembroke Pines Charter School, and The Collegiate School at FSU Panama City). Anne\u2019s College serves over 4,000 students via approximately 200 full-time faculty and nearly 80 full-time staff. For more information about the Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences visit: https://annescollege.fsu.edu/ . Contact Info Search Committee Co-Chairs: Francis Fincham and Tom Ledermann University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applicants should also include a letter of application, names of three references with contact information, and a statement of research. Transcripts, work samples (such as published manuscripts and teaching artifacts), and three letters of recommendation will be required of candidates selected for an interview. Review of candidates will begin 11/30/2026 and will continue until filled. We urge interested candidates to submit materials as soon as possible. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63406&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "OPS Cooks/Hospitality Assistants - FSU Childcare (Multiple Positions)", "description": "Job Title OPS Cooks/Hospitality Assistants - FSU Childcare (Multiple Positions) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63406 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Part-Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department FSU Childcare & Early Learning Program Responsibilities Assist in meal preparation (per USDA standards), meal delivery, loading and unloading dishwasher, stocking food, and paper goods and general kitchen duties as it relates to the childcare facility. Qualifications High school diploma/equivalent. Ability to follow verbal and written instructions. Ability to communicate verbally and in writing. Ability to lift/move up to 25 lbs. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range $15 per hour How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an OPS/temporary job. Hours are flexible and depend on the Center's needs; typically 10 - 20 hours per week. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check , including a fingerprint-based screening via AHCA\u2019s Clearinghouse pursuant to Section 1012, Florida Statutes, for positions in a FSU Developmental Research School or Section 409.175, Florida Statutes, for positions in a Childcare or Summer Camp position. Visit the AHCA Clearinghouse Screenings webpage for more information. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63405&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "OPS Teaching Classroom Assistants - FSU Childcare (Multiple Positions)", "description": "Job Title OPS Teaching Classroom Assistants - FSU Childcare (Multiple Positions) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63405 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Part-Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department FSU Childcare & Early Learning Program Responsibilities Assist faculty in the supervision of young children, six weeks to five years of age, in daily activities. Assist with housekeeping tasks, such as wiping down tables, cleaning the floors, etc. Assist with other needs of FSU Childcare as needed. Qualifications A high school diploma or equivalent and some experience working with children. Preferred Qualifications Associate's degree or a degree in Early Childhood Education, Early Childhood Special Education, Child Development, or Family and Child Science. Other Information Applicable DCF-mandated post-hire training will be required. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range $15 per hour. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an OPS/temporary job. Hours are flexible and depend on the Center's needs; typically 10 - 20 hours per week. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check , including a fingerprint-based screening via AHCA\u2019s Clearinghouse pursuant to Section 1012, Florida Statutes, for positions in a FSU Developmental Research School or Section 409.175, Florida Statutes, for positions in a Childcare or Summer Camp position. Visit the AHCA Clearinghouse Screenings webpage for more information. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63425&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Open Rank Professor, 9 Month Salaried (Multiple Positions in Computer Engineering -Department of Electrical & Computer Engineering FAMU-FSU College of Engineering)", "description": "Job Title Open Rank Professor, 9 Month Salaried (Multiple Positions in Computer Engineering -Department of Electrical & Computer Engineering FAMU-FSU College of Engineering) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63425 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The Department of Electrical & Computer Engineering (ECE) at the Florida A&M University (FAMU)-Florida State University (FSU) College of Engineering invites applications from highly qualified individuals for multiple tenure-track faculty positions in Computer Engineering in Tallahassee, Florida. Responsibilities Candidates are expected to develop research programs that are internationally recognized with significant and sustained funding, incorporate interdisciplinary collaboration with researchers across campus, have a strong commitment to teaching excellence in undergraduate and graduate courses, supervise undergraduate, graduate and post-doctoral researchers, and participate in college and professional service. Qualifications Candidates must possess an earned Ph.D. in computer engineering, computer science, electrical engineering, or a closely related discipline, and demonstrate documented potential for outstanding research. Helpful The FAMU-FSU College of Engineering is the nexus of two major public universities, each with a distinct mission but focused on world-class engineering education and research. Created by the Florida Legislature in 1982, the joint university is the college of engineering for both Florida A&M and Florida State universities. This unique combination of focus, resources and mission from our parent university has created on our campus a truly innovative atmosphere that leverages the benefits of the traditional HBCU model with the innovations of an R-1 public research university. After completing pre-requisites at their home university, FAMU and FSU students learn, study and research together at our independent campus with joint-appointed faculty and staff. Students graduate from their enrolling university and from the FAMU-FSU College of Engineering. Both FAMU and FSU are part of the State University System of Florida and are accredited by the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools Commission on Colleges. Additionally, all seven (7) of the college\u2019s eligible undergraduate degree programs are accredited by the Engineering Accreditation Commission of ABET . Contact Info Any questions about the position should be directed to Dr. Rodney Roberts, Search Committee Chair, at rroberts@eng.famu.fsu.edu University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include the following documents: A cover letter A full curriculum vitae A 2 to 3-page research statement including research interests and plans and how the proposed research efforts will connect to other efforts in the department and universities. A 1-page statement on teaching and philosophy No more than four selected publications for review The names and contact information of four potential references Faculty Information The Department of Electrical & Computer Engineering (ECE) at the Florida A&M University (FAMU)-Florida State University (FSU) College of Engineering invites applications from highly qualified individuals for multiple tenure-track faculty positions in Computer Engineering in Tallahassee, Florida. We are seeking faculty members with expertise in Computer Networks Security, Data Science, AI, Computer Vision, Robotics & Autonomy, Embedded Computing, and Cyber-physical Systems Security. This position is at the assistant level, but well-qualified candidates will be considered at a higher rank. The ECE Department currently has 37 faculty, 100+ graduate students, 450+ undergraduate students, and annual research expenditures exceeding $20M. The two universities and outstanding research facilities in the affiliated research buildings/centers provide opportunities for collaboration with faculty in Computer Science and Scientific Computing, the Center for Advanced Power Systems (CAPS) FAMU Center for Cyber Security, National High Magnetic Field Laboratory (NHMFL), Center for Intelligent Systems, Control and Robotics (CISCOR), FSU Institute of Molecular Biophysics , FSU Jim Moran College of Entrepreneurship , and FSU College of Medicine. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Applications will be reviewed beginning on December 1, 2026. Acceptance and review of applications will continue until the position is filled. The appointment is anticipated to begin in August 2027. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63367&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Assistant Director of Affiliation Agreements, 12 Month Salaried (0.5 FTE) (Office of Academic Services & Intern Support - Anne's College)", "description": "Job Title Assistant Director of Affiliation Agreements, 12 Month Salaried (0.5 FTE) (Office of Academic Services & Intern Support - Anne's College) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63367 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Part-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Office of Academic Services and Intern Support (OASIS) | Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences Responsibilities Coordinate the full lifecycle of affiliation agreements and Memorandum of Understanding (MOUs), including drafting, routing, review, execution, and renewal. Serve as the primary point of contact for academic departments, university administrative offices, legal counsel, and external partner organizations regarding affiliation agreements. Maintain a centralized database of active agreements and supporting documentation. Monitor agreement expiration and renewal timelines to prevent disruptions to clinical, internship, practicum, and other experiential learning placements. Ensure agreements comply with university policies, accreditation standards, and applicable legal requirements. Track agreement status and provide updates to faculty, administrators, and external partners. Develop and maintain efficient workflows and documentation processes that improve operational effectiveness. Assist academic programs in establishing new partnerships by facilitating timely execution of required agreements. Qualifications Academic master\u2019s degree from an accredited institution in education or a closely related field. Experience in administrative coordination, contract administration, project coordination, or a related field. Preferred Qualifications Excellent organizational and project management skills with exceptional attention to detail. Strong written and verbal communication skills. Proficiency with document management systems and Microsoft Office applications. Experience working with contracts, affiliation agreements, or Memorandums of Understanding. Knowledge of accreditation requirements related to clinical, practicum, internship, or experiential learning programs. Demonstrated ability to manage multiple priorities while meeting deadlines. Experience maintaining confidential records and databases. Ability to collaborate effectively with internal and external stakeholders. Other Information The Office of Academic and Intern Support (OASIS) in Annes College is seeking a highly organized and collaborative professional to serve as the Assistant Director of Affiliation Agreements & Partnerships. This position plays a vital role in supporting the College's expanding network of clinical, internship, practicum, and experiential learning partnerships by managing affiliation agreements and Memorandums of Understanding (MOUs) with school districts, clinical sites, hospitals, healthcare systems, community organizations, agencies, and other external partners. This position will provide centralized oversight of affiliation agreements, ensuring timely execution, regulatory compliance, accurate recordkeeping, and effective collaboration with university offices and external partners. The roots of FSU\u2019s Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences date back to the university\u2019s establishment, and it is the oldest college of its kind in Florida. The College is home to six academic departments united through a common goal to maximize human potential. In total, the College includes the Department of Educational Leadership & Policy Studies, Department of Educational Psychology & Learning Systems, Department of Human Development & Family Sciences, Department of Health, Nutrition & Food Sciences, Department of Sport Management, School of Teacher Education, numerous research centers, and three laboratory schools (Florida State University School, FSU Pembroke Pines Charter School, and The Collegiate School at FSU Panama City). Anne\u2019s College serves over 4,000 students via approximately 200 full-time faculty and nearly 80 full-time staff. Contact Info Jessica Tucker University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Tallahassee as a community is a vibrant mid-size city with abundant opportunities \u2013 from government internships and legislative initiatives to special events, shopping, dining, and outdoor activities. Tallahassee is located near the Gulf Beaches of Florida and enjoys abundant sunshine and four seasons with a mild winter climate. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applicants should also include a letter of application and names of three references with contact information. Review of candidates will begin 09/08/2026 and will continue until filled. We urge interested candidates to submit materials as soon as possible. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This is a part-time, 20 hours per week (0.5 FTE) faculty position. This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63407&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Assistant Professor 9 Month Salaried (School of Information)", "description": "Job Title Assistant Professor 9 Month Salaried (School of Information) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63407 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department College of Communication & Information School of Information Responsibilities We are seeking a faculty colleague whose research and teaching will be in the broad domain of cybersecurity and who will employ a behavioral, sociotechnical, and/or technical perspective. Specific areas of research interest may include, but are not limited to, how cybersecurity interacts with areas such as artificial intelligence (AI), human-computer interaction (HCI), data science, information policy, information ethics, and computer networking. Successful candidates will have strong technical and/or analytical skills and be able to articulate a research agenda that aligns with the broader research interests of the iSchool. They must also clearly demonstrate the ability to work effectively within a highly interdisciplinary environment. Candidates should also indicate a clear plan for actively seeking external funding. In addition to strong research, the iSchool values highly effective and innovative teaching. Successful applicants must demonstrate a commitment to excellence in teaching in cybersecurity-related areas. The successful candidate will be expected to teach at all levels, including courses in the iSchool\u2019s bachelor\u2019s, master\u2019s, and doctoral degree programs. Experience teaching online, as well as face-to-face, is preferred. Faculty typically teach two courses per semester each academic year. All faculty members are expected to advise students, serve on iSchool, College, and University committees, and be active in professional and academic organizations. Qualifications Doctoral degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant Professor. Qualified applicants will have a Ph.D. or equivalent doctorate in information science, information systems, information technology, or a cognate field. Other Information The School of Information is one of three academic units within the College of Communication and Information at Florida State University. The FSU iSchool offers a Bachelor\u2019s degree program with majors in Information Technology (IT) and Information, Communication, and Technology (ICT); Master\u2019s degree programs in Information Technology and Information; and a Ph.D. program in Information. The iSchool faculty also operates the eHealth Lab and iSensor Lab, and is a founding partner in FSU\u2019s Innovation Hub, an innovation center and fab lab/makerspace for teaching and research that utilizes technologies including virtual/augmented reality, 3D printing, and 3D visualization. The School of Information, which launched in 1926, was formally founded in 1947 and is nationally ranked among the top information science graduate schools in the country. The iSchool's Master\u2019s in Information Technology program is nationally ranked at #8 among online IT programs, #5 among IT programs for veterans, and the ALA-accredited Master's in Information is ranked among U.S. News & World Report's \u201cBest Graduate Programs in Library and Information Science\u201d as 12th overall. School of Information faculty have been awarded over $50 million in federal, state, local, and foundation research grants, and maintain strong connections to the community through various information, literacy, and service initiatives. Funding has been received from NIH, IMLS, NSF, and the DOD as well as The Robert Wood Johnson Foundation, The McKnight Foundation, and others. iSchool faculty have strong collaborations with researchers in the College of Medicine, College of Social Work, College of Nursing, College of Education, Health and Human Sciences, and College of Arts and Sciences. More information about the School of Information is available online at: http://ischool.cci.fsu.edu/ The iSchool is a member of the College of Communication and Information and has a student population of approximately 390 undergraduates and 566 graduate students. The iSchool boasts 18 tenured/tenure-track and 10 full-time non-tenure-track faculty members. The College is a leader on campus and is nationally recognized for its distance and online education programs. For more information about the college, see https://cci.fsu.edu/. Contact Info Inquiries should be directed to: George Moore 850-644-5775 gmm26c@fsu.edu University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. All applications must include a cover letter, CV, research statement, and teaching statement. The School of Information (iSchool) at Florida State University seeks to fill one (1) nine-month tenure-track faculty position at the Assistant Professor level. Review of applications will begin on September 30, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63363&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Assistant Professor in Counseling Psychology, 9 Month Salaried (Educational Psychology & Learning Systems - Anne's College)", "description": "Job Title Assistant Professor in Counseling Psychology, 9 Month Salaried (Educational Psychology & Learning Systems - Anne's College) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63363 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Educational Psychology & Learning Systems | Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences Responsibilities This position will involve the following: research/scholarship in any substantive area related to counseling psychology. graduate teaching (e.g., assessment courses, clinical courses). supervision of doctoral students in clinical practicum settings. chairing and serving on graduate student supervisory committees. mentoring/supervising doctoral student research. serving on program, departmental, and college committees. program/curriculum development and evaluation of the APA-accredited doctoral program. Qualifications Ph.D. or terminal degree from an accredited institution in Counseling Psychology, or a closely related field is required. Candidates must demonstrate a strong commitment to research and scholarship, teaching, supervision, program development, and the integration of science and practice, while serving as a professional role model. Preferred Qualifications We encourage applicants with expertise in Counseling Psychology, knowledge of APA-accreditation procedures, and familiarity with national training issues in professional psychology. Additionally, candidates with experience conducting and publishing research in areas relevant to counseling psychology are strongly encouraged to apply. We seek candidates with counseling or supervision experience, prior teaching experience at the graduate or undergraduate level, and a developing or well-established independent research program. A record of success, or strong potential for success, in teaching, research, and service is highly valued. Preference will be given to candidates who hold a Ph.D. in Counseling Psychology from an APA-accredited program and who demonstrate a commitment to the professional identity of a health service psychologist. Current licensure, or eligibility for licensure within the first year of employment, as a psychologist in Florida is strongly preferred. Additionally, prior tenure-track experience and demonstrated potential or proven success in securing external research funding are highly desirable. Other Information The Department of Educational Psychology and Learning Systems (EPLS) invites applications for a tenure-earning Assistant Professor position within the Psychological and Counseling Services (PCS) program, specifically for the Combined Counseling Psychology & School Psychology doctoral program. Our faculty brings a broad range of experiences and research interests, and we are eager to welcome a new team member who will enhance our department. We seek an exceptional candidate with strong training and professional identity in the field of Counseling Psychology. The EPLS department is home to the Assessment, Learning Evaluation, & Counseling (ALEC) Center , which serves as a hub for training doctoral students and conducting research. The department also has a NASP-accredited School Psychology program and CACREP-approved programs in Mental Health Counseling, School Counseling, and Career Counseling. Our faculty brings a broad range of experiences and research interests, and we are eager to welcome a new team member who will enhance our department, academic programs, and ALEC. The roots of FSU\u2019s Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences date back to the university\u2019s establishment, and it is the oldest college of its kind in Florida. The College is home to six academic departments united through a common goal to maximize human potential. In total, the College includes the Department of Educational Leadership & Policy Studies, Department of Educational Psychology & Learning Systems, Department of Human Development & Family Sciences, Department of Health, Nutrition & Food Sciences, Department of Sport Management, School of Teacher Education, numerous research centers, and three laboratory schools (Florida State University School, FSU Pembroke Pines Charter School, and The Collegiate School at FSU Panama City). Anne\u2019s College serves over 4,000 students via approximately 200 full-time faculty and nearly 80 full-time staff. Contact Info Dr. Debra Osborn Search Committee Chair University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Tallahassee as a community is a vibrant mid-size city with abundant opportunities \u2013 from government internships and legislative initiatives to special events, shopping, dining, and outdoor activities. Tallahassee is located near the Gulf Beaches of Florida and enjoys abundant sunshine and four seasons with a mild winter climate. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applicants should also include a letter of application, names of three references with contact information, a statement of teaching interests, and a research statement. Transcripts, work samples (such as teaching artifacts or manuscripts), and three letters of recommendation will be required of candidates selected for an interview. Review of candidates will begin 10/02/2026 and will continue until filled. We urge interested candidates to submit materials as soon as possible. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63368&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Assistant Professor in Sport Management, 9 Month Salaried (Department of Sport Management - Anne's College)", "description": "Job Title Assistant Professor in Sport Management, 9 Month Salaried (Department of Sport Management - Anne's College) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63368 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Sport Management | Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences Responsibilities The individual hired will be required to maintain an active research agenda, possess strong knowledge of quantitative and/or qualitative research methods for the effective mentoring of master\u2019s and doctoral student research, teach undergraduate and graduate courses (including teaching online courses), seek external funding, aid in developing external partnerships, and contribute to department and university growth through appropriate service activities. Qualifications Earned doctorate degree in Sport Management or related field; college/university teaching experience; mentoring experience; evidence of scholarly productivity; experience procuring external funding, or evidence of ability to procure external funding. An individual\u2019s program of research should align with one of the department\u2019s core content areas. Preferred Qualifications Preference will be given to individuals with a research interest aligned with business-related content (e.g., marketing, finance, economics, management). Preference will also be given to individuals with a record of procuring external funding. Other Information Candidates are being sought for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in the Department Sport Management in the Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences. The department has four core areas: Legal and Policy Studies, Management, Marketing, and Media and Cultural Studies. This is a nine-month position, with possible summer employment. Candidates should be available to start in the Fall 2027 semester (approximately August 9, 2027). The roots of FSU\u2019s Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences date back to the university\u2019s establishment, and it is the oldest college of its kind in Florida. The College is home to six academic departments united through a common goal to maximize human potential. In total, the College includes the Department of Educational Leadership & Policy Studies, Department of Educational Psychology & Learning Systems, Department of Human Development & Family Sciences, Department of Health, Nutrition & Food Sciences, Department of Sport Management, School of Teacher Education, numerous research centers, and three laboratory schools (Florida State University School, FSU Pembroke Pines Charter School, and The Collegiate School at FSU Panama City). Anne\u2019s College serves over 4,000 students via approximately 200 full-time faculty and nearly 80 full-time staff. Contact Info Dr. James Du Search Committee Chair Questions regarding the application submission system and process should be directed to the application coordinator: Katherine Maddox Sr. Administrative Specialist University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Tallahassee as a community is a vibrant mid-size city with abundant opportunities \u2013 from government internships and legislative initiatives to special events, shopping, dining, and outdoor activities. Tallahassee is located near the Gulf Beaches of Florida and enjoys abundant sunshine and four seasons with a mild winter climate. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applicants should also include (1) a current curriculum vitae, (2) a letter of interest highlighting their qualifications for the position, (3) the names and contact information of three references, (4) a statement of research, and 5) a statement of teaching philosophy. Transcripts and three letters of recommendation will be required of candidates selected for an interview. Review of applications will begin October 19, 2026. We urge interested candidates to submit materials as soon as possible. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63365&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Assistant Professor in Sport Psychology, 9 Month Salaried (Educational Psychology & Learning Systems - Anne's College)", "description": "Job Title Assistant Professor in Sport Psychology, 9 Month Salaried (Educational Psychology & Learning Systems - Anne's College) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63365 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Educational Psychology & Learning Systems | Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences Responsibilities The candidate will be expected to serve on doctoral committees and supervise student research, in addition to teaching and providing service to the program, department, college, and university. Candidates are also responsible for developing a program of research and scholarly activity in the realm of sport psychology. Qualifications Candidates for this position should have an earned doctorate from a recognized doctoral program in Sport Psychology or a closely related field (e.g., Kinesiology, Exercise Science). Preferred Qualifications Prior tenure-track experience and demonstrated potential or proven success in securing external research funding are highly desirable. Prior experience mentoring doctoral students is also preferred. Other Information The program is seeking a candidate with clearly expressed interest in sport psychology research and professional issues. The successful candidate will demonstrate an aptitude for conducting research, teaching, and mentoring graduate students, as well as a commitment to both the Sport Psychology MS and PhD programs. We are seeking a candidate who will contribute to strengthening program quality and student recruitment. The successful candidate will also demonstrate skills related to the quality teaching of sport psychology courses. This top-ranked program has a vibrant Sport Psychology Lab and connections to the Institute of Sport Science and Medicine (ISSM) . The roots of FSU\u2019s Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences date back to the university\u2019s establishment, and it is the oldest college of its kind in Florida. The College is home to six academic departments united through a common goal to maximize human potential. In total, the College includes the Department of Educational Leadership & Policy Studies, Department of Educational Psychology & Learning Systems, Department of Human Development & Family Sciences, Department of Health, Nutrition & Food Sciences, Department of Sport Management, School of Teacher Education, numerous research centers, and three laboratory schools (Florida State University School, FSU Pembroke Pines Charter School, and The Collegiate School at FSU Panama City). Anne\u2019s College serves over 4,000 students via approximately 200 full-time faculty and nearly 80 full-time staff. Contact Info Search Committee Co-Chairs: Brady DeCouto David Eccles University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Tallahassee as a community is a vibrant mid-size city with abundant opportunities \u2013 from government internships and legislative initiatives to special events, shopping, dining, and outdoor activities. Tallahassee is located near the Gulf Beaches of Florida and enjoys abundant sunshine and four seasons with a mild winter climate. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applicants should also include a letter of application, names of three references with contact information, a statement of teaching interests, and a research statement. Transcripts, work samples (such as teaching artifacts or manuscripts), and three letters of recommendation will be required of candidates selected for an interview. Review of candidates will begin 10/02/2026 and will continue until filled. We urge interested candidates to submit materials as soon as possible. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63386&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Violin, 9 Month Salaried - College of Music", "description": "Job Title Assistant Professor of Violin, 9 Month Salaried - College of Music Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63386 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department College of Music Responsibilities Teach undergraduate and graduate-level violin students. Recruit and maintain a successful teaching studio. Serve on doctoral and master\u2019s committees and juries. Maintain a professional career as a performing artist. Participate in university and professional service activities nationally and internationally as appropriate. Additional responsibilities may include coaching chamber music and teaching courses in the candidate\u2019s area of expertise. Qualifications Hold a doctoral degree or demonstrate a record of equivalent performance and teaching experience. Hold a record of successful university-level studio teaching experience and proven artistry as a professional performer. Demonstrate strong commitment to the recruitment of outstanding students. Demonstrate a proven commitment to creating an environment which contributes to the vibrancy and economy of the university community and engages students. Other Information Seeking new knowledge and deeper understanding of music in interdisciplinary contexts through innovative research, music performance, and creative activity, The College of Music at Florida State University is the largest such college in the Southeast and one of the largest university-based music programs in the nation. We are home to over 600 undergraduate and over 300 graduate students, who represent nearly every state in the nation and 26 foreign countries. Contact Info Alexander Jimenez , Professor of Conducting and Director of Orchestral Activities University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. In addition to the online application, please attach a single document that includes: Cover Letter (1-2 pages) Curriculum Vitae Contact information for four professional references (mailing address, phone, email). Links to video recordings made within the past five years that include: A 20-minute teaching video. A performance video (s) demonstrating a variety of styles. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled and will begin August 2027. However, for priority consideration, please complete all application materials by September 28, 2026. Review of applications will begin immediately and will remain ongoing until the position is filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63374&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried - Elementary Mathematics Education School of Teacher Education - Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences", "description": "Job Title Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried - Elementary Mathematics Education School of Teacher Education - Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63374 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department School of Teacher Education in the Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences Responsibilities Applicants will be expected to engage in research and seek external funding related to Mathematics Education for Elementary Students, teach undergraduate courses (specifically elementary mathematics methods courses) and graduate courses, collaborate with Elementary Education faculty, advise and mentor Master\u2019s and Doctoral students, conduct research that informs the field, collaborate with STEM faculty, and provide service to the university, local community partners, and the profession. Qualifications Earned doctorate in Elementary Education, Mathematics Education (or a related field such as Curriculum & Instruction with a focus on STEM education) by August 2027. A strong record of scholarship commensurate with position, as indicated by peer-reviewed journal publications, conference presentations, and collaborative projects. A productive and innovative research agenda that operates within a strong theoretical and empirical approach to understanding some facet of Elementary Mathematics Teaching or Learning Experience teaching at elementary and post-secondary levels. Preferred Qualifications Previous experience securing and/or working on externally funded research projects. Experience collaborating with STEM faculty and/or elementary schools. A research focus on learning technologies, AI, and/or data science in the context of mathematics and statistics teaching and learning. Other Information The School of Teacher Education in the Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences at Florida State University invites applications for a nine-month, tenure-earning assistant professor of Elementary Mathematics Education position to start in August of 2027. Faculty in the Mathematics Education Program in the School of Teacher Education strive to develop a deep understanding of, and respect for, our teaching candidates and colleagues. The fac ulty have a long history of internationally recognized scholarship and a track-record of award-winning scholarship and consistent external funding. Our goal is to inform the field\u2019s understanding of mathematics teaching and learning through research and policy development aimed at transforming lives and striving towards collective wellness and more sustainable ways of being . For information about the Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences, visit https://annescollege.fsu.edu . For more information about the program, visit https://annescollege.fsu.edu/mathematics-education The roots of FSU\u2019s Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences date back to the university\u2019s establishment, and it is the oldest college of its kind in Florida. The College is home to six academic departments united through a common goal to maximize human potential. In total, the College includes the Department of Educational Leadership & Policy Studies, Department of Educational Psychology & Learning Systems, Department of Human Development & Family Sciences, Department of Health, Nutrition & Food Sciences, Department of Sport Management, School of Teacher Education, numerous research centers, and three laboratory schools (Florida State University School, FSU Pembroke Pines Charter School, and The Collegiate School at FSU Panama City). Anne\u2019s College serves over 4,000 students via approximately 200 full-time faculty and nearly 80 full-time staff. For more information about the Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences visit: https://annescollege.fsu.edu/ . Contact Info Christine Andrews-Larson University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applicants should also include a letter of application, names of three references with contact information, and a statement of teaching interests. Transcripts, work samples (such as teaching artifacts or manuscripts), and three letters of recommendation will be required of candidates selected for an interview. Review of candidates will begin Oct 2, 2026 and will continue until filled. We urge interested candidates to submit materials as soon as possible. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63400&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Associate Director of Student and Alumni Engagement, Student Success Collective/FSU Libraries and Undergraduate Studies", "description": "Job Title Associate Director of Student and Alumni Engagement, Student Success Collective/FSU Libraries and Undergraduate Studies Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63400 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department FSU Division of University Advancement Florida State University is currently in the leadership phase of a comprehensive campaign. As the leadership phase of the campaign begins, the Division of University Advancement is accelerating the hiring of additional advancement operations professionals\u2019 campus-wide and is excited to build out its team. For Advancement professionals who are interested in being a part of a comprehensive campaign from the beginning for their career development, the timing is ideal to join our team. Responsibilities The position is responsible for developing, implementing, and managing an alumni engagement plan that supports the Division of University Advancement's goals, leverages the advancement infrastructure of the Student Success Collective (SSC), Undergraduate Studies and FSU Libraries and adheres to Council for Advancement and Support of Education (CASE) best practices and metrics. It leads college-wide initiatives that foster meaningful connections among students, alumni, donors, parents, friends and volunteers that contribute to philanthropic priorities. The role also oversees collection, maintenance, and strategic use of alumni data. Lead the development and execution of a comprehensive alumni engagement plan for FSU Libraries and Undergraduate Studies (UGS), through student and alumni enculturation programming, communications, activities and events. Foster participation in experiential learning, networking, philanthropy, and volunteerism by connecting current students with alumni through mentorship and engagement activities. Partner with FSU Libraries and UGS staff to enhance student-alumni interactions through in-person and virtual events. Plan and execute Unit-led events, including conference receptions, Homecoming activities, and outreach programs, ensuring seamless coordination and impactful experiences for alumni and key stakeholders. Align alumni engagement efforts with FSU Libraries and UGS fundraising priorities by integrating development goals into outreach programming that supports long-term donor relationships. Collaborate with FSU Libraries and UGS development and DUA donor relations teams to manage stewardship touchpoints that strengthen connections with donors and key stakeholders. Support and manage key FSU Libraries and UGS alumni volunteers, volunteer groups, or advisory boards/councils, partnering with the development team to foster meaningful involvement, engagement and leadership. This may include contributing to agenda development, conducting research and creating events that inspire and empower volunteer leaders. Recommend alumni for volunteer leadership roles and contribute to donor pipeline development through incorporating best practice for discovery, CRM documentation, and recommending potential donors to development colleagues. Leverage existing DUA programming (e.g., Alumni Affinity Networks, Seminole Clubs, Homecoming activities, Seminole 100 and Alumni Awards) to engage FSU Libraries and UGS alumni and ensure FSU Libraries and UGS colleagues are aware of programming. Support campus-wide alumni engagement by staffing signature and regional events, recruiting alumni volunteers, submitting alumni award nominations, and encouraging Seminole 100 applications. Curate and amplify compelling stories about FSU Libraries and UGS students, alumni and donors. Respond to alumni inquiries. Partners with FSU Libraries, UGS, and DUA communications teams to develop an alumni communications plan for that complements central DUA outreach to alumni and donors. Effectively convey key updates, news, and engagement opportunities from FSU Libraries, UGS, DUA, and FSU, ensuring meaningful connections to FSU Libraries and UGS alumni. May manage and distribute email campaigns for FSU Libraries and UGS alumni-facing communications. This may include generating content, creating graphics and collaborating with DUA, FSU Libraries, and UGS communications team members to develop email marketing strategy. Extracts data files to upload for email distribution lists. Evaluate alumni engagement communications; provide analytics and marketing reports on all aspects of email communications. Serve as the alumni data steward for the FSU Libraries and UGS, ensuring compliance with DUA data policies and procedures to maintain accuracy, security and usability, this includes identifying and coding student/alumni participation in key program areas. Analyze alumni demographics and engagement trends to develop targeted in-person and virtual outreach strategies, fostering deeper connections with key alumni segments. Establish and assess relevant metrics to evaluate engagement effectiveness, using data insights to refine strategies and optimize outreach. Recommend new initiatives and engagement opportunities based on alumni and donor feedback, leveraging insights to strengthen relationships and enhance involvement. Track expenses and process expense reconciliations adhering to FSU and DUA policies and procedures. May develop and manage an alumni engagement budget or other funds at the discretion of FSU Libraries or UGS. May supervisor one full-time staff position. Stay abreast of the changing landscape within higher education impacting alumni engagement. Other duties as assigned. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and four years' experience or a high school diploma or equivalent and eight years of experience. (Note: or a combination of post high school education and experience equal to eight years.) A valid Florida or Georgia driver's license or the ability to obtain. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . The position is open until filled Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63394&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Associate Director of Student and Alumni Engagement, Student Success Collective/International Programs", "description": "Job Title Associate Director of Student and Alumni Engagement, Student Success Collective/International Programs Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63394 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department FSU Division of University Advancement Florida State University is currently in the leadership phase of a comprehensive campaign. As the leadership phase of the campaign begins, the Division of University Advancement is accelerating the hiring of additional development officers\u2019 campus-wide and is excited to build out its team. For Advancement professionals who are interested in being a part of a comprehensive campaign from the beginning for their career development, the timing is ideal to join our team. Responsibilities The position is responsible for developing, implementing, and managing an alumni engagement plan that supports the Division of University Advancement's goals, leverages the advancement infrastructure of the Student Success Collective (SSC), The Graduate School and International Programs, and adheres to Council for Advancement and Support of Education (CASE) best practices and metrics. It leads college-wide initiatives that foster meaningful connections among students, alumni, donors, parents, friends and volunteers that contribute to philanthropic priorities. The role also oversees collection, maintenance, and strategic use of alumni data. Lead the development and execution of a comprehensive alumni engagement plan for The Graduate School and International Programs, constituents through student and alumni enculturation programming, communications, activities and events. Foster participation in experiential learning, networking, philanthropy, and volunteerism by connecting current students with alumni through mentorship and engagement activities. Partner with Graduate School and International Programs staff to enhance student-alumni interactions through in-person and virtual events. Plan and execute Unit-led events, including conference receptions, Homecoming activities, and outreach programs, ensuring seamless coordination and impactful experiences for alumni and key stakeholders. Align alumni engagement efforts with Graduate School and International Programs fundraising priorities by integrating development goals into outreach programming that supports long-term donor relationships. Collaborate with Graduate School and International Programs development and DUA donor relations teams to manage stewardship touchpoints that strengthen connections with donors and key stakeholders. Support and manage key Graduate School and International Programs alumni volunteers, volunteer groups, or advisory boards/councils, partnering with the development team to foster meaningful involvement, engagement and leadership. This may include contributing to agenda development, conducting research and creating events that inspire and empower volunteer leaders. Recommend alumni for volunteer leadership roles and contribute to donor pipeline development through incorporating best practice for discovery, CRM documentation, and recommending potential donors to development colleagues. Leverage existing DUA programming (e.g., Alumni Affinity Networks, Seminole Clubs, Homecoming activities, Seminole 100 and Alumni Awards) to engage Graduate School and International Programs alumni and ensure Graduate School and International Programs colleagues are aware of programming. Support campus-wide alumni engagement by staffing signature and regional events, recruiting alumni volunteers, submitting alumni award nominations, and encouraging Seminole 100 applications. Curate and amplify compelling stories about Graduate School and International Programs students, alumni and donors. Respond to alumni inquiries. Partner with Graduate School, International Programs, and DUA communications teams to develop an alumni communications plan for that complements central DUA outreach to alumni and donors. Effectively convey key updates, news, and engagement opportunities from Graduate School, International Programs, DUA, and FSU, ensuring meaningful connections to Graduate School and International Programs alumni. May manage and distribute email campaigns for Graduate School and International Programs alumni-facing communications. This may include generating content, creating graphics and collaborating with DUA, Graduate School and International Programs communications team members to develop email marketing strategy. Extracts data files to upload for email distribution lists. Evaluate alumni engagement communications; provide analytics and marketing reports on all aspects of email communications. Serve as the alumni data steward for the Graduate School and International Programs, ensuring compliance with DUA data policies and procedures to maintain accuracy, security and usability, this includes identifying and coding student/alumni participation in key program areas. Analyze alumni demographics and engagement trends to develop targeted in-person and virtual outreach strategies, fostering deeper connections with key alumni segments. Establish and assess relevant metrics to evaluate engagement effectiveness, using data insights to refine strategies and optimize outreach. Recommend new initiatives and engagement opportunities based on alumni and donor feedback, leveraging insights to strengthen relationships and enhance involvement. Track expenses and process expense reconciliations adhering to FSU and DUA policies and procedures. May develop and manage an alumni engagement budget or other funds at the discretion of The Graduate School and International Programs. May supervisor one full-time staff position. Stay abreast of the changing landscape within higher education impacting alumni engagement. Other duties as assigned. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and four years of experience; or a high school diploma or equivalent and eight years of experience. (Note: post-high school education may substitute for experience at the equivalent rate.) A valid Florida or Georgia Driver's License or the ability to obtain upon hire. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63416&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Director of Post Award, Sponsored Research Administration", "description": "Job Title Director of Post Award, Sponsored Research Administration Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63416 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Sponsored Research Administration within the Office of Research seeks to fill the position of Director of Post Award. Responsibilities This position provides strategic leadership for and oversight of Sponsored Research Administration \u2013 Post Award and Cost & Data Management teams including but not limited to: supervision and training/cross-training for staff; post-award modifications; completion of sub-recipient risk monitoring, and invoice submission in alignment with sponsor and/or Uniform Grant Regulations; fiscal review of expenditures for reasonableness and accuracy, institutional commitments (fiscal), securing appropriate internal reviews and approvals; invoicing and collections; submission of interim and final financial reports; FSU response to all internal and external audits; cash management (LOC) drawdowns and reconciliation, indirect costs negotiations; preparation of reports on productivity of the research enterprise, and data quality assurance. This position facilitates and advance research and sponsored project activities through various efforts to include but not limited to promoting SRA as a customer-oriented department; increasing the collegiality between SRA and the campus community; and reviewing and analyzing policies, procedures, and practices with a goal of automating and streamlining and/or reducing administrative burdens to the extent possible. Participate in and lead efforts to deliver and continually improve research and sponsored project related training and educational opportunities for faculty, students and staff. This position keeps abreast of changing regulations to ensure fiscal compliance with sponsor and institutional policies, procedures, and regulatory guidance. Troubleshoot issues with federal, state, and local agencies which are problematic to the administration of sponsored projects. Develop and implement policies as needed for prudent management practices, compliance and accountability relative to sponsored projects administration such as 2 CFR 200, FAR and other state and sponsor regulations. Analyze, interpret and disseminate to the campus community information relative to federal, state, and sponsor regulations to ensure institutional compliance and consult with faculty, staff and administrators regarding compliance and other procedural issues. Provide expertise, guidance and leadership to academic and administrative senior management on compliance and sponsored research administration matters. Build strong relationships with campus administrators, faculty and staff; and work in partnership with other University offices to enhance the institution's research enterprise. Responsible for ensuring the development and operation of appropriate management information systems and databases that are adequate for the administration of post-award activities for the University's research and sponsored project activities including the implementation of new tools to automate office functions. Develop relationships with federal, state, and sponsor representatives and participate in professional development activities and organizations to keep abreast of changes and updates regarding sponsor requirements. Responsible for the formulation and administration of the annual operating budget for SRA Post Award and ensuring appropriate expenditure of all funds allocated. Performs other duties as assigned as it relates to post-award activities Qualifications Masters degree and five years of experience or a Bachelor\u2019s degree and seven years of experience. Preferred Qualifications At least four years of experience in leadership of a post award department is preferred CRA, CPRA, CFRA, or comparable professional certification is preferred. Significant and progressively responsible leadership experience in sponsored research administration with a substantial emphasis on post-award administration. Experience within a large, complex research-intensive university environment, preferably a Carnegie R1 institution. Demonstrated expertise with federal regulations governing sponsored projects, including Uniform Guidance (2 CFR 200) and Federal Acquisition Regulations (FAR), as well as related sponsor requirements and state regulations. Experience leading audit responses, financial compliance programs, cost analysis activities, and institutional policy development. Proven success leading organizational change, process improvement initiatives, and technology-enabled operational enhancements. Experience supervising large teams and developing high-performing staff. Contact Info All applications, nominations, and inquiries are invited. Applications should include, as separate documents, a CV or resume and a letter of interest addressing the themes in this profile. WittKieffer is assisting Florida State University in this search. Applications will be received until the position is filled. We strongly encourage candidates submit their materials as soon as possible for full consideration. Nominations and inquiries can be directed to: Jessica Herrington, Robert Springall, and Roxana Woudstra at FSUDirectorPA@wittkieffer.com . University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63375&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Teaching Faculty I, 12 Month Salaried - Elementary Education - School of Teacher Education - Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences", "description": "Job Title Teaching Faculty I, 12 Month Salaried - Elementary Education - School of Teacher Education - Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63375 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department School of Teacher Education in the Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences Responsibilities Teach undergraduate and graduate courses in the Elementary Education program, including but not limited to content specific methodology courses, Classroom Management, Curriculum Development, and Practitioner Research. Supervise pre-service teachers in K-6 educational settings, and/or various other content and general methods consistent with candidate expertise and program needs. Teach four courses in each of the fall and spring semesters and two courses in the summer. Provide service to K-12 schools, the Elementary Education Program, the College, and the profession. Qualifications Earned doctorate in Elementary Education, Curriculum & Instruction, or a related field. Strong organizational, communication, and interpersonal skills. A minimum of three years teaching experience in K-12 educational settings. Commitment to and experience working with all student populations. Commitment to engaging with best practice initiatives in instruction and pedagogy, mentoring, and curriculum design and development. Preferred Qualifications Experience supervising pre-service teachers in K-6 educational settings Knowledge of and experience with current best practices in instructional strategies/methods in K-6 education consistent with the Elementary program curriculum and Florida education standards. Experience working with English Language Learners Experience mentoring pre-service and in-service teachers Successful teaching of face-to-face and online education courses at the college or university level. Other Information The School of Teacher Education is committed to high quality personnel preparation programs; service to the state of Florida; and high-quality scholarly research in elementary education, early childhood education, reading/language arts, foreign and second language education, special education, blindness and low vision, science education, math education, social science education, English education, and related areas. Programs consistently rank among the best in the nation, particularly the Curriculum & Instruction and Special Education programs. The School strives to provide undergraduate and graduate students with world-class training in teaching, research and professional development. Through the guidance and mentorship of faculty, students graduate to serve as educational leaders who will contribute to the betterment of a pluralistic, global society in the context of the state of Florida's needs for an educated, global-minded citizenry. In addition to mentoring and preparing the next generation of educators, faculty engage in a wide range of research activities. Faculty work routinely appears in prestigious publications and is cited by peers. Recent Academic Analytics National Rankings placed the School of Teacher Education as fifth in the nation for number of articles published and third in article citations. Furthermore, faculty receive support from a robust Office of Research to pursue research opportunities, professional awards, and more. The roots of FSU\u2019s Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences date back to the university\u2019s establishment, and it is the oldest college of its kind in Florida. The College is home to six academic departments united through a common goal to maximize human potential. In total, the College includes the Department of Educational Leadership & Policy Studies, Department of Educational Psychology & Learning Systems, Department of Human Development & Family Sciences, Department of Health, Nutrition & Food Sciences, Department of Sport Management, School of Teacher Education, numerous research centers, and three laboratory schools (Florida State University School, FSU Pembroke Pines Charter School, and The Collegiate School at FSU Panama City). Anne\u2019s College serves over 4,000 students via approximately 200 full-time faculty and nearly 80 full-time staff. For more information about the Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences visit: https://annescollege.fsu.edu/ . Contact Info Laura Bell University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applicants should also include a letter of application, names of three references with contact information, and a statement of teaching interests. Transcripts, work samples (such as teaching artifacts), and three letters of recommendation will be required of candidates selected for an interview. Review of candidates will begin October 19th and will continue until filled. We urge interested candidates to submit materials as soon as possible. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63409&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Assistant Professor 9 Month Salaried (School of Communication Science & Disorders)", "description": "Job Title Assistant Professor 9 Month Salaried (School of Communication Science & Disorders) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63409 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department College of Communication & Information School of Communication Science & Disorders Responsibilities This is a full-time, tenure-track position, with a 9-month appointment; academic year requirements include teaching at the undergraduate and/or graduate level, research and service. Candidates with research experience in voice, swallowing, hearing loss, and/or clinical education leadership are especially encouraged to apply. Qualifications Doctoral degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant Professor. Qualifications for the Assistant Professor rank include: 1. Earned doctorate in communication science and disorders or related areas. 2. Experience with teaching and research. 3. Experience with external grant awards is preferred. Other Information Florida State University is classified by the Carnegie Foundation as a very high research activity institution with outstanding research facilities and infrastructure support. In addition, the state of Florida has recognized Florida State University as one of two preeminent research universities in the state. The School of Communication Science and Disorders is in the College of Communication and Information at Florida State University. Students can earn undergraduate, masters', and doctoral degrees. The masters' program includes both on-campus and distance learning cohorts. The School is consistently ranked number one in Florida and in the top 10% of programs nationally. The environment is highly collaborative with faculty members who have intersecting research interests that include many aspects of clinical, translational, and basic research. The School is located in a newly remodeled stand- alone building with ample space for faculty, research laboratories, and diverse clinical programs. There is an on-site speech, language and hearing clinic, a satellite clinic, and a mobile speech and hearing clinic that services Tallahassee and the surrounding counties. For more information about the School of Communication Science and Disorders, visit our website at http://commdisorders.cci.fsu.edu/ Contact Info Carla Wood Florida State University School of Communication Science and Disorders 201 W. Bloxham Street Tallahassee, FL. 32306-1200 Carla.wood@cci.fsu.edu FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. The School of Communication Science and Disorders at Florida State University invites applications for the position of Assistant Professor beginning Fall 2027. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position is being advertised as open until filled. Application Review will start October 1, 2026. This position requires successful completion of a Level 2 criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=62901&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Laser Safety Officer", "description": "Job Title Laser Safety Officer Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 62901 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Environmental Health and Safety Responsibilities Responsible for implementing and maintaining laser safety programs, which includes training staff, monitoring operations, and ensuring compliance with relevant safety standards and regulations. Responsible for complete knowledge of Federal and State regulations which relate to laser safety in a university environment. Develop and maintain laser safety programs and procedures in compliance with state and national regulations. Ensure all lasers and laser systems are registered and classified according to guidelines set by relevant authorities. Serves as the Certified Laser Safety Officer for the university community. Determines the exposure potential for non-ionizing radiation workers through laser hazard evaluations and protocols. Conducts regular inspections and audits of laser facilities and operations to identify potential hazards and ensure safety measures are in place. Investigate laser-related incidents or accidents, determining the cause and recommending corrective actions. Be well-versed in relevant safety standards and regulations set forth by organizations such as the American National Standards Institute (ANSI), Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA), and the International Electrotechnical Commission (IEC). Manage and monitor the disposal of laser decommissioning and update of laser inventory, in accordance with environmental regulations. Maintain records of laser safety inspections, incidents, training, and equipment maintenance. Ensures compliance with all regulations and ordinances. Performs periodic instrument calibration, adjusting and repairs when necessary. Performs inventory and leak testing of x-ray units in accordance with license conditions and all applicable regulations. Remain constantly vigilant to changes or advances that may have an impact on EH&S related programs through proactive methods such as audits, research, interactions with colleagues at related institutions and by attending professional courses or society meetings. Keep abreast of new developments in laser technology, safety standards, and regulations and incorporate this knowledge into the organization\u2019s safety program. Immediately report any findings that may affect University programs to supervisors and assist in determining and implementing necessary policy changes to ensure best practices are realized. Member of the radiation safety committee and the laser safety subcommittee. Qualifications Bachelor's degree in physics, engineering, health physics, IH, or related scientific field and two years' experience or a high school diploma or equivalent and six years of experience. (Note: or a combination of post high school education and experience equal to six years) Possess a Laser Safety Officer certification or the ability to obtain one within one year of employment. A valid Florida or Georgia driver's license or the ability to obtain one. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being re-advertised. Previous applicants need not apply. This position is open until filled Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63389&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "OAS Testing Center Coordinator (Multiple Positions)", "description": "Job Title OAS Testing Center Coordinator (Multiple Positions) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63389 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Office of Accessibility Services (OAS) Department of Student Support and Transitions (DSST) Florida State University 108 Student Services Building 874 Traditions Way, Tallahassee, Florida 32306-4167 Responsibilities Manages the daily operations of the testing center and supervises OPS proctoring staff. Prepares the facility, exam materials, and equipment for daily use. Ensures equipment is in proper working order. Promotes strong customer service, professionalism, confidentiality, and academic integrity. Guides students and instructors through test service eligibility, setup, and scheduling steps. Including additional support to students requiring special accommodation, such as individual proctoring needs coordination of DAW activities, OAS scholarship programming, and assisting in overseeing programs and services. Maintains the exam registration system and the exam calendar. Make scheduling adjustments and special provisions as able. Troubleshoots, resolves, and reports all issues that occur in the OAS Testing Center. Coordinates expanded OAS operations for final exam week in Fall and Spring semesters. This includes alternative schedules and extended hours. Assists with the development and implementation of internal and external, independent and collaborative programming (e.g., workshops, training, events, orientations, etc.). Including but not limited to: DAW and Graduation/Celebration (internal, OAS Students). Reviews exam policies and procedures to ensure compliance with all national and local proctoring standards. Researches assessment best practices and advises fellow staff accordingly. Completes special research projects to improve assessment services. Performs other duties as assigned that support academic integrity initiatives and the mission of the department. Qualifications Bachelor's and two years of experience or a high school diploma or equivalent and six years or experience. (Note: or a post high school education and experience equal to six years). Contact Info Amber Wagner or Elizabeth Rudisill Office: (850) 644-9566 Fax: (850) 645-1852 Email: oas@fsu.edu Office of Accessibility Services (OAS) University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . The position is open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63381&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Director of Development, College of Social Sciences and Public Policy", "description": "Job Title Director of Development, College of Social Sciences and Public Policy Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63381 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department FSU Division of University Advancement Florida State University is currently in the leadership phase of a comprehensive campaign. As the leadership phase of the campaign begins, the Division of University Advancement is accelerating the hiring of additional development officers\u2019 campus-wide and is excited to build out its team. For Advancement professionals who are interested in being a part of a comprehensive campaign from the beginning for their career development, the timing is ideal to join our team. Responsibilities The Director of Development will strategically execute a personal solicitation program resulting in philanthropic support by maximizing the identification, cultivation, solicitation and stewardship of prospects for gifts at the $100,000 and up level for College of Social Sciences and Public Policy. This individual will secure, on an annual basis, private support at the major and principal gift level and will be responsible for identification of potential major and principal gift prospects. The Director of Development will be expected to uphold and exemplify the operating practices of the Division of University Advancement while raising philanthropic dollars in support of the mission of Florida State University. Works with the Dean, and the other members of the College of Social Sciences and Public Policy development, communication and alumni team to develop and execute strategic fundraising initiatives on behalf of the College and the university. Develops, coordinates, and executes an annual major gift plan, implementing fund-raising activities designed to meet an established monetary goal while also hitting a set suite of metrics. Establishes new relationships resulting in philanthropic investment, maintains existing relationships, which may generate new philanthropic investments, and provides prospect/donor-related assessments and feedback for the College and the Division. Identifies, qualifies and sustains a donor prospect portfolio with individuals who have a giving capacity of $500,000 or more. Travels frequently, and secures gifts and pledges from alumni, parents, faculty, staff, and friends of FSU. Exhibits and promotes a comprehensive understanding of the philanthropic priorities of the College, effectively matching the specific interests of prospects to those needs. Plans for and initiates direct activities with prospects that are designed to enhance the affiliation between the prospect and FSU. Effectively communicates FSU\u2019s mission and represents FSU to external stakeholders. Central Development Collaboration Coordinates with the Division of University Advancement colleagues to identify prospects for planned giving, corporate and foundation giving in partnership with the Office of University Research, and principal giving in partnership with the Principal Gifts Team. Protects confidential information. Perform other related duties as required and assigned. Administrative/Events Assists in the facilitation of meetings, communications, informational exchanges and project / philanthropic coordination with the faculty and faculty chairs. Prepares proposals and gift agreements as required for proper gift documentation. Prepares correspondence with prospects and documents communications, solicitation activity and gift information in compliance with the FSU Foundation\u2019s reporting guidelines. Creates, inspires, and maintains donor loyalty, interest and enthusiasm through stewardship communication and activities designed to express recognition, appreciation and the impact of their gift(s). Implementation of such a stewardship plan may include but should not be limited to letters, communication of unit or university initiatives, invitations to appropriate activities, meetings, events, student engagement or the facilitation of campus visits. Board/Volunteer Management Assists in the management of all volunteer boards associated with the College of Social Sciences and Public Policy. Qualifications Master's degree and four years of experience in a related advancement field or a Bachelor's degree and six years of related experience. Higher education can substitute for experience at a comparable rate. A valid Florida Driver's License or the ability to obtain upon hire. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. This role requires driving and travel. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63327&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried (College of Criminology and Criminal Justice)", "description": "Job Title Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried (College of Criminology and Criminal Justice) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63327 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department College Of Criminology and Criminal Justice The College of Criminology and Criminal Justice at Florida State University is a vibrant academic community which fosters an environment of collaborative research and intellectual stimulation among its faculty and students. The College invites applications for assistant professor positions to begin Fall 2027. The areas of specialization are open. Responsibilities \u2022 Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate administrator of a state university \u2022 Responsible for teaching, research, service, and related administrative activities \u2022 Responsible for academic advising and related activities \u2022 May represent the university, college/school, or department/unit on university and/or Statewide committees Qualifications Applicants must have demonstrated effectiveness in research and teaching. Candidates should have a Ph.D. in Criminology and Criminal Justice or a related field (such as sociology, psychology, or public policy). ABD candidates who anticipate degree completion no later than August 2027 will also be considered. A Juris Doctorate alone is not sufficient for consideration. Contact Info Any questions regarding the position may be directed to search committee chair Sonja Siennick at ssiennick@fsu.edu . University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Interested persons should complete an application and submit a cover letter, statements on research and teaching, and a curriculum vitae. In addition, they should arrange for three letters of recommendation to be sent to CCCJ-SearchCommittee@fsu.edu with the subject line \u201cLetter of Recommendation for [applicant].\u201d Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Review of applications will begin on September 28, 2026, and will continue until the positions are filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63329&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Associate Professor, 9 Month Salaried (College of Criminology and Criminal Justice)", "description": "Job Title Associate Professor, 9 Month Salaried (College of Criminology and Criminal Justice) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63329 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department College of Criminology and Criminal Justice The College of Criminology and Criminal Justice at Florida State University is a vibrant academic community which fosters an environment of collaborative research and intellectual stimulation among its faculty and students. The College invites applications for a tenure-track associate or full professor position to begin Fall 2027. The areas of specialization are open. Responsibilities \u2022 Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate administrator of a state university \u2022 Responsible for teaching, research, service, and related administrative activities \u2022 Responsible for academic advising and related activities \u2022 May represent the university, college/school, or department/unit on university and/or Statewide committees Qualifications Applicants must have demonstrated excellence in research and teaching. Candidates should have a Ph.D. in Criminology and Criminal Justice or a related field (such as sociology, psychology, or public policy). A Juris Doctorate alone is not sufficient for consideration. Review of applications will begin on September 28, 2026. Contact Info Any questions regarding the position may be directed to search committee chair Sonja Siennick at ssiennick@fsu.edu . University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. In addition, you should arrange for three letters of recommendation to be sent to CCCJ-SearchCommittee@fsu.edu with the subject line \u201cLetter of Recommendation for [applicant].\u201d Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Review of applications will begin on September 28, 2026, and will continue until the positions are filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63299&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried (Molecular Biodesign)", "description": "Job Title Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried (Molecular Biodesign) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63299 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Chemistry & Biochemistry | College of Arts & Sciences Responsibilities The Department of Chemistry & Biochemistry seeks to fill a tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor at the intersection of chemistry, biology, and medicine. Leveraging the resources of the Institute of Molecular Biophysics (IMB), this search is open to all areas of the chemical sciences with a focus on molecular biodesign, including biochemistry, organic chemistry, medicinal chemistry, bioanalytical chemistry, chemical biology, bioinorganic chemistry, and biophysical chemistry. Outstanding candidates are sought to pursue innovative experimental research that advances the molecular understanding of biological systems and enables the discovery and development of new therapeutics. The successful candidate will be expected to develop a nationally and internationally recognized and externally funded research program in addition to teaching undergraduate and graduate courses. Qualifications A doctoral degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in a related field with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service is required. Candidates whose research incorporates artificial intelligence and machine learning are encouraged to apply. Contact Info Questions may be directed to the Faculty Search Team . University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applications must include the following: Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Research Prospectus Teaching Statement Applicants should also arrange for three letters of recommendation to be sent via email to The Faculty Search Team . Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Application review will begin on October 19, 2026. This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63298&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried (Theoretical/Computational Chemistry & Biochemistry) - Multiple Positions", "description": "Job Title Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried (Theoretical/Computational Chemistry & Biochemistry) - Multiple Positions Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63298 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Chemistry & Biochemistry | College of Arts & Sciences Responsibilities The Department of Chemistry & Biochemistry at Florida State University seeks candidates for two tenure-track faculty positions at the rank of Assistant Professor in theoretical/computational chemistry and biochemistry. One position is open to all areas of theory and computation relevant to the chemical and biochemical sciences. The second position will focus on leveraging advances in artificial intelligence (AI) and machine learning (ML) for chemistry and biochemistry, broadly defined. Applications where AI/ML work is complemented by experimental validation are also encouraged. The successful candidates will be expected to develop nationally and internationally recognized and externally funded research programs in addition to teaching undergraduate and graduate courses. Qualifications A doctoral degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in a related field with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service is required. Contact Info Questions may be directed to the Faculty Search Team . University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applications must include the following: Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Research Prospectus Teaching Statement Applicants should also arrange for three letters of recommendation to be sent via email to The Faculty Search Team . Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Review of applications will begin on October 16, 2026. This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63287&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried (Accounting Department - Herbert Wertheim College of Business) - Fall 2027", "description": "Job Title Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried (Accounting Department - Herbert Wertheim College of Business) - Fall 2027 Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63287 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Accounting | Herbert Wertheim College of Business Responsibilities Florida State University, Department of Accounting, invites applications for a tenure-track assistant professor position beginning August 2027. This position will be required to publish in leading scholarly journals, along with teaching undergraduate and graduate courses. You will also continue research efforts and progress towards promotion and tenure. Qualifications All candidates should have a Ph.D. in Accounting. Preferred Qualifications Candidates must demonstrate an ability to publish in leading scholarly journals and a commitment to excellence in teaching. All areas of research and teaching expertise will be considered. Applicants with a professional background in financial planning may have an opportunity to teach a specialized wealth management course and should note this in their applications. Contact Info Allen Blay Department Chair University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applicants should submit their curriculum vitae, at least one working paper, and three reference letters by email to acctg-recruiting1@business.fsu.edu . Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=62884&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Grants Officer Open Level (Multiple Vacancies)", "description": "Job Title Grants Officer Open Level (Multiple Vacancies) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 62884 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Sponsored Research Administration | Pre-Award Responsibilities Grants Officer I This entry-level position will advise and assist faculty and staff in pre-award and post-award non-financial sponsored research, instruction, and public service activities, including proposal preparation, review, submission, and tracking of sponsored research, instruction, and public service activities from public sources. Negotiate basic agreements by serving as the primary liaison with funding/sponsoring agencies. Review sub-recipient documents and determine contract/vendor relationships. Accept awards and coordinate post-award non-financial activities. Maintain regular contact with principal investigators, deans, chairs, departmental administrators, and funding agency officials regarding interpretation and application, and procedures. Grants Officer II This intermediate-level position will advise and assist faculty and staff in pre-award and post-award nonfinancial sponsored research, instruction, and public service activities, including, but not limited to, proposal preparation, review, submission, and tracking of sponsored research, instruction, and public service activities from public sources. Negotiate basic and complex agreements by serving as the primary liaison with funding/sponsoring agencies. Review sub-recipient documents. Accept awards and coordinate post-award non-financial activities. Maintain regular contact with principal investigators, deans, chairs, departmental administrators, and funding agency officials regarding interpretation, application, and procedures. Grants Officer III This advanced-level position will advise and assist faculty and staff in pre-award and post-award non-financial sponsored research, instruction, and public service activities, including, but not limited to, proposal preparation, review, submission, and tracking of sponsored research, instruction, and public service activities from public sources. Negotiate basic and complex agreements by serving as the primary liaison with funding/sponsoring agencies. Review sub-recipient documents. Accept awards and coordinate post award non-financial activities. Maintain regular contact with principal investigators, deans, chairs, departmental administrators, and funding agency officials regarding interpretation, application, and procedures. Mentor staff. Have a limited delegation of signature authority for the Vice President for Research. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and two years of experience; or a high school diploma/equivalent and six years of relevant experience. (Note: a combination of post high school education and experience equal to six years.) Level I - Bachelor\u2019s degree and 2 years\u2019 experience or a combination of post high school education and experience equal to 6 years. Level II - Bachelor\u2019s degree and 3 years\u2019 experience or a combination of post high school education and experience equal to 7 years. Level III - Bachelor\u2019s degree and 4 years\u2019 experience or a combination of post high school education and experience equal to 8 years plus CRA certification. These positions require successful completion of the eSPEAR certification series within the first six months from the start date. Preferred Qualifications Experience and the ability to communicate effectively verbally and in writing. Ability to comprehend and interpret state, federal, and sponsoring agencies' rules, regulations, policies, and laws regarding sponsored research. Ability to work effectively in a fast-paced, changing environment and to interact with people at all levels diplomatically, tactfully, and professionally. Preferred experience with contract review and negotiations (e.g., FAR clauses, federal contracting, SBIRs, and STTRs). Helpful Who is the ideal candidate for this position? You will be known as the go-to person for a specific department range within SRA. You have a good rapport with others and can work closely with department representatives, faculty members, and colleagues in SRA via telephone, Zoom/Teams, and e-mail. You will also work directly with grants/contracts/administrative officers at a sponsor (e.g., FL Department of Health, National Science Foundation), which likewise requires diplomacy, tact, and good communication skills for resolving issues and negotiating. You are detail-oriented and analytical, as well as a good multitasker and problem solver. You enjoy learning something new every day. You are both a team player and an independent worker. What is a typical day in this position? Every day can be different. One day, you may be submitting several proposals and setting up award time extensions while, the next day, you could be reviewing and negotiating contracts, reviewing a budget and budget justification for an upcoming proposal, and reaching out to a faculty member about their upcoming amendment for time and money. You will attend team meetings regularly and a full staff meeting monthly. If you enjoy working in a medium-sized department, which is a collegial professional and has you learning something new all of the time, you'll be happy in SRA. There are many training opportunities that can be attended virtually and in person. What can I expect in the first 60 \u2013 90 days? In the first few weeks, you will meet your team and the entire SRA staff. Our IT team will make sure you are up and running usually by the end of your first day. Then, you will be able to get acquainted with our website and our policies and procedures. You will be shadowing and working closely with team members, completing the eSPEAR Certificate Series online training, and starting to work on certain tasks independently. At the 6-month mark, you will notice that you've learned much and are comfortable in your position. Our staff is always available to answer any questions you may have while learning your new position. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. A cover letter must be provided to be considered for this position. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is based in Tallahassee and is eligible for a hybrid work schedule. The schedule is Monday-Friday 8:00 AM-5:00 PM. This position is being advertised as open until filled. Applications will be reviewed as received. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=61131&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Faculty Psychologist (Two Positions) \u2013 Clinical Assistant Professor, 12 Month Salaried (Student Affairs/Admissions - Medicine)", "description": "Job Title Faculty Psychologist (Two Positions) \u2013 Clinical Assistant Professor, 12 Month Salaried (Student Affairs/Admissions - Medicine) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 61131 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department College of Medicine, Student Affairs/Admissions Responsibilities The FSU College of Medicine (COM) Office of Student Counseling Services provides psychological and educational support services to graduate students in the Medicine, Physician Assistant, Bridge to Medicine, and Biomedical Sciences programs. The faculty psychologist will be responsible for providing individual therapy and personal counseling to matriculated students for general mental health concerns, adjustment disorders, personal stressors, and the promotion of well-being; for advising students and developing strategies to address academic deficiencies and to facilitate academic success; for the initial evaluation, screening, and referral as appropriate of matriculated students for psychiatric care; and for developing and managing a network of referral relationships with qualified practitioners who can provide additional services for students if required. All services are provided on-site in the FSU COM via in-person or telehealth scheduled appointments. As faculty, the incumbent will be expected to be active in teaching, clinical service, and research consistent with the College of Medicine's mission. Qualifications Applicants must hold a doctoral degree from an American Psychological Association (APA)-approved counseling or clinical psychology program to include an APA-approved pre-doctoral internship and Florida licensure as a psychologist, or eligibility to obtain within 90 days of employment. Preferred Qualifications At least two years of experience in counseling or clinical psychology, with a minimum of one year of post-doctoral clinical experience in individual and group counseling, to include psychological assessments, and/or consultations. Strong oral and written communication skills. Preference given to candidates with postdoctoral work experience with college students or with young adults in a health science setting and/or experience providing academic support services. Doctorate level training in the science of learning, including educational psychology or school psychology. Helpful Who is an ideal candidate for the role? This role is ideal for a team-oriented candidate looking for an opportunity to work in a small office with three psychologists and one administrative support employee in a collaborative environment. The candidate must enjoy and be passionate about providing clinical services to the graduate student population, which includes not only therapy services but also academic support services. What is a typical day? A typical day primarily involves provision of direct service (academic and/or mental health support) to College of Medicine graduate students in individual appointments. Some group services may be provided in either an academic or therapy context. This faculty position also includes a small percentage of scholarly and teaching responsibilities. Contact Info Taylor Thompson, Ph.D. 850/644-0492 tlthompson@admin.fsu.edu University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. Anticipated Salary Range This position is expected to offer a salary in the range of $95,000 \u2013 $105,000; however, final compensation will be determined based on experience and qualifications. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our interactive too l to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://hr.fsu.edu/facultyjobs. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . The job opening serves to recruit for two non-tenure earning positions. There is no remote work option for these positions. This job opening is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=59627&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Family Physician/Open Rank Professor, 12 Month Salaried \u2013 Multiple Positions (Family Medicine & Rural Health - Medicine - Tallahassee, FL)", "description": "Job Title Family Physician/Open Rank Professor, 12 Month Salaried \u2013 Multiple Positions (Family Medicine & Rural Health - Medicine - Tallahassee, FL) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 59627 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department College of Medicine, Family Medicine & Rural Health Responsibilities The Department of Family Medicine and Rural Health is seeking academic family medicine physicians to fill full-time 12-month open rank faculty positions at a minimum rank of either Assistant or Associate Professor, dependent upon qualifications and experience. This is a clinical position and is not tenure-earning eligible. The positions will involve substantial teaching and supervision of health professional students as well as assisting in the delivery of an innovative, integrated curriculum and practice in a clinical facility. The positions will include around 40% direct patient care at an affiliated primary care practice (credentialing required). The Department has research interests in the areas of health equity, community health, rural health, and innovative health care. Qualifications Applicants must have a doctoral degree (MD or DO) in an appropriate field from an accredited institution and personal and professional goals which are consistent with the mission of the FSU College of Medicine. Applicants must have completed an approved U.S. Residency Program. Applicants must have Board Certification in Family Medicine or other acceptable discipline and participate in maintenance of certification. Applicants should have relevant academic, clinical, and professional experience, excellent skills in communication and collaboration, and be passionate about the field of family medicine and rural health. Additional specific requirements and qualifications include: Must possess, or obtain within 90 days of hire, a valid Florida license to practice medicine in accordance with Chapter 458, Florida Statutes. Current Basic Life Support (BLS) Healthcare Provider Certification by a certifying agency, or the ability to obtain prior to hire. Ability to foster an educational environment conducive to patient-centered medical student and physician assistant education. Demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Post-job offer, but prior to hire, the following will be required: Documentation of current PPD (Purified Protein Derivative) test as performed by a qualified physician reporting negative results within the past six months. Documentation of physical examination completed by a qualified healthcare provider/physician within the past six months. Within 30 days of hire, must provide: Documentation of vaccination for Tetanus within the last 10 years. Proof of immunization OR positive titers for Hepatitis B. Preferred Qualifications Experience in teaching medical students and primary care research is highly desired. Clinical experience post-residency/fellowship is desired. Scholarly interest, knowledge and experience with health equity or community-based health outcomes or clinical research is desired. Knowledge and experience with medical informatics is desired. Other Information The Florida State University College of Medicine (FSU COM) has a focused mission of training patient-centered physicians devoted to the needs of rural, underserved, minority, and elderly populations. FSU COM is very \u201cFamily Medicine friendly\u201d with family physicians holding several key administrative positions including Dean of the College. As a community-based medical school, FSU COM is particularly well-suited for conducting research in primary care and community settings. Contact Info Ms. Ute Sartin, Assistant Director, Email: ute.sartin@med.fsu.edu Ms. Danyel White, Sr. Administrative Specialist, Email: danyel.white@med.fsu.edu University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our interactive too l to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://hr.fsu.edu/facultyjobs. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applications should include the following: Cover letter of interest Curriculum vitae Letters of Reference (refer to steps below) 2 - 3 page teaching, mentoring, and service statement that describes prior experiences and future plans 2 - 3 page research statement that briefly summarizes your significant research accomplishments and describes your future research plans Request Letters of Reference This position requires that you have 3 - 4 confidential professional letters of recommendation submitted on your behalf. Follow the steps below to request these letters through our system: 1) After submitting your application, click the Explore Jobs link; 2) Click the My References link; 3) Click the Send/View Reference Request button next to the appropriate position; and 4) Follow the steps on that page to send your references a system generated email requesting they submit a letter of recommendation on your behalf. You may also return to the My References link and click on \"Send/View Reference Request\" to see if your references have responded, add additional references, or resend requests. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. Applications will be reviewed as received. This job opening serves to recruit for two positions. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=61261&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Open Rank Professor, 12 Months Salaried (Geriatrics - Medicine)", "description": "Job Title Open Rank Professor, 12 Months Salaried (Geriatrics - Medicine) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 61261 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department College of Medicine, Geriatrics Responsibilities The Department of Geriatrics is seeking an academic geriatric physician to fill a full-time 12-month open-rank faculty position at a minimum rank of either Assistant or Associate Professor, dependent upon qualifications and experience. The position will involve substantial teaching and supervision of health professional students as well as assisting in the delivery of an innovative, integrated curriculum and practice in a clinical facility. The positions will include around 50% direct patient care at an affiliated primary care practice (credentialing required). The Department has research interests in the areas of geriatrics workforce enhancement and geriatric syndromes. Qualifications Applicants must have a doctoral degree (MD or DO) in an appropriate field from an accredited institution; a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service; and personal and professional goals that are consistent with the mission of the FSU College of Medicine. Applicants must have completed an approved U.S. Residency Program. Applicants must have Board Certification in Geriatric Medicine, or the ability to obtain within one year of hire and participate in maintenance of certification. Must possess or obtain a valid Florida license to practice medicine in accordance with Chapter 458, Florida Statutes. Ability to foster an educational environment conducive to patient-centered medical students, physician assistants and other healthcare students' education. Preferred Qualifications Experience in teaching healthcare students is highly desired. Relevant academic, clinical, and professional experience; excellent skills in communication and collaboration; and be passionate about the field of geriatric medicine. Contact Info Regina Scott: regina.scott@med.fsu.edu University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our interactive too l to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://hr.fsu.edu/facultyjobs. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This is a clinician-educator position and is not tenure-earning eligible. This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=60738&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Standardized Patient Coordinator (Clinical Learning Center - Medicine)", "description": "Job Title Standardized Patient Coordinator (Clinical Learning Center - Medicine) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 60738 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department College of Medicine, Clinical Learning Center Responsibilities Coordinates all aspects of the Standardized Patient (SP) Program in the Clinical Learning Center (CLC) to provide encounters that allow students/residents to practice and be evaluated. Oversees and assists with orientation, training, evaluation and quality improvement and assurance of the SPs by monitoring SP portrayal and documentation accuracy and counseling to improve performance. Manages data within the SP Program to include the collection and analysis of data, preparation of reports and payments, assessing SP performance and provisions of data to faculty evaluation of student performance. Maintains and prints reports as requested by the Director of the CLC. Assists in preparing for, and coordinating, the CLC and FOSCE (formative objective student clinical examination)/OSCE (objective student clinical examination) sessions, as requested by the Director of the CLC, including software programming for student and faculty evaluation. Assists with Outreach & Advising SSTRIDE Summer Camp; provides visiting groups with tours of facilities including Harvey sessions and interactions as health care providers, etc. Responsible for exam rooms being equipped with appropriate books, medical supplies and equipment and maintains sufficient inventory levels. Performs outreach marketing services to increase awareness of SP Program at FSU College of Medicine. In addition, recruits and manages the SPs. Promotes an atmosphere of teamwork in accomplishing the mission and goals of the FSU COM to include participating in the delivery of academic support services for special projects or in meeting key departmental deadlines. Other related duties as deemed by the Director of the CLC. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and two years of experience; or high school diploma/equivalent experience equal to six years. (Note: post-high school education can substitute for experience at the equivalent rate.) Contact Info Debra Danforth (debra.danforth@med.fsu.edu) Main number (850) 644-9800 University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. Anticipated Salary Range Low $50,000\u2019s, commensurate with experience/education. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our interactive too l to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being readvertised as Open Until Filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63230&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Postdoctoral Research Associate \u2013 Computational Solid Mechanics at the FAMU\u2013FSU College of Engineering", "description": "Job Title Postdoctoral Research Associate \u2013 Computational Solid Mechanics at the FAMU\u2013FSU College of Engineering Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63230 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The FAMU-FSU College of Engineering Responsibilities The successful candidate will join a highly interdisciplinary team of engineers, computer scientists, applied mathematicians, and computational scientists to develop next-generation computational methods, publish in leading journals and conferences, mentor graduate students, and contribute to major federally funded research initiatives. Develop next-generation numerical methods for computational solid mechanics. Design and implement robust finite element algorithms for nonlinear mechanics problems. Develop AI-enabled acceleration strategies for nonlinear finite element analysis and large-scale computational mechanics. Develop novel iterative solvers, multigrid methods, Krylov subspace algorithms, learned preconditioners, and nonlinear solution strategies for large-scale mechanics problems. Develop scalable computational algorithms for large-scale engineering and biomedical simulations Advance the state of the art in computational solid mechanics, scientific computing, numerical linear algebra, and scientific machine learning. Conduct large-scale computational simulations and analyze numerical results. Publish research in leading journals and conferences in computational mechanics, scientific computing, applied mathematics, and computational engineering. Collaborate with researchers across engineering, computer science, applied mathematics, and biomedical engineering. Contribute to competitive research proposals to federal agencies and private foundations. Mentor graduate and undergraduate researchers. Qualifications Ph.D. in Mechanical Engineering, Aerospace Engineering, Computer Science, Biomedical Engineering, Applied Mathematics, or a closely related discipline. Strong background in computational solid mechanics, finite element methods, scientific computing, numerical methods, or computer graphics. Excellent programming skills in C/C++ and Python, with experience developing large-scale scientific software. Experience with object-oriented software development and modern software engineering practices. Demonstrated record of scholarly publications in high-quality conferences and peer-reviewed journals. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively in interdisciplinary research environments. Preferred Qualifications Experience with nonlinear finite element methods and computational mechanics. Experience with iterative solvers, multigrid methods, Krylov subspace methods, preconditioning techniques, and nonlinear solution algorithms. Experience developing scientific machine learning, AI-based acceleration techniques, or learned numerical methods for computational mechanics. Experience with reduced-order modeling, multiscale methods, uncertainty quantification, or high-performance scientific computing. Experience developing computational simulation, visualization, or interactive software systems. Experience mentoring graduate or undergraduate researchers. Other Information About the College of Engineering Located in Tallahassee, Florida, the FAMU\u2013FSU College of Engineering is the nation's only jointly operated college of engineering, combining the complementary strengths of Florida State University and Florida A&M University. The College offers an exceptionally collaborative and interdisciplinary research environment with internationally recognized expertise in artificial intelligence, computational science, quantum science and engineering, advanced manufacturing, biomedical engineering, high-performance computing, and materials research. Faculty and students benefit from close collaborations with the National High Magnetic Field Laboratory, the Center for Advanced Power Systems, regional healthcare partners, and a growing network of federal laboratories and industry collaborators. Helpful The NexCom Laboratory (Laboratory for Next-Generation Computation) at the FAMU\u2013FSU College of Engineering invites applications for a Postdoctoral Research Associate in Computational Surgery. The NexCom Laboratory develops next-generation computational methods that integrate scientific computing, artificial intelligence, and emerging computational paradigms to solve challenging problems in engineering, medicine, and science. Our research spans computational mechanics, scientific computing, computer graphics, machine learning, computational modeling, and quantum computing, with an emphasis on developing transformative computational technologies with real-world impact. Our research focuses on nonlinear computational solid mechanics, finite element methods, scientific machine learning, iterative and nonlinear solvers, multigrid methods, Krylov subspace methods, reduced-order modeling, multiscale modeling, and high-performance scientific computing. We are particularly interested in developing AI-enabled acceleration strategies that improve the convergence, efficiency, robustness, and scalability of numerical algorithms for large-scale nonlinear mechanics problems. Contact Info Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Questions about the position should be directed to Dr. Suvranu De , Search Committee Chair. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an OPS/temporary job. Based on the duties, this position may require completion of a criminal history background check . This position is open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63217&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Psychiatrist, Clinical Director | FSU BehavioralHealth", "description": "Job Title Psychiatrist, Clinical Director | FSU BehavioralHealth Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63217 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department FSU College of Medicine | Florida Medical Practice Plan, Inc. FSU BehavioralHealth\u2122 2507 Callaway Rd. Tallahassee, FL 32303 Responsibilities Provide quality outpatient psychiatric medical care that aligns with the College of Medicine's mission, goals, and objectives, while adhering to current standards of psychiatric practice. Demonstrate clinical leadership and collaboration in support of patient care, education, and program development, with experience in academic medicine. Document patient history, mental and emotional state, diagnostic evaluation, treatment and disposition and clinically appropriate and timely coding for insurance reimbursement in the patient's Electronic Medical Record. Complete clinically appropriate and timely coding for accurate insurance reimbursement including treatment plan as required. Serves as Practice Clinical Director for FSU BehavioralHealth\u2122, providing leadership and oversight for patient care, safety, quality improvement, clinic operations, and patient experience. Acts as a primary resource for clinicians, collaborates with Practice Managers on operational and budgetary matters, and fosters positive clinician and staff relationships. Oversees clinician meetings, performance management, supervision, coverage, and call schedules. Ensures compliance with regulatory and reimbursement requirements and supports the development of clinical protocols, policies, emergency procedures, and quality improvements initiatives. Provides comprehensive psychiatric care by evaluating patients, diagnosing mental health conditions, developing treatment plans, and coordinating referrals when needed. Collaborates with multidisciplinary healthcare teams to support patient care, monitor treatment progress, and provide patient education, counseling, and appropriate diagnostic testing. May also serve as a clinical preceptor for students and residents and provide consultation to Psychiatric Advanced Practice Registered Nurses (APRNs). Qualifications Doctoral degree (MD or DO) and completion of necessary internship, three years of psychiatric residency, and one year of post-residency in psychiatry. Valid licensure in Florida in accordance with Chapter 458, Florida Statutes; or licensed in another state with the ability to obtain FL Licensure within 30 days of hire. Valid Board Certification in Psychiatric Medicine or appropriate discipline. Current Federal DEA license. Current Basic Life Support (BLS) Healthcare Provider Certification by certifying agency, or the ability to obtain prior to hire. Post-job offer, but prior to hire, the following is required: Current PPD (Purified Protein Derivative) test as performed by a qualified physician from within the past 6 months. Physical examination completed by a qualified healthcare provider/physician from within the past 6 months. Within 30 days of hire, you must provide: Documentation of vaccination for Tetanus within the last 10 years. Proof of immunization OR positive titers for Hepatitis B. Preferred Qualifications Experience in clinical leadership, especially within academic medicine settings. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63235&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Research Faculty I,12 month Salaried (Quantum Scientific Computing-FAMU\u2013FSU College of Engineering)", "description": "Job Title Research Faculty I,12 month Salaried (Quantum Scientific Computing-FAMU\u2013FSU College of Engineering) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63235 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The NexCom Laboratory (Laboratory for Next-Generation Computation) at the FAMU\u2013FSU College of Engineering invites applications for a Research Faculty I position in Quantum Scientific Computing. Responsibilities The successful candidate will play a key role in building a nationally recognized research program in Quantum Scientific Computing. The position offers the opportunity to conduct cutting-edge interdisciplinary research, develop externally funded research programs, build collaborations across engineering, mathematics, computer science, and quantum information science, supervise graduate students and postdoctoral researchers, and help establish the NexCom Laboratory as a leader in next-generation computational science. Develop novel quantum algorithms for scientific computing and engineering applications. Investigate opportunities for quantum advantage in computational mechanics, scientific computing, and engineering simulation. Develop scalable quantum algorithms for finite element methods, linear systems, eigenvalue problems, optimization, and multiscale simulation. Develop algorithms for both NISQ and fault-tolerant quantum computing (FTQC) architectures. Advance modern quantum algorithmic frameworks, including block encoding, QSVT, and quantum linear algebra. Develop quantum machine learning (QML) and hybrid quantum-classical methods for engineering and scientific computing. Implement, benchmark, and evaluate algorithms using state-of-the-art quantum software frameworks and quantum hardware platforms. Collaborate with researchers across engineering, computer science, mathematics, physics, and quantum information science. Lead and contribute to competitive research proposals to federal agencies, industry, and private foundations. Publish research findings in leading journals and conferences. Supervise graduate students, postdoctoral researchers, and research staff. Qualifications Ph.D. in Mechanical Engineering, Aerospace Engineering, Applied Mathematics, Computer Science, Physics, Electrical Engineering, Computational Science, or a closely related discipline. Demonstrated expertise in scientific computing, computational mathematics, numerical linear algebra, or computational mechanics. Demonstrated knowledge of quantum computing, quantum algorithms, or quantum information science. Strong programming skills in Python and C/C++. Experience with quantum software frameworks such as Qiskit, PennyLane, Cirq, Classiq, or similar platforms. Demonstrated record of scholarly publications in high-quality conferences and peer-reviewed journals. Demonstrated ability to develop innovative research ideas and work collaboratively in interdisciplinary research environments. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Preferred Qualifications Experience developing quantum algorithms for scientific computing, computational mechanics, or engineering applications. Experience with quantum machine learning, variational quantum algorithms, hybrid quantum-classical algorithms, or quantum optimization. Background in finite element methods, computational mechanics, scientific computing, numerical linear algebra, or high-performance computing. Experience using cloud-based quantum computing platforms and current quantum hardware. Experience developing externally funded research proposals. Experience mentoring graduate students, postdoctoral researchers, or research staff. Other Information About the College of Engineering Located in Tallahassee, Florida, the FAMU\u2013FSU College of Engineering is the nation's only jointly operated college of engineering, combining the complementary strengths of Florida State University and Florida A&M University. The College offers an exceptionally collaborative and interdisciplinary research environment with internationally recognized expertise in artificial intelligence, computational science, quantum science and engineering, advanced manufacturing, biomedical engineering, high-performance computing, and materials research. Faculty and students benefit from close collaborations with the National High Magnetic Field Laboratory, the Center for Advanced Power Systems, regional healthcare partners, and a growing network of federal laboratories and industry collaborators. Helpful The NexCom Laboratory develops next-generation computational methods that integrate scientific computing, artificial intelligence, and emerging computational paradigms to solve challenging problems in engineering, medicine, and science. Our research spans computational mechanics, scientific computing, machine learning, computational modeling, computer graphics, and quantum computing, with an emphasis on developing transformative computational technologies with real-world impact. Quantum Scientific Computing is an emerging interdisciplinary field at the intersection of quantum computing, scientific computing, applied mathematics, and computational science. Our research seeks to discover and exploit quantum advantages for computationally intensive problems arising in engineering, physics, and data science. We investigate both Noisy Intermediate-Scale Quantum (NISQ) and Fault-Tolerant Quantum Computing (FTQC) paradigms, developing algorithms that deliver practical performance gains on near-term quantum hardware while laying the theoretical foundations for scalable quantum scientific computing on future fault-tolerant quantum computers. Current research focuses on quantum algorithms for finite element analysis, computational mechanics, scientific computing, linear systems, eigenvalue problems, reduced-order modeling, multiscale methods, quantum machine learning (QML), and quantum optimization. Emphasis is placed on modern quantum algorithmic frameworks, including block encoding, Quantum Singular Value Transformation (QSVT), quantum linear algebra, and hybrid quantum-classical algorithms. Our goal is to identify, develop, and demonstrate quantum algorithms that provide meaningful quantum advantages for engineering and scientific computing problems across both NISQ and FTQC architectures. Contact Info Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Questions about the position should be directed to Dr. Suvranu De, Search Committee Chair, at sde@eng.famu.fsu.edu . University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range This is a 12-month, permanent, non-tenure-track faculty appointment at Florida State University with a competitive salary and benefits package. The starting date for this position is negotiable. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applications should include the following documents: A letter of interest Most current curriculum vitae A research statement The names and contact information of three references Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63236&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Open Rank Tenure Track 9 Month Salaried (Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering Florida A&M University - Florida State University College of Engineering)", "description": "Job Title Open Rank Tenure Track 9 Month Salaried (Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering Florida A&M University - Florida State University College of Engineering) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63236 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The Department of Electrical & Computer Engineering (ECE) at the Florida A&M University (FAMU)-Florida State University (FSU) College of Engineering invites applications from highly qualified individuals for multiple tenure-track faculty positions in Computer Engineering in Tallahassee, Florida. Responsibilities Successful candidates are expected to develop research programs that are internationally recognized with significant and sustained funding, incorporate interdisciplinary collaboration with researchers across campus, have a strong commitment to teaching excellence in undergraduate and graduate courses, supervise undergraduate, graduate and post-doctoral researchers, and participate in college and professional service. Qualifications Candidates must possess an earned Ph.D. in computer engineering, computer science, electrical engineering, or a closely related discipline, and demonstrate documented potential for outstanding research. Helpful The ECE Department currently has 37 faculty, 100+ graduate students, 450+ undergraduate students, and annual research expenditures exceeding $20M. The two universities and outstanding research facilities in the affiliated research buildings/centers provide opportunities for collaboration with faculty in Computer Science and Scientific Computing, the Center for Advanced Power Systems (CAPS) , FAMU Center for Cyber Security , National High Magnetic Field Laboratory (NHMFL ), Center for Intelligent Systems, Control and Robotics (CISCOR) , FSU Institute of Molecular Biophysics , FSU Jim Moran College of Entrepreneurship , and FSU College of Medicine . The FAMU-FSU College of Engineering is the nexus of two major public universities, each with a distinct mission but focused on world-class engineering education and research. Created by the Florida Legislature in 1982, the joint organization is the college of engineering for both Florida A&M and Florida State universities. This unique combination of focus, resources and mission from our parent organization has created on our campus a truly innovative atmosphere that leverages the benefits of the traditional HBCU model with the innovations of an R-1 public research university. After completing pre-requisites at their home organization, FAMU and FSU students learn, study and research together at our independent campus with joint-appointed faculty and staff. Students graduate from their enrolling university and from the FAMU-FSU College of Engineering. Both FAMU and FSU are part of the State University System of Florida and are accredited by the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools Commission on Colleges. Additionally, all seven (7) of the college\u2019s eligible undergraduate degree programs are accredited by the Engineering Accreditation Commission of ABET . Contact Info Applications will be reviewed beginning on December 1, 2026. Acceptance and review of applications will continue until the position is filled. The appointment is anticipated to begin in August 2027. Any questions about the position should be directed to Dr. Rodney Roberts, Search Committee Chair, at rroberts@eng.famu.fsu.edu University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include: A cover letter A full curriculum vitae A 2 to 3-page research statement including research interests and plans and how the proposed research efforts will connect to other efforts in the department and universities. A 1-page statement on teaching and philosophy No more than four selected publications for review The names and contact information of four potential references Faculty Information We are seeking faculty members with expertise in Computer Networks Security, Data Science, AI, Computer Vision, Robotics & Autonomy, Embedded Computing, and Cyber-physical Systems Security. This position is at the assistant level, but well-qualified candidates will be considered at a higher rank. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Position is open until filled Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63224&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Postdoctoral Research Associate-Department of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering at the Florida A&M University-Florida State University College of Engineering", "description": "Job Title Postdoctoral Research Associate-Department of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering at the Florida A&M University-Florida State University College of Engineering Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63224 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering Responsibilities The successful candidate will work within a highly interdisciplinary team of engineers, computer scientists, surgeons, and medical educators to develop novel computational methods, publish in leading journals and conferences, mentor graduate students, and contribute to the development of major externally funded research initiatives. Develop novel AI and computer vision algorithms for objective assessment of surgical technical performance from video. Design and evaluate next-generation video foundation models for surgical skill assessment. Develop explainable AI methods that generate clinically meaningful and actionable formative feedback. Develop multimodal computational methods that integrate video, motion, and other data sources to improve assessment accuracy. Investigate longitudinal models of surgical skill acquisition and performance. Collaborate with surgeons and medical educators to validate computational methods using clinical and simulated surgical datasets. Publish research in leading journals and conferences in artificial intelligence, computer vision, biomedical engineering, and surgical education. Contribute to the preparation of competitive proposals to federal agencies and private foundations. Mentor graduate and undergraduate researchers. Qualifications Ph.D. in Computer Science, Mechanical Engineering, Electrical Engineering, Biomedical Engineering, or a closely related discipline. Strong background in artificial intelligence, machine learning, computer vision, or computational science Excellent programming skills in Python and experience with modern machine learning frameworks such as PyTorch, TensorFlow, or Scikit-learn. Demonstrated record of scholarly publications in high-quality conferences and peer-reviewed journals. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively in interdisciplinary research environments. Preferred Qualifications Experience with video understanding, video foundation models, vision-language models, self-supervised learning, or explainable AI. Experience with biomedical imaging, healthcare data, or human performance analysis. Experience mentoring graduate or undergraduate researchers. Other Information About the College of Engineering Located in Tallahassee, Florida, the FAMU\u2013FSU College of Engineering is the nation's only jointly operated college of engineering, combining the complementary strengths of Florida State University and Florida A&M University. The College offers an exceptionally collaborative and interdisciplinary research environment with internationally recognized expertise in artificial intelligence, computational science, quantum science and engineering, advanced manufacturing, biomedical engineering, high-performance computing, and materials research. Faculty and students benefit from close collaborations with the National High Magnetic Field Laboratory, the Center for Advanced Power Systems, regional healthcare partners, and a growing network of federal laboratories and industry collaborators. Helpful The NexCom Laboratory (Laboratory for Next-Generation Computation) at the FAMU\u2013FSU College of Engineering, invites applications for a Postdoctoral Research Associate in AI for Video-Based Surgical Skill Assessment. The NexCom Laboratory develops next-generation computational methods that combine scientific computing, artificial intelligence, and emerging computational paradigms to solve challenging problems in engineering, medicine, and science. Our research spans scientific machine learning, computer vision, explainable AI, quantum computing, and computational modeling, with an emphasis on developing transformative computational technologies with real-world impact. This position offers an exceptional opportunity to help shape the future of AI-enabled surgical education. Our research seeks to fundamentally transform how surgical technical performance is assessed by developing intelligent systems that learn directly from surgical video, objectively evaluate technical skill, provide meaningful formative feedback, and support competency-based surgical training. By combining modern computer vision, video foundation models, self-supervised learning, multimodal machine learning, explainable AI, and human performance modeling, we are developing scalable computational methods that reduce reliance on subjective expert evaluation while improving the consistency, accessibility, and effectiveness of surgical training. Contact Info Questions about the position should be directed to Dr. Suvranu De , Search Committee Chair. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an OPS/temporary job. Based on the duties, this position may require completion of a criminal history background check . This position is open until filled Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63207&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Project Manager, Strategic Partnerships and Innovation", "description": "Job Title Project Manager, Strategic Partnerships and Innovation Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63207 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Strategic Partnerships and Innovation within the Office of Research seeks to fill the Project Manager position. Responsibilities This position is responsible for developing, leading and implementing detailed Project Management Plans (PMP). Manage and lead project teams, direct the work of the activity leaders, prioritize the various lines of effort, and shift resources. Collaborate with all parties associated with projects to ensure they are working according to plan. Implement project management principles and concepts with an in-depth understanding of project controls processes/procedures and systems. Develop and implement processes for meeting deliverables and goals. Is responsible for monitoring projects to keep on track, on schedule, and within budget. Utilize tools such as Smartsheet and Trello to plan and track projects and deliverables. Gather data, conduct data analysis, and create dashboards and reports. Will require working on several projects simultaneously. Prepare regular status reports and advise on critical areas and progress toward milestones. Also will provide operational support including securing and managing resources and facilities. Support events and programs (such as Discovery Days, Industry Days or the Industry Affiliate Program), grants, SPI operations, and large projects. Schedule and facilitate meetings, which includes but is not limited to preparing agendas and meeting minutes by documenting document decisions, identify issues, and identifying action items. Other duties as it relates to the project management and the advancement and implementation of SPI events and objectives. Qualifications Bachelors degree and a minimum of four years or a high school diploma/equivalent and eight years of relevant experience facilitating projects. Preferred Qualifications Four or more years related experience. Experience with Smartsheet or other project management software. Project management certification (PMP). Experience in a research or higher education environment. Contact Info Cassidy Cooksey at RSCH-workforce@fsu.edu University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63220&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried - American Political Behavior", "description": "Job Title Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried - American Political Behavior Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63220 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Political Science - College of Social Sciences & Public Policy Responsibilities The Department of Political Science in the College of Social Sciences & Public Policy at Florida State University seeks applications for a tenure-track assistant professor position to begin in Fall 2027. We seek candidates whose research focuses on American political behavior, including, but not limited to, the political behavior of the general public, groups, or political elites, public opinion, and political psychology. Must be able to offer undergraduate and doctoral level courses in Political Behavior. Qualifications Candidates must have earned a PhD degree in Political Science or a related discipline by the time of appointment, or shortly thereafter, with a demonstrated record of excellence in research and teaching. Successful candidates are expected to add to the department\u2019s strengths in quantitative, experimental, and/or formal methods. Contact Info Professor Andy Ballard University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applicants should submit: A letter of application indicating research and teaching interests A curriculum vitae Writing samples Three letters of recommendations A graduate school transcript Confidential Letters of Reference: This position requires that you have three confidential professional letters of recommendation submitted on your behalf. Follow the steps below to request these letters through our system: 1) After submitting your application, click the Explore Jobs link; 2) Click the My References link; 3) Click the Send/View Reference Request button next to the appropriate position; and 4) Follow the steps on that page to send your references a system generated email requesting they submit a letter of recommendation on your behalf. You may also return to the My References link and click on \"Send/View Reference Request\" to see if your references have responded, add additional references, or resend requests. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. Review of applications will begin September 15, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63229&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried - Comparative Politics", "description": "Job Title Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried - Comparative Politics Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63229 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Political Science - College of Social Sciences & Public Policy Responsibilities The Department of Political Science in the College of Social Sciences & Public Policy at Florida State University seeks applications for a tenure-track assistant professor position to begin in Fall 2027. We seek candidates whose research focuses on comparative politics. The search is open with respect to specialization within the comparative politics subfield. Must be able to offer undergraduate and doctoral level courses in Comparative Politics. Qualifications Candidates must have earned a PhD degree in Political Science or a related discipline by the time of appointment, or shortly thereafter, with a demonstrated record of excellence in research and teaching. Successful candidates are expected to add to the department\u2019s strengths in quantitative, experimental, and/or formal methods. Contact Info Professor Quintin Beazer University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applicants should submit: A letter of application indicating research and teaching interests A curriculum vitae Writing samples Three letters of recommendations A graduate school transcript Confidential Letters of Reference: This position requires that you have three confidential professional letters of recommendation submitted on your behalf. Follow the steps below to request these letters through our system: 1) After submitting your application, click the Explore Jobs link; 2) Click the My References link; 3) Click the Send/View Reference Request button next to the appropriate position; and 4) Follow the steps on that page to send your references a system generated email requesting they submit a letter of recommendation on your behalf. You may also return to the My References link and click on \"Send/View Reference Request\" to see if your references have responded, add additional references, or resend requests. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. Review of applications will begin on September 15, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=62492&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Director of NMR/MRI Program at the NHMFL", "description": "Job Title Director of NMR/MRI Program at the NHMFL Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 62492 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Chemistry & Biochemistry | College of Arts & Sciences | National High Magnetic Field Laboratory Responsibilities The National High Magnetic Field Laboratory (NHMFL, MagLab), in partnership with Florida State University (FSU), invites applications and nominations for the Director of the NMR/MRI Program position. The successful candidate will be appointed as a tenured Full Professor in the Department of Chemistry & Biochemistry in the College of Arts & Sciences. This position offers a unique opportunity to lead a world-class magnetic resonance user facility and research program at the forefront of high-magnetic-field science. The Director will provide visionary scientific and administrative leadership for the NMR/MRI program, overseeing both: A national user facility serving a broad and growing external user community An internationally recognized research program in magnetic resonance science The incumbent will articulate and execute a strategic vision that advances high-magnetic-field instrumentation and experimental capabilities, expands the user base, and integrates emerging technologies into magnetic resonance research and applications. Main Duties Involve: Leading and managing the NMR/MRI user facility, including staff and operations Developing and sustaining a high-impact, externally funded research program Securing funding to expand instrumentation and scientific capabilities Fostering collaborations across institutions and disciplines Enhancing and supporting a broad national and international user community Driving innovation through new methodologies, instrumentation, and data-centric approaches Academic Role: The Director will also contribute to the academic mission of Florida State University through: Participating in graduate and undergraduate education and mentoring Engaging in interdisciplinary research initiatives Qualifications Requirements: A PhD in chemistry, biochemistry, physics, or a related discipline An outstanding record of scientific achievement in solid-state NMR, MRI, or related magnetic resonance techniques Demonstrated successes in leading complex research programs or user facilities Proven ability to secure external funding Preferred Qualifications Experience with national user facilities or large-scale instrumentation programs Expertise in advanced magnetic resonance techniques An established record of excellence in research, teaching, and mentorship consistent with appointment at the Full Professor level A compelling vision for advancing the field through emerging technologies, including AI and data science A demonstrated commitment to fostering a positive and collaborative workplace aligned with MagLab Values Other Information Facilities and Capabilities: The NHMFL NMR/MRI User Program operates a state-of-the-art suite of instruments, including: 1.5 GHz (36 T) Series-Connected Hybrid (SCH) magnet for solid-state NMR Ultra-wide bore 900 MHz system for solid-state NMR and imaging 600 MHz Dynamic Nuclear Polarization (DNP) systems Multiple instruments ranging from 850 MHz, 800MHz, 600MHz, and lower A defining strength of the program is its radio-frequency technology group. It comprises scientists, engineers, and technical staff who design and construct highly efficient, custom-made solid-state NMR probes and MRI coils, enabling rapid development and deployment of novel experimental capabilities. These capabilities support cutting-edge research across physics, chemistry, biology, materials science, and chemical and biochemical engineering, enabled by the MagLab's unique high-field magnet technologies. Contact Info Please direct nominations and inquiries to the Search Committee . University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our interactive too l to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://hr.fsu.edu/facultyjobs. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applicants should submit the following: Curriculum vitae Statement of research accomplishments and future vision Statement of leadership philosophy and vision for the NMR/MRI program Contact information for three references Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. Review of applications will begin on August 1, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63146&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Liberty Lab Director - Research Faculty 12 Month Salaried (Open Rank)", "description": "Job Title Liberty Lab Director - Research Faculty 12 Month Salaried (Open Rank) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63146 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The Institute for Governance and Civics at Florida State University Homepage | Institute for Governance & Civics | FSU America\u2019s Liberty Lab is a distinctive program that sets the IGC apart nationally. It uses the methods of the hard sciences and social sciences to study liberty itself. Just as traditional labs test hypotheses through experimentation and data, the Liberty Lab will investigate where and how liberty thrives-and where it does not using polling, surveys, and cognitive science. The Lab will serve as a hub for: data collection and empirical analysis across our four pillars of liberty (constitutional liberty, economic liberty, conscience liberty, and educational liberty); original survey research and public opinion polling; field and natural experiments on policy and institutional design; use of advanced cognitive research methods; and evaluation of real-world laws and regulations. Responsibilities The Institute for Governance and Civics at Florida State University seeks candidates for a Research Faculty position that is also the Lab Director for our cognitive lab, America\u2019s Liberty Lab. We are particularly interested in researchers whose work addresses real policy outcomes. We expect research faculty to publish in academic outlets as well as write white papers and other work read by policy makers. The goal is to link topflight cognitive and academic research with nonpartisan public policy discussions. We seek candidates from a broad array of academic backgrounds, including (but not limited to): psychology, political science, economics, communications, public policy, history, religion, and more. The successful candidate also will be expected to possess sufficient managerial skills to head up the Liberty Lab. The Lab Director will assist with the initial equipping and design of the new cognitive lab facilities, coordinate with faculty over their research, ensure student access to the Lab, work with the IGC Director, the branch head for Data, Analyses, and Polling, and communications team to publicize the Lab's research, and oversee Lab practice and procedures, including IRB approvals, access to lab spaces and equipment and related matters. Applicants should have experience with EEGs, eye tracking, and biopac equipment. Qualifications Minimum Requirements: Completed Ph.D. by the date of hire. Research interests that contribute to the study of liberty and American civics. Potential for high impact publications. Commitment to the mission of enhancing civic awareness as well as a readiness to contribute to the intellectual life and programmatic development of the IGC. Applicants must have a Ph.D. degree upon taking the position. Contact Info FSU, Institute for Governance and Civics if you have additional questions Lynn Woodworth jlw25c@fsu.edu University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Salary is commiserate upon experience, education and minimal qualifications and salary is competitive. Candidates will be considered for open rank. This appointment will initially be for one year. Renewal will be based on satisfactory performance. FSU\u2019s research faculty positions are not tenured but do contain renewal protections. There is no expectation of teaching with a research faculty position at FSU. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63058&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Research & Special Projects Librarian, 12-Month Salaried", "description": "Job Title Research & Special Projects Librarian, 12-Month Salaried Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63058 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department College of Law Research Center Responsibilities Florida State University seeks a creative, enthusiastic, and innovative law librarian to serve as the Research & Special Projects Librarian. This position provides research and reference support to College of Law faculty and students and contributes to specialized library initiatives supporting the College's research, teaching, and public service mission. In addition to core research and instruction responsibilities, this librarian will have a dedicated role in developing and supporting special projects, including work on the Florida Workers' Compensation Archive and research support for the Election Law Center. These projects offer an opportunity to contribute to innovative, high-impact work involving legal research, archival and digital collections, and public-facing legal information resources. Provides reference and research support to faculty and student research, including in-depth research assistance at the reference desk, email support, and in-person consultations. Contributes to the development, organization, description, promotion, and sustainability of special projects, including the Florida Workers' Compensation Archive. Provides research, current awareness, and resource development support for the Election Law Center, in collaboration with faculty, staff, students, and other stakeholders. Works collaboratively on projects involving digital collections, archival materials, government information, legal history, and specialized research resources. Participates in legal research instruction via workshops, guest lectures, and other opportunities in various formats, including online, hybrid, and face-to-face instruction. Contributes to the College of Law and the profession through committee work, research, publishing, and/or participation in professional organizations. Represents the Research Center on various colleges, campus, and library system committees and at meetings and other functions. Facilitates collaborative relationships within the College of Law and with campus partners. Other duties as assigned. Qualifications Master's degree from an accredited institution in library science and appropriate experience as a professional librarian consistent with university guidelines. Preferred Qualifications J.D. and Master's in library science from accredited institutions. Alternatively, substantial experience as a professional librarian or researcher that meets university guidelines may substitute for one of the degrees. Proficiency in legal research and information technologies. Excellent interpersonal, written, and oral communication skills and the ability to work effectively and collaboratively with varied groups. Excellent organizational, project management, time-management, and analytical skills. Strong service orientation and the ability to work independently and as part of a team. Ability to meet the Research Center's research, service, and leadership requirements. Other Information Overview: This librarian will be part of a highly collaborative, forward-thinking library that is a valued contributor to the College of Law's mission. The ideal candidate will have strong legal research skills, excellent communication and organizational abilities, the ability to thrive in a team-oriented environment and be eager to develop or apply experience in archival or special collections work. We welcome experienced and entry-level applicants, including Spring/Summer 2026 graduates. Environment: The Florida State University Legal Research Center is an innovative, exciting library with a collaborative approach to decision-making. The library serves Florida State University faculty, staff and students, students and faculty of other local colleges and universities, attorneys, and the general public. The College of Law offers an intellectually rigorous legal education in a welcoming, collegial atmosphere that is supportive of students, faculty, and staff. Florida State University is located in Tallahassee, Florida's beautiful capital city, a place that combines the atmosphere and amenities of a larger city with the charm and affordable cost of living in a smaller town. Florida has no state or local income tax. Contact Info Elizabeth Farrell Clifford University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Salary is commensurate with education and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Please include a cover letter with a complete statement of qualifications, a full resume of education and relevant experience, and the names, telephone numbers, and email addresses of at least three people who are knowledgeable about your qualifications for this position. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This is a full-time, 12-month specialized faculty appointment, though we welcome applications from candidates interested in a reduced FTE arrangement (minimum .75 FTE). Relocation assistance may be available for the successful candidate. This position is being advertised as open until filled . The start date is flexible. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63053&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Open Rank Professor, 9 Month Salaried (Department of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering Florida A&M University \u2013 Florida State University College of Engineering)", "description": "Job Title Open Rank Professor, 9 Month Salaried (Department of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering Florida A&M University \u2013 Florida State University College of Engineering) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63053 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The Department of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering at the Florida A&M University-Florida State University College of Engineering. Responsibilities The successful candidate is expected to establish and maintain a robust externally funded research program, have a strong commitment to teaching excellence in undergraduate and graduate courses, and participate in college and professional service. Qualifications Candidates must possess an earned Ph.D. in Mechanical or Aerospace Engineering or a closely related discipline, demonstrate the ability to create and sustain an internationally recognized research program in their field of expertise, and have a strong interest in engineering education. Other Information The FAMU-FSU College of Engineering is the nexus of two major public universities, each with a distinct mission but focused on world-class engineering education and research. Created by the Florida Legislature in 1982, the joint organization is the College of Engineering for both Florida A&M and Florida State universities. This unique combination of focus, resources, and mission from our parent organizations has created on our campus a truly innovative atmosphere that leverages the benefits of the traditional HBCU model with the innovations of an R-1 public research university. After completing the prerequisites at their home universities, FAMU and FSU students learn, study, and research together at our independent campus, with jointly appointed faculty and staff. Students graduate from their enrolling university and from the FAMU-FSU College of Engineering. Both FAMU and FSU are part of the State University System of Florida and are accredited by the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools Commission on Colleges. Additionally, all seven of the college\u2019s eligible undergraduate degree programs are accredited by the Engineering Accreditation Commission of ABET . Helpful The MAE Department currently has about 36 faculty, 150+ graduate students, ~800 undergraduate students, and annual research expenditures exceeding $36M. A new graduate program in Aerospace Engineering started in the fall of 2025 within the Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering Department. Additional investments in aerospace include over $100M investments in our Panama City, FL campus Inspire . We expect that the candidate would join our existing Center for Intelligent Systems, Control, and Robotics (CISCOR), but outstanding opportunities exist for collaboration with a number of additional centers of excellence including: the High Performance Materials Institute (HPMI,), the Florida Center for Advanced Aero-Propulsion (FCAAP), and the Aerospace, Mechatronics and Energy Center (AME). Potential applicants seeking more information are encouraged to visit our website Department of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering . Contact Info The appointment is anticipated to begin in August 2027. Any questions about the position should be directed to Dr. Jonathan Clark, Search Committee Chair, at clarkj@eng.famu.fsu.edu . University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include the following documents: A cover letter A full curriculum vitae A 2-page research statement. This statement should clearly indicate how the proposed research efforts will connect to other efforts in the department and universities. A 1-page teaching statement No more than four selected publications for review The names and contact information of four potential references Faculty Information The Department of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering is pleased to invite applications from highly qualified individuals for tenure-track faculty positions in the field of dynamics and control in Tallahassee, Florida. This position is at the assistant level, but well-qualified candidates will be considered at a higher rank. We are interested in candidates whose robotic research is grounded in mechanical engineering, including but not limited to aerial/aquatic/space robotics, dynamics/mechanisms, soft robotics, manipulation/surgical robotics, human-robot interface, sensing and perception, Artificial Intelligence/Machine Learning, and Optimal/feedback controls. Other areas of Dynamics and controls will also be considered, particularly if they complement existing program strengths. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Application review will begin on September 1, 2026. Acceptance and review of applications will continue until the position is filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63052&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Open Rank Professor. 9 Month Salaried (Department of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering Florida A&M University \u2013 Florida State University College of Engineering)", "description": "Job Title Open Rank Professor. 9 Month Salaried (Department of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering Florida A&M University \u2013 Florida State University College of Engineering) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63052 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The Department of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering at the Florida A&M University-Florida State University College of Engineering Responsibilities The successful candidate is expected to establish and maintain a robust externally funded research program, have a strong commitment to teaching excellence in undergraduate and graduate courses, and participate in college and professional service. Qualifications Candidates must possess an earned Ph.D. in Mechanical or Aerospace Engineering or a closely related discipline, demonstrate the ability to create and sustain an internationally recognized research program in their field of expertise, and have a strong interest in engineering education. Other Information The FAMU-FSU College of Engineering is the nexus of two major public universities, each with a distinct mission but focused on world-class engineering education and research. Created by the Florida Legislature in 1982, the joint organization is the College of Engineering for both Florida A&M and Florida State universities. This unique combination of focus, resources, and mission from our parent university has created on our campus a truly innovative atmosphere that leverages the benefits of the traditional HBCU model with the innovations of an R-1 public research university. After completing the prerequisites at their home university, FAMU and FSU students learn, study, and research together at our independent campus, with jointly appointed faculty and staff. Students graduate from their enrolling university and from the FAMU-FSU College of Engineering. Both FAMU and FSU are part of the State University System of Florida and are accredited by the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools Commission on Colleges. Additionally, all seven of the college\u2019s eligible undergraduate degree programs are accredited by the Engineering Accreditation Commission of ABET . Helpful The MAE Department currently has about 36 faculty, 150+ graduate students, ~800 undergraduate students, and annual research expenditures exceeding $36M. A new graduate program in Aerospace Engineering started in the fall of 2025 within the Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering Department. Additional investments in aerospace include over $100M investments in our Panama City, FL campus Inspire. We expect that the candidate would join our existing Florida Center for Advanced Aero-Propulsion (FCAAP), and outstanding opportunities exist for collaboration with a number of additional centers of excellence including: the High Performance Materials Institute (HPMI), the Center for Intelligent Systems, Control, and Robotics (CISCOR), and the Aerospace, Mechatronics and Energy Center (AME). Potential applicants seeking more information are encouraged to visit Department of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering . Contact Info Any questions about the position should be directed to Dr. Chiang Shih, Search Committee Chair, at shih@eng.famu.fsu.edu . University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita and include: A cover letter A full curriculum vitae A 2-page research statement. This statement should clearly indicate how the proposed research efforts will connect to other efforts in the department and universities. A 1-page teaching statement No more than four selected publications for review The names and contact information of four potential references Faculty Information The Department of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering is pleased to invite applications from highly qualified individuals for tenure-track faculty positions in the field of Aerospace (Propulsion, Structures, and Space Guidance, Navigation, and Controls) in Tallahassee, Florida. This position is at the assistant level, but well-qualified candidates will be considered at a higher rank. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . The appointment is anticipated to begin in August 2027. Application review will begin on September 1, 2026. Acceptance and review of applications will continue until the position is filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=62870&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Associate Radiation Safety Officer", "description": "Job Title Associate Radiation Safety Officer Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 62870 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Environmental Health and Safety Responsibilities Evaluates Principal Investigator Proposal applications for the use of radioactive materials and subsequent: laboratory setup, on-site inspection and surveillance during use, and post use closeout surveillance of FSU laboratories and satellite facilities. Inspects analytical, medical, and veterinary x-ray machines and linear accelerator facilities for compliance with regulatory requirements. Responsible for complete knowledge of Federal and State regulations which relate to radiation safety in a university environment. Serves as the Radiation Safety Officer during their absence. Determines the exposure potential for radiation workers and implements appropriate control measures, including special decontamination projects, to keep personnel exposures as low as reasonably achievable. Oversee the radioactive waste program including collection, storage, and disposal. Arranges for the transportation and disposal of long-lived radioactive waste. Ensures compliance with all regulations and ordinances. Prepares training curriculum for and helps teach the Radiation Safety Course. Also provides on-the-job training to laboratory users and new employees in areas that include biological effects of radiation, instrumentation, dosimetry, physics, licensing and regulatory requirements, general laboratory safety, and applied health physics. Manages radioactive material inventories for the Principal Investigators by examining records of purchase, use and disposal; maintains their technical accuracy and timeliness in accordance with license conditions and regulatory requirements. Assists the non-ionizing radiation safety program, serving as the Assistant University Laser Safety Officer, and addressing magnetic field, electromagnetic field, radio frequency, microwave and other non-ionizing safety concerns. Performs periodic radiation detection instrument calibration, making adjustments and repairs when necessary. Performs inventory and leak testing of radioactive sealed sources in accordance with license conditions and all applicable regulations. Performs specialized computer related tasks, such as adaptation of computer programs for databases of radioactive material inventories, dose records and automated reporting. Performs environmental monitoring by sample collection and analysis and performs member-of-the-public dose assessments. Remains constantly vigilant to changes or advances that may have an impact on EH&S related programs through proactive methods such as audits, research, interactions with colleagues at related institutions and by attending professional courses or society meetings. Immediately report any findings that may affect University programs to supervisors and assist in determining and implementing necessary policy changes to ensure best practices are realized. Performs special projects as needed, such as researching approaches to improve radiation detection, reducing dose to personnel, minimizing environmental releases, minimizing waste disposal costs, decommissioning inactive facilities and equipment, and revising departmental policies and procedures in response to regulatory and technological changes. Qualifications Bachelor degree and five years of experience in physics, medical physics, other physical science, engineering, or applied mathematics or a post high school education or equivalent and related combination of education and same experience equal to nine years. Must meet requirements for Radiation Safety Officer under F.A.C. 64E-5.648 at time of hire. A valid State of Florida or Georgia Driver\u2019s License or ability to obtain upon hire. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is open until filled This position is being re-advertised. Previous applicants need not apply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63001&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Principal Faculty & Open Rank Professor, 12 Months Salaried (School of Physician Assistant Practice - College of Medicine)", "description": "Job Title Principal Faculty & Open Rank Professor, 12 Months Salaried (School of Physician Assistant Practice - College of Medicine) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63001 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department School of Physician Assistant Practice - College of Medicine Responsibilities The Principal Faculty member has the primary responsibility of teaching, student evaluation, advising and mentoring. Will serve as course director and teach courses in the PA program. Guides scholarly pursuits of students and provides academic and career advice to students. Participates in student selection and admissions process as well as participates in student orientation, recruitment events and student evaluations. Serve as advisor to a small cohort of students. Remediates students in didactic and clinical areas when appropriate. Also serves on program-specific committees. Participates in scholarly activities resulting in publication and/or presentation at regional and national meetings. Attends appropriate state and national professional meetings. Participates in the development of grant applications, accreditation reports, and assessment. Maintains clinical competency/practice and knowledge of current best practices within the profession. Participates in the development, monitoring, refining and assessment of plans to achieve the vision of the program, consistent with the broader missions and strategic directions of the College of Medicine. Participates in program accreditation activities. Assists with the implementation of quality assurance practices to ensure continual curriculum and program assessment and evaluation as stipulated by ARC-PA. Additional duties as assigned by the Program Director. Qualifications PA-C (Master\u2019s degree or higher), MD, DO, or Ph.D. in an appropriate field from an accredited institution with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Current NCCPA or physician board certification. Current valid Florida Physician Assistant or Physician license, or eligibility for Florida licensure. Current Florida or Georgia Driver\u2019s License, or the ability to obtain prior to hire. Knowledgeable in current practice standards and the roles of physician assistants. Preferred Qualifications Minimum three years of clinical experience. Contact Info Dr. Benjamin Smith University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Salary is $120,000 - $130,000, commensurate with experience and education. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . The position is non-tenure/non-tenure earning. Rank is commensurate with experience. This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=62991&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried - Fall 2027 (Department of Accounting - Herbert Wertheim College of Business)", "description": "Job Title Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried - Fall 2027 (Department of Accounting - Herbert Wertheim College of Business) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 62991 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Accounting | Herbert Wertheim College of Business Responsibilities Florida State University, Department of Accounting, invites applications for a tenure-track assistant professor position beginning August 2027. This position will be required to publish in leading scholarly journals, along with teaching undergraduate and graduate courses. You will also continue research efforts and progress towards promotion and tenure. Qualifications All candidates should have a Ph.D. in accounting. Preferred Qualifications Candidates must demonstrate an ability to publish in leading scholarly journals and a commitment to excellence in teaching. All areas of research expertise will be considered, although we have a strong preference for candidates with an interest in teaching financial accounting. Contact Info For questions about this position, please contact: Dr. Allen D. Blay Department Chair and EY Professor University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applicants should submit their curriculum vitae, at least one working paper, and three reference letters by email to acctg-recruiting1@business.fsu.edu . Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63030&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Genetic Counselor (Open Rank Professor, 12 Month Salaried) Medicine - IPRD", "description": "Job Title Genetic Counselor (Open Rank Professor, 12 Month Salaried) Medicine - IPRD Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63030 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department College of Medicine Institute for Pediatric Rare Disease (IPRD) - Genetic Counseling Program Responsibilities The successful candidate will join a rapidly growing, multidisciplinary team dedicated to advancing precision medicine and improving outcomes for children with rare genetic disorders. Faculty at IPRD contribute to a collaborative academic environment that integrates genomics, translational research, clinical care, and professional and graduate education. Primary responsibilities will be as follows: Clinical: Provide genetic counseling services to patients and families, including genetic risk assessment, test selection and interpretation, and communication of results in collaboration with medical geneticists and other healthcare professionals. Teaching and Training: Contribute to the development and delivery of coursework in the Master\u2019s Degree Program in Genetic Counseling. Provide clinical supervision to genetic counseling students and participate in interprofessional education initiatives across the College of Medicine. Research: Engage in mentored, independent, or collaborative research focused on genetics, genomics, or genetic counseling practice. Qualifications Master\u2019s degree from an accredited genetic counseling program. Certification or eligibility for certification by the American Board of Genetic Counseling (ABGC). State of Florida Genetic Counselor licensure is required within one year of hire. Demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Current Basic Life Support (BLS) Healthcare Provider Certification by a certifying agency, or the ability to obtain prior to hire. Post-job offer, but prior to hire, the following will be required: Documentation of current PPD (Purified Protein Derivative) test as performed by a qualified physician, reporting negative results within the past six (6) months. Documentation of physical examination completed by a qualified healthcare provider/physician within the past six (6) months. Within 30 days of hire, the candidate must provide: Documentation of Tetanus immunization within 10 years. Documentation of Hepatitis B vaccine or positive antibody titer. Preferred Qualifications Prior clinical experience in pediatric or rare disease genetics. Evidence of scholarly activity, such as peer-reviewed publications, participation in funded research, or contributions to curriculum development. Experience supervising or mentoring genetic counseling students. Contact Info Dr. Ashley Cannon University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This is a non-tenure earning position and is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=62970&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Test Proctor (Part-Time, OPS - Multiple Openings) - Office of Digital Learning & Academic Technology", "description": "Job Title Test Proctor (Part-Time, OPS - Multiple Openings) - Office of Digital Learning & Academic Technology Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 62970 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Part-Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Office of Digital Learning & Academic Technology Responsibilities The FSU Office of Digital Learning & Academic Technology (ODL) is seeking customer-service-oriented Test Proctors to join our team as we support quality online instruction at Florida State University. We offer a collegial, innovative work culture that\u2019s passionate about excellence, quality, and collaboration. As a Test Proctor, you\u2019ll be part of creating a welcoming, secure experience for our testers. Primary responsibilities include admitting testers in and out of our testing facility, proctoring exams, and office-administrative work. These responsibilities are described below. Admit testers in and out of the facility. Upon entrance: Greet testers as they enter the testing lobby. Check the testers\u2019 registration and photo ID. Confirm all devices are turned off. Ensure all unauthorized items are put away. Review any important test-specific policies with the tester. Provide testing materials based on test requirements. Upon exit: Greet testers as they exit the testing room. Collect any test materials, including scratch paper. Close the test registration. Proctor testers. Use camera system, screen monitoring software, and traditional proctoring methods to monitor testers. Pay careful attention to key areas to identify suspicious behavior. Report any concerns to a supervisor to address sensitive matters. Complete office-administrative work. Maintain cleanliness of the facility. Shred used scratch paper, reference sheets, and other sensitive documents. Monitor and respond to personal work emails. During slower periods, assist the testing team and department with special projects and tasks. Qualifications High school diploma or equivalent Due to NCTA and CLEP test regulations: 21 years of age or older and not doing undergraduate-level coursework at *any* college or university. Able to work at least 20 hours a week within business hours, after 11:00am. Able to work at least 15 additional hours during extended hours weeks. See the \u201cConsiderations\u201d section below for details. Able to maintain a consistent work schedule. Able to follow procedures precisely and pay attention to detail. Able to carefully handle secure and confidential information. Able to provide courteous customer service. Able to maintain positivity and professionalism in a diverse, team-based environment. Able to work effectively under high-stress situations. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor\u2019s degree (BA/BS) or associate\u2019s degree (AA/AS). 1 year or more of customer service experience. Student or work experience in a college or university setting. Experience working with secure and confidential materials or information. Proficiency using computers. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range This position starts at $15.00 an hour and can earn up to $15.75 per hour. Increases may be granted for strong job performance. Vacation and sick leave are not included with this position. However, staff working in this position may be approved for planned and unplanned absences. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an OPS/temporary job. Based on the duties, this position may require completion of a criminal history background check . Training is provided on the job and typically takes two weeks to complete. See testing.fsu.edu for standard business hours. During peak times of the semester (i.e., the last week of the spring and fall semesters or after an unexpected closure), the testing center may extend these hours to meet service demands. See FSU\u2019s extended Academic Calendar for more information. This position is eligible to earn overtime pay of time-and-a-half (1.5 times the normal pay rate) when working more than 40 hours in a 1-week period. This position is being advertised until April 15. Applications will be reviewed periodically throughout the year as departmental needs arise. Qualified candidates will be contacted via email when a need arises, and interviews must be scheduled in advance (no walk-ins). Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=62968&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Test Proctor - Office of Digital Learning & Academic Technology (Full-time, OPS) (Multiple Vacancies)", "description": "Job Title Test Proctor - Office of Digital Learning & Academic Technology (Full-time, OPS) (Multiple Vacancies) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 62968 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Office of Digital Learning & Academic Technology Responsibilities The FSU Office of Digital Learning & Academic Technology (ODL) is seeking customer-service-oriented Test Proctors to join our team as we support quality online instruction at Florida State University. We offer a collegial, innovative work environment that\u2019s passionate about excellence, quality, and collaboration. As a Test Proctor, you\u2019ll be part of creating a welcoming, secure experience for our testers. Primary responsibilities include admitting testers in and out of our testing facility, proctoring exams, and office-administrative work. These responsibilities are described below. Admit testers in and out of the facility. Upon entrance : Greet testers as they enter the testing lobby. Check the testers\u2019 registration and photo ID. Confirm all devices are turned off. Ensure all unauthorized items are put away. Review any important test-specific policies with the tester. Provide testing materials based on test requirements. Upon exit : Greet testers as they exit the testing room. Collect any test materials, including scratch paper. Close the test registration. Proctor testers . Use camera system, screen monitoring software, and traditional proctoring methods to monitor testers. Pay careful attention to key areas to identify suspicious behavior. Report any concerns to a supervisor to address sensitive matters. Complete office-administrative work . Maintain cleanliness of the facility. Shred used scratch paper, reference sheets, and other sensitive documents. Monitor and respond to personal work emails. During slower periods, assist the testing team and department with special projects and tasks. Qualifications Due to NCTA and CLEP test regulations: 21 years of age or older and not doing undergraduate-level coursework at *any* college or university. Able to work at least 25 hours a week within business hours. Able to work at least 15 additional hours during extended hours weeks. See the \u201cConsiderations\u201d section below for details. Able to maintain a consistent work schedule. Able to follow procedures precisely and pay attention to detail. Able to carefully handle secure and confidential information. Able to provide courteous customer service. Able to maintain positivity and professionalism in a team-based environment. Able to work effectively under high-stress situations. Preferred Qualifications Able to work 40 hours a week during business hours. Bachelor\u2019s degree (BA/BS) or associate\u2019s degree (AA/AS). 1 year or more of customer service experience. Student or work experience in a college or university setting. Experience working with secure and confidential materials or information. Proficiency using computers. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range This position starts at $15.00 an hour and can earn up to $17.50 per hour with strong job performance over time (+$1.50) and increased job responsibilities (+$1.00). Vacation and sick leave are not included with this position. However, staff working in this position may be approved for planned and unplanned absences. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an OPS/temporary job. Based on the duties, this position may require completion of a criminal history background check . Training is provided on the job and typically takes two weeks to complete. See testing.fsu.edu for standard business hours. During peak times of the semester (i.e., the last week of the spring and fall semesters or after an unexpected closure), the testing center may extend these hours to meet service demands. See FSU\u2019s extended Academic Calendar (https://registrar.fsu.edu/calendar/extended) for more information.. This position is eligible to earn overtime pay of time-and-a-half (1.5 times the normal pay rate) when working more than 40 hours in a 1-week period. This position is being advertised until April 15, 2027. Applications will be reviewed periodically throughout the year as departmental needs arise. Qualified candidates will be contacted via email when a need arises, and interviews must be scheduled in advance (no walk-ins). Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=62866&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Residency Coordinator Maggie Allesee National Center for Choreography (MANCC) (Full-time, OPS)", "description": "Job Title Residency Coordinator Maggie Allesee National Center for Choreography (MANCC) (Full-time, OPS) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 62866 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The Maggie Allesee National Center for Choreography (MANCC) Responsibilities Residency Administration & Artist Support Logistics & Hospitality: Book artist lodging and transportation; greet artists upon arrival (including airport pick-ups) and provide campus/facility/MANCC orientations. On-Site Support: Serve as a responsive point of contact for artists during their residencies. Event Planning: Plan, staff, and coordinate Entrypoint events and residency activities. Contracts & Documentation: Shepherd contracts through the signature process; track all residency-associated documents and maintain accurate records. Meetings & Evaluation: Schedule and document planning meetings, residency orientation and wrap-up meetings, and distribute/track post-residency evaluations. Office Management & Fiscal Administration Financial Tracking: Work closely with University Business Administration staff to process, track, and record fiscal expenditures. Administrative Support: Take comprehensive notes for external meetings with artists; coordinate travel arrangements for MANCC staff. Operations: Order equipment and supplies. Communications & Production Support Promotional Materials: Coordinate the production and printing of promotional materials, including artist fact sheets, posters, and building signage. Technical Liaison: Coordinate basic production and technical support through the FSU School of Dance as needed. Production Support. Provide light production support as needed. Qualifications Bachelor's degree; or a high school diploma or equivalent and experience equal to four years. (Note: post high-school education and/or experience may substitute at a comparable rate.) Ability to work up to 40 hours per week (typically Monday\u2013Friday, 8:30 AM \u2013 5:30 PM) with flexibility for occasional evening and weekend hours based on residency needs. Shares a genuine desire to support a range of contemporary artists and their creative processes. A valid State of Florida or Georgia Driver\u2019s License or the ability to obtain prior to hire and access to a reliable personal vehicle for local errands and airport runs (mileage will be reimbursed). Solid written and verbal communication skills; ability to interface professionally with MANCC staff, faculty, students, School of Dance administration, community members, and visiting artists. Exceptional organizational skills with experience managing schedules, setting meetings, and taking detailed meeting minutes. Proficiency in basic computer skills (email, word processing, calendar software) and data entry, with the ability and willingness to learn new platforms. Preferred Qualifications Experience coordinating travel arrangements and tracking expenses. Familiarity with the Mac platform and software such as Microsoft Office (including Calendar and SharePoint), Adobe Creative Suite, iContact, and SmugMug. Basic experience with Adobe InDesign. A basic background in technical production and a general understanding of audio, video, and computer-related hardware/software. Strong interpersonal skills: mature, responsible, collaborative, possesses a sense of humor. Other Information The Maggie Allesee National Center for Choreography (MANCC) is one of only two national residency centers for choreography in the United States located within a major research institution. Embedded within Florida State University\u2019s School of Dance, MANCC operates from one of the country\u2019s premier dance facilities. We offer unparalleled opportunities for contemporary choreographers and their collaborators to research, develop, and write about new work within a supportive creative community. The Residency Coordinator works collaboratively with the MANCC staff\u2014including the Director, Assistant Director, and Media Specialist\u2014to support choreographic residencies and provide basic administrative support. This role is responsible for the seamless administration of artist residencies, day-to-day office management, and light production support. Helpful This position offers a fantastic opportunity to be part of a nationally recognized Center and a dedicated team. The Residency Coordinator will connect with a wide range of contemporary artists, deepen their understanding of the national dance field, and engage closely with the School of Dance, FSU, and the greater Tallahassee community. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an OPS/temporary job. Based on the duties, this position may require completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. This position requires flexibility for occasional evening and weekend hours based on residency needs. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=62895&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Open Rank Professor, 9 Month Salaried (National High Magnetic Field Laboratory (NHMFL), Department of Mechanical and Aerospace- The Florida University-Florida State University College of Engineering)", "description": "Job Title Open Rank Professor, 9 Month Salaried (National High Magnetic Field Laboratory (NHMFL), Department of Mechanical and Aerospace- The Florida University-Florida State University College of Engineering) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 62895 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The Department of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering (MAE) at FAMU-FSU College of Engineering and the National High Magnetic Field Laboratory (MagLab) seek an open rank tenure-line faculty position. Responsibilities The Department of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering (MAE) at FAMU-FSU College of Engineering and the National High Magnetic Field Laboratory (MagLab) seek an open rank tenure-line faculty position with a target research Senior Large-Scale Cryogenics R&D Engineer to provide technical leadership in the design, development, and operation of mission-critical cryogenic infrastructure supporting world-leading high magnetic field research and power applications. This role requires deep expertise in large-scale cryogenic systems and a demonstrated ability to lead complex engineering projects in a research environment. Qualifications Candidates must possess an earned Ph.D. in mechanical or aerospace Engineering or a closely related discipline, demonstrate the ability to create and sustain an internationally recognized research program in their field of expertise, and have a strong interest in engineering education. The successful candidate is expected to establish and maintain a robust externally funded research program, have a strong commitment to teaching excellence in undergraduate and graduate courses, and participate in college and professional service. Helpful The FAMU-FSU College of Engineering is the nexus of two major public universities, each with a distinct mission but focused on world-class engineering education and research. Created by the Florida Legislature in 1982, the joint organization is the College of Engineering for both Florida A&M and Florida State universities. This unique combination of focus, resources, and mission from our parent organization has created on our campus a truly innovative atmosphere that leverages the benefits of the traditional HBCU model with the innovations of an R-1 public research university. After completing the prerequisites at their home universities, FAMU and FSU students learn, study, and research together at our independent campus, with jointly appointed faculty and staff. Students graduate from their enrolling university and from the FAMU-FSU College of Engineering. Both FAMU and FSU are part of the State University System of Florida and are accredited by the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools Commission on Colleges. Additionally, all seven of the college\u2019s eligible undergraduate degree programs are accredited by the Engineering Accreditation Commission of ABET . Contact Info Application review will begin on September 1, 2026. Acceptance and review of applications will continue until the position is filled. The appointment is anticipated to begin in August 2027. Any questions about the position should be directed to Dr. Wei Guo, Search Committee Chair, wguo@magnet.fsu.edu . University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include: A cover letter A full curriculum vitae A 2-page research statement. This statement should clearly indicate how the proposed research efforts will connect to other efforts in the department and universities. A 1-page teaching statement No more than four selected publications for review The names and contact information of four potential references Faculty Information The Department of Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering (MAE) currently has about 36 faculty, 150+ graduate students, ~800 undergraduate students, and annual research expenditures exceeding $36M. A new graduate program in Aerospace Engineering started in the fall of 2025 within the Department of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering. Additional investments in aerospace include over $100M investments in our Panama City, FL campus Inspire FSU . We expect that the candidate would join our existing Florida Center for Advanced Aero-Propulsion , and outstanding opportunities exist for collaboration with a number of additional centers of excellence including: the High Performance Materials Institute (HPMI) , the Center for Intelligent Systems, Control, and Robotics (CISCOR) , and the Aerospace, Mechatronics and Energy Center (AME) . Potential applicants seeking more information are encouraged to visit our website at https://www.eng.famu.fsu.edu/mae. The National High Magnetic Field Laboratory (MagLab) is the largest and highest-powered magnet lab in the world. The MagLab hosts more than 1,000 visiting scientists each year. Researchers use our facilities for free, advancing understanding of materials, new technologies, energy, health, the environment, and even the universe. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=62234&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Director, Center for Advanced Power Systems (Research Faculty III, 12 Month Salaried)", "description": "Job Title Director, Center for Advanced Power Systems (Research Faculty III, 12 Month Salaried) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 62234 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Center for Advanced Power Systems (CAPS) Responsibilities The Center for Advanced Power Systems, established in 2000, is an internationally recognized research and education center specializing in the development, simulation, and testing of advanced concepts in superconducting and conventional electric power systems, as well as materials applications. The Center\u2019s mission is to develop and implement systems-driven research and education programs focused on technology issues in electric power systems, modeling and simulation, advanced controls, advanced component development, and testing. All of these are accomplished in collaboration with key stakeholders to meet the needs of governmental agencies and the nation\u2019s electric utilities. The Director serves as the executive officer and is responsible for the overall leadership and maintaining a high level of externally funded research and development activities of the Center. Duties of the Director include, but are not limited to, the following: Ensure the Center maintains, builds, and strengthens its reputation as a national and international Power and Energy Center of Excellence, demonstrating leadership in both research and innovation. Update, execute, and continuously monitor the Center\u2019s Performance Plan, which supports the Strategic Plans of FSU and the FAMU-FSU College of Engineering. Foster and grow an environment of teamwork, collaboration, and scholarly inquiry, supporting innovative research and the pursuit of new ideas across the Center\u2019s disciplines. Articulate the Center\u2019s mission and promote CAPS\u2019 programs and capabilities to government, industry, and academia, nationally and internationally. Cultivate and expand strategic partnerships with industry to accelerate technology transfer, joint research initiatives, and workforce development opportunities. Ensure that the educational missions of FSU reflected in the outcomes of the Center. Broaden the Center\u2019s research and funding portfolio. Play a critical role in hiring the Center\u2019s research and tenure-line faculty. Interface with the FSU Sponsored Research Administration and FSU Research Foundation on research proposals and the pre- and post-award processes. Qualifications A terminal degree from an accredited institution in a related field, such as an Engineering or Physical Science discipline. The candidate must be a U.S. citizen and hold a Department of Defense security clearance at a minimum Secret level. Candidates should have demonstrated intellectual leadership, management skills, and a strong track record of securing government funds or corporate sponsorship for large research programs. Preferred Qualifications Experience in grant writing and proposal development, as well as serving as a Principal Investigator on federally funded contracts and grants. Demonstrated experience in leading research program development. Other Information The Center is located in Tallahassee/Leon County\u2019s Innovation Park, home to more than 35 cutting-edge research and manufacturing organizations, including the Florida Agricultural and Mechanical University \u2013 Florida State University College of Engineering, the National High Magnetic Field Laboratory, the Applied Superconductivity Center, the High-Performance Materials Institute, the Florida Center for Advanced Aero-propulsion, and the FSU Aero-propulsion, Mechatronics and Energy Center. Contact Info Rohit Gupta Russell Reynolds Associates Direct: +1-415-352-3367 Mobile: +1-415-5354548 rohit.gupta@russellreynolds.com Jacqueline Arends Russell Reynolds Associates Direct: +1-202-654-7847 Mobile: +1-703-7171006 jacqueline.arends@russellreynolds.com Rachel Brouwer Administrative Specialist, Center for Advanced Power Systems (CAPS) 850-645-2157 rachel.brouwer@fsu.edu University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our interactive too l to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://hr.fsu.edu/facultyjobs. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. The Search Committee will begin reviewing applications on Monday, March 16th and will continue until the position is filled. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being re-advertised. Previous applicants need not reapply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=62864&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Open Rank Teaching Faculty, 12 Month Salaried (Student Services & Undergraduate Affairs - Florida A&M University-Florida State University College of Engineering)", "description": "Job Title Open Rank Teaching Faculty, 12 Month Salaried (Student Services & Undergraduate Affairs - Florida A&M University-Florida State University College of Engineering) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 62864 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The Office of Student Services and Undergraduate Affairs (SSUA) at the Florida A&M University-Florida State University College of Engineering. Responsibilities This invitation for applications covers one full-time Non-Tenure-Track instructor who will also act as Director of the Engineering Living Learning Community (ELLC) at FSU. The instructor will work collaboratively to establish a welcoming and supportive environment for our first-year engineering students and will teach multiple sections of First-Year Engineering Lab (FYEL). The FYEL course orients students to engineering, the disciplines offered, degree requirements, and the engineering profession. The course helps students develop communication and problem-solving skills and acclimates them to project-based learning. The ELLC director will collaborate with departments and other FYEL instructors on curriculum development, designing class projects, assessment, and teaching as needed. In addition, the instructor will participate in new student orientation and advising, facilitate student participation in engagement activities, coordinate with pre-engineering advisors and department major advisors, collaborate with other college staff (recruitment coordinator, director of student engagement, and director of student access) to increase retention, and help monitor retention rates and other performance-based metrics. Qualifications Applicants must have earned a Ph.D. in an engineering discipline, engineering education, or equivalent field. Industrial experience, while not required, would be very valuable. Candidates must possess excellent communication skills, a commitment to innovative teaching methods, and a desire to serve and prepare students for successful college and professional careers. An interest in engineering education best practices, research and assessment, and demonstrated knowledge and interest in first-year engineering programming and initiatives are desirable attributes. Helpful SSUA is responsible for the administration of undergraduate academic policies and procedures at the college and for providing academic services and support to students. Potential applicants seeking more information are encouraged to visit our website at https://eng.famu.fsu.edu/students/ssua and https://eng.famu.fsu.edu/. Contact Info Applications will be reviewed beginning July 6, 2026. Acceptance and review of applications will continue until the position is filled. Any questions about the position should be directed to Dr. Michelle Rambo-Roddenberry, Search Committee Chair, at mroddenberry@eng.famu.fsu.edu . University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include: A cover letter A full curriculum vitae A 2-page teaching statement. This statement should clearly indicate how the proposed teaching plan aligns with existing courses, degree programs, and pre-engineering, for our students from both universities that we serve. The names and contact information of three potential references. Faculty Information The Office of Student Services and Undergraduate Affairs (SSUA) at the Florida A&M University-Florida State University College of Engineering is pleased to invite applications from highly qualified individuals for a full-time, non-tenure track teaching faculty position with primary responsibilities in undergraduate teaching. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is open until filled Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=62801&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Research Faculty I - 12 Month Salaried (Pre-Clinical and Materials MRI (NHMFL))", "description": "Job Title Research Faculty I - 12 Month Salaried (Pre-Clinical and Materials MRI (NHMFL)) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 62801 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department National High Magnetic Field Laboratory Responsibilities Position Overview: The National High Magnetic Field Laboratory (MagLab) at Florida State University invites applications for a research faculty position focused on magnetic resonance imaging (MRI). Based at the Tallahassee facility, this role centers on supporting and collaborating with researchers in the internationally recognized NMR/MRI User Program, with emphasis on preclinical MRI/MRS, in-cell studies, and materials-oriented research. The successful candidate will play a key role in developing in vivo MRI and MRS methods at ultra-high magnetic field (21.1 T) and demonstrating their application in rodent models. This position offers the opportunity to contribute to rapidly advancing research areas while leveraging exceptional infrastructure, engineering support, and a highly collaborative scientific environment. Develop and implement advanced in vivo MRI and MRS methodologies at ultra-high field (21.1 T). Support and collaborate with internal and external users of the MagLab\u2019s NMR/MRI facilities. Provide technical and scientific expertise in the design of protocols, planning of experiments, and the acquisition and analysis of data. Manage and operate an 11.7-T Bruker MRI system with NMR microscopy and diffusion capabilities. Contribute to collaborative research projects and pursue independent research initiatives. Disseminate research findings through publications and conference presentations. Engage with national and international collaborators and user communities. Qualifications Ph.D. in engineering, neuroimaging, applied physics, applied mathematics, chemistry/biochemistry, computer science, or a related field relevant to MRI. Preferred Qualifications Strong foundation in MRI physics and image formation principles. Demonstrated experience developing MRI/MRS/MRSI pulse sequences. Programming expertise in MRI pulse sequence development (e.g., Bruker Paravision) and data processing (e.g., MATLAB or similar). Proven publication record. Ability to work effectively in collaborative, multidisciplinary environments. Experience managing or contributing to shared research facilities. Expertise in preclinical MRI/MRS, including: Animal protocol development Structural, metabolic, and functional 1H imaging Heteronuclear imaging (spin-1/2 and quadrupolar nuclei) Spectroscopy and spectroscopic imaging Other Information Professional Opportunities: Opportunity to pursue independent and collaborative research programs. Encouragement to apply for external funding (salary is not contingent on grant support). Participation in national and international conferences and professional organizations. Helpful Facilities and Resources: The MagLab hosts a world-unique 21.1-T MRI/MRS system, featuring: 105-mm bore Advanced gradient systems and multinuclear RF coils State-of-the-art Bruker NEO console These capabilities are supported by: Onsite animal housing facilities Dedicated MRI hardware engineering staff The position also involves collaboration with the AMRIS facility at the University of Florida (Gainesville), with occasional travel required. Research Environment: The MagLab is the world\u2019s premier magnet laboratory, housing state-of-the-art high-field instrumentation and a long history of innovation in NMR and MRI technologies. The NMR/MRI User Facility hosts hundreds of users from around the world each year. Contact Info Please contact William Brey if you have any questions. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applications must include: Curriculum vitae Statement of research accomplishments and future vision Statement of leadership philosophy and vision for the NMR/MRI program Contact information for three references Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. Review of applications begins August 1, 2026, and continues until the position is filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=62785&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Core Faculty & Open Rank Professor, 12 Month Salaried (College of Medicine OBGYN Residency Program) Pensacola, FL", "description": "Job Title Core Faculty & Open Rank Professor, 12 Month Salaried (College of Medicine OBGYN Residency Program) Pensacola, FL Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 62785 Location Pensacola, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department College of Medicine, COM OBGYN Residency Program Responsibilities The successful candidate will provide comprehensive obstetric and gynecologic care while serving as a mentor, teacher, and clinical supervisor for residents and FSU medical students. We are looking for a candidate committed to clinical excellence, surgical mastery, and the advancement of women\u2019s health in Northwest Florida. Clinical Teaching and Supervision of Residents Core Program Clinical Teaching Clinical Practice in Obstetrics and Gynecology (OB-GYN) or applicable Subspecialty General Administration GME Committees/Meetings GME Lecturing/Teaching Conferences GME Recruiting/Interviewing GME Research/Scholarly Activity Resident Evaluation/Monitoring Program Evaluation The successful candidate will have the opportunity to shape the program in their vision and recruit core faculty. Qualifications Doctoral degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Valid FL medical license, or licensed in another state with the ability to obtain FL licensure. Must be board certified/Board Eligible in Obstetrics and Gynecology by the American Board of Obstetrics and Gynecology (ABOG) Must have a minimum of 3 years of faculty and administrative experience in an ACGME accredited Obstetrics and Gynecology residency program. Preferred Qualifications Effective professional management skills, including the ability to plan, organize and schedule work in an efficient and productive manner, focusing on key priorities and meeting deadlines. Outstanding interpersonal, leadership, mentoring and teaching skills. A strong work ethic and desire to participate in a team-oriented, performance-driven health system. Ability to communicate with others in a clear, understandable, and professional manner in person, on the phone, electronically, and in writing. Ability to build and lead high-performing teams; must be able to provide clear and accurate direction and guidance. Have strong administrative and team building skills. Candidates with recent scholarly activity such as peer reviewed funding, publication of original research or review articles in peer-reviewed journals, chapters in textbooks, publication or presentation of case reports or clinical series at scientific society meetings, or participation in national committees or educational organizations are highly encouraged to apply. Other Information The City of Pensacola, FL Pensacola, Florida, is a captivating blend of deep Southern heritage and breathtaking coastal beauty, often distinguished from the rest of the state by its \"Old Florida\" feel and rich history. Known as the \"City of Five Flags,\" its identity is rooted in over 450 years of history, which is most evident in the wrought-iron balconies and brick-paved streets of its vibrant downtown. Unlike the high-rise-dominated skylines of South Florida, Pensacola maintains a more grounded, soulful atmosphere where historic preservation meets a thriving modern culinary and arts scene. Beyond its history, the city is defined by its powerful connection to the military and the Gulf. As the \"Cradle of Naval Aviation,\" it serves as the home base for the Blue Angels, whose roaring practice flights are a local staple. Just across the bay, the landscape shifts to the stunning Gulf Islands National Seashore, where the sand is famously white\u2014composed of nearly pure Appalachian quartz\u2014and the water transitions from clear shallows to deep emerald hues. Pensacola offers a unique pace of life that balances rugged coastal adventure with warm, Southern hospitality. Contact Info Jessee Graham University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://hr.fsu.edu/facultyjobs. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Faculty Information This faculty position is jointly affiliated with Florida State University (FSU) and Ascension Sacred Heart. Appointment is contingent upon the successful completion of all onboarding and employment requirements of both institutions. These requirements include, but are not limited to: a comprehensive credentialing process through Ascension Sacred Heart Medical Staff Office, background screening, professional reference checks, drug screening, and submission of a self-query report from the National Practitioner Data Bank (NPDB). Please note that Ascension Sacred Heart credentialing process may take up to 90 days from the date the offer is accepted. Final appointment and the ability to initiate clinical responsibilities are contingent upon the approval of medical staff membership and clinical privileges by Ascension Sacred Heart. Further details regarding onboarding and credentialing processes will be provided during the interview and offer stages. List of Ascension Sacred Heart Program Director Requirements (PDF). Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This is a Clinical Non-Tenure earning position. This position is listed as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=62705&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "IGNITE Communications & Marketing Manager", "description": "Job Title IGNITE Communications & Marketing Manager Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 62705 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The Division of Research seeks to fill the role of IGNITE Communications & Marketing Manager. The Strategic Partnerships and Innovation team within the Division of Research consists of the IGNITE Incubation Program, Commercialization, and Business & Industry Solutions organizational units. This position primarily supports the IGNITE Incubation Program and Commercialization. The IGNITE Incubation Program promotes, encourages, and enhances the research activities of FSU faculty, staff, and students, and brings together the strengths of FSU and the region, providing a critical interface to move university and community research into the marketplace, stimulate high-tech and biotech industries, and create jobs. Clients are FSU faculty, staff, and students; small business owners; and technology and economic development leaders in the community, especially representatives of government, business, and industry. https://www.research.fsu.edu/ignite-tallahassee/ Commercialization is responsible for the identification, evaluation, development, protection, and commercialization of FSU intellectual property rights. For Commercialization, marketing and communication is primarily outward facing telling the stories of the public impacts of the utilization of research results and marketing to promote partnerships and find partners to develop and advance FSU intellectual property. https://www.research.fsu.edu/research-offices/oc Responsibilities The IGNITE Communications & Marketing Manager is responsible for developing an overall marketing and communications strategy for the IGNITE Incubation Program and Commercialization within the Strategic Partnerships & Innovation team. The position reports directly to the IGNITE Program Director of the incubation program and indirectly to the Associate Director for Strategic Partnerships & Innovation. The IGNITE Communications & Marketing Manager serves in a professional communicator role and requires training and experience in oral and written communication. Responsibilities include: Developing and implementing an overall marketing and communications strategy for the IGNITE Incubation Program and Commercialization, as well as leading, coordinating, and executing strategic initiatives to enhance visibility and community engagement. Developing visual and written content and material that represents the marketing identity of Strategic Partnerships & Innovation team and the FSU Division of Research. Creating, editing, and delivering high profile marketing and promotional materials such as brochures, flyers, newsletters, and digital & multimedia content. Draft and maintain updated marketing collateral for both external and internal stakeholders. Coordination on a wide variety of programs and activities designed to promote and publicize strategic initiatives (including but not limited to conferences, events, exhibition booths, roadshows, etc.). Engagement and collaboration with community and partner organizations to increase awareness of program initiatives. Lead and execute multichannel marketing campaigns in coordination with the communication team in the Office of the Vice President for Research (OVPR). Serves as a media contact; organizes and coordinates events, seminars, forums, and press releases in coordination with FSU OVPR and University Communications & Marketing. Other duties as assigned related to the marketing and communication for Strategic Partnerships & Innovation. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and four years\u2019 experience related to media, communications, and/or marketing services or a combination of post high school education and experience equal to eight years. Preferred Qualifications Experience with university research, incubation, or technology transfer communications and marketing or other technology-based area. Must have excellent written and verbal communications skills and demonstrated project management skills. Contact Info Cassidy Cooksey at rsch-workforce@fsu.edu University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our interactive too l to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://jobs.fsu.edu. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Upload at least two visual and/or writing samples or a link to your portfolio with your application. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=62758&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Project OPAL - Early Childhood Assessor/Interventionist - Florida Center for Reading Research (Part-time, OPS) (Multiple Vacancies)", "description": "Job Title Project OPAL - Early Childhood Assessor/Interventionist - Florida Center for Reading Research (Part-time, OPS) (Multiple Vacancies) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 62758 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Florida Center for Reading Research Responsibilities Administering standardized assessments Implementing a structured, research based small group intervention Maintaining accurate records and adhering to research protocols Coordinating with teachers and research staff to ensure effective implementation Traveling to assigned sites daily Qualifications High school diploma or equivalent Experience working with children ages 4-6. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor's degree or higher in a related field (e.g., Early Childhood Education, Elementary Education, Child Development, Psychology) Previous teaching or classroom experience Experience working in a research based educational or child development setting Ideal candidates are dependable, personable, comfortable working independently in the field, and excited to make a positive impact in local communities. Other Information The Florida Center for Reading Research is seeking enthusiastic and reliable individuals to serve as Early Childhood Assessors and Interventionists for Project OPAL. In this role, you will play a key part in supporting the literacy development on pre-kindergarten and kindergarten children by administering assessments and implementation of a 12-week phonemic awareness intervention. Hiring and paid training will begin in June/July 2026, with field work running from August 2026 through May 2027. This is a great opportunity for individuals interested in gaining hands-on field experience, contributing to meaningful community-based research, and working with a supportive project team throughout the school year. Contact Info For additional information regarding this position please contact Karli Willis: kborowski@fcrr.org University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. Anticipated Salary Range Starting at $15 - $18 per hour, commensurate with education and experience. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://jobs.fsu.edu. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an OPS/temporary job. Based on the duties, this position may require completion of a criminal history background check . This position will be for 15-20 hours/week. Candidates should be available Monday through Friday between 8:00AM and 3:00PM, aligned with local school hours. This position requires reliable transportation and willingness to travel to schools within your designated region on a daily basis. Work will be performed in Lowndes and Brooks Counties, Georgia, and Walton, Washington, and Holmes Counties, Florida. Applicants may reside within 50 miles of any of the listed counties. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=62756&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Open Rank Professor, 9 Month Salaried (National High Magnetic Field Laboratory (NHMFL) and the Florida A&M University (FAMU)-Florida State University (FSU) College of Engineering)", "description": "Job Title Open Rank Professor, 9 Month Salaried (National High Magnetic Field Laboratory (NHMFL) and the Florida A&M University (FAMU)-Florida State University (FSU) College of Engineering) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 62756 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The National High Magnetic Field Laboratory (NHMFL) and the Department of Chemical & Biomedical Engineering (CBE) at the Florida A&M University (FAMU)-Florida State University (FSU) College of Engineering invite applications from highly qualified individuals for a faculty position at the NHMFL with an academic home as a tenured or tenure-track faculty member in CBE through Florida State University. Responsibilities The successful candidate is expected to have a strong commitment to teaching excellence in undergraduate and graduate courses and participate in college and professional services. Qualifications Candidates must possess an earned Ph.D. in chemical or biomedical engineering, or a closely related discipline, and demonstrate documented potential for outstanding research, leadership, and education. Helpful We are seeking faculty candidates for a full professor position, however, exceptional candidates at other ranks will be considered. Contact Info Any questions about the position should be directed to Dr. Ayyalusamy Ramamoorthy, Search Committee Chair, at aramamoorthy@magnet.fsu.edu . Additional information about both universities and the department may be found at http://www.eng.famu.fsu.edu University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our interactive too l to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://hr.fsu.edu/facultyjobs. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include: A cover letter A full curriculum vitae A 2 to 3-page research statement. This statement should clearly indicate how the proposed research efforts will connect to other efforts in the NHMFL and CBE. A one-page teaching statement No more than three selected publications for review The names and contact information of four potential references Faculty Information The NHMFL is the world's premier magnet laboratory with state-of-the-art high magnetic field facilities and has a history in development and application of ultra-high field NMR and MRI/S magnets and instrumentation. The MR User Facility hosts hundreds of users from around the world each year. We are seeking candidates with expertise and research in magnetic resonance imaging although other application areas of NMR may be considered. The candidate will be expected to lead research efforts and user support at the NHMFL in MRI and NMR and be a full academic member with teaching duties in CBE. Successful candidates are expected to develop research programs that are recognized internationally with significant and sustained external funding, incorporate interdisciplinary collaboration with researchers across campus and through the NHMFL user program, and demonstrate a strong commitment to excellence in education. Teaching undergraduate and graduate courses and supervising undergraduate, graduate and post-doctoral researchers are expected. CBE has a dynamic group of faculty members actively involved in research encompassing various areas of biomedical engineering, chemical engineering, and materials science and engineering. Several faculty members from CBE have laboratories and are affiliated with the NHMFL performing research in NMR and MRI. Successful candidates will have many opportunities to interact and collaborate with other programs at FSU including the College of Medicine, Institute of Molecular Biophysics, the Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry, and the Department of Physics and the FAMU College of Pharmacy & Pharmaceutical Sciences. The NHMFL is operated for the National Science Foundation by a collaboration of institutions comprising Florida State University, the University of Florida, and Los Alamos National Laboratory. The FAMU-FSU College of Engineering is the unique combination of two outstanding universities with overlapping but distinct missions - the nation's top Historically Black College/University and a Tier-1 top 20 public research university. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Application review will begin September 15, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. The appointment is expected to begin August 2027. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=62748&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar (Multiple Openings) College of Nursing - Institute on Digital Health and Innovation", "description": "Job Title Postdoctoral Scholar (Multiple Openings) College of Nursing - Institute on Digital Health and Innovation Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 62748 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department College of Nursing Institute on Digital Health and Innovation (IDHI) Responsibilities Scholars will engage in a variety of mentored research and professional development activities with the support of IDHI Director, Dr. Lisa Hightow-Weidman, MPH, MD; Co- Director, Dr. Kate Muessig, PhD; and/or other faculty within the IDHI. Link to Faculty bios . Scholars will be supported in building a mentorship network tailored specifically to their development needs and research areas of interest. At the start of the fellowship, scholars will work with their mentorship team to create an individual development plan which will include training goals and activities. Scholars will be encouraged and supported through networking opportunities with professionals and faculty across a variety of disciplines in the top-rated research universities and institutions in the U.S. and globally. IDHI leadership and collaborating partners have extensive experience supporting the professional development of early career trainees and faculty, including skill-building in: research grant proposal development; manuscript development and publication; qualitative and quantitative research methods; behavioral intervention development, implementation, and evaluation; and career planning and advancement. In addition to being integrated with ongoing research projects, scholars will have protected time and mentorship to develop their own independent research ideas and portfolios. This may include activities such as: publishing dissertation manuscripts, writing an NIH training and/or career development awards (e.g. F series, K series), attending professional meetings and conferences, guest lecturing, and engaging in professional service activities. The specific balance of collaborative research and independent research will be discussed with the mentorship team and tailored to meet the scholar\u2019s professional development goals. Qualifications Doctorate or appropriate terminal degree in Public Health, Nursing, Psychology, Social Work, Sociology, Anthropology or another related discipline conferred within the last five years. Background in behavioral and social science research. Experience with qualitative and/or quantitative research methods. Experience and/or interest in research focused on HIV prevention and care, mental health, stigma and the social determinants of health. Have an interest in advancing digital health, artificial intelligence, and technology-enhanced healthcare solutions. Demonstrated commitment to interdisciplinary research, team science, and improving health outcomes. Please upload a cover letter with your online application. Preferred Qualifications Experience and/or interest in LGBTQ+/sexual and gender minority (SGM) health and research. Experience conducting intervention health research and/or practice. Experience and/or interest in digital health tools, interventions, and research/practice applications. Other Information Established in 2022, the Institute on Digital Health and Innovation (IDHI) within the Florida State University College of Nursing promotes individual, public health, and health equity through collaborative and synergistic partnerships for the development, evaluation, and dissemination of digital health tools, technologies, and innovations. The mission of IDHI is to advance digital health science, technologies, and tools focused on solving real world needs of patients, providers, and populations through research, training, and innovation to maximize health and eliminate health inequities. IDHI is currently accepting applications for postdoctoral fellowship positions. This mentored fellowship is designed to prepare exceptional early career scholars for an independent research-focused career in academia, government, civil society, the private or non-profit sector. Scholars will build their own research portfolio and collaborate with peer scholars and IDHI faculty and professionals at FSU and partnering institutions. IDHI faculty lead numerous federally-funded research networks and studies, including the NIH-funded Adolescent Medicine Trials Network for HIV Interventions (ATN) Scientific Leadership Center and the HealthMpowerment digital health initiative . More information about past and on-going research studies . Contact Info Crissi Rainer University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. Anticipated Salary Range Salary range of $65,000 to $70,000, commensurate with experience. In addition, scholars will be provided with a generous discretionary fund to support professional development and research activities. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://jobs.fsu.edu. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Please upload a cover letter with your online application. Considerations This is an OPS/temporary job. Based on the duties, this position may require completion of a criminal history background check . Full-time: Monday - Friday, 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m., with flexibility for some occasional evening and weekend hours to accommodate study needs. This position is being advertised as open until filled. It's preferred that this role be in person in Tallahassee, FL. A remote position may be considered in exceptional circumstances. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=62712&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar (Institute for Pediatric Rare Diseases) Medicine", "description": "Job Title Postdoctoral Scholar (Institute for Pediatric Rare Diseases) Medicine Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 62712 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department College of Medicine, Institute for Pediatric Rare Diseases Responsibilities Utilize linked clinical datasets to examine relationships between genetic variation and health outcomes. Conduct literature review and evidence extraction to support gene-and variant-level curation for neurodevelopmental disorders. Contribute to data organization and quality control for curated gene lists, variant datasets, and phenotype annotations. Assist with database updates, including incorporation of new evidence and verification of existing entries. Participate in manuscript preparation, including drafting assigned sections, figure/table development, and reference management. Support grant-related activities, such as literature synthesis, preliminary data compilation, and methods documentation. Collaborate with multidisciplinary team members (e.g., genetics, bioinformatics, clinical collaborators) and attend project meetings. Follow established standards for data rigor, reproducibility, and documentation. Mentor trainees or students as appropriate on discrete tasks, under senior guidance. Qualifications Ph.D. (or equivalent doctoral degree) in genetics, genomics, epidemiology, bioinformatics, biomedical informatics, neuroscience, public health, or a related field conferred within the last five years. Strong foundation in human genetics or genomics or related scientific field. Proficiency in data analysis and statistical or computational tools (e.g., R, Python, SQL, or equivalent). Ability to critically evaluate scientific literature and synthesize findings across genetics and clinical domains. Strong written and verbal communication skills, with experience contributing to manuscripts, abstracts, or reports. Ability to work independently on assigned tasks while collaborating effectively within a multidisciplinary research team. Familiarity with data privacy, ethics, and governance requirements for human health and genetic data. Preferred Qualifications Demonstrated experience working with health record\u2013derived clinical data (e.g., EHRs, data registries, or longitudinal clinical datasets). Experience with phenotypic data curation and harmonization, including diagnosis codes, clinical measures, or structured health outcomes. Experience conducting genotype\u2013phenotype association or correlation analyses, including handling phenotypic heterogeneity. Exposure to longitudinal outcome analyses using clinical data. Experience supporting or contributing to NIH-funded research, including preliminary data generation or grant writing. Demonstrated interest in translational or clinically oriented genetic research. Prior mentoring of students or trainees on data analysis or curation tasks. Contact Info Janelle Stanton , Ph.D. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://jobs.fsu.edu. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an OPS/temporary job. Based on the duties, this position may require completion of a criminal history background check . This is a full-time role. This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=62697&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Occupational Safety & Health Engineer", "description": "Job Title Occupational Safety & Health Engineer Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 62697 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Environmental Health & Safety Responsibilities Recently named a Forbes \u2018Best In-State Employer\u2019, Florida State University is a complex, constantly evolving academic environment where classrooms, laboratories, residence halls, and public spaces must operate safely and reliably in support of learning, research, and campus life. The Industrial Safety & Health Engineer plays a fundamental role in maintaining these environments. The Industrial Safety & Health Engineer is a new position within the EHS team that was created to provide hands-on support within the Facilities Maintenance organization. This role is focused on identifying and evaluating safety and health hazards, preventing workplace-related injuries and illnesses, responding to EHS concerns, and ensuring compliance with safety standards. Through this work, the role strengthens FSU\u2019s risk posture and helps ensure a safe, healthy campus environment that advances the university\u2019s mission as it continues to grow. This position assists in evaluating and recommending controls for potentially unsafe environmental, health, and safety conditions at the University, applying knowledge of federal, state, and local regulations and University policies. As part of the Environmental Health & Safety team, you will specifically: Responsible for administering and providing guidance for occupational safety programs. Some examples include lifting devices (portable cranes, hoists, slings), powered industrial trucks, PPE hazard assessments, new equipment startup, and EHS audits. Support the development of new EHS programs and the improvement of existing programs. Supports the development and delivery of EHS training to Facilities staff. Evaluate work environments to identify potential health and safety risks and hazards. Develop and implement corrective actions to address hazards. Provide recommendations to Facilities and other stakeholders for corrective actions to ensure compliance with regulations and University requirements. Collaborate with EHS and Facilities staff to evaluate program gaps. Support risk and self-assessments to identify program gaps and opportunities for improvements. Perform other tasks to support the improvement of the safety culture and management system structure. Collaborate with EHS, Facilities departments, and University staff to conduct comprehensive investigations for incidents, including injuries, near misses, safety concerns, etc. Respond to workplace emergencies or accidents to safeguard life and property damage, and to investigate the root cause and contributing factors of incidents. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and two years of related safety and health experience or a high school diploma or equivalent and six years of experience. (Note: or a combination of post-high-school education and experience equal to 6 years.) Preferred Qualifications Strong communication and customer-service skills, with the ability to collaborate effectively across departments and with external customers. Demonstrated ability to make sound decisions under pressure and maintain operational continuity during emergencies or adverse conditions. Working knowledge of EHS regulations. Experience building a positive safety culture. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our interactive too l to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://jobs.fsu.edu. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . The work schedule is from 8:00 a.m. to 4:30 p.m., with a 30-minute lunch break. This position is open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=62656&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Senior Industry Liaison - Office of Research", "description": "Job Title Senior Industry Liaison - Office of Research Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 62656 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Business & Industry Solutions - Office of Research Responsibilities The Senior Industry Liaison is responsible for building a portfolio of new industry partners and expanding existing industry collaboration with an emphasis on facilitating industry sponsored research utilizing the unique research capabilities, facilities, and intellectual property at FSU. The Senior Industry Liaison supports meetings between FSU research faculty/staff, potential industry partners, and administration. The successful candidate works directly with industry leadership, Deans, Department Chairs, and most importantly with research faculty/staff to match the expertise and facilities at FSU with the needs of industry. The Senior Industry Liaison educates Colleges, Departments, and researchers on interactions with industry to develop successful and productive collaborations- including differences in academia and industry objectives and successfully meeting and managing expectations. Supports Industry Research Days where companies are invited in targeted areas to campus for shared learning about industry needs and campus research capabilities. Works directly with community partners and organizations engaged in economic development and partnership efforts. Participates in and supports development and implementation of the FSU Industry Affiliate Program. The Affiliate program brings industry partners in the same sector into an annual membership- based model to support collaboration around specific FSU research areas. Qualifications Master's degree and two years of industry business development or corporate engagement experience or a Bachelor's degree and four years experience industry business development or corporate engagement experience. Preferred Qualifications Physics or engineering background. Contact Info Cassidy Cooksey - rsch-workforce@fsu.edu University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our interactive too l to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://jobs.fsu.edu. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=62655&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Teaching Faculty Open Rank, 9 or 12 Month Salaried - History, Social Science (Panama City Campus)", "description": "Job Title Teaching Faculty Open Rank, 9 or 12 Month Salaried - History, Social Science (Panama City Campus) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 62655 Location Panama City, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Social Science, Interdisciplinary Program | FSU Panama City Florida State University is one of the nation\u2019s top public universities and FSU Panama City amplifies the university\u2019s efforts to preserve, expand, and disseminate knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and human services professions. FSU Panama City is located 100 miles west of Tallahassee on the beautiful North St. Andrews Bay and is only three miles from the beaches of the emerald coast. FSU PC currently houses 20 bachelor's programs, 9 master's programs, and 1 doctoral program, and boasts a small faculty-to-student ratio, which gives students a more personalized academic experience. Please visit https://pc.fsu.edu/promise for information about our FSU PC Promise to students and https://pc.fsu.edu/ for more information about our campus. FSU Panama City also recently opened a brand new, residential housing complex on campus and right on the water. This new apartment-style complex at FSU PC houses both undergraduate and graduate students. For more information about our on-campus housing, visit https://seminolelandingfsu.com/ . Responsibilities Teach both dual-enrollment and other undergraduate courses for the FSU Liberal Studies curriculum & for the Interdisciplinary Social Sciences major with a special emphasis on the following areas: American History, World History, and additional Social Science based on expertise. Work with colleagues on campus and in the community to recruit students, promote FSU Panama City Interdisciplinary Social Science Program, and engage with local initiatives to benefit student experiences and program access Collaborate with colleagues at the FSU Tallahassee ISS (Interdisciplinary Social Science) program for course coordination and committee service. Be an engaged faculty member for the FSU Panama City Campus. Opportunities are available to engage in research and oversee student projects, though not specifically required for this teaching position. Qualifications PhD in History or related field, from an accredited institution. Candidates who are ABD (all but dissertation) will be considered, and candidates who have a Master\u2019s degree in History with a related doctoral degree will also be considered. Preferred Qualifications We especially seek candidates who have previous university teaching experience Are qualified to teach a variety of courses in the ISS curriculum Have direct experience facilitating support for students in career goals Successful candidates are expected to have a strong commitment to excellence in teaching and be dedicated to students. Other Information The FSU PC Interdisciplinary Program in Social Science (ISS) is designed to provide a broad background for students to understand public affairs and study complex issues and problems facing the social world with an interdisciplinary orientation. Students in this program are encouraged to apply a spectrum of perspectives to specific public policies and social issues. This academic program is flexible so that students may pursue their own individual specialized and pre-professional interests. Contact Info Dr. Amy Polick, Associate Dean - apolick@fsu.edu University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our interactive too l to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://hr.fsu.edu/facultyjobs. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applicants are encouraged to submit the following materials with their application for consideration: A cover letter describing university teaching experience, courses you feel qualified to teach, and why you are seeking this position. Current curriculum vitae Evidence of teaching effectiveness (copies of teaching evaluations and other data). Also, in the FSU application system, applicants must provide names and email contact information for at least 3 references, who will receive notifications to submit a letter of reference on your behalf. Please ensure that those references respond to this inquiry and submit their letters through the FSU application system. Additional information to help with providing letters of reference is below: Confidential Letters of Reference: Follow the steps below to request these letters through our system: 1) After submitting your application, click the Careers link. 2) Click the My References link. 3) Click the Send/View Reference Request button next to the appropriate position 4) Follow the steps on that page to send your references a system-generated email requesting they submit a letter of recommendation on your behalf. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position will be on campus at FSU Panama City in Panama City, FL. This position is being advertised as open until filled. The review of applications will start on June 5th, 2026. Applications received by the review date are assured full consideration. This position will begin in Fall 2026. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=62644&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Postdoctoral Research Associate \u2013 Superconducting Magnet Technology (High-Field Inserts) (Full-time, OPS)", "description": "Job Title Postdoctoral Research Associate \u2013 Superconducting Magnet Technology (High-Field Inserts) (Full-time, OPS) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 62644 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department National High Magnetic Field Laboratory (MagLab) - Materials Science & Technology (MS&T) Responsibilities The MS&T division at the National High Magnetic Field Laboratory seeks a highly motivated Postdoctoral Research Associate to contribute to the development of next-generation superconducting magnet technologies for high-field insert magnets. This role focuses on advancing conductor, coil, and magnet integration technologies enabling record-setting magnetic fields for scientific research. Design, build, and test high-field superconducting insert coils using advanced high-temperature superconductor technologies Develop and optimize coil architectures, winding approaches, and insulation systems for high-stress, high-field environments Contribute to mechanical, thermal, and electromagnetic modeling of insert magnets Perform experimental characterization including quench behavior, stability, and degradation mechanisms Support integration of insert coils within resistive or superconducting outsert magnet systems Collaborate with multidisciplinary teams across magnet design, cryogenics, and instrumentation Document results in technical reports, publications, and presentations Application of AI and machine-learning techniques (e.g., surrogate modeling, design optimization, inverse design, uncertainty quantification) to improve magnet performance, robustness, and manufacturability. Qualifications Ph.D. in Materials Science, Applied Physics, Electrical Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, or a related field Experience with superconducting materials or magnet systems Demonstrated experimental skills in cryogenic or high-field environments Strong analytical and problem-solving abilities Effective written and verbal communication skills Preferred Qualifications Experience with high-temperature superconductors (HTS), particularly REBCO Background in superconducting magnet design, coil fabrication, or testing Familiarity with finite element modeling tools (e.g., COMSOL, ANSYS) Experience with quench detection and protection methods Knowledge of mechanical behavior of conductors under high Lorentz forces Experience with instrumentation and data acquisition. Other Information Working Environment: This position involves hands-on work in laboratory settings, including cryogenic systems and high magnetic field facilities. The role requires close collaboration with scientists, engineers, and technical staff in a fast-paced R&D environment. Research Environment: The National High Magnetic Field Laboratory is the largest and highest-powered magnet laboratory in the world, supported by the National Science Foundation and the State of Florida. The MS&T Division develops cutting-edge magnet technologies and provides an exceptional environment for postdoctoral researchers, including: Access to state-of-the-art fabrication, cryogenic, and testing facilities. Collaboration with leading scientists and engineers across NHMFL and its partner institutions. A strong environment of mentorship and professional development, with many alumni progressing to successful careers in academia, national laboratories, and industry. Opportunities: Contribute to world-record magnet development efforts Publish in leading scientific journals and present at international conferences Engage with a globally recognized team in high-field magnet science and technology Helpful What You Gain at FSU Opportunity to work at a world-renowned national research laboratory. Meaningful contributions to scientific discovery and student learning. A collaborative environment that values your expertise and invests in your growth. Contact Info For additional information, please contact Kayla West at knwest@fsu.edu . University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://jobs.fsu.edu. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Application materials should include: A cover letter describing research interests and relevant experience A curriculum vitae Contact information for at least two professional references Considerations This is an OPS/temporary job. Based on the duties, this position may require completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=62562&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Assistant in Research, 12 Month Salaried - Maggie Allesee National Center for Choreography (MANCC)", "description": "Job Title Assistant in Research, 12 Month Salaried - Maggie Allesee National Center for Choreography (MANCC) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 62562 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Maggie Allesee National Center for Choreography (MANCC) School of Dance Responsibilities MANCC is seeking to fill the position of Assistant Director of Creative Research and Operations. Maggie Allesee National Center for Choreography (MANCC), as one of only two national residency centers for choreography in the United States located in or in partnership with a major research institution, supports choreographers and their collaborators to research, develop, and write about new work. Embedded within Florida State University\u2019s School of Dance, MANCC operates from one of the country\u2019s premiere dance facilities and offers unparalleled opportunities for contemporary choreographers to hone their artistic practice and develop new work inside a creative community. Artist Research & Residency Support Investigate artists\u2019 specific themes and areas of inquiry to provide tailored support for their creative goals. Organize research-driven activities, including scholar meetings, \"embodied sharings,\" and community events (including occasional evening/weekend sessions). Implement and manage post-residency evaluation processes to assess the effectiveness of MANCC\u2019s creative research support. Monitor the trajectory of MANCC projects, documenting premieres, awards, and touring schedules. Summarize artist evaluations and research outcomes for inclusion in grant reports and future funding requests. Development & Grant Management Manage end-to-end grant processes, including support of proposal development and the submission of post-award reports. Collaborate with University Business Administrators (UBA) staff to review grant budgets for accuracy and track expenditures to ensure award compliance. Support collaborations with regional, federal, and private funders, as well as partner organizations. Maintain detailed grant records to ensure administrative transparency and compliance. Media & Dissemination Collaborate on a media strategy\u2014encompassing social media, newsletters, and the website\u2014to showcase artist research and MANCC events. Facilitate the work of writers-in-residence to ensure creative processes are supported. Support special initiatives related to potential artist-led book publications or scholarly articles. Student Mentorship & Instruction Recruit, train, and manage a cohort of undergraduate and graduate interns and student staff. Provide ongoing mentorship and stewardship for students, specifically those pursuing the \"Dance to Arts Administration\" pathway. Serve as the Instructor of Record for Arts Administration internship courses and directed independent study. Special Initiatives & Administration Assist in improving the long-term utility and accessibility of MANCC\u2019s archives for scholarly research. Write project descriptions and post-residency summaries to communicate MANCC\u2019s seasonal activities to the public. Provide flexible administrative assistance related to residency operations as needed. Qualifications Master\u2019s Degree in Arts Administration, Dance, Performance Studies, or a related field in the Humanities or highest-level degree from an accredited institution or 7+ years of professional experience in the field of Arts Administration, Dance or Performance. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant In Research. Proven experience in budget development and expenditure tracking Demonstrated success in mentoring and supervising students or entry-level staff. Ability to manage complex logistics for public events. Willingness to work a flexible schedule, including occasional evenings and weekends. A commitment to recruiting and supervising cohorts of students. Additional education and experience as required by position. Other Information Housed within Florida State University\u2019s School of Dance, the Maggie Allesee National Center for Choreography (MANCC) celebrated its 20th anniversary in 2024-2025. The center supports choreographers and their collaborators to research, develop, and write about new work. The FSU School of Dance was established ninety years ago and has offered a professional dance major for sixty of those years. It has been recognized as a leader among college dance programs. Graduates of our programs include dancers, teachers, scholars, and leaders in companies, schools, universities, and art organizations in the United States and abroad. Our facility, Montgomery Hall, is one of the best in the nation. The Florida State University College of Fine Arts is a place where learning and creativity are cultivated through instruction, research, and practice. The College is a close-knit community of faculty, students, and professionals that functions as an art and design conservatory and liberal arts hybrid within a major research university. It is home to a unique combination of visual arts, performing art, and design studios, classrooms, performance spaces, galleries, and a museum. The current student enrollment encompasses approximately 850 undergraduate and 300 graduate students, working to become successful artists, designers, researchers, and professionals in their fields. The College comprises the School of Dance, the School of Theatre, the Department of Interior Architecture & Design, the Department of Art, the Department of Art Education, and the Department of Art History. It is supported by more than 100 full-time faculty, 50 adjunct faculty, 110 staff members, and a budget of approximately $19.3 million. The College also houses several non-academic units, including the Museum of Fine Arts (MoFA), the Facility for Arts Research (FAR), and the Maggie Allesee National Center for Choreography (MANCC). Many of the College\u2019s programs rank among the most respected in the nation and feature specialized programs that leverage relationships between departments and museums to enrich the degree-based curriculum. Contact Info Ansje Burdick \u2013 aburdick@fsu.edu University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our interactive too l to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://hr.fsu.edu/facultyjobs. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applicants are required to submit: Letter of interest Resume Name, addresses, telephone numbers, and email addresses of three references Confidential Letters of Reference: Follow the steps below to request these letters through our system: 1) After submitting your application, click the Explore Jobs link; 2) Click the My References link; 3) Click the Send/View Reference Request button next to the appropriate position; and 4) Follow the steps on that page to send your references a system generated email requesting they submit a letter of recommendation on your behalf. You may also return to the My References link and click on \"Send/View Reference Request\" to see if your references have responded, add additional references, or resend requests. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. Review of candidates will begin on June 22, 2026, and will continue until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=62403&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Open Rank Teaching Faculty, 9 or 12 Month Salaried - Hospitality Management (Panama City Campus)", "description": "Job Title Open Rank Teaching Faculty, 9 or 12 Month Salaried - Hospitality Management (Panama City Campus) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 62403 Location Panama City, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department FSU Panama City Hospitality and Tourism Management Program https://pc.fsu.edu/hospitality Florida State University is one of the nation\u2019s top public universities, and FSU Panama City amplifies the university\u2019s efforts to preserve, expand, and disseminate knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and human services professions. FSU Panama City is located 100 miles west of Tallahassee on the beautiful North St. Andrews Bay and is only three miles from the beaches of the Emerald Coast. FSU PC currently houses 20 bachelor's programs, 9 master's programs, and 1 doctoral program, and boasts a small faculty-to-student ratio, which gives students a more personalized academic experience. Please visit https://pc.fsu.edu/promise for information about our FSU PC Promise to students and https://pc.fsu.edu/ for more information about our campus. FSU Panama City also recently opened a brand new, residential housing complex on campus and right on the water. This new apartment-style complex at FSU PC houses both undergraduate and graduate students. For more information about our on-campus housing, visit https://seminolelandingfsu.com/ . Responsibilities Develop and teach face-to-face and online courses in the Hospitality and Tourism Management curriculum with a special emphasis on core courses in the program (including: financial analysis, leadership, marketing for hospitality, managing revenues, lodging, and/or catering management). Work with colleagues on campus, and from the Dedman College of Hospitality at the Tallahassee campus, to support the program with course coordination, curriculum development, and committee service. Provide high quality instruction, career advising/mentorship, and student service to our on-campus and online students. Be an engaged faculty member fostering relationships with local hospitality and tourism education and industry partners. Opportunities are available to engage in research, though not specifically required for this teaching faculty position. Qualifications PhD or DBA in Hospitality Management, or strongly related field, from an accredited institution. Candidates who are ABD will be considered, and candidates who have a Master\u2019s degree in Hospitality Management with a related doctoral degree will also be considered. Preferred Qualifications Preferred qualifications include: previous university teaching experience, demonstrated ability to teach online, and applied, industry experience. We especially seek candidates who can teach a broad range of undergraduate Hospitality Management courses. Successful candidates are expected to have a strong commitment to excellence in teaching and be dedicated to student success. Helpful Florida State University Panama City\u2019s Hospitality Management Bachelor\u2019s degree program is offered in-person with the flexibility for students to combine online with face-to-face courses. Overall, the program prepares students for leadership and management positions in hospitality and tourism businesses and organizations. The FSU Dedman College of Hospitality is world-renowned for their faculty and programs. The Dedman College\u2019s Hospitality Management program has been ranked as a top 10 program in the world by the Global Ranking of Academic Subjects. For more information about the Dedman College of Hospitality please visit https://dedman.fsu.edu/ . Contact Info Dr. Amy Polick, Associate Dean for Academic Affairs, FSU Panama City - apolick@fsu.edu University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our interactive too l to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://hr.fsu.edu/facultyjobs. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applicants are encouraged but not required to submit the following materials with application for consideration: A cover letter describing applied experiences specific to Hospitality Management, university teaching experience, courses in the Hospitality and Tourism Management program the applicant feels qualified to teach, and why you are seeking this position. Current curriculum vitae. A leadership statement highlighting values in leadership for student academic and clinical success. Evidence of teaching effectiveness (copies of teaching evaluations and other data). Applicants may also upload additional, relevant material to support your application in the FSU application system. If the system does not allow this information to be uploaded, email hr@pc.fsu.edu to arrange submission of materials. Confidential Letters of Reference: Follow the steps below to request these letters through our system: 1) After submitting your application, click the Careers link. 2) Click the My References link. 3) Click the Send/View Reference Request button next to the appropriate position and 4) Follow the steps on that page to send your references a system generated email requesting they submit a letter of recommendation on your behalf. You may also return to the My References link and click on \"Send/View Reference Request\" to see if your references have responded, add additional references, or resend requests. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . The position will begin in Fall 2026 with consideration for Spring 2027 if circumstances warrant. This position will be on-site in Panama City, Florida. This position is being advertised as open until filled. The review of applications will start May 11, 2026. Applications received by the review date are assured full consideration. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=62396&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Assistant in Research, 12 Month Salaried (NHMFL) \u2013 Multiple Vacancies", "description": "Job Title Assistant in Research, 12 Month Salaried (NHMFL) \u2013 Multiple Vacancies Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 62396 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department National High Magnetic Field Laboratory (MagLab) - DC Field Facility (DCFF) Responsibilities As a member of the DCFF user support team, the Research Faculty member supports a world-leading scientific user program built on a unique suite of resistive, superconducting, and hybrid magnet systems, specialized experimental techniques, and deep staff expertise. In this role, you will help enable high-impact experiments across condensed matter physics, materials science, and related fields by advancing DCFF capabilities, supporting user experiments, and ensuring safe, excellent, and collaborative operations. User Support & Experimental Operations Provide hands-on scientific and technical support to external and internal users conducting high-field experiments, ensuring safe and efficient execution of measurements. Guide users, as needed, in all aspects of an experiment: planning, preparation, instrument configuration, data acquisition, troubleshooting, data analysis, manuscript preparation. Maintain an active presence and consistent communication throughout the experiment, in an effort to ensure high quality experimental results. Instrumentation Development Design, build, optimize, and document advanced measurement systems, including various types of experimental probes and setups, tailored to user science needs. Lead improvements to reliability, robustness, and performance of existing DCFF scientific infrastructure. Collaborate with engineering, electronics, cryogenics, and machine shop teams to implement new capabilities. Research & Scientific Output Conduct collaborative research leveraging DCFF capabilities. Participation in publishing peer-reviewed papers, contributing to MagLab science highlights, and conference presentations. Identify emerging scientific opportunities and help shape future facility directions and proposals. Operational Excellence & Leadership Participate in magnet scheduling, experiment triage, and facility planning aligned with the MagLab mission and priorities. Contribute to developing standard operating procedures, technical documentation, and training materials. Demonstrate collaborative leadership within a multidisciplinary environment that includes mentoring students, postdocs, and early-career users. Qualifications Ph.D. in Physics, Materials Science, or a closely related field. Demonstrated expertise in experimental condensed matter physics or instrumentation relevant to high magnetic fields. Experience with cryogenics, low-noise measurements, high-precision instrumentation, data acquisition systems, or magnet-related experimental techniques. Strong record of scientific/technical productivity (publications, presentations, technical reports, designs). Excellent communication skills and ability to collaborate with a broad range of individuals. Active, can-do, perpetual-learner mindset that maintains a focus on service to user experiments. Commitment to maintaining an environment of safety excellence. Preferred Qualifications Experience working in high magnetic field research environment. Experience with the measurement techniques listed here . Experience working in large-scale user facilities or multi-user laboratory environments. Demonstrated success in developing measurement platforms, control systems, or advanced probes. Experience mentoring students or leading small project teams. Familiarity with facility operations, scheduling, and user program management. Ability to secure external funding to support scientific or instrumentation efforts. Contact Info For additional information, please contact Kayla West at knwest@fsu.edu . University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our interactive too l to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://hr.fsu.edu/facultyjobs. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. This position requires that you have three confidential professional letters of recommendation submitted on your behalf. Follow the steps below to request these letters through our system: 1) After submitting your application, click the Careers link; 2) Click the My References link; 3) Click the Send/View Reference Request button next to the appropriate position; and 4) Follow the steps on that page to send your references a system generated email requesting they submit a letter of recommendation on your behalf. You may also return to the My References link and click on \"Send/View Reference Request\" to see if your references have responded, add additional references, or resend requests. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position is being advertised as open until filled. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=62368&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Teaching Faculty I, 12 Month Salaried - Applied Behavior Analysis Psychology (Panama City Campus)", "description": "Job Title Teaching Faculty I, 12 Month Salaried - Applied Behavior Analysis Psychology (Panama City Campus) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 62368 Location Panama City, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department FSU Panama City \u2013 Psychology Department Florida State University is one of the nation\u2019s top public universities, and FSU Panama City amplifies the university\u2019s efforts to preserve, expand, and disseminate knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and human services professions. FSU Panama City is located 100 miles west of Tallahassee on the beautiful North St. Andrews Bay and is only three miles from the beaches of the Emerald Coast. FSU PC currently houses 20 bachelor's programs, 9 master's programs, and 1 doctoral program, and boasts a small faculty-to-student ratio, which gives students a more personalized academic experience. Please visit https://pc.fsu.edu/promise for information about our FSU PC Promise to students and https://pc.fsu.edu/ for more information about our campus. FSU Panama City also recently opened a brand new, residential housing complex on campus and right on the water. This new apartment-style complex at FSU PC houses both undergraduate and graduate students. For more information about our on-campus housing, visit https://seminolelandingfsu.com/ . Responsibilities Teaching in both the ABA Master\u2019s Program and the undergraduate psychology program at FSU Panama City. Mentoring graduate students and supervising clinical capstone studies for the ABA program. Engaging in service to the ABA program, psychology program, and FSU PC campus. Qualifications PhD in Psychology, Behavior Analysis, or related field with doctoral preparation in Behavior Analysis/ABA. ABD (All But Dissertation) are welcome to apply if degree completion is expected by start of the position. Must be a doctoral-level behavior analyst who meets requirements for teaching in an Association for Behavior Analysis International-accredited, Verified Course Sequence program. Preferred Qualifications Certification as a board-certified behavior analyst, experience in the clinical application of ABA across a variety of health-related populations (e.g., autism, aging, mental health, etc.), minimum of two years of experience teaching at the university level, experience conducting and overseeing applied research and mentoring student engagement with research and/or clinical projects. We especially seek candidates who are qualified to teach a variety of courses across different areas in behavior analysis and Psychology (e.g., grad-level courses in Ethics, Skinner\u2019s Theory of Behaviorism, Basic Principles of Behavior, and a breadth of undergrad areas in Psychology), have experience with Behavior Analyst Certification Board credentialing requirements and Association for Behavior Analysis International accreditation policies, and demonstrated, superior ability to teach high-quality courses at the university level. Other Information The Department of Psychology at Florida State University (FSU) has a well-established, nationally recognized, top-ranked Master's Degree program in Psychology with a major in Applied Behavior Analysis (ABA) that serves students at both the FSU Tallahassee and Panama City campuses. The FSU ABA Master\u2019s program is accredited by the Association for Behavior Analysis International (ABAI) and emphasizes a scientist-practitioner model, providing students with the education, training, and supervised clinical experiences required to sit for the Board-Certified Behavior Analyst exam (BCBA) upon graduation. In addition to the ABA Master\u2019s program, FSU also offers a Bachelor's Degree program in Psychology, which includes courses in Clinical, Cognitive, Developmental, and Social Psychology, as well as Neuroscience and Behavior Analysis. For more information about the FSU ABA program, visit https://pc.fsu.edu/aba/program . Contact Info Leah Koehler, PhD, BCBA-D Chair of Search Committee ABA Program Director lkoehler@fsu.edu University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our interactive too l to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://hr.fsu.edu/facultyjobs. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applicants are encouraged but not required to submit the following materials with application for consideration: A cover letter describing applied experiences specific to Social Work, university teaching experience, courses in the Social Work program the applicant feels qualified to teach, and why you are seeking this position. Current curriculum vitae. A leadership statement highlighting values in leadership for student academic and clinical success. Evidence of teaching effectiveness (copies of teaching evaluations and other data). Applicants may also upload additional, relevant material to support your application in the FSU application system. If the system does not allow this information to be uploaded, email HR@pc.fsu.edu to arrange submission of materials. Confidential Letters of Reference: Follow the steps below to request these letters through our system: 1) After submitting your application, click the Careers link. 2) Click the My References link. 3) Click the Send/View Reference Request button next to the appropriate position and 4) Follow the steps on that page to send your references a system generated email requesting they submit a letter of recommendation on your behalf. You may also return to the My References link and click on \"Send/View Reference Request\" to see if your references have responded, add additional references, or resend requests. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled Review of applications are ongoing and will continue until the position is filled or closed. This position will begin in Summer or Fall 2027, with the ability to start sooner if circumstances allow. This position will be on-site in Panama City, FL. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=62231&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Construction Project Manager (Levels I \u2013 III) (Multiple Vacancies)", "description": "Job Title Construction Project Manager (Levels I \u2013 III) (Multiple Vacancies) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 62231 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Planning, Design & Construction Responsibilities The Planning, Design & Construction department offers career ladders for many of our positions which allow tenured employees promotional opportunities within their job. The successful candidate will be hired at the most appropriate level of Project Specialist/Manager, based on education and experience. This position will be responsible for managing the design and/or construction process of capital improvement projects, assuring projects are designed in compliance with university, state and federal standards and programmatic requirements and completed on schedule, within budget and in compliance with a contractually defined scope and quality standards. Project scopes may include all building systems and a wide variety of project types, with a moderate level of complexity such as a clinic/laboratory. Develops project(s) description and scopes of work. Manages project communication with multiple entities related to assigned projects including but not limited to project customer, internal and external stakeholders, Design Professionals (internal and external), Consultant(s), Construction Manager(s), and vendor(s). Coordinates, conducts and/or participates in efficient, well-planned, and productive meetings throughout assigned project(s). Identifies, interfaces with, and gathers input from appropriate stakeholders. Interprets client questions/requests and responds with answers and solutions. Utilizes project management system keeping project information up to date. Recommends selection of, negotiates with and coordinates the work of Design Professionals, Consultant(s), Construction Managers and vendor(s). Assures contracts/agreements reflect client needs and project parameters. Reviews contract/agreement documentation for compliance and initiates change orders and amendments. Ensures project funding in place for project encumbrances. Monitors and processes payments for work of Design Professionals, Consultant(s), Construction Managers and vendor(s) as required for projects. Responsible for the project management process throughout entire project. Coordinates work of multiple projects. Develops project budget using resources available. Interacts with Design Professionals, users, resource personnel and others to attain the most cost-effective method for completing project. Monitors accounts/expenditures; reconcile statements. Ensures funding is in place for budget expenditures. Provides advice, prepares, and monitors project schedules for review to assure project needs are met as directed. Assures projects remain on schedule throughout course of design and/or construction. Monitors projects throughout lifecycle to assure scope, time and budget requirements are met. Highlights key decisions for the project team in advance of deadlines. Utilizes project management system keeping project information up to date. Provides briefings and reports that are accurate and contain appropriate detail and provides evaluations of Professionals involved in projects as requested. May provide direction, assignments, feedback, coaching, and/or counseling to a project team. Advises and mentors staff on all contract management aspects, reviews design for code compliance, and recommends change orders and substitutions for materials, equipment, and workmanship. May serves as Subject matter expert and advisor to leadership on complex project requirements. Qualifications Level I \u2013 Project Specialist - Bachelor's degree in Architecture, Engineering, or Construction Management and one year of related experience, or a combination of related post high school education and experience equal to five years. Level II \u2013 Project Manager - Bachelor's degree in Architecture, Engineering, or Construction Management and five years of related experience or a combination of related post high school education and experience equal to nine years. Level III \u2013 Senior Project Manager - Master\u2019s degree in Architecture, Engineering, Construction Mgmt, or Business Admin and seven years related experience or a Bachelor's degree and nine years related experience, or a combination of post high school education and experience equal to 13 years. A valid State of Florida or Georgia Driver\u2019s License or ability to obtain upon hire. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our interactive too l to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://jobs.fsu.edu. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=62220&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Quality Control Director - Planning, Design & Construction", "description": "Job Title Quality Control Director - Planning, Design & Construction Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 62220 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Planning, Design & Construction Responsibilities Manages the quality control and quality assurance, compliance, and technical standards for PD&C. Develops, maintains, and enforces a comprehensive Quality Management Plan processes including but not limited to building envelope and mechanical, electrical, plumbing, fire protection, and technology commissioning for projects. Oversees, manages, and establishes processes and university input for campus design standards and continuous improvement in quality management processes, including annual campus design standards updates. Provides expert guidance to project teams on technical issues, regulatory requirements, and best-practice construction methodologies. Monitors and conducts comprehensive reviews of project design documents, technical specifications, and construction activities to ensure compliance with campus design standards, building codes, safety regulations, BOG regulations, and industry best practices. Lead schedule development requirements and operational coordination of project commissioning activities during design and construction for projects. Provides expert scheduling advice to leadership and recommends scheduling incentive strategies when appropriate. Coordinate project activities across internal departments and external partners to ensure seamless execution and operational readiness for building and/or system turnover. Ensure Design Agreements include required campus design standards edition per project and maintain accurate project records, including deviation requests and deviation approvals by project. Responsible for stakeholder engagement and executive communication. Serve as a primary liaison between project teams, departmental staff, senior administration, and campus stakeholders. Communicate project progress, risks, and recommendations through reports, presentations, and executive briefings. Engage customers to assess needs, manage expectations, and ensure satisfaction throughout the project lifecycle. Lead effective coordination among all project participants and represent the department in internal and external forums. Provide strategic leadership and supervision for staff on assigned projects, including setting direction, delegating assignments, and delivering ongoing feedback, coaching, and counseling to ensure successful outcomes. Develop and implement policies and workplace practices that promote staff engagement, accountability, and high performance. Qualifications Bachelor's degree in Construction Management, Engineering, Architecture, or related field and six years of experience related to the duties of the position, or a high school diploma or equivalent and ten years' experience. (Note: a combination of post-high-school education and experience equal to ten years of the same experience) University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. Anticipated Salary Range The anticipated starting salary range is $100,000 - $130,000, commensurate with education and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our interactive too l to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://jobs.fsu.edu. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This posting is open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=62137&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Program Director & Open Rank Professor, 12 Month Salaried (COM Residency Program Administration Internal Medicine) Jacksonville, FL", "description": "Job Title Program Director & Open Rank Professor, 12 Month Salaried (COM Residency Program Administration Internal Medicine) Jacksonville, FL Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 62137 Location Jacksonville, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department College of Medicine, COM Residency Program Administration Responsibilities The Program Director oversees the Internal Medicine Residency Program (\u201cIM Program\u201d or \u201cProgram\u201d) under the guidance of the Designated Institutional Official (DIO). The Program Director handles the general management, curriculum development, hiring, and teaching and mentoring of the Program. The Program Director sets the strategic vision of the Program and ensures its standards, quality, and reputation. The Program Director is expected to support the collaboration of the IM Program with physician practices and hospital clinical services in a way that improves value and quality, and that fosters a positive environment for professional practice and medical education. The Program Director will also work in collaboration with the existing program leadership to ensure outstanding educational offerings within Ascension St. Vincent's Riverside Hospital. Clinical Teaching and Supervision of Residents Core Program Clinical Teaching Clinical Practice in Internal Medicine or applicable Subspecialty General Administration GME Committees/Meetings GME Lecturing/Teaching Conferences GME Recruiting/Interviewing GME Research/Scholarly Activity Resident Evaluation/Monitoring Program Evaluation Qualifications Doctoral degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization and a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Valid FL medical license, or licensed in another state with the ability to obtain FL licensure. Must be board certified in Internal Medicine by the American Board of Internal Medicine. Must have a minimum of 3 years of faculty and administrative experience in an ACGME accredited internal medicine residency program. Preferred Qualifications Effective professional management skills, including the ability to plan, organize and schedule work in an efficient and productive manner, focusing on key priorities and meeting deadlines. Outstanding interpersonal, leadership, mentoring and teaching skills. A strong work ethic and desire to participate in a team-oriented, performance-driven health system. Ability to communicate with others in a clear, understandable, and professional manner in person, on the phone, electronically, and in writing. Ability to build and lead high-performing teams; must be able to provide clear and accurate direction and guidance. Strong administrative and team building skills. Other Information Ascension St. Vincent's Riverside \u2013 Jacksonville, FL Ascension is one of the nation\u2019s leading non-profit and Catholic health systems, with a Mission of delivering compassionate, personalized care to all with special attention to those most vulnerable. In FY2024, Ascension provided $2.1 billion in care of persons living in poverty and other community benefit programs. Across 16 states and the District of Columbia, Ascension\u2019s network encompasses approximately 106,000 associates, 26,000 aligned providers, 105 wholly owned or consolidated hospitals, and 34 senior living facilities. Additionally, through strategic partnerships, Ascension holds an ownership interest in 26 other hospitals. Ascension St. Vincent's Riverside in Jacksonville, Florida, is a full-service 528-bed hospital founded by the Daughters of Charity in 1916. Over the decades, the hospital expanded, with a new patient tower completed in 1968. In 1996, the Ascension St. Vincent's Health System acquired the facility. Today, it is a prominent hospital offering a range of specialty care, continuing its mission of compassionate healthcare for the Jacksonville community. Helpful The successful candidate will have the opportunity to shape the program in their vision and recruit core faculty. Candidates with recent scholarly activity such as peer reviewed funding, publication of original research or review articles in peer-reviewed journals, chapters in textbooks, publication or presentation of case reports or clinical series at scientific society meetings, or participation in national committees or educational organizations are highly encouraged to apply. Contact Info Jessee Graham: jjgraham@fsu.edu University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our interactive too l to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://hr.fsu.edu/facultyjobs. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This is a clinical/non-tenure earning role, and rank is commensurate with experience. This position is open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=62123&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "CLIA Lab Director/Open Rank Professor, 12 Months Salaried (CLIA Lab Diagnostics - Medicine)", "description": "Job Title CLIA Lab Director/Open Rank Professor, 12 Months Salaried (CLIA Lab Diagnostics - Medicine) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 62123 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department College of Medicine, CLIA Lab Diagnostics Institute for Pediatric Rare Diseases (IPRD) Responsibilities Serve as CLIA Laboratory Director with accountability for quality, compliance, and test result approval. Ensure adherence to CLIA, CAP, CMS, and Florida Department of Health regulations. Participate in formulating laboratory policies, standard operating procedures, and quality management systems. Supervise variant scientists and genetic counselors. Participate in validation of assays, proficiency testing, and continual quality improvement. Have primary responsibility for final clinical interpretation and written reports for all clinical genome sequencing cases. Provide consultation to clinicians and genetic counselors on test utilization and interpretation. Partner with IPRD leadership to expand services statewide and build collaborations with healthcare systems and industry. Qualifications Ph.D., M.D. or equivalent from an accredited institution with training in genetics, genomics, human genetics, or a related field within the biological sciences. Board certification/eligibility (ABMGG -LGG). Eligible for Florida licensure as a Laboratory Director. At least 2 years of experience working in a high-complexity CLIA laboratory. Strong background in next-generation sequencing, preferably genome sequencing. Demonstrated leadership ability in laboratory management, quality assurance, and compliance. Preferred Qualifications 3 - 5 years of experience working in a high-complexity CLIA-certified genome sequencing laboratory. Prior experience directing or helping to establish a CLIA-certified genome sequencing laboratory. Demonstrated expertise in rare disease diagnostics and application of ACMG/AMP variant interpretation guidelines. A strong record of collaboration in multidisciplinary genomic medicine teams, including clinicians, genetic counselors, variant scientists, and technologists. Experience in mentoring and training junior faculty, fellows, or laboratory staff in genomic diagnostics. Evidence of scholarly contributions, such as publications, invited presentations, or participation in professional working groups (e.g., ClinGen, ACMG). Familiarity with laboratory information management systems (LIMS), genomic databases, and bioinformatics workflows for high-throughput sequencing. Experience partnering with healthcare systems, industry, or public health agencies to expand access to genomic testing. Helpful The Florida Institute for Pediatric Rare Diseases (IPRD) seeks an American Board of Medical Genetics and Genomics (ABMGG) board-certified or board-eligible Laboratory Genetics and Genomics (LGG) faculty member to help lead its CLIA-certified Genome Sequencing Laboratory. This position is one of several new recruitments in clinical genetics and genomics as IPRD builds a multidisciplinary team of experts in genomic medicine at Florida State University. Together, our team of laboratory directors, variant scientists, medical geneticists, genetic counselors, and technologists will form a collaborative and interactive environment dedicated to advancing precision medicine for patients and families across Florida. The IPRD genome sequencing diagnostic facility is designed for statewide reach and national impact. It will support integration of genome sequencing into newborn screening and rare disease diagnosis, while also serving as a platform for translational research and innovation. As part of a growing team of genomic medicine specialists at FSU, the CLIA Laboratory Director will have the unique opportunity to help guide the laboratory\u2019s expansion, foster collaborations with healthcare systems and industry partners, and help position IPRD as a statewide hub of excellence in genomic diagnostics and clinical research. The Laboratory Director will ensure compliance with all CLIA and CAP regulations, help oversee high-complexity testing, and provide expert consultation to physicians and genetic counselors. Working within a dynamic team framework, the Director will play a leadership role in establishing standards, mentoring colleagues at multiple professional levels, and contributing to the integration of genomic testing into both clinical care and research programs. The position offers the opportunity for protected research time, up to 50 percent for candidates with strong research training or demonstrated potential. This research effort is expected to be supported by external grant funding, either as a principal investigator or as part of a collaborative research team. Contact Info Dr. Cynthia Vied: iprd@med.fsu.edu University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our interactive too l to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://hr.fsu.edu/facultyjobs. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This is an Open Rank Professor and Clinical (non-tenure earning) position. Rank is commensurate with experience. This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=62120&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Variant Scientist/Open Rank Professor, 12 Months Salaried - Genome Sequencing Laboratory (CLIA Lab Diagnostics - Medicine)", "description": "Job Title Variant Scientist/Open Rank Professor, 12 Months Salaried - Genome Sequencing Laboratory (CLIA Lab Diagnostics - Medicine) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 62120 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department College of Medicine, CLIA Lab Diagnostics Institute for Pediatric Rare Diseases (IPRD) Responsibilities Variant Analysis & Interpretation Perform comprehensive review, classification, and annotation of genetic variants identified by whole genome sequencing, following ACMG/AMP and ClinGen guidelines. Curate evidence from public databases (e.g., ClinVar, gnomAD, OMIM), scientific literature, and internal laboratory data. Participate in multidisciplinary review of variants with laboratory directors, medical geneticists, and genetic counselors. Clinical Reporting Draft clinical reports for genome sequencing tests, ensuring clarity and clinical utility. Communicate findings to CLIA Lab Director. Contribute to laboratory variant databases and knowledge management systems. Quality & Compliance Ensure all variant interpretation and reporting activities comply with CLIA, CAP, and laboratory quality management standards. Assist in maintaining standard operating procedures for variant interpretation and reporting. Participate in proficiency testing, audits, and continual quality improvement initiatives. Collaboration & Education Collaborate with bioinformaticians, technologists, and other laboratory personnel on test development and validation. Support teaching and training activities, including workshops and case discussions with students, residents, fellows, and clinicians. Stay current with advances in genomic technologies, variant interpretation frameworks, and clinical genetics literature. Qualifications Master\u2019s degree or PhD in Human Genetics, Genomics, Genetic Counseling, Molecular Biology, Bioinformatics, or related field from an accredited institution. Experience in clinical genomic data analysis and variant interpretation (can include fellowship or postdoctoral experience). Familiarity with ACMG/AMP variant classification guidelines. Strong knowledge of human genetics, Mendelian disease mechanisms, and rare disease biology. Experience with genomic databases and tools (ClinVar, OMIM, HGMD, gnomAD, LOVD, UCSC Genome Browser, etc.). Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with ability to convey complex genetic findings to variety of audiences. Preferred Qualifications At least 2 years of experience in clinical genomic data analysis and variant interpretation (can include fellowship or postdoctoral experience). Experience with genome sequencing in a CLIA-certified laboratory setting. Prior experience with laboratory information management systems (LIMS) and variant databases. Familiarity with bioinformatics pipelines for next-generation sequencing. Experience working in multidisciplinary clinical genomics teams. Helpful The Florida Institute for Pediatric Rare Diseases (IPRD) is seeking Variant Scientists to join its CLIA-certified Genome Sequencing Diagnostic Facility. This role is one of several new positions in clinical genetics and genomics for which IPRD is actively recruiting, as we build a multidisciplinary team of experts in genomic medicine at Florida State University. The Variant Scientists will play a critical role in the interpretation and reporting of genomic data generated in the laboratory, with a primary focus on rare disease diagnostics, while working in a collaborative environment with colleagues across multiple professional levels. The Variant Scientist will be integral to the success and growth of IPRD\u2019s statewide genomics initiative to provide genome sequencing for newborns and rare disease patients across Florida. As demand for clinical genome sequencing increases, this position will expand in scope, with opportunities to contribute to laboratory innovation, clinical trials, and genomic data-sharing initiatives. By joining a lively and interactive team of laboratory directors, medical geneticists, genetic counselors, technologists, and researchers, the Variant Scientist will help establish FSU and IPRD as leaders in delivering clinically actionable genomic insights to patients and families. This position is central to IPRD\u2019s mission of bringing advanced genomic medicine to patients and families across Florida. Working closely with the CLIA Laboratory Director and other experts in genomics, the Variant Scientist will ensure the highest standards of accuracy and clinical relevance in genomic test interpretation. Contact Info Dr. Cynthia Vied: iprd@med.fsu.edu University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our interactive too l to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://hr.fsu.edu/facultyjobs. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This is an Open Rank Professor and Clinical (non-tenure earning) position. Rank is commensurate with experience. This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=62042&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Chair for Biomedical Sciences & Professor, 12 Month Salaried (Medicine Academic Affairs - College of Medicine)", "description": "Job Title Chair for Biomedical Sciences & Professor, 12 Month Salaried (Medicine Academic Affairs - College of Medicine) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 62042 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department College of Medicine, Medicine Biomedical Sciences Responsibilities Strategic Direction & Leadership: Provides strategic leadership for the department, articulating a vision for its future growth and impact in alignment with the medical school's mission and strategic plan. Fosters and supports a large interdisciplinary community of faculty researchers, educators, students and trainees. Faculty Development: Responsible for the recruitment, mentorship, administrative supervision, and evaluation of all employed, contracted, and volunteer faculty in the Department. Champions the department's faculty, including their professional development, and ensures excellence in research, teaching, and service. Plays a key role in recruitment and retention of outstanding faculty, students, and staff. Innovation and Research Development: Maintains an active, extramurally funded research program while also fostering an environment of innovative inquiry within the department by enhancing research infrastructure and grants oversight. Collaboration with Other University and College of Medicine Programs: Fosters interprofessional and cross-organizational collaboration and respect for all disciplines and roles among faculty and trainees and across the university to advance FSU Health. Curriculum Improvement: Provides direction in the design, development and management of the curriculum in the basic medical sciences. Oversees curricular enhancements through implementation of adult learning principles and integration of advanced technologies into curriculum delivery by the biomedical science faculty. Works with faculty across the school to ensure refinement of biomedical science content in a case-based curriculum model, including the representation of biomedical science education in clinical phases of the curriculum. Qualifications Doctoral Degree (PhD, MD/PhD, DO/PhD, or equivalent) in biomedical sciences or related discipline from an accredited institution with a demonstrated record of achievement as an accomplished scholar in teaching, academic research, and service. Academic achievements must meet the criteria for the rank of full Professor. Preferred Qualifications Clinical experience or experience in clinical collaborations are a plus. Established record of excellence in managing and advancing extramurally funded research programs (NIH, NSF, foundations, industry grants, etc.). A proven track record of successful leadership in medical education, including mentoring faculty, with significant experience in academic administration, program development, and implementation. Exceptional strategic leadership capabilities, coupled with outstanding communication, interpersonal, and collaborative skills, with a demonstrated ability to build relationships across a variety of stakeholders, including faculty, students, staff, and external partners. Extensive experience managing and enhancing medical and biomedical education programs at both the undergraduate and graduate levels, with a focus on innovative and evidence-based practices. Demonstrated experience developing, advancing, and implementing innovative biomedical science curricula and medical education programs. A demonstrated ability to work collaboratively with institutional leadership, faculty, and external organizations to drive academic excellence, strengthen educational outcomes, and promote the College\u2019s mission and vision. A record of nationally recognized achievement in research and clinical or educational pursuits commensurate with the rank of tenured full Professor. Other Information At FSU College of Medicine, we are committed to fostering the development of future healthcare leaders who are dedicated to responding to the evolving needs of the healthcare landscape. If you are a visionary leader passionate about transforming medical education and making a meaningful impact, we invite you to apply and contribute to shaping the future of healthcare. Together, we aim to advance groundbreaking research that addresses critical health challenges, drives innovation in biomedical science, and translates discoveries into real-world solutions\u2014improving lives across Florida and beyond. Helpful The Chair of Biomedical Sciences plays a pivotal role in the academic leadership for the discipline. The Chair should have a record of sustained accomplishments and evidence of leadership in a basic science discipline and medical education, and is expected to maintain a record of personal success in the discipline and participate in teaching, scholarly activity and research, and professional and community services. The Chair must serve as a role model for and represent both faculty and trainees. Contact Info Dawn Snyder Chief Financial Officer and Assistant Dean dawn.snyder@med.fsu.edu University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our interactive too l to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://hr.fsu.edu/facultyjobs. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is assigned to a tenure-track job code; however, the final appointment classification will be based on the selected candidate\u2019s qualifications and experience. Eligibility for a tenure-track appointment is not guaranteed and will be determined in alignment with FSU\u2019s policies, applicable guidelines, and the outcome of the formal review process. This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=61931&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Open Rank Professor, 9 Month Salaried (Earth, Ocean and Atmospheric Science)", "description": "Job Title Open Rank Professor, 9 Month Salaried (Earth, Ocean and Atmospheric Science) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 61931 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Earth, Ocean and Atmospheric Science | College of Arts & Sciences Responsibilities The Department of Earth, Ocean and Atmospheric Science (EOAS) at the Florida State University (FSU) invites applications for an open-rank tenure-track Professor position in Physical Oceanography. This is an endowed professorship to support an expert in the field of Physical Oceanography whose research and teaching are exemplary. The William K. Dewar Endowed Professorship will provide supplemental funding to support their research and teaching, as well as operational and programmatic expenses. Appointees are expected to develop and maintain a vigorous externally funded research program in their specialty area of interest and to teach courses and contribute to both the undergraduate and graduate degree programs in the department. Qualifications Candidates must hold a doctoral degree or the highest degree appropriate from an accredited institution in Geosciences or a related field. The ideal candidate should have a solid background in addressing fundamental research questions about the functioning of the ocean and have characteristics that encompass original thinking, unconventional ideas, brilliance, innovative, novel, interdisciplinary approaches, and deep theoretical insights. Applications from those skilled in observational analyses, measurements, modeling, theory, and/or interdisciplinary investigations will be particularly welcomed. Other Information EOAS is housed in a recent building (2020) with state-of-the-art facilities and laboratories, has approximately 40 academic faculty members and 135 graduate students, and offers undergraduate and/or graduate degrees in Geology, Meteorology, Oceanography, and Environmental Sciences. FSU also hosts a local High Performance Computing Center. Aside from the faculty within EOAS, the successful candidate can expect collaborations with the Center for Ocean-Atmosphere Prediction Studies, the Geophysical Fluid Dynamics Institute, the Coastal and Marine Lab, and the departments of Mathematics and Scientific Computing. Contact Info Inquiries may be addressed to: Dr. Eric Chassignet Search Committee Chair echassignet@fsu.edu Other search committee members are: Dr. Alyssa Atwood: aatwood@fsu.edu Dr. Mark Bourassa: mbourassa@fsu.edu Dr. Lisa Herbert: lherbert@fsu.edu Dr. Junhong Liang: junhong.liang@fsu.edu University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our interactive too l to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://hr.fsu.edu/facultyjobs. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=59569&PostingSeq=1": {"error": "RuntimeError: job description not shown (closed?)"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=61774&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Certified Medical Assistant, Full-Time, Multiple Positions (FSU Florida Medical Practice Plan - Medicine)", "description": "Job Title Certified Medical Assistant, Full-Time, Multiple Positions (FSU Florida Medical Practice Plan - Medicine) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 61774 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department FSU PrimaryHealth\u2122 , FMPP Operations - College of Medicine 2911 Roberts Avenue Tallahassee, FL 32310 FSU SeniorHealth\u2122 , FMPP Operations - College of Medicine 4449 Meandering Way Tallahassee, FL 32308 FSU Neuromodulation\u2122 , FMPP Operations - College of Medicine 2000 Levy Avenue, Suite 0337 Tallahassee, FL 32310 FSU Health Lipidolgy\u2122 , FMPP Operations - College of Medicine 2390 Phillips Road Tallahassee, FL 32308 FSU Health Precision Pediatrics at IPRD , FMPP Operations - College of Medicine 2390 Phillips Road Tallahassee, FL 32308 Responsibilities These positions work at multiple practices within the Florida Medical Practice Plan, including FSU PrimaryHealth\u2122, FSU SeniorHealth\u2122, FSU BehavioralHealth\u2122, FSU Neuromodulation\u2122, FSU Health Lipidolgy\u2122, and FSU Health Precision Pediatrics at IPRD. Primary location/practice will be determined and assigned based on practice needs and individual abilities/availability. Floats to other FMPP Clinics as needed. These positions provide assistance in all aspects of patient care in conjunction with administrative and clinical staff at Florida Medical Practice Plan clinics. Performs clinical and administrative duties in support of assigned area or clinic at a proficient level and independent of supervision. Makes recommendations to improve programs, products, processes or services. Under the direction of the Practice Manager, performs all aspects of intake for patients, including taking accurate histories, patient vital signs, vision and hearing screens, and other screenings or questionnaires as needed by the assigned clinician. Ensures all electronic health record (EHR) information is current and accurate. Prepares exam room and equipment to assist clinicians with exams and/or procedures. Provides concise and informative patient presentations to clinicians prior to exam. Responsible for carrying out clinical tasks in accordance with established standing orders and protocols to ensure consistent, high-quality patient care. Must meet competency guidelines in performing minor procedures such as point of care testing, venipunctures, blood pressure checks, splinting and applying wound dressings, as needed. Performs high-level disinfection of exam rooms and equipment. Assists clinicians during entire patient encounter, documents the visit as it occurs in real time. Accurately and thoroughly completes clinical notes of patient visits, orders, and procedures performed by the clinician for review and approval of the clinician. May perform as medical scribe for assigned clinician, as needed. Anticipates clinicians' needs to facilitate a smooth and efficient workflow. Performs duties in a discreet and tactful manner so as not to distract the physician from medical care at the direction of a provider. Performs other clerical duties and tasks to improve provider productivity and clinic workflow as assigned. Assists with coordination of patient care between visits. Triages patient phone calls and provides in-basket management support for clinicians. Notifies patients of test results and other follow-up tasks as directed by clinicians. Manages patient expectations and is able to resolve patient concerns independently. Assists with schedule coordination for diagnostic testing. Obtains prior authorizations as needed for diagnostic testing, medications and procedures as needed. Assists with traces and regulatory readiness for quality and patient care. Assists with front office administration duties such as screening incoming phone calls, answering routine questions and scheduling patient appointments as directed for FMPP clinics. Assists in monitoring the clinical schedule for no shows and rescheduling opportunities. Maintains communication with the clinic team including nursing staff and/or clinician regarding unscheduled patients and patients who appear to need care prior to the first available appointment. Assists with referral coordination by exhibiting an understanding of insurance guidelines, obtaining authorizations as required by insurance, using standard procedures within EHR and following up on referrals as requested by the clinician. Exhibits a willingness to float to all areas of need. Performs administrative and clinical duties as assigned. Completes billing transfers with laboratory companies/outside vendors. Position may be required to work one late evening per month. Attends one customer service training session from a list of courses identified by practice leadership. On a monthly basis, participates in an all-staff meeting. Promotes an atmosphere of teamwork in accomplishing the mission and goals of FMPP. Qualifications High school diploma or GED and two years of experience. (Note: post-high school education may substitute for experience at the equivalent rate.) Valid Certified Medical Assistant Certification (CMA, NCMA, RMA or CCMA). Current Basic Life Support (BLS) Healthcare Provider Certification issued by a certifying agency, or the ability to obtain prior to hire. Ability to work full-time and float to other FMPP clinics, as needed. Post-job offer/prior to hire requirements: Documentation of current PPD (Purified Protein Derivative) test as performed by a qualified physician reporting negative results within the past six months. Documentation of physical examination completed by a qualified healthcare provider/physician within the past six months. Within 30 days of hire requirements: Documentation of Tetanus immunization within 10 years. Documentation of Hepatitis B vaccine or positive antibody titer. Preferred Qualifications Experience with applicable computer software and programs, such as Microsoft Outlook, Word, Excel, and Electronic Health Records (EHR), or comparable programs. Experience demonstrating effective customer service skills. Experience communicating effectively verbally and in writing. Experience establishing and maintaining effective working relationships. Experience utilizing problem solving skills. Experience maintaining accurate records and retrieving files from active/archive sources. Knowledge of medical resources and terminology. Experience working with Pediatrics. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our interactive too l to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://jobs.fsu.edu. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select \u201cyes\u201d to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for eligibility information and required documentation , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This posting serves to recruit for multiple positions and is open until filled. Schedule: Full-time | Monday - Friday, 8am - 5pm Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=61868&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Open Rank Professor, Tenure-track or Tenured, 9 or 12 Month Salaried (multiple vacancies) - College of Nursing", "description": "Job Title Open Rank Professor, Tenure-track or Tenured, 9 or 12 Month Salaried (multiple vacancies) - College of Nursing Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 61868 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department College of Nursing Join a nationally recognized leader in nursing education, known for research distinction and educational innovation. With simulation space in a brand new $126 million FSU Health building, $12 million to design a new building, and a transformative $10 million gift, the FSU College of Nursing is hiring additional faculty for strategic growth. Responsibilities The FSU College of Nursing is seeking to hire 9 or 12 month Tenure-track or Tenured faculty members who are invested in conducting high impact research, teaching nursing students, and contributing the to the service needs of the College. Responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Developing and maintaining a cohesive program of research focused on health conditions, populations, and/or methodological skills. Actively pursuing extramural funding for research or programmatic efforts. Funding can be from federal, state, industry, and foundations. Actively engaging in scientific dissemination via conference presentations, peer-reviewed publications, and white papers. Preparing and teaching research aligned courses to nursing trainees. Providing service to the college, university, community, and the profession. Engaging in the provision of mentorship commensurate with academic rank. Participating in and meaningfully contributing to departmental and team meetings. Qualifications Candidates must hold an earned doctorate from an accredited university. Candidates will have a record of funding excellence and a record of achievement in teaching, scientific inquiry, and service. Demonstrate teaching excellence in undergraduate, MSN, or DNP programs. While candidates at the Assistant Professor level, must illustrate promise for an independent research career, candidates for Associate or full Professor appointments should have a strong record of funding, scholarly productivity, and leadership skills. For more information about our research portfolio, please visit: https://nursing.fsu.edu/research . Preferred Qualifications Experience in mentorship of colleagues and students at a level appropriate to rank. A record of funding from federal agencies. We are actively seeking faculty candidates with training and/or research experience in the following areas: Digital Health, Artificial Intelligence (AI), Innovation and Entrepreneurship,Chronic Disease Management, Pain Management, Community Health, Pediatrics and Child Health, and Mental Health. Contact Info Dr. Susan Baker, Associate Dean for Faculty Affairs, at sabaker@fsu.edu . University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our interactive too l to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://hr.fsu.edu/facultyjobs. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. In your application, please include the following documents: Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae (CV) Please do not include reference letters with your application; they will be collected later in the recruiting process. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Rank commensurate with experience. This position is being advertised for multiple positions and is open until filled. Some positions are eligible for remote work. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=61873&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar - Florida Center for Prevention Research (Full-time, OPS) (Multiple Vacancies)", "description": "Job Title Postdoctoral Scholar - Florida Center for Prevention Research (Full-time, OPS) (Multiple Vacancies) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 61873 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The Florida Center for Prevention Research (FCPR) Responsibilities Support data acquisition, cleaning, and management for large-scale opioid-related datasets (e.g., state administrative data, health care utilization data, survey data, geospatial data). Conduct quantitative and, as applicable, geospatial analyses for technical reports, peer-reviewed manuscripts, and presentations at professional conferences. Prepare, submit, and amend IRB protocol and data use agreements related to opioid and substance use research. Contribute to the writing of technical and evaluation reports for FL state partners (e.g., agency funders). Serve as lead and co-author on conference proposals and manuscripts using data from Applied Opioid Research and related projects. Assist in conceptualizing, drafting, and revising grant proposals to internal and external funding sources that advance FCPR\u2019s mission and research. Participate in team meetings with university and state stakeholders and contribute to translation of research findings for policy and practice audiences. Qualifications A Ph.D. in Public Health, Epidemiology, Social Work, Psychology, Education, Human Development & Family Science, or a related social or behavioral science field. ABD candidates who will complete all degree requirements prior to the start date are eligible to apply. Proof of degree conferral is required before employment begins. Demonstrated proficiency in quantitative research methods, including data management and analysis using statistical software (e.g., SPSS, Stata, R, SAS, MPlus, Python). Experience working with medium to large datasets (e.g., survey, administrative, or health data). Highly proficient with standard computer software and collaboration platforms, including Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, PowerPoint), Teams, and SharePoint (or similar tools). Excellent written and verbal communication skills, including experience contributing to manuscripts, reports, and conference presentations. Ability to work both independently and collaboratively in fast-paced, team-based research environment. Strong organizational skills and attention to details to manage multiple projects and deadlines. Availability to travel and participate in occasional overnight, out-of-town meetings and conferences. Preferred Qualifications Research experience focused on opioid misuse, Opioid Use Disorder (OUD), Medication for OUD, overdose prevention, or broader substance use epidemiology. Experience with prevention or intervention programs in family, school, or community contexts, especially those addressing substance use or associated risk/protective factors. Training and experience in advanced quantitative methods (e.g., longitudinal analysis, structural equation modeling, multilevel modeling, causal inference methods, geospatial modeling, or machine learning). Experience with data management and secondary analysis of large administrative, health services, or population-based datasets (e.g., Medicaid/claims data, EHR data, state surveillance systems, or multi-wave survey data). Experience preparing technical or evaluation reports for government or community partners. Other Information The Florida Center for Prevention Research (FCPR) at Florida State University seeks a dedicated postdoctoral scholar to join our team as a mentored researcher on the Applied Opioid Research project funded by the Florida Department of Children and Families. We seek candidates with an established or developing program of research focused on opioid research or closely related to substance use topics whose work and passions align with the FCPR mission. This position offers the opportunity to collaborate with an interdisciplinary team of researchers at FCPR, including affiliate faculty from the FSU College of Social Work, Department of Human Development & Family Science, and Geography, as well as state partners engaged in opioid research, data analysis, and prevention policy. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://jobs.fsu.edu. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an OPS/temporary job. Based on the duties, this position may require completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=61869&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Teaching Faculty - Undergraduate didactic-focused, 9 or 12 Month Salaried (multiple vacancies) - College of Nursing", "description": "Job Title Teaching Faculty - Undergraduate didactic-focused, 9 or 12 Month Salaried (multiple vacancies) - College of Nursing Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 61869 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department College of Nursing Join a nationally recognized leader in nursing education, known for research distinction and educational innovation. With simulation space in a brand new $126 million FSU Health building, $12 million to design a new building, and a transformative $10 million gift, the FSU College of Nursing is hiring additional faculty for strategic growth. The Florida State University College of Nursing invites applications for full-time, non-tenure-track Specialized Teaching Faculty \u2013 Didactic positions. These appointments may be offered on a 9-month or 12-month salaried basis, depending on program needs and candidate qualifications. Responsibilities The FSU College of Nursing is seeking to hire a collaborative educator to teach in our in-person, on-campus undergraduate didactic-focused program, based in Tallahassee, Florida (FL). Responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Provide didactic, lab and/or clinical nursing instruction in community health, pediatrics, or mental health. Promote student success through highly engaged teaching. Participate in planning, organizing, and developing curriculum. Supervise, evaluate, and mentor students. Appropriately document student progress. Participate in and meaningfully contribute to departmental and team meetings. Provide academic service and educational excellence through courteous, informed, accessible, and professional engagement. Other duties as assigned. These roles focus on high-quality didactic instruction in the undergraduate nursing program and support the college\u2019s mission to prepare practice-ready, compassionate nurse leaders. Faculty are expected to be actively engaged in teaching, student mentorship and academic service in a collaborative, on-campus environment. For more information about our academic programs, please visit the following link: Academics . Qualifications An academic doctorate (PhD, DNP) or highest-level terminal degree in nursing from an accredited institution is required. Active FL Registered Nurse (RN) or Advanced Practice Registered Nurse (APRN) license; or licensed in another state with eligibility to obtain FL licensure within 30 days of hire. Candidates must have relevant teaching experience in pediatrics, mental health, or community health. Preferred Qualifications Strong written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. Demonstrated ability to work well with students, faculty, and staff at all levels within a collaborative environment. Experience with Microsoft Word, Excel and Outlook or equivalent software. Experience supervising and training employees. Experience meeting project deadlines. Contact Info Dr. Susan Baker, Associate Dean for Faculty Affairs, at sabaker@fsu.edu . University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our interactive too l to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://hr.fsu.edu/facultyjobs. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Please include the following documents in your application: Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae (CV) including a listing of courses developed and taught Teaching Philosophy, not to exceed two pages Up to three official teaching evaluations from your most recent teaching experiences Please do not include reference letters with your application; they will be collected later in the recruiting process. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . These are full-time, in-person positions, and the level is commensurate with experience. Successful candidates must relocate to Tallahassee, Florida. Candidates must be willing to work a flexible schedule at multiple local sites. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=61578&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Open Rank Research Faculty, 12 Month Salaried (Florida State University Office of the Dean, FAMU-FSU College of Engineering Permanent, Non-Tenure Track Position)", "description": "Job Title Open Rank Research Faculty, 12 Month Salaried (Florida State University Office of the Dean, FAMU-FSU College of Engineering Permanent, Non-Tenure Track Position) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 61578 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Florida State University (FSU) invites applications for a Research Faculty position in AI for Surgical Simulation and Skill Assessment, within the FAMU-FSU College of Engineering. Responsibilities This position offers an exciting opportunity to join a growing interdisciplinary research program that integrates AI, computer vision, and virtual reality (VR) to create next-generation systems for surgical training and evaluation. The successful candidate will help design AI-driven, data-informed simulation platforms that objectively assess performance, accelerate skill acquisition, and enable adaptive, personalized learning. The position is ideally suited for a researcher passionate about combining machine learning, real-time simulation, and human performance modeling to create intelligent, interactive environments that enhance both technical precision and decision-making in surgery. The candidate will collaborate across departments and research centers, publish in leading journals, mentor students, and play an active role in securing competitive external funding to expand this rapidly advancing area. Responsibilities: Conduct research in AI-enabled surgical simulation and video-based skill assessment. Develop novel algorithms and techniques for real-time simulation, workflow analysis, and performance evaluation. Integrate deep learning and computer vision approaches into VR/AR surgical training systems. Collaborate with faculty members and researchers from medical schools to advance the field of surgical simulation and assessment. Design and execute human subjects studies, in partnership with clinicians and human factors experts, to evaluate system effectiveness and training outcomes. Prepare and submit competitive research proposals for external funding. Publish research findings in high-quality journals and present them at leading conferences. Mentor graduate students and postdoctoral researchers. Qualifications Doctoral degree in Computer Science, Mechanical Engineering, or a related discipline. Experience in C/C++ and Python programming, computer graphics, haptics, or physics-based real-time computing. Proficiency in machine learning and deep learning frameworks such as TensorFlow, PyTorch, or Scikit-learn. Experience in video-based assessment, computer vision, or VR/AR simulation development is strongly preferred. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively with other faculty members and researchers from various backgrounds. Strong publication record in relevant areas of research Demonstrated ability to secure external funding Preferred Qualifications Experience in mentoring graduate students and postdoctoral researchers is preferred Other Information The FAMU-FSU College of Engineering is a joint college of two nationally recognized universities, Florida A&M University and Florida State University, located in Tallahassee, Florida. The college offers undergraduate and graduate degree programs across six departments. The successful candidate will have the opportunity to collaborate with world-class researchers through the College\u2019s many interdisciplinary centers, including the High-Performance Materials Institute, Center for Advanced Power Systems, and the InSPIRE Institute. The position will be based in the Artificial Intelligence, Imaging, and Medical Simulation (AIMS) Laboratory, a state-of-the-art facility at FSU dedicated to advancing AI-driven surgical simulation, video-based skill assessment, and intelligent training technologies. Helpful This is a 12-month, permanent, non-tenure-track faculty appointment at Florida State University with a competitive salary and benefits package. The starting date for this position is negotiable. Contact Info Questions about the position should be directed to Dr. Suvranu De, Search Committee Chair, at sde@eng.famu.fsu.edu University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our interactive too l to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://hr.fsu.edu/facultyjobs. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=61128&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried - Askew School of Public Administration and Policy", "description": "Job Title Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried - Askew School of Public Administration and Policy Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 61128 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Askew School of Public Administration and Policy Responsibilities The person hired will teach two courses per semester for both Fall and Spring in an academic year. Courses to be taught are Homeland Security Policy and Practice, as well as a redeveloped course on disaster impacts on communities, both domestically and internationally. The new faculty member will be encouraged to develop or redevelop courses focused on policy and public administration related to national security, domestic security, and disaster response. Also, the successful candidate will be a core member of the school faculty engaged in research and collaboration, teaching in the MPA and PhD in Public Administration programs, and mentoring doctoral students. Qualifications A PhD in public administration, public policy, or another related field, by the time of appointment is required. An ideal candidate will have academic and operational experience in homeland security, emergency management, and/or intelligence. Other Information The Askew School of Public Administration and Policy is a core academic unit of the College of Social Sciences and Public Policy at Florida State University. Located in Florida's capital city, the Askew School has repeatedly been recognized as one of the best MPA programs in the U.S. and as one of the top ten faculties internationally as measured by the number of refereed articles published in the journals of our field. Our affiliated centers include: The Center for Disaster Risk Policy, which does extensive consulting, training, and support in emergency management for domestic and international organizations; and the Florida Center for Public Management, which offers the nation's largest Certified Public Manager program state-wide with full-time trainers. The Askew School has also established a Sustainability and Governance Lab to foster research collaboration among faculty, students, and community leaders working on sustainability. Contact Info Dr. Keon-Hyung Lee, Askew School of Public Administration and Policy School Director - klee2@fsu.edu University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our interactive too l to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://hr.fsu.edu/facultyjobs. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applicants should include a letter of interest, curriculum vitae, research statement, teaching statement, and a list of three references. Please include \u201cAssistant Professor Position\u201d as the subject of the email. Confidential Letters of Reference: This position requires that you have three confidential professional letters of recommendation submitted on your behalf. Follow the steps below to request these letters through our system: 1) After submitting your application, click the Explore Jobs link; 2) Click the My References link; 3) Click the Send/View Reference Request button next to the appropriate position; and 4) Follow the steps on that page to send your references a system generated email requesting they submit a letter of recommendation on your behalf. You may also return to the My References link and click on \"Send/View Reference Request\" to see if your references have responded, add additional references, or resend requests. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled and will begin in Fall 2026. Application materials will be reviewed starting November 1, 2025. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=61092&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Teaching Faculty, 9 or 12 Month Salaried (Open Rank) - Accounting (Panama City Campus)", "description": "Job Title Teaching Faculty, 9 or 12 Month Salaried (Open Rank) - Accounting (Panama City Campus) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 61092 Location Panama City, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department FSU Panama City houses an Association to Advanced Collegiate School of Business (AACSB)-Accredited undergraduate program in Accounting from the FSU College of Business ( Accounting | FSU Panama City ). Florida State University is one of the nation\u2019s top public universities and FSU Panama City amplifies the university\u2019s efforts to preserve, expand, and disseminate knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and human services professions. FSU Panama City is located 100 miles west of Tallahassee on the beautiful North St. Andrews Bay and is only three miles from the beaches of the emerald coast. FSU PC currently houses 20 bachelor's programs, 9 master's programs, and 1 doctoral program, and boasts a small faculty-to-student ratio, which gives students a more personalized academic experience. Please visit https://pc.fsu.edu/promise f or information about our FSU PC Promise to students and https://pc.fsu.edu/ for more information about our campus. FSU Panama City also recently opened a brand new, residential housing complex on campus and right on the water. This new apartment-style complex at FSU PC houses both undergraduate and graduate students. For more information about our on-campus housing, visit https://seminolelandin g fsu.com/ . Responsibilities This position has an emphasis on teaching core accounting courses, engagement of research to maintain AACSB Scholarly Academic qualifications, and service to the department. The FSU PC Accounting program maintains small class sizes, which allows for a well-rounded faculty experience across teaching, research, and service. Teaching accounting courses that serve the undergraduate Accounting and Business Administration programs at FSU Panama City. Engaging in research or other activities to be current in the field of Accounting in support of our AACSB-accredited Accounting program. Provide administrative service and leadership to the undergraduate Accounting program as the program coordinator. Provide mentorship, advising and support to students. Work with colleagues as a team for the business programs and for the campus. Qualifications PhD or DBA in Accounting (degree must be completed by the start date of the position) and a minimum of one-year teaching experience at the university level. Candidates who are ABD will be considered and candidates who have a Master\u2019s in Accounting with a business-related terminal degree will also be considered. Preferred Qualifications Doctoral degree from an AACSB-accredited institution. Demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, research, and service. Applied experience in Accounting. Industry certifications specific to Accounting. Ability to teaching a variety of courses across different areas in Accounting (e.g., taxation, financial accounting, accounting information systems, etc.). Other Information This program prepares students for careers in accounting, builds a strong foundation for professional certifications and licenses, and provides students with a well-rounded understanding of business through a rigorous and cutting-edge curriculum. For a list of courses in the FSU PC curriculum, please visit https://pc.fsu.edu/accounting/program. Contact Info Dr. Amy Polick, Associate Dean, - apolick@fsu.edu University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our interactive too l to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://hr.fsu.edu/facultyjobs. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applicants are encouraged but not required to submit the following materials with application for consideration: A cover letter describing university teaching experience, other related experiences (including professional and applied experiences), teaching philosophy, accounting courses the applicant feels qualified to teach, and why you are seeking this position. Current curriculum vitae A teaching statement describing how you support students through challenging and rigorous coursework while maintaining high pedagogical skill and course integrity. Evidence of teaching effectiveness (copies of teaching evaluations and other data). Also, in the FSU application system, applicants must provide names and email contact information for at least 3 references, who will receive notifications to submit a letter of reference on your behalf. Please ensure that those references respond to this inquiry and submit their letters through the FSU application system. Confidential Letters of Reference: Follow the steps below to request these letters through our system: 1) After submitting your application, click the Explore Jobs link; 2) Click the My References link; 3) Click the Send/View Reference Request button next to the appropriate position; and 4) Follow the steps on that page to send your references a system generated email requesting they submit a letter of recommendation on your behalf. You may also return to the My References link and click on \"Send/View Reference Request\" to see if your references have responded, add additional references, or resend requests. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is located on site in Panama City, FL. Review of applications will begin on October 20, 2025, and continue until the position is filled or closed. Applications received by the review date are assured full consideration. This position is open until filled will begin as early as Spring 2026 or Summer/Fall 2026 if circumstances warrant. Faculty rank will be determined based on experience. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=61027&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Tenure-Track Open Rank Professor, 9 Month Salaried (The Department of Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering- Florida A&M University -Florida State University College of Engineering- Multiple Positions)", "description": "Job Title Tenure-Track Open Rank Professor, 9 Month Salaried (The Department of Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering- Florida A&M University -Florida State University College of Engineering- Multiple Positions) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 61027 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The Department of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering at the Florida A&M University-Florida State University College of Engineering is pleased to invite applications from highly qualified individuals for tenure-track faculty positions in the field of dynamics and control in Tallahassee, Florida. Responsibilities The successful candidate is expected to establish and maintain a robust externally funded research program, have a strong commitment to teaching excellence in undergraduate and graduate courses, and participate in college and professional service. We are interested in candidates whose robotic research is grounded in mechanical engineering in fields including but not limited to aerial/aquatic/space robotics, dynamics/mechanisms, soft robotics, manipulation/surgical robotics, human-robot interface, sensing and perception, Artificial Intelligence/Machine Learning, and Optimal/feedback controls. Other areas of Dynamics and controls will also be considered, particularly if they complement existing program strengths. Qualifications Candidates must possess an earned Ph.D. in Mechanical or Aerospace Engineering or a closely related discipline, demonstrate the ability to create and sustain an internationally recognized research program in their field of expertise, and have a strong interest in engineering education. Contact Info Any questions about the position should be directed to Dr. Jonathan Clark, Search Committee Chair, at clarkj@eng.famu.fsu.edu. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our interactive too l to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://hr.fsu.edu/facultyjobs. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must the following documents: A cover letter A full curriculum vitae A 2-page research statement. This statement should clearly indicate how the proposed research efforts will connect to other efforts in the department and universities. A 1-page teaching statement No more than four selected publications for review The names and contact information of four potential references Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Application review will begin on October 1, 2025. Acceptance and review of applications will continue until the position is filled. The appointment is anticipated to begin in August 2026 Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=60978&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Medical Technologist (Institute for Pediatric Rare Diseases - Medicine)", "description": "Job Title Medical Technologist (Institute for Pediatric Rare Diseases - Medicine) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 60978 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department College of Medicine, Institute for Pediatric Rare Diseases Responsibilities This position plays a key developmental and leadership role in the processing, analysis, and quality control of clinical genomic tests that support IPRD's mission to improve diagnosis and treatment for children with rare diseases across Florida. The incumbent will define the goals of the Sunshine Genetics Newborn Screening program and develop new protocols for the whole genome sequencing diagnostic test. The incumbent will also serve as the point of contact and compliance coordinator for the Newborn Screening Program. The successful candidate will work under the supervision of the Laboratory Director and Technical Supervisor and will contribute to daily lab operations, including nucleic acid extraction, library preparation, sequencing, and data tracking as part of high-complexity clinical testing in a CLIA-certified laboratory with a focus on next-generation sequencing (NGS), and molecular diagnostics. Develops and implements testing techniques for the Newborn Screening Program. Performs pre-analytical, analytical, and post-analytical procedures for next generation sequencing including PCR testing and validation. Prepares, labels, and processes biological specimens with accuracy and attention to detail. Accurately documents and interprets results. Follows all standard operating procedures and safety protocols. Participates in quality control and quality assurance activities to ensure result reliability. Monitors reagent and supply inventory; performs routine maintenance and calibration of equipment. Troubleshoots instruments and assay problems and documents the issue and resolution. Stays updated with the latest advancements in genomic technologies and methodologies to enhance laboratory practices. Identifies and reports instrument malfunctions or test discrepancies to the supervisor promptly. Assists in validation and verification studies for new assays or equipment. Stays informed on advancements in molecular diagnostics and participates in ongoing training. Serves as point of contact and compliance coordinator for the Newborn Screening Program with the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA), the Centers for Medicare and Medicaid Services (CMS), and the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC), who oversee the federal standards outlined in the Clinical Laboratory Improvement Amendments (CLIA). Works closely with other laboratory staff, clinicians, and researchers to interpret and communicate genomic data. Ensures all laboratory activities comply with regulatory standards and guidelines, including CUA, CAP, and HIPAA. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and three years of experience; or a high school diploma/equivalent and experience equal to seven years. (Note: post-high school education can substitute for experience at the equivalent rate.) License Requirement: Valid Florida Medical Technologist or Technician license, or the ability to obtain within 60 days of hire. Contact Info Cynthia Vied, Ph.D. cynthia.vied@med.fsu.edu University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our interactive too l to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://jobs.fsu.edu. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=60442&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Senior Licensing Manager", "description": "Job Title Senior Licensing Manager Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 60442 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The Office of Commercialization within the Office of Research seeks to fill the Senior Licensing Manager position. Responsibilities This position is responsible for managing the identification, evaluation protection and commercialization of intellectual property rights. Works with FSU faculty and staff to evaluate research developments to identify potential commercial opportunities, obtain invention disclosures, advise on best practices in order to maximum revenue potential for IP license, and initiates strategies for success. Works with outside firms to design protection for identified intellectual property. Independently negotiates and drafts legal license agreements developing terms, structure, and agreement language with established companies and/or identifies potential startup company opportunities. With regards to startup companies, works to identify potential entrepreneurs and help direct them to resources available for establishing a company capable of successfully licensing University IP; fosters relationships between licensee and faculty/staff inventors to aid in commercialization of licensed IP, including the facilitation and encouragement of sponsored research in the inventors' laboratories. The position also manages a portfolio of license agreements and ensures contract terms are met in a timely manner by licensee. Serves as university representative responsible for dissemination of information through various forms of presentations to internal and external groups affiliated with or interested in FSU research and IP; represents department at designated local, regional, and national intellectual property programs, conferences, business meetings and related events; develops office marketing plan and oversees social media strategy, trends, reporting and success rate campaigns. Responsible for day-to-day training, guidance and mentorship to junior staff members and department intern(s). Assists with special projects as designated by the director on an as needed basis. Provides hands-on support to Office of Commercialization programs and events to include, but not limited to: university internal distribution of grants; events displaying University technologies/intellectual property; faculty and staff recognition events; and any other program, projects or events that Office of Commercialization is involved in or supports. Qualifications Master's degree in appropriate area of specialization and two years of experience; or a Bachelor's degree in an appropriate area of specialization and four years of relevant experience. (Note: Higher education may be accepted at the equivalent rate.) Preferred Qualifications Ability to demonstrate critical thinking based upon in-depth data, substantiating information, considering and respecting others' input, personal values, and ethics. Ability to effectively train and direct the work of others. Ability to represent the University in appointed area as required. Knowledge of and ability to interpret and apply related federal, state, and local laws, ordinances, rules and regulations. Ability to develop and implement policies, procedures, goals, and objectives. Ability to develop and implement a successful marketing plan/strategy. Contact Info Cassidy Cooksey at ccooksey@fsu.edu University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our interactive too l to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://jobs.fsu.edu. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position requires annual Financial Disclosure based on Florida Statutes 112.3144 and 112.3145. This position is opened until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63728&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Athletic Fields Specialist II", "description": "Athletic Fields Specialist II Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63728 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Florida State University Grounds Department Responsibilities Responsible for performing highly skilled work related to the inspection, preventative maintenance, system modification, installation and repair of irrigation systems, drainage systems, soil profiles, natural grass turf systems and synthetic turf systems within the Mike Long Track and Field Facility, and the Beach Volleyball Facility. Performs highly skilled work in the implementation of the maintenance of turfgrass, synthetic surfaces, clay and dirt management including moisture control, disease and pest identification, irrigation system repair and scheduling, and knowledge of current NCAA regulations pertaining to field layout and management. Manages all daily maintenance and grounds operations of the Mike Long Track and Field facility, as well as the Beach Volleyball facility to ensure safe, championship caliber playing and competition surfaces. Coordinates facility setup and breakdown for these facilities for NCAA competitions, practices, camps, recruiting events, and other events hosted. Performs string trimming, edging, blowing, removal of leaves, debris, and litter at Athletics Department owned fields as needed. Performs aeration, overseeding, vertical mowing, sweeping, grooming, and topdressing of fields. Assists in field renovations across all Athletic Department owned fields to include, grading, sodding, and irrigation repairs, grooming synthetic turf, proper setup for games, practices, and outside events. Qualifications A bachelor's degree in a turfgrass field and one year of related work experience or an associate's degree in a turf grass background and three years of related experience. A valid Florida or Georgia driver's license or the ability to obtain one upon hire University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select \u201cyes\u201d to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for Veterans\u2019 Preference eligibility requirements and Veterans\u2019 Preference required documentation (PDF) , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63547&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Groundskeeper", "description": "Groundskeeper Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63547 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Florida State University Grounds Department Responsibilities Responsible for groundskeeping maintenance tasks within zones on Florida State University properties as assigned to consistently maintain a safe, clean, sustainable, and attractively landscaped environment for the students, faculty, and staff of our institution. Performs groundskeeping tasks such as mowing, edging, raking, mulching, power blowing, weed eating, pulling weeds, light pruning, and watering plants. Responsible for debris removal, leaf removal, trash pickup and other tasks to keep grounds clean and presentable. Maintains areas by spreading landscape materials such as pine straw, bark, or rocks. Assists with landscaping tasks such as planting shrubs and trees. Assists in maintaining turf areas by utilizing push mowers to ensure an attractively landscaped environment on campus. Prepares landscaped areas with soil excavation, turf removal and resodding. Safely operates and maintains grounds equipment to ensure the health and appearance of university grounds. Ensures that all manual and power equipment is in proper working condition and reports maintenance problems to the supervisor. Performs other tasks as assigned by supervisor or higher authority. Others tasks as assigned by supervisor. Qualifications Minimum of a 9th Grade Education Valid Florida or Georgia driver's license Class E or the ability to obtain one upon hire. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select \u201cyes\u201d to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for Veterans\u2019 Preference eligibility requirements and Veterans\u2019 Preference required documentation (PDF) , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being re-advertised. Previous applicants need not apply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63714&PostingSeq=1": {"error": "RuntimeError: job description not shown (closed?)"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63422&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Senior Administrative Specialist \u2013 Applied Superconductivity Center (NHMFL)", "description": "Senior Administrative Specialist \u2013 Applied Superconductivity Center (NHMFL) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63422 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department National High Magnetic Field Laboratory Join the world-renowned National High Magnetic Field Laboratory at Florida State University (FSU) and support groundbreaking scientific discovery in a collaborative, high-tech environment. FSU was recently recognized as one of America\u2019s Best-in-State Employers for its strong workplace culture and employee-centered values. Responsibilities Manage assigned administrative functions for the Applied Superconductivity Center (ASC), with primary responsibility for supporting the department\u2019s grant management activities. Key Responsibilities: Manage administrative requirements of contracts and grants to include the development and submission of grant proposals, setting up of grant awards, periodic and final reports, interpretation of grant regulations and procedures, development and implementation of administrative procedures for managing and utilizing grant resources, and monitoring project progress and completion. Interface with MagLab, Colleges, and Sponsored Research, coordinate grant activities among institutions, subcontractors, and other stakeholders. Coordinate the assigned administrative functions of the Applied Superconductivity Center and effectively interface with its director and deputy director. Work collaboratively within MagLab, FSU and with external stakeholders to solve any issues in a timely manner. This may require navigation through complex interactions for the benefit of the research and educational goals of ASC. Provide backup coordination for the ASC building manager and lab managers, e.g. safety, preparedness, communications etc. Assist the ASC director or the designee of the director in other functions as appropriate, including but not limited to planning and the execution of departmental events, coordination of local workshops, facilitation of seminars, or activities at conferences. Provide backup support for personnel activities to include supervision of recruitment/hiring, help with onboarding, supervision of appointments and reappointments, supervision of visas and compliance, and overall liaison of other personnel related activities across colleges, departments, and MagLab. Coordinate activities that help support the positive work environment at ASC. Provide backup support for the daily fiscal functions including budget reconciliations, procurement administration, and travel administration. Perform work with high accuracy and low error rates. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and four years of experience; or a high school diploma or equivalent and eight years of experience. (Note: a combination of post high school education and experience equal to eight years.) Helpful What You Gain at FSU Opportunity to work at a world-renowned national research laboratory. Meaningful contributions to scientific discovery and student learning. A collaborative environment that values your expertise and invests in your growth. Contact Info For additional information, please contact Chris Segal . University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position is being readvertised. Previous applicants need not reapply. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63729&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Academic Program Specialist", "description": "Academic Program Specialist Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63729 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department College of Social Work Responsibilities Provides comprehensive academic advising, student support, recruitment, and program administration services for the College of Social Work's Master of Social Work (MSW) campus programs. Supports prospective and current students through advising, enrollment management, outreach initiatives, policy interpretation, and coordination of academic program operations to promote student success and program effectiveness. The MSW team is looking for a driven applicant that can join the College of Social Work providing exceptional customer service when providing advising to prospective and current MSW students! The team is excited to welcome a self-starter who is interested in bringing innovation to the role. This position advises campus students, so in-person work is required. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and two years of experience or a high school diploma or equivalent and six years of experience. (Note: or a combination of post high school education or experience equal to six years.) Preferred Qualifications Master\u2019s degree in higher education, counseling, communications, social work or like-minded fields. Contact Info For more information please contact: Fran Gomory, fgomory@fsu.edu University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Anticipated salary to range between low $40,000's to $50,000, commensurate with education and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Resume required and cover letter preferred to help understand applicant's interest in the role and how it fits into their ultimate career goals. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63675&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried (Finance - Herbert Wertheim College of Business) (Multiple Openings)", "description": "Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried (Finance - Herbert Wertheim College of Business) (Multiple Openings) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63675 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Finance Herbert Wertheim College of Business The Department of Finance provides an active research environment including the Truist seminar series and the Truist Beach Conference. Faculty have access to summer research grants, graduate student research assistants, travel support and an excellent collection of databases. Responsibilities Florida State University's Herbert Wertheim College of Business seeks applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Finance. The incumbent is expected to teach at the undergraduate and/or graduate levels and develop a research agenda that targets top-tier journals. Candidates with expertise in Wealth Management are invited to apply. The position is scheduled to start in Fall 2027 Qualifications Candidates for this position must have earned or be near completion of a Ph.D. in Finance or Financial Economics. Degree must be conferred by August 1, 2027. Contact Info Please contact Irena Hutton if you have any questions. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Florida State University is a Carnegie-classified R1 research university located in Tallahassee, Florida, the state capital, with enrollment exceeding 46,000 students. In the 2027 U.S. News & World Report Best Colleges rankings, Florida State ranks No. 59 among national universities and No. 24 among public universities in the United States. The Herbert Wertheim College of Business enrolls approximately 8,500 students seeking business degrees across undergraduate, master\u2019s, and doctoral programs. The Department of Finance offers programs and courses at the undergraduate, master\u2019s, and Ph.D. levels. Graduate offerings include the Master of Science in Finance (MSF), the Ph.D. in Business Administration with a major in Finance, and MBA programs offered in full-time, evening, and online formats. Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Candidates graduating in 2026/2027 are also required to submit transcripts. Review of applications will begin immediately. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled or March 1, 2027. Please send recommendation letters to Irena Hutton . Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63693&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Classroom Support Specialist - Information Technology Services", "description": "Classroom Support Specialist - Information Technology Services Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63693 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Information Technology Services Responsibilities Responsible for providing technical customer support for internal desktop systems, software, hardware, and network infrastructure. Installs, configures, and troubleshoots desktop systems, workstations, printers, servers, and network issues. Serves as a principal point of contact to answer inquiries and initiate resolution of problems. Communication may be on-site, electronic, or by phone. May respond to requests from the help desk to support end-users on various desktop systems issues and assess assigned priority levels. This position is part of ITS Classroom Support, which is the first line of support for instructors in over 250 classrooms around FSU. It is a very active, fast-paced environment, and the employee must learn about numerous new technologies. Qualifications A high school diploma or equivalent and two years of experience. (Note: post high-school education and/or experience may substitute at a comparable rate.) A valid State of Florida or Georgia Driver\u2019s License or the ability to obtain prior to hire. Preferred Qualifications Thoroughly familiar with Windows 10 and/or 11 Customer support experience University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select \u201cyes\u201d to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for Veterans\u2019 Preference eligibility requirements and Veterans\u2019 Preference required documentation (PDF) , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . The schedule for this position is variable, but the usual hours are from 12:30PM to 9:30PM. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63640&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Director of Stamps Program, ONF, PSP - Instructional Specialist I, 12 Month Salaried", "description": "Director of Stamps Program, ONF, PSP - Instructional Specialist I, 12 Month Salaried Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63640 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Office of National Fellowships Presidential Scholars Program Stamps Scholars Program Undergraduate Studies Responsibilities We are seeking an experienced and innovative higher education program administrator to help us launch our partnership with the Stamps Scholars program, as well as work collaboratively with our premier, merit scholarship program, the Presidential Scholars, and with our Office of National Fellowships. Strategic Program Leadership Provides strategic leadership and administrative oversight for a portfolio of high-impact scholar and fellowship programs to include the Stamps Scholars Program, Office of National Fellowships, and Presidential Scholars Program. Serves as primary lead for the Stamps Scholars Program. Oversees program planning, operations, assessment, reporting, budget management, and implementation of initiatives that support student success and advance institutional goals. Develops and maintains strong relationships with university leadership, donors, faculty, and external partners to enhance program effectiveness and expand opportunities for students. Teaching and Student Development Teaches Presidential Scholars seminars and facilitates educational experiences that promote academic excellence, interdisciplinary learning, leadership growth, and student engagement. Responsible for curricular development including objectives, revisions, and teaching assignments. Responsible for updating Simple Syllabus and Coursedog. Guides students in exploring scholarship and fellowship opportunities, research experiences, graduate and professional school preparation, career planning, and other developmental pathways. Student Recruitment, Success, and Enrichment Leads efforts to recruit, retain, and support highly motivated students through innovative academic, leadership, service, and co-curricular programming. Designs and implements transformative student experiences that foster intellectual engagement, leadership development, research and creative activity, civic responsibility, and post-graduate success. Provides advising and mentorship to students as they pursue academic, professional, and personal development opportunities. Team Leadership and Fellowship Advancement Provides leadership and supervision for professional and student staff supporting the Presidential Scholars Program and Office of National Fellowships. Oversees fellowship advising, application support, campus nomination processes, outreach initiatives, and applicant development efforts that increase participation and success in nationally competitive scholarships and fellowships. Leads operational planning, staff development, and continuous improvement efforts while fostering collaborative partnerships across the university and beyond. Assessment and Continuous Improvement Evaluates program effectiveness using measures of student engagement, retention, academic achievement, leadership development, post-graduate outcomes, and fellowship success. Uses data to inform continuous improvement and prepares reports and recommendations for the Associate Dean and university stakeholders. Qualifications Master's degree and three years of experience in higher education program management. Preferred Qualifications Demonstration of strong interpersonal skills and the ability to effectively work with a wide range of individuals and constituencies in a community, and the ability to foster a cooperative work environment. Experience managing and overseeing an operating budget. Ability to provide subject matter expertise and counsel others. Ability to develop and implement policies, procedures, goals, and objectives. Ability to evaluate process effectiveness and develop change or alternatives. Ability to train and supervise employees. Contact Info Dr. Craig Filar University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range $75,000 - $80,000, commensurate with education & experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Note: A cover letter outlining your interest and relevant experience is also required as part of your submission. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . First round of applications will be reviewed in November 2026. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63710&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Grants Specialist - UBA/College of Social Work", "description": "Grants Specialist - UBA/College of Social Work Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63710 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department University Business Administrators - College of Social Work Responsibilities This position is responsible for the coordination, organization and tracking of public and private funded research within the College of Social Work. Position serves as a liaison between the College, funding agencies, the Research Foundation, Sponsored Research, and other relevant organizations. Coordinates, organizes, tracks, and monitors contract & grant post-award funding activities. Advises and assists assigned faculty, centers and institutes, and staff in regard to these post-award activities. Activities include but are not limited to identification and resolution of compliance and funding issues; proper spend based on grant specifications, budget amendments, re-budgets, preparation of financial reports preparation of financial reports; tracking of salary commitments; coordinating project close-outs; Contracts & Grants (C&G) document organization and storage; and C&G related procurement and travel functions. Position is responsible for scheduling regular meetings with Principal Investigators (PI) to discuss their funded projects and other C&G related commitments. Assist with FACET related questions for C&G. Advises and assists assigned faculty, centers and institutes, and staff in pre-award activities. Activities include but are not limited to review of terms for compliance concerns; budget, transmittal, and cost share preparation; uploading proposal documents; proposal document tracking organization and storage; and serving as a liaison between the College, funding agencies, Research Foundation, Sponsored Research, and other relevant organizations. Serves as staff on the CSW Research Committee. Prepares monthly reconciliation documents for distribution to assigned PIs. Communicates awards, outside collaboration and other C&G activity as appropriate to key personnel. Advises the Deans/Directors/PIs on recommendations concerning the development, revision and/or interpretation of policies relating to research activities. Regularly attends C&G training to enhance understanding of relevant issues and procedures. Provides analysis of and recommendations regarding internal/external regulations, rules, policies, procedures, and guidelines. Assists with special projects and duties as assigned by direct supervisor or dean. Qualifications A Bachelor's degree and one year of experience; or a high school diploma or equivalent and five years of experience. (Note: a combination of post high school education and experience equal to five years.) Preferred Qualifications The ideal candidate will demonstrate strong attention to detail, critical thinking, and the ability to effectively manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment. Excellent written and verbal communication skills, a commitment to outstanding customer service, and the ability to interact professionally is essential. Preference will be given to candidates with pre-award and post-award grant administration experience. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63721&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Heavy Equipment Operator 3", "description": "Heavy Equipment Operator 3 Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63721 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department FSU Maintenance Construction Labor Department Responsibilities Operates commercial vehicles such as a backhoe, boom truck, dump truck, trencher, and front-end loader. Assists in concrete finishing, form setting, fence construction, air hammer operation, street repairs, and parking lot maintenance. Maintains records and time keeping and performs related duties as assigned. Qualifications High school diploma or equivalency and ten years of external professional experience or a post high school education and experience equal to 10 years. A valid State of Florida or Georgia CDL Class B driver\u2019s license or ability to obtain upon hire University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State Unive