ersity Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select \u201cyes\u201d to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for Veterans\u2019 Preference eligibility requirements and Veterans\u2019 Preference required documentation (PDF) , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63730&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Program Manager, Academic & Student Services", "description": "Program Manager, Academic & Student Services Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63730 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department University Housing Responsibilities STUDENT GROUP ADVISING: Serve as the advisor for student leadership groups, including the Inter-Residence Hall Council (IRHC) and National Residence Hall Honorary (NRHH) chapter; plan and implement training for executive board members and hall councils; coordinate travel arrangements and serve as the delegation advisor for student group conferences; provide oversight of fiscal management of various funds related to IRHC and NRHH; work closely with Student Government Association (SGA) to ensure compliance with policies, procedures, and advisor training. STUDENT PROGRAMMING: work with staff and students to develop and implement large scale programs in accordance with Residential Curriculum; assess annual and on-going NRHH and IRHC programs and officer training. LEADERSHIP DEVELOPMENT: Develop and conduct ongoing training and professional development for hall council advisors; coordinate and develop strategies to connect student engagement with student learning; coordinate COMPASS Leadership retreat; complete other duties as assigned in support of University Housing. CAMPUS REPRESENTATION: work with campus partners to share resources for students and staff related to leadership development; participate and represent leadership programs in campus wide traditions such as Family Weekend, Homecoming, and philanthropy. SUPERVISION: Provide daily leadership, supervision, professional development, and evaluation for a graduate assistant working in Residence Life with a focus on student leadership and programming. Qualifications Master's degree in higher education administration, student personnel, counseling or related field and one year of experience. Full-time or graduate housing/residence life experience in college/university setting required. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is open until filled Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63686&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Senior Accounting Specialist - UBA/Center for Academic Professional Development", "description": "Senior Accounting Specialist - UBA/Center for Academic Professional Development Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63686 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department University Business Administrators - Center for Academic Professional Development (CAPD) Responsibilities This position manages the Center for Academic Professional Development (CAPD) accounts receivable, cash handling operations, auxiliary billing, and the FSU marketplace systems. Provides day-to-day guidance and coordination of accounts receivable and cash handling operations for the Center for Academic Professional Development (CAPD). Ensures compliance with University policy related to accounts receivables and cash handling. Interprets, develops, recommends and implements departmental policies and procedures to ensure compliance with University policy and ensures that the Center has the appropriate internal controls in place, including the proper assignment of duties. Trains cashiering staff on cashiering policies and is responsible for the daily revenue receipt matching. Serves as the direct contact for all outside customer service financial issues and questions. Manages responsibilities matching inhouse and FSU accounting and operational software systems. Oversees highly specialized invoicing processing through the department\u2019s Registration system and FSU Auxiliary Billing in OMNI. Develops procedures for auxiliary billing and manages the interfaces and functionalities within these systems. Serves on all teams that map interfaces for all business operations between local and cloud environments. Responds to functionality issues and provides solutions and follow-up. Develops and maintains partnerships throughout the University in order to attain CAPD departmental goals and objectives. Conducts detailed financial analyses by auditing, verifying, and performing complex financial reconciliations of departmental receivables operations and follow-ups on delinquent items. Prepares financial statements and reports identifying problem accounts and works to ensure the collection of funds through written and oral communication. Collaborates with the Budget Manager on the implementation of accounting procedures, reconciliation procedures, and reports that support the business functions of CAPD. Manages the business revenue activities of CAPD by monitoring and verifying the accuracy of charges on invoices printed from the internal accounting system. Verifies all transactions are uploaded or downloaded correctly and problem solves if they do not match daily. Processes refunds and payment transfers. Investigates and responds to credit card disputes for participants. Confirms all registration charges between university accounts receivable and internal CAPD business systems. Reviews and approves all staff cashiering transactions in OMNI and the CAPD Registration System. Creates integrated financial/statistical reports and financial statements to monitor and track daily activities for CAPD administration. Serves as one of two Purchasing-Card holders and sole Travel Card holder for CAPD and is responsible for ensuring purchase and travel requests meet university policies and that appropriate accounting information is utilized prior to card approvals. Maintains records, requests, and receipts for payment and provides monthly reporting. Serves as backup for Procurement purchase orders and travel expense reports as needed and ensures activities follow university, state, and federal policies and procedures. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and four years of accounting related experience or a combination of post high school education and accounting related experience equal to eight years. Preferred Qualifications The preferred candidate should have purchasing experience and knowledge of myFSU/FSU systems. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . The anticipated start date for this position will be January 2027. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63709&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Senior Enrollment Management Specialist, Graduation", "description": "Senior Enrollment Management Specialist, Graduation Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63709 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Office of the University Registrar Responsibilities The Office of the University Registrar is a unit within the Division of Enrollment Management, which is comprised of four distinct units: Office of Admissions, Office of the University Registrar, Office of Financial Aid, and Technology Operations. Enrollment Management\u2019s integrated services provide distinctive support throughout the student's development and progression in their academic experience \u2013 from recruitment through commencement. Through collaboration, communication, and commitment, all units within Enrollment Management achieve the highest level of student-centered service to current and prospective students and families and to campus partners across the University. Responsible for operations of the graduation section in the Office of the University Registrar. Makes decisions regarding graduation eligibility; participates in counseling and guidance activities involved with the implementation of procedures regarding University graduation requirements. Assists with the planning and execution of logistical functions related to University commencement ceremonies. Reviews student transcripts and degree audits to make determinations regarding compliance with graduation requirements and eligibility based upon an effective working knowledge of degree requirements for the awarding of degrees. Implements University rules and regulations regarding graduation decisions. Searches for duplicate credit hours within the reports to uncover errors, discrepancies, and perform GPA calculations. Uses professional judgment to determine degree-applicable hours on a case-by-case basis depending on student's major, specific courses completed, and other considerations. Collaborates with Assistant Registrar for Graduation to assist with commencement event logistics. Serves as the first point of contact for commencement inquiries and serves as a resource to internal and external stakeholders. Works as part of the graduation team to assist in the management, planning and execution of commencement events. Assists with managing on-site event production, set-up, and clean-up. Assists with recruiting, training, and supervising graduation ambassadors. Responsible for maintaining, updating, developing, and evaluating commencement procedures. Makes suggestions and recommendations to senior leadership for efficient operation. Represents the University during commencement ceremonies, organizing student flow and ensuring compliance with commencement policies and procedures. Assists with organizing, planning and executing all graduation ceremony logistics, including but not limited to coordinating schedules, seating arrangements, ceremony layout design, etc. Acts as a liaison between graduates and third-party vendors to provide ceremony-related support. Responsible for posting Associate of Arts degrees and other completed certificates to student records. Coordinates with third-part vendor for weekly diploma reorders as well as bulk orders at the end of each semester. Assists in the review and evaluation of policies and procedures, making suggestions and recommendations for the efficient operation of the section and the promotion of increased retention and graduation rates to senior leadership. Qualifications A Bachelor's degree and one year of experience; or a high school diploma or equivalent and five years of experience. (Note: a combination of post high school education and experience equal to five years.) Preferred Qualifications A Bachelor's degree in an appropriate area of specialization and one year of experience related to the responsibilities of the job are preferred. We seek enthusiastic candidates who are detail-oriented, and who work well independently as well as in a team. Candidates should have the ability to review, analyze, formulate, and organize data and information and follow through on assignments. Applicants should be able to establish and maintain effective working relationships and should possess a strong sense of initiative while managing multiple responsibilities concurrently. Candidates should be able to communicate effectively both verbally and in writing. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Candidates must attach a resume to be considered for the position. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63659&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Teaching Faculty I, 9 Month Salaried (Finance - Herbert Wertheim College of Business)", "description": "Teaching Faculty I, 9 Month Salaried (Finance - Herbert Wertheim College of Business) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63659 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Finance Herbert Wertheim College of Business Responsibilities Florida State University\u2019s Herbert Wertheim College of Business seeks applications for a non-tenure track full-time teaching faculty position in Finance. The expected teaching load is four courses per semester. Specific course assignments are dependent upon the department\u2019s needs. In addition to teaching, the candidate is expected to participate in the department, college and university service activities. The department presently has a need for industry outreach. The position is scheduled to start in Fall 2027. Qualifications Candidates for this position must have earned or be near completion of a Ph.D. in Finance or related discipline. Degree must be conferred prior to the position start date. Preferred Qualifications Candidates should demonstrate the ability to independently develop and manage courses and have a record of excellent teaching at the AACSB accredited institution. Preference will be given to the applicants with industry experience. Excellent written and communication skills in English are required. Contact Info Please contact The Recruitment Team if you have any questions. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Florida State University is a Carnegie-classified R1 research university located in Tallahassee, Florida, the state capital, with enrollment exceeding 46,000 students. In the 2027 U.S. News & World Report Best Colleges rankings, Florida State ranks No. 59 among national universities and No. 24 among public universities in the United States. The Herbert Wertheim College of Business enrolls approximately 8,500 students seeking business degrees across undergraduate, master\u2019s, and doctoral programs. The Department of Finance offers programs and courses at the undergraduate, master\u2019s, and Ph.D. levels. Graduate offerings include the Master of Science in Finance (MSF), the Ph.D. in Business Administration with a major in Finance, and MBA programs offered in full-time, evening, and online formats. Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Candidates graduating in 2026/2027 are also required to submit transcripts. Recommendation letters can be submitted with the application or emailed to The Recruitment Team . Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Review of applications will begin immediately. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled or March 1, 2027. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63543&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Business Manager - UBA / Human Resources", "description": "Business Manager - UBA / Human Resources Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63543 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department University Business Administrators - Human Resources Responsibilities This position is responsible for the management of financial and administrative operations at the Office of Human Resources and the Employee Assistance Program. Responsible for the administration of financial budgets, fiscal functions, procurement, financial reporting, travel, and human resources functions. Serves as the Budget Manager for the Office of Human Resources (HR) and Employee Assistance Program (EAP). Approves and monitors financial transactions in compliance with University policies and procedures. Responsible for the financial management, reporting, and reconciliation of general ledgers. Directs and implements the annual budget process. Assists with the development and implementation of internal control policies and procedures to ensure sound fiscal management and compliance of financial services. Resolves financial discrepancies and serves as the point of contact for resolution of any disbursement issues. Responsible for the AR billing of the Background Check auxiliary program. Maintains all accounts receivable records and reports. Responsible for the payment and audit of vendor invoices. Serves as liaison for HR with Auxiliary Services and all internal auxiliary customers. Manages, updates, and documents processes and procedures to accomplish job duties and tasks. Responsible for budget and revenue forecasting as well as financial statements for auxiliary accounts. Responsible for the tracking and maintenance of staff rate and for preparing and updating rate allocation reports and projections. Monitors biweekly actives reports and payroll cost center reports and initiates necessary action for resolution of any errors. Serves as the HR Department Manager approving job postings, job offers and ePAFs. Provides supervision, training, and coordination of departmental staff performing fiscal and administrative functions related to procurement, travel, property management, and human resources. Proxies p-card transactions and performs the monthly p-card reconciliation's for assigned cardholders. Ensures transactions are timely and accurate with the appropriate accounting information, description and follow State and University policies and procedures. Develops and maintains partnerships throughout the university to attain office and department goals and objectives. Coordinates and/or serves on committees for planning and implementing activities and events. Assist with special assignments, as needed, including HR Department Representative Meetings. Qualifications A Bachelor's degree and two years of experience; or a high school diploma or equivalent and six years of experience. (Note: a combination of post high school education and experience equal to six years.) Preferred Qualifications Demonstrated ability to take ownership of day-to-day business and fiscal operations, anticipate operational needs, and independently identify and implement solutions. Demonstrated ability to build collaborative relationships and serve as a trusted business partner to organizational leadership and internal stakeholders. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being re-advertised. Previous applicants need not reapply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63494&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Digital Platform Associate (OPS, Remote-eligible), Institute on Digital Health and Innovation (IDHI)", "description": "Digital Platform Associate (OPS, Remote-eligible), Institute on Digital Health and Innovation (IDHI) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63494 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Florida State University College of Nursing Institute on Digital Health and Innovation (IDHI) Responsibilities Established in 2022, the Institute on Digital Health and Innovation (IDHI) within the Florida State University College of Nursing advances digital health science, technologies, and tools focused on solving real world needs of patients, providers, and populations through research, training, and innovation to maximize health. The mission of IDHI is to advance individual and public health through collaborative and synergistic partnerships focused on the development, evaluation, and dissemination of digital health tools, technologies, and innovations. IDHI\u2019s HealthMpowerment (HMP) is a mobile optimized digital health platform designed to deliver health and wellness content to young people. The platform has been used in more than 20 research studies worldwide across topics such as sexual health, medication adherence, and mental health. The Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC) has identified HMP as an evidence-based intervention for HIV risk reduction. The platform is actively used and continuously evolving, supported by a team of researchers, developers, and operations staff. The Digital Platform Associate is a hands-on, execution focused role supporting the day-to-day implementation of research studies using the HMP platform. This role combines content development, platform operations, and quality assurance. The majority of work involves building and managing content in the platform, testing features, and supporting study teams. This role may be best suited for candidates who enjoy hands on, detail-oriented work within structured systems, balancing creative and technical tasks while building and testing content in digital platforms in a digital health research setting. Qualifications Bachelor\u2019s degree and one year of relevant experience, or a combination of post high school education and experience equal to five years. Knowledge of public health principles and health education practices. Preferred Qualifications Master\u2019s degree in a related field such as public health, health communication, or information science. Experience with digital health or behavioral health interventions. Familiarity with research studies or clinical trials. Experience creating multimedia content such as basic video, audio, or visual materials; using tools such as Canva, iMovie, Audacity, or similar editing platforms; and testing software or mobile apps. Experience supporting users or managing participant or customer communications. Understanding of how multimedia content supports engagement and user experience in digital platforms. Strong attention to detail and ability to identify issues in complex workflows. Strong organizational skills and ability to manage multiple tasks at once. Strong written and verbal communication skills. Comfort working within structured systems and following detailed processes. Ability to handle repetitive tasks with a high level of accuracy. Interest in digital products, user experience, or content within apps and platforms. Proficiency in Microsoft Office including Outlook, Word, Excel, and PowerPoint. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range $28.85 per hour, commensurate with experience/education. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an OPS/temporary job. Based on the duties, this position may require completion of a criminal history background check . Full-time, 40 hours per week. This role has been designated as eligible for remote work based on the job functions. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63712&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "FSUS Classroom Substitute, 2026-2027 (Part-time, OPS) (Multiple Vacancies)", "description": "FSUS Classroom Substitute, 2026-2027 (Part-time, OPS) (Multiple Vacancies) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63712 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Florida State University Schools Responsibilities Substitutes for teachers grades K-12. Works with teachers in the classroom to help students. Supervises the classroom in teacher's absence. Completes paperwork under the teacher's direction. May include other student supervisory duties as needed. Qualifications High school diploma or equivalent. Must be able to provide three professional references Preferred Qualifications Bachelor's degree with experience working in a school setting. Florida Teaching Certificate. Other Information We proudly serve as a laboratory K-12 school, blending the rigors of academic achievement with a commitment to educational research and innovation. We draw upon the resources of a world-class university, bringing cutting-edge practices and insights directly into our classrooms. This dynamic approach ensures that our students benefit from the latest advancements in pedagogy and fosters an environment where curiosity and exploration are celebrated. Florida State University Schools is not just a place of learning; it's a community dedicated to empowering the leaders of tomorrow. We invite you to explore the possibilities at FSUS and join us on a journey of academic excellence, personal growth, and a commitment to making a positive impact on the world. Contact Info Jaye Corbett University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range $15.25 per hour. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an OPS/temporary job. Based on the duties, this position may require completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63722&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Garage/Parking Lot Technician", "description": "Garage/Parking Lot Technician Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63722 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department FSU Facilities Waste Management Department Responsibilities Responsible for performing preventative upkeep maintenance in parking garages across campus. This includes performing cleanliness checks within the parking structure, entrances, exits, landings, elevators, and stairwells within each parking garage. Empties trash receptacles, sweeps, and blows litter and debris as necessary. Notes where maintenance repair is required and reports complex issues and/or problems to the supervisor. Uses appropriate equipment, including power washer and blower, to ensure cleanliness and maintenance of each structure. Eliminates stains within parking structure, including parking spaces and pillars/columns. Inspects and cleans parking garage signage. Inspects and cleans gates, gate arms, card readers, etc. Ensures parking garages remain in good and safe operating condition. Reports non-routine issues to the supervisor. Maintains parking lots in a clean, safe, and orderly manner by mowing, blowing, mobile sweeping, trimming, weeding, and performing minor pest management. Responsible for cleaning debris from grounds, pathways, and parking lots; maintains grounds maintenance equipment. May assist in removing and stacking cardboard as related to job duties. As needed, will load and unload cardboard including operating cardboard baler. Operates University vehicles as required. Performs other related duties assigned by supervisor. Qualifications High school diploma or equivalency and two years of experience or a combination of post high school education and experience equal to two years. Technical or vocational degree may substitute for experience. A valid Florida or Georgia driver's license or the ability to obtain one upon hire. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select \u201cyes\u201d to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for Veterans\u2019 Preference eligibility requirements and Veterans\u2019 Preference required documentation (PDF) , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63720&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Plumber (Open Rank)", "description": "Plumber (Open Rank) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63720 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Florida State University Facilities Maintenance Department Responsibilities Responsible for installation, repair and maintenance of piping and associated components. Installs, maintains and repairs piping valves, faucets, sinks, sewers, vents and other sanitary fixtures. Installs and maintains gas and airstream piping and associated fixtures. Checks, repairs and replaces steam boilers and safety devices and controls. Flushes and cleans boilers, storage and return tanks, hot water heaters, etc. Reads and follows blueprints and other verbal or written instructions in order to complete repair orders. Drives University vehicles as required. Responsible for other duties as assigned within the department. Qualifications Plumber 1 & 2 : Requires a high school diploma or equivalency and two years of related work experience or a combination of post high school education and experience equal to 2 years. Technical or vocational degree in plumbing, electrical work, HVAC or other trade, may substitute for the required years of experience. Plumber 3 : Requires a high school diploma or equivalency and four years of related work experience. Must have an active State of Florida, Local Journeyman, or Master Plumber's License. Plumber 4 : Requires a high school diploma or equivalency and six years of related work experience. Must have an active State of Florida, Local Journeyman, or Master Plumber's License. A valid Florida or Georgia Class E Driver's license or the ability to obtain one upon hire. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select \u201cyes\u201d to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for Veterans\u2019 Preference eligibility requirements and Veterans\u2019 Preference required documentation (PDF) , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=62859&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Senior Custodial Supervisor 5:00 am", "description": "Senior Custodial Supervisor 5:00 am Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 62859 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Facilities - Custodial Services Responsibilities Supervises Custodial Supervisors. Provides training and instruction. Sets goals and objectives and determines workloads. Plans and establishes methods and frequency for cleaning. Communicates with the supervisory chain of command regarding daily operations and personnel-related matters. Prepares forms and investigates incidents of on-the-job accidents/injuries of employees. Maintains accurate and up-to-date daily attendance and leave records. Conducts general inspections of buildings for overall cleanliness and sanitation. Identifies deficiencies in cleaning and conducts follow-up inspections to ensure that corrective measures have been taken to bring cleaning up to established standards. Identifies and reports carpet cleaning or other maintenance needs as needed. Initiates work orders as necessary. Coordinates and schedules all special custodial projects within assigned building(s). Serves as liaison between custodial staff and other staff and faculty members. Works closely and communicates with building occupants to ensure that custodial work does not disrupt operations. Provides quality customer service and promotes a positive working relationship between custodial staff and customers. Responsible for inventory control of custodial supplies and equipment. Issues supplies and equipment and ensures proper use. Inspects equipment and ensures proper maintenance and daily cleaning of carts, vacuums, floor machines, etc. Initiates work orders for carpet cleaning, maintenance, repairs, pest control, and other services that cannot be performed by custodial staff. Operates University-owned vehicles as necessary. Performs other duties as assigned. Qualifications High school diploma or equivalency and two years experience or a combination of post high school education and experience equal to two years. Relevant training may substitute for experience. A valid State of Florida or Georgia Driver\u2019s License or ability to obtain upon hire. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select \u201cyes\u201d to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for Veterans\u2019 Preference eligibility requirements and Veterans\u2019 Preference required documentation (PDF) , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . The work schedule is 5:00am to 1:30pm with a 30-minute break. This position is being re-advertised. Previous applicants need not apply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63509&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Senior Custodial Worker 5:00am", "description": "Senior Custodial Worker 5:00am Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63509 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Facilities - Custodial Services Responsibilities Cleans and maintains carpeted flooring by vacuuming, spot cleaning, or extracting, and using a wet-dry cleaning machine. Vacuums walk-off mats, upholstered furnishings, and fabric patrician furniture. In the absence of the supervisor, this position may oversee work assignments to ensure that all essential duties are completed and performed in accordance with established standards. This position may act as a lead worker and oversee special projects as assigned and assist the Custodial Supervisor with administrative tasks including maintaining inventory and issuing supplies. Cleans and maintains tile, wood, and concrete flooring by sweeping, dust mopping, and wet mopping. Applies floor stripper, sealer, finish, and restoration products. Uses automatic floor scrubber, wet vacuum, and buffers and burnishers to strip and maintain floors. Dusts and wet cleans horizontal and vertical surfaces including: tables, chairs, counters, desks, bookshelves, sills and ledges, diffusers, vents, walls, elevator tracks, doors, marker and chalk boards, trays, interior glass and windows, venetian blinds, etc. Cleans and sanitizes water coolers and public restrooms. Restocks supplies of tissue, towels, and hand soap. Empties waste receptacles and removes trash and other debris, excluding hazardous and toxic materials and materials deposited in \"SHARP\" boxes. Cleans and maintains custodial equipment. Reports equipment and supply needs to supervisor. Reports needed repairs, secures property to prevent damage, places caution signs, cleans entrances and other walkways and breezeways, etc. Performs other duties as assigned. Qualifications Completion of 9th Grade. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select \u201cyes\u201d to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for Veterans\u2019 Preference eligibility requirements and Veterans\u2019 Preference required documentation (PDF) , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . The work schedule is 5am to 1:30pm with a 30-minute break from 9am to 9:30am. This positions being re-advertised. Previous applicants need not apply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63638&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Administrative Associate (English)", "description": "Administrative Associate (English) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63638 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of English | College of Arts & Sciences Responsibilities The Administrative Associate provides administrative support for the Department of English and serves as an assistant to the Department Chair. This role helps coordinate faculty records and reviews, manages scheduling and communications, and supports department facilities, events, and daily office operations. In this role, you will be responsible for: Managing the Department Chair\u2019s calendar, scheduling meetings, maintaining documents, and coordinating communications with faculty, students, and staff. Welcoming visitors, answering office calls, reserving shared rooms, and handling department mail, deliveries, and shipping. Helping organize faculty recruitment visits, including preparing schedules and arranging meetings. Preparing and tracking faculty work assignments and activity reports, checking records for accuracy, and ensuring required materials are submitted on time. Coordinating documents and deadlines for faculty evaluations, promotions, tenure, and reviews of tenured faculty. Working with faculty and university offices to assemble and submit supporting materials. Maintaining records of instructor qualifications, assisting with faculty award submissions, and coordinating faculty participation in commencement ceremonies. Coordinating building access, keys, office moves, and space use. Maintaining department signs, bulletin boards, required workplace notices, and the mailroom. Arranging maintenance and repairs for shared office equipment and keeping common supplies stocked. Planning department events, including awards ceremonies, graduate student open houses, staff gatherings, and retirement celebrations. Arranging event spaces, catering, and setup. Providing backup support for department purchasing card transactions and ensuring purchases follow university policies and funding requirements. Supporting special projects and other administrative needs while maintaining accurate, confidential records and following applicable policies and regulations. Qualifications High School diploma or equivalent and three years of experience. (Note: post-high school education may substitute for experience at the equivalent rate.) Preferred Qualifications The English Department is seeking an individual who communicates clearly and effectively, possesses excellent customer service skills, strong organization, and attention to detail. The individual should be comfortable managing priorities, working collaboratively, using common office software, and gathering and organizing information. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Anticipated starting salary for the position is in the mid $30,000's. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select \u201cyes\u201d to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for Veterans\u2019 Preference eligibility requirements and Veterans\u2019 Preference required documentation (PDF) , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . A work sample will be conducted for applicants selected for interview. This position is being re-advertised. Previous applicants need not reapply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63706&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Advanced Practice Registered Nurse, 9 Month Salaried - University Health Services", "description": "Advanced Practice Registered Nurse, 9 Month Salaried - University Health Services Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63706 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Part-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department University Health Services Responsibilities Provides quality outpatient general medical primary patient care consistent with the Health Center\u2019s goals and objectives and the current standard of medical care. Performs complete physical examinations. Following approved Advanced Practice Registered Nurse (APRN) protocols, performs diagnostic examinations and examinations for specific complaints in the identification of illnesses and injuries. Initiates diagnostic laboratory tests, x-rays, and other procedures as medically indicated. May perform indicated minor surgical and non-invasive diagnostic procedures. Makes medical assessments and initiates procedures and/or treatments within established protocols under the direction of the physician. Documents the patient history, physical and emotional state, diagnostic findings and treatment in the patient\u2019s medical record/Electronic Medical Record (EMR). Reviews and discusses with patient the results of laboratory, x-ray, and other procedures. Makes medically indicated referrals to other specialists/consultants as necessary. Confers with physician regarding patient management when appropriate. May function as a preceptor for Nurse Practitioner students. Actively participates in the revision of APRN protocols annually. Assists in the development of educational and instructional materials and programs. As needed, assists in patient triage and phone inquiries and orientation and training of personnel assisting with patient care. Attends and participates on committees, conducts case presentations, and during periods of reduced clinical demand (ie: summer), may support other administrative, outreach, or operational tasks as needed to support the overall mission and function of the department. During non-peak times, responsibilities may shift to include cross-training, special projects and other duties as assigned. Qualifications Master's Degree and 2 years of experience. Graduate from an accredited Advanced Registered Nurse Practitioner program. Certification as an Advanced Registered Nurse Practitioner in accordance with Chapter 464, Florida Statutes. Current APRN nursing license. Current CPR Certification or ability to obtain within 30 days of hire University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position requires pre-employment TB testing and successful completion of post hire OSHA training. This is a 9 month position working mid August through mid May. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63063&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Assistant Director, Animal Care", "description": "Assistant Director, Animal Care Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63063 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Laboratory Animal Resources within the Office of Research seeks to fill the Assistant Director of Animal Care position. Responsibilities This position is responsible for providing direction for the daily operation of the animal care and husbandry program. Provides strategic oversight for all LAR-maintained facilities. Relieves the LAR Director of a wide variety of internal duties and on-the-ground decision making. Supervises the functions and activities of LAR direct animal care staff. Ensures that animal care staff follow established operating procedures. Schedules, assigns and re-assigns work to ensure efficient utilization of manpower, equipment and facilities. Determines needs and makes recommendations for staffing and new/replacement equipment and/or services. Coordinates hiring, orienting, training, assessing, disciplinary action and termination procedures for LAR direct animal care staff. Communicate with faculty and investigators to determine project requirements for animal resources, housing, and care. Complete and coordinate complex projects and reports, which may require significant contact with other departments and outside organizations. Participates in and provides input for planning, design and commissioning of renovations and new spaces. Develops changes to operational policies for LAR animal care and husbandry programs. This position preforms rounds in animal facilities to ensure maintenance of required sanitation standards and conformance to AAALAC, USDA, Guide, IACUC and department policies and guidelines; observes and reports noticeable deficiencies. Provides detailed written inspection reports of all the animal facilities routinely to the LAR Director. Participates in department and IACUC inspections, AAALAC site visits and other regulatory visits. Ensures that equipment and facilities are maintained in operational condition. Ensures that equipment or facility issues are reported in a timely fashion and follows through to ensure the problems are resolved. Serves as departmental property manager. Responsible for information and inventory management, and coordinating supply orders while remaining within budgetary constraints. This position provides technical expertise and instruction in animal use and experimentation. Will Assist with colony health surveillance monitoring program as needed. Will serve as acting supervisor of cage wash personnel in absence of Cage Wash and Ancillary Services Supervisor. Oversees integrated pest management program. Attends regional or national meetings periodically to remain current with industry standards and to promote teamwork and growth in LAR. Participates in emergency response planning and contingency planning for animal facilities. Rotates after hours, weekend, and holiday coverage with Cage Wash and Ancillary Services Supervisor. Perform other duties as assigned related to operation of animal facilities and animal care program. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and four years experience in a related science or research services field or a Masters and two years experience in a related science or research services field. Must hold a current LATG Certification issued by AALAS. Preferred Qualifications Experience managing personnel and operations within an academic laboratory animal care program American Association for Laboratory Animal Science Certified Manager of Animal Resources (CMAR) certification Master\u2019s degree in laboratory animal science, veterinary science, biological science, business administration, public administration, or a related field Demonstrated ability to build and maintain collaborative relationships with investigators, animal care staff, veterinary staff, and institutional partners Contact Info Cassidy Cooksey at rsch-workforce@fsu.edu University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range The anticipated salary range for this position is $100,000 - $140,000. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position is being readvertised. Previous applicants need not reapply. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Applicants must submit a cover letter outlining their qualifications, leadership experience, and leadership philosophy. The letter should include a discussion of how the applicant would balance the highest standards of animal welfare and regulatory compliance while supporting and facilitating the research and teaching missions of the University. Applicants must provide a minimum of three professional references familiar with their work performance and leadership abilities, including each reference's relationship to the applicant, email address, and telephone number. Applicants that do not submit all required materials will not be considered. This position participates in a rotation of after hours, weekend, and holiday on-call with other LAR supervisory personnel. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63708&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Certified Medical Assistant, 9 Month Salaried - University Health Services", "description": "Certified Medical Assistant, 9 Month Salaried - University Health Services Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63708 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department University Health Services Responsibilities Provides assistance to medical staff in designated aspects of patient care in conjunction with the clinical staff at University Health Services. Performs clinical and administrative duties in support of assigned area at a level commensurate with their training and experience. Under direction of the Lead Clinician and Medical Director, assists clinicians and nurses with routine medical care for patients. Ensures all electronic health record (EHR) information is current. Documents basic intake items in the EHR. Sets up for and assists providers with exams and procedures. Gives non-intravenous injections, medication administration and handles minor procedures such as collection & testing of specimens, splinting and applying dressings, visual acuity testing, ear lavage and other duties as privileged to complete. Performs disinfection and cleaning of rooms in between patient visits. Stocks room with supply items and assists with maintaining medical equipment. May act as a clinical chaperone for provider during an exam. Performs intake for patients, including obtaining vital signs and height and weight. Assists with patient needs between visits. Manages patient phone calls and provides EHR management support for clinicians. Notifies patients of test results and other follow-ups as needed. Manages patient expectations and is able to resolve patient concerns with consultation with provider, if needed. May assist in obtaining additional information for clinicians regarding information from patients regarding their care. Provides preventative health and wellness information to students, utilizing electronic and print resources. Advises patients regarding clinical appointments. Educates patient regarding health center policy and procedure, as well as services provided. Seeks consultation with clinical staff as appropriate. Performs other duties as assigned by Nursing Supervisor. These may include committee participation, meetings, special projects, or as float personnel to other clinics. During periods of reduced clinical demand (ie: summer), may support other administrative, outreach, or operational tasks as needed to support the overall mission and function of the department. During non-peak times, responsibilities may shift to include cross-training, special projects and other duties as assigned. Qualifications High school diploma or equivalency and two years experience or a combination of post high school education and experience equal to two years. Current CPR Certification or ability to obtain within 30 days of hire. Must possess valid certification as a Medical Assistant. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select \u201cyes\u201d to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for Veterans\u2019 Preference eligibility requirements and Veterans\u2019 Preference required documentation (PDF) , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position requires pre-employment TB testing and successful completion of post hire OSHA training. This is a 9 month position working mid August through mid May. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63707&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Physician's Assistant, 9 Month Salaried - University Health Services", "description": "Physician's Assistant, 9 Month Salaried - University Health Services Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63707 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department University Health Services Responsibilities Provides outpatient general medical primary care to eligible patients, following approved guidelines. Performs complete physical examinations and diagnostic examinations for the identification and evaluation of illnesses and injuries. Initiates laboratory tests, x-rays and other procedures as medically necessary. May perform indicated minor surgical and non-invasive procedures. Confers with physician regarding patient management when appropriate. Documents medical history, physical and emotional state, diagnostic findings, and treatment in the patient's Electronic Medical Record. Reviews and discusses tests and examination results with patient. Counsels and instructs patient regarding current complaint. Monitors medication and initiates therapies within established guidelines under physician direction. Participates in professional and administrative committees and performs other duties as assigned. Attend clinical meetings and case presentations. Assists in the development of educational and instructional materials and programs. May function as preceptor for clinical students. During periods of reduced clinical demand (ie: summer), may support other administrative, outreach, or operational tasks as needed to support the overall mission and function of the department. During non-peak times, responsibilities may shift to include cross-training, special projects, and other duties as assigned Qualifications Master of Science in Physician Assistant Studies and two years of experience. Must meet certification and license requirements as outlined in Chapter 458, Florida Statues. Current CPR Certification or ability to obtain within 30 days of hire. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position requires pre-employment TB testing and successful completion of post hire OSHA training. This is a 9 month position working mid August through mid May. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63711&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Program Director - Rural Health Data & Analytics, Southwest & Northwest Regions - Preventative Care & Care At Home (Rural Health Transformation Program - College of Medicine)", "description": "Program Director - Rural Health Data & Analytics, Southwest & Northwest Regions - Preventative Care & Care At Home (Rural Health Transformation Program - College of Medicine) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63711 Location Remote Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Rural Health Transformation Program - College of Medicine Florida State University\u2019s College of Medicine has been awarded more than $19 million through the Rural Health Transformation Program to strengthen healthcare access and outcomes in rural Florida. The funding will support six new projects focused on critical needs including behavioral health, preventive care, food insecurity, telehealth, at-home care and healthcare workforce development. Through partnerships with communities and healthcare organizations across Northwest and Southwest Florida, FSU is working to bring innovative, practical solutions directly to rural communities and help close longstanding gaps in care. Responsibilities Data Management, Integration, and Governance: Direct planning, implementation, administration, and continuous improvement of data management, integration, governance, and reporting. Provide leadership to healthcare partner data personnel and collaborate with technical staff across participating organizations to ensure consistent implementation of data governance standards, reporting, and data management processes. Manage and maintain multiple data systems supporting RHTP Bundle 1 NW and SW activities. Develop/oversee data collection, validation, quality assurance processes across participating organizations. Coordinate acquisition and integration of data from multiple sources. Train and supervise regional data analysts to support the program. Performance Measurement and Reporting: Develop, administer, and maintain performance measurement and reporting systems that monitor project milestones, implementation progress, quality metrics, healthcare utilization outcomes, workforce measures, and population health indicators. Support program accountability, operational decision-making, funding requirements, and continuous quality improvement through the delivery of dashboards, data visualizations, and routine performance reports. Evaluation and Analytics: Conduct data analysis and evaluation activities to assess program implementation, effectiveness, outcomes, and impact. Produce analytical reports and recommendations that support strategic planning, program evaluation, and evidence-based decision-making. Produce summary reports, data visualizations, infographics, presentations, and other analytical products for internal and external audiences. Stakeholder and Technical Support: Coordinate with partners to support effective data collection, reporting, and performance measurement activities. Provides technical assistance, training, and consultation regarding data systems, reporting requirements, and program data processes. Collaborate with implementation teams, practice facilitators, evaluators, healthcare leaders, and community stakeholders to support program objectives. Qualifications Master's degree and four years of experience related to technical services. (Higher education can substitute for experience at the equivalent rate.) Reliable transportation, and a valid Driver's License or the ability to obtain prior to hire. Contact Info Georgia Arnold Program Director Behavioral Sciences and Social Medicine University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position will be supporting Bundle 1 - Preventative Care & Care At Home Northwest and Southwest regions on the Rural Health Transformation Program Map . For purposes of this position, the geographic regions are defined as follows: Northwest Florida Region : Includes Bay, Calhoun, Escambia, Franklin, Gadsden, Gulf, Holmes, Jackson, Jefferson, Leon, Liberty, Okaloosa, Santa Rosa, Wakulla, Walton, and Washington counties. Southwest Florida Region : Includes Charlotte, Collier, DeSoto, Glades, Hardee, Hendry, Highlands, Lee, Manatee, Okeechobee, and Sarasota counties. This position has been designated as eligible for remote work based on the current position/job functions. This position requires regular travel in support of program activities and responsibilities. Travel may occur within the employee\u2019s assigned region and throughout the State of Florida, as needed. The frequency and location of travel may vary based on programmatic and operational needs. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63705&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Program Manager, Facility & Grounds", "description": "Program Manager, Facility & Grounds Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63705 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department This position is with NorthWest Regional Data Center Responsibilities This position is with Northwest Reginal Data Center IP Facilities with heavy but not exclusive emphasis on electrical. Responsible for co-managing the daily 24x7x365 facility operations for Northwest Regional Data Center (NWRDC), including but not limited to the building and grounds, physical security, utilities and power, emergency backup power, and HVAC. Co-manages all day-to-day facility-related operations and maintenance for NWRDC, including direct oversight of the building and grounds, physical security, power, emergency backup systems, and HVAC. This includes direct responsibility for maintenance and repairs, new circuit installation & monitoring for IT Equipment, related work orders, and contractor and FSU Facilities engagements. Also responsible for co-managing and facilitating data center infrastructure upgrades/changes, including managing maintenance contracts, as well as managing computer room air conditioners (CRAC) and power distribution units (PDU). Advises the Associate Director for Administrative Services, the Executive Director, and senior management on issues and needs related to the data center facility. This position is a direct report to the IT Manager. Assists in short-term and long-term planning for data center and facility-related items and advises the management team on issues and needs related to the data center facility. Responsible for the documentation and inventory of all data center facility-related changes. Maintains inventories of all data center facilities items, such as electrical circuits. Provides around-the-clock support and oversight of the data center facility, including after-hours response and notifications, as needed or required for a 24 x 7 x 365 High Availability Data Center. Other duties and responsibilities as required, including some driving of state vehicles to run errands related to facility management. Participates in approved professional development opportunities per NWRDC\u2019s policy. Professional development and training is defined as learning undertaken by the employee to maintain and advance their skills, knowledge, and competencies, specifically as they relate and add value to the individual, job, and workplace. NWRDC provides support for a wide range of state and local government, as well as K-20 organizations across the State of Florida. These organizations are dependent on NWRDC in order to accomplish their missions. This requires NWRDC to maintain services 24 x 7 x 365, even during times of crisis or emergency. As such, all NWRDC staff are considered essential staff for operations of the State of Florida. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and four years' experience related to facilities and/or grounds services or a high school diploma or equivalent and eight years of experience in the same area. (Note: or a combination of post high school education and same experience equal to eight years.) A valid Florida or Georgia driver's license, Class E or the ability to obtain one upon hire. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63553&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Quality Control Coordinator", "description": "Quality Control Coordinator Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63553 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Facilities - Custodial Services Responsibilities Responsible for assisting and recommending the development of policies and procedures to effectively administer a Building Services Quality Control Program. Reviews Building Services Frequencies and Procedures to ensure each room type is assigned the appropriate level of custodial care. Collaborates with the Assistant Director to address the needs of each area and ensure that cleaning schedules are provided to the University campus with proper timelines. Develops checklists for field surveys and administer reviews of reports, studies, specifications, and surveys to make recommendations related to program improvements, project assignments, inspection results, and employee performance to the Assistant Director. Plays a key role in long- and short-term planning for the department. Oversee the daily operations and scheduling of all quality control inspections. Performs regular field surveys of campus building conditions and determines if services provided meet established quality standards. Ensure all assigned buildings meet and/or exceed appearance, cleanliness, and safety standards. Confirms FSU employees are utilizing appropriate methods, equipment, and chemicals as per established processes and procedures. Communicates with vendors, consultants, department heads, and building liaison representatives to ensure that cleaning services are being performed at an acceptable level. Supervises Quality Control Associate. Ensures documentation is accurately recorded and collected. Submits work orders to escalates preventive maintenance, broken, defective, or safety concerns for maintenance and repairs. Makes recommendations to the Assistant Director to improve campus buildings, working with all levels of campus personnel concerning requirements of each department. In collaboration with the supervisor, manages the data within the quality control program. Utilizes facilities software to draft and review inspection reports for completeness and accuracy. Analyzes the inspections to determine the root cause of deficiencies and shares insights and training with the Custodial Operations Team. Performs other duties as assigned within the department. Operates University vehicles as needed to complete assigned work. Qualifications High school diploma or equivalent and experience equal to six years or a combination of post high school education and experience equal to six years.) A valid Florida or Georgia driver's license or the ability to obtain one upon hire. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . The work schedule is from 5am to 1:30pm with a 30-minute break. This position is being re-advertised. Previous applicants need not apply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63423&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "RHT Project Lead, Health and Lifestyle, Southwest Region (Rural Health Transformation Program - College of Medicine)", "description": "RHT Project Lead, Health and Lifestyle, Southwest Region (Rural Health Transformation Program - College of Medicine) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63423 Location Hybrid Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Rural Health Transformation Program - College of Medicine Florida State University\u2019s College of Medicine has been awarded more than $19 million through the Rural Health Transformation Program to strengthen healthcare access and outcomes in rural Florida. The funding will support six new projects focused on critical needs including behavioral health, preventive care, food insecurity, telehealth, at-home care and healthcare workforce development. Through partnerships with communities and healthcare organizations across Northwest and Southwest Florida, FSU is working to bring innovative, practical solutions directly to rural communities and help close longstanding gaps in care. Responsibilities Coordinates daily operations involving multidisciplinary teams that include partner organizations and other project stakeholders. Supports scheduling, partner communications, convening logistics, and documentation management. Coordinates and maintains multiple collaborative relationships both internally and externally to support project goals. Provides support to program manager and participates in planning and execution of research activities. Reviews technical operations to ensure all processes and protocols adhere to established policies and procedures. Coordinates meetings, maintains project timelines, prepares agendas and meeting minutes, monitors milestones, and facilitates communication to ensure timely completion of project deliverables. Provides administrative and project management support for program operations. Tracks performance measures, prepares progress reports, assists with AHCA and sponsor reporting requirements, maintains project documentation, monitors subrecipient activities, coordinates required approvals, and supports continuous quality improvement activities. Ensures compliance with university, sponsor, and regulatory requirements. Coordinates budgetary and operational activities including purchasing, travel, contracts, reimbursements, and consultant activities. Assists with monitoring expenditures, maintaining project records, scheduling trainings and events, coordinating logistics, and supporting implementation of program activities across multiple service sites. Supports the Principal Investigator and program leadership by assisting with strategic planning, grant administration, stakeholder engagement, dissemination activities, presentations, and preparation of reports, manuscripts, and other project materials. Performs other related duties assigned in support of program objectives. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and two years of experience; or a high school diploma/equivalent and experience equal to six years. (Note: post-high school education can substitute for experience at the equivalent rate.) Reliable transportation, and a valid Florida or Georgia Driver's License or the ability to obtain prior to hire. Contact Info Georgia Arnold University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position will be supporting Initiative 9 - Health & Lifestyle Southwest region, which is defined as Charlotte, Collier, DeSoto, Glades, Hardee, Hendry, Highlands, Lee, Manatee, Okeechobee, and Sarasota on the Rural Health Transformation Program Map . This position requires regular travel in support of program activities and responsibilities. Travel may occur within the employee\u2019s assigned region and throughout the State of Florida, as needed. The frequency and location of travel may vary based on programmatic and operational needs. This job opening is being readvertised. Previous applicants need not reapply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63433&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Senior Administrative Specialist", "description": "Senior Administrative Specialist Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63433 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Career Center Responsibilities Career Center Executive Administrative Support Executive Support: Initiates coordination of campus-wide programs Administrative Strategy: Recommends and implements internal operating procedures to improve administrative workflow and office systems. Coordinates activities involving the Career Center units - Career Advising, Counseling, & Instruction (CACI), Experiential Learning (EL), Employer Relations (ER), and the Center for Career Research (CCR). Space Management: Serves as the primary administrator for room scheduling software. Manages room bookings, setup, and cleanup for academic courses, in-services and special events. Calendar & Event Operations: Proactively maintains the internal master calendar, clear communication channels, and logistics handoffs between event leads, marketing, assessment, and technology support teams. Staff Meetings: Plans and executes logistics for all internal staff meetings and leadership team meetings. Dunlap Building Management & Operations Facility Oversight: Serves as the Building Manager for the Dunlap Success Center. Serves as the primary point of contact liaising directly with Facilities, Housekeeping, and Emergency Management Services (EMS) to resolve issues, oversee workspace readiness, and execute opening/closing procedures. New and Separating Staff Logistics: Facilitates process for new hires, including space preparation, welcome packages, space access (key and card swipe), and initial equipment setup. CC Operations Support Assists the Administration and Operations team with operational deliverables, cyclical workflows, such as program reviews and career outcomes roadmaps, document management in Teams, and special projects. Interprets and administers office policy. Develops office procedures. Assesses operational needs, inventories supplies, gathers vendor quotes for equipment, furniture, print materials, and office supplies and makes purchases using a purchasing card. Provides backup coverage for contract management and P-Card proxies as needed. Front Desk Oversight Recruits, hires, trains, and schedules student assistants to deliver high-level customer service at the second-floor reception area. Manages general email communications. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and four years of experience; or a high school diploma or equivalent and eight years of experience. (Note: post-high school education may substitute for experience at the equivalent rate.) University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Anticipated starting salary low $50,000's. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being re-advertised. Previous applicants need not apply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=62669&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Waste Management Support Worker (Multiple Vacancies)", "description": "Waste Management Support Worker (Multiple Vacancies) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 62669 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Facilities - Waste Management Responsibilities Empties small outdoor trash collection receptacles on campus and collects plastic bottles and cans. Transports waste and recyclable materials to the Solid Waste / Recycling department using a utility vehicle. Empties multi-stream recycling stations after university events. Performs monitoring and upkeep of campus for litter to ensure the cleanliness of assigned zones. Maintains a safe, clean, sustainable, and attractive environment for the students, faculty, and staff of our institution. Responsible for picking up pallets and items left on loading docks in support of cardboard collection throughout campus from designated sites and disposing of those materials into their properly specified compactors. Pressure washes trash receptacles as assigned. Ensures that all manual and power equipment is clean and in proper working condition and reports maintenance problems to the supervisor. Assists in keeping the Waste Management Facility's outdoor areas clean, grounds, fence lines, and roll-off container areas in the compound. Performs other tasks as assigned by supervisor or higher authority. Requires a valid driver's license for driving utility vehicles. Qualifications Completion of ninth grade. A valid State of Florida or Georgia Driver\u2019s License or ability to obtain upon hire. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our interactive too l to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://jobs.fsu.edu. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select \u201cyes\u201d to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for eligibility information and required documentation , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being re-advertised. Previous applicants need not apply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63178&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Business Analyst", "description": "Business Analyst Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63178 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Division of Enrollment Management | Technology Operations Unit Responsibilities The Division of Enrollment Management is comprised of four distinct units: Office of Admissions, Office of the University Registrar, Office of Financial Aid, and Technology Operations. Enrollment Management\u2019s integrated services provide distinctive support throughout the students\u2019 development and progression in their academic experience \u2013 from recruitment through commencement. Through collaboration, communication, and commitment, all units within Enrollment Management achieve the highest level of student-centered service to current and prospective students and families as well as to campus partners across the University. The Technology Operations Unit within Enrollment Management provides technology support, technology-based solutions, systems configuration, identity and data management, and analysis across the division. The unit works closely with subject matter experts in Admissions, Registrar, and Financial Aid to meet the operational and reporting needs of various stockholders across campus. Responsible for creating, designing, and maintaining financial aid reporting and analysis. Serves as data management analyst and leverages financial aid data with other key institutional data. Designs, develops, and maintains financial aid databases and reports for state, federal, and institutional reports such as Board of Governors, IPEDS, Common Data Set (CDS) as well as other reports that aid in the leveraging of financial aid. Optimizes the use of PS query and interactive visualization software to develop departmental dashboards for a variety of reporting needs that include financial aid data as well as data from other campus departments. Responsible for accessing university data stores and creating ad hoc reporting datasets to complete institutional reports for administration. Develops and maintains Snowflake reports for use by functional end users across campus. Utilizes the current Snowflake software to assess and analyze information to respond to official requests for Financial Aid data. Meets with clients to determine data needs to create informational databases. Analyzes data for accuracy and presented in a logical, consistent manner for timely dissemination. Makes recommendations to senior leadership for the enhancement or creation of Snowflake queries and PS queries. Collects and analyzes financial aid data to respond to surveys that profile FSU for publications and University reporting. Maintains historical documentation relating to various surveys. Assists with the gathering and evaluation of financial aid data for Board of Governor (BOG) reporting. Identifies efficiencies, participates in testing, advises of regulatory changes, and ensure compliance with quality assurance. Assist with admissions and enrolled student reporting. Provides support to departmental and administrative clients in the use of PS Query and current Snowflake software as well as their best practices. Maintains documentation for training purposes on these products. Assists in developing strategies to aid in streamlined data management. Researches problems within sections programs and presenting findings to ensure compliance with state, federal, and institutional regulations. Makes recommendations to senior leadership for the enhancement of overall processes. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and two years of experience; or a high school diploma/equivalent and six years of relevant experience. (Note: a combination of post high school education and experience equal to six years.) Preferred Qualifications Bachelor's degree and two years of experience in enrollment services. Ability to multi-task within a fast-paced work environment. Experience implementing and/or supporting new initiatives (policy, technology, procedure, etc.). Preferred candidates will have experience with interactive visualization software. Strong organizational, analytical, and communication skills desired. Previous experience and comfort working with a variety of computer software applications, databases, and student information systems (PeopleSoft). Ability to manage multiple projects and responsibilities at the same time. Prior experience analyzing data to create reports, to identify trends and to make decisions. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range The anticipated salary range for this position is around $50,000 annually, commensurate with education and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being re-advertised. Previous applicants need not reapply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63703&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Research Director for Election Law Center (Research Faculty I 12 Month Visiting)", "description": "Research Director for Election Law Center (Research Faculty I 12 Month Visiting) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63703 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department College of Law Responsibilities The Research Director of the College of Law Election Law Center will be responsible for conducting and overseeing the Center\u2019s empirical and statistical research projects and preparing reports and articles to disseminate the results of this research to academic, governmental, and public audiences. The Director will be involved in developing methodologies for conducing the Center\u2019s studies, obtaining the necessary data, and conducting rigorous statistical analysis. The research the Director will oversee focuses on various election administration issues and legal questions relating to the electoral process. For example, the Center seeks to compare expert witness predictions concerning the likely impact of changes to election-related rules and procedures on metrics such as voter registration or turnout to the actual results of those legal provisions (when they are allowed to take effect). This study will help determine the accuracy and reliability of various methodologies, models, data sets, and statistical techniques frequently employed in election-related litigation. Likewise, the Center seeks to update earlier studies concerning the accuracy of information contained within voter registration databases and the inclusion of ineligible registrants, particularly in light of the rise of automatic voter registration, online registration, and interstate systems facilitating the exchange of voter information among certain states. From a qualitative perspective, the Center will also examine differences among states\u2019 laws governing provisional ballots and canvassing. Additionally, the Research Director will assist the Executive Director of the Election Law Center in cultivating and sustaining external and internal partnerships to advance the Center\u2019s short-term and long-term goals. Qualifications A PhD in political science, mathematics, statistics, or economics is required. Applicants with PhDs in public administration, public policy, or related fields will be considered on a case-by-case basis if they have extensive training and experience with statistical analysis and empirical research. Preferred Qualifications Required Skills Background in quantitative and statistical analysis Strong research and writing skills A collaborative and solutions-focused mentality Contact Info Maureen Wagner Vinson Executive Director of Election Law Center Florida State University College of Law Mwagner3@law.fsu.edu University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Anticipated salary range: $110,000-negotiable, depending upon experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63698&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Staff Attorney for Election Law Center (Instructional Specialist I 12-Month Visiting)", "description": "Staff Attorney for Election Law Center (Instructional Specialist I 12-Month Visiting) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63698 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department College of Law Responsibilities The Staff Attorney for the College of Law Election Law Center will be responsible for assisting with the Center\u2019s legal and other research projects; engaging in legal research and drafting for amicus briefs; coding cases for databases; gathering, organizing, and summarizing primary sources for online dissemination; and preparing reports, presentations, training materials, and articles to distribute to academic, governmental, and public audiences. This research will focus on election administration, as well as constitutional and statutory issues relating to the electoral process. Specific areas of research will depend in part on litigation that may arise in federal and state court. The staff attorney will also help prepare fifty-state surveys, for example concerning the differences among states\u2019 laws governing provisional ballots and canvassing. The staff attorney will also assist with the preparation of caselaw databases concerning various issues such as Due Process challenges to election outcomes as well as remedies under Section 2 of the Voting Rights Act. The staff attorney may also assist with the Center\u2019s work concerning election emergencies, including gathering and reviewing the legislative history of existing laws in the field and preparation of a potential model statute. Finally, the staff attorney will also help with the Election Law Center\u2019s ongoing project on federal and state election contests by locating, summarizing, and organizing relevant primary sources for eventual public access through an interactive website. Additionally, the Staff Attorney will assist the Executive Director of the Election Law Center in cultivating and sustaining external and internal partnerships to advance the Center\u2019s short-term and long-term goals. Qualifications A JD is required. Applicants with an undergraduate or graduate degree in political science, history, public administration, mathematics, statistics, or economics are preferred, but not required. Preferred Qualifications Required Skills Strong research and writing skills Ability to organize and synthesize large amounts of information A collaborative and solutions-focused mentality Non-partisan dedication to generating accurate research outcomes Contact Info Maureen Wagner Vinson Executive Director of Election Law Center Florida State University College of Law Mwagner3@law.fsu.edu University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Anticipated salary range $100,000-negotiable, depending upon experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63768&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Events Assistant", "description": "Events Assistant Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63768 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department College of Law Responsibilities As part of the Faculty Support Office, this position works closely with the Event Manager and helps plan, organize, and promote outreach and informational events; assists with Faculty/Program events; provides administrative, clerical & instructional support to faculty as needed; and provides exam support . Assists with faculty events, including reserving rooms for events and booking guest travel. Orders catering, generates graphics & media for posting, and creates an RSVP link. Must coordinate tech needs and make signage as needed. May attend the weekly event planning meetings. Events include (but not limited to): Collegewide Events, Enrichment Speakers, Summer Presentation Series, Distinguished Environmental Lecture, Legal Writing Workshops, Clinic events, etc. Assist with preparing the monthly staff newsletter, preparing and updating forms, staff phone list, staff photos, and assisting with other admin activities and special projects. Ensures all new employees are added to contact lists, websites, and directories. Ensures the effective operation of the Faculty Support Office's daily operations: Greets visitors to the Faculty Support Office; Communicates regularly with faculty, deans, guests, and judges; Manages mail delivery to Adjunct Faculty. Monitors, updates, and maintains all designated bulletin boards, including ensuring faculty publication display cases and room signage are current. Ensures that all notices, materials, and announcements are up to date and displayed in an aesthetically pleasing manner. Provides back-up support to other staff for travel authorizations and Canvas course entry. Assists with exam administration each semester and orders lunches for exam staff. Required to have both a travel and a purchasing card and to be fully trained on both. Must be familiar with CANVAS, OSCAR, and FEAS. Provides rosters, creates add/drop sheets, attendance and seating charts; tracks attendance for all classes and reports monthly to the Associate Dean of Student Affairs. May provide clerical assistance to faculty as requested/assigned. Qualifications High School diploma or equivalency and four years of experience, or a combination of post-high school education and experience equal to four years. Contact Info Janine Welch, College of Law Associate Dean for Administration jwelch@law.fsu.edu University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select \u201cyes\u201d to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for Veterans\u2019 Preference eligibility requirements and Veterans\u2019 Preference required documentation (PDF) , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63761&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Administrative Specialist (Finance & Administration - College of Medicine)", "description": "Administrative Specialist (Finance & Administration - College of Medicine) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63761 Location Hybrid Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department FSU College of Medicine - Administrative Services The Office of MED Administrative Services provides centralized administrative support, operational leadership, and expertise to the academic departments and programs within the Florida State University College of Medicine. Working collaboratively with faculty, staff, departmental leadership, and College and University administration, the office supports a broad range of functions, including recruitment and employment actions, faculty development and advancement, position description/salary change administration, personnel reporting, regulatory compliance, and organizational operations. Through consistent processes, data-informed decision-making, and a commitment to service excellence, MED Administrative Services promotes operational efficiency, accuracy, compliance, and alignment with the strategic priorities of the College and the University. Responsibilities Serve as a primary administrative resource for assigned departments, building effective working relationships and coordinating faculty and staff employment processes. Processes, tracks, and documents position and salary-related transactions including salary adjustments, position updates, incentives, sign-on bonuses, and other approved actions. Supports faculty development and advancement processes, including appointments, evaluations, promotion and tenure, reappointments, post-tenure reviews. Coordinates and tracks personnel transactions, including recruitment, hiring, onboarding, funding changes, and separations. Maintains and reconciles personnel records across University and College systems to ensure accuracy, compliance, and timely processing. Assist with FACET, Assignment of Responsibility (AOR), instructor funding, and other faculty and administrative reporting requirements. Supports process improvements, special projects, and the development of standardized administrative procedures. Collaborates with departments, College leadership, and University offices to resolve administrative issues and promote responsive, consistent service delivery. Qualifications A Bachelor's degree and two years of experience; or a high school diploma/equivalent and six years of experience. (Note: post-high school education can substitute for experience at the equivalent rate.) Preferred Qualifications Experience in human resources administration, employment processes, faculty development and advancement processes, or related administrative functions, preferably in higher education. Strong organizational, communication, interpersonal, and problem-solving skills, with a commitment to service excellence. Demonstrated ability to build and maintain effective working relationships, collaborate across departments, and support a variety of stakeholders. Experience maintaining, reviewing, and reconciling personnel or administrative data to ensure accuracy and compliance. Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications, particularly Excel, and experience with SharePoint or similar collaboration platforms. Demonstrated ability to manage competing priorities, meet deadlines, and maintain accuracy and attention to detail. Ability to exercise sound judgment, maintain confidentiality, and adapt to changing priorities in a collaborative environment. Helpful The FSU College of Medicine Administrative Services seeks a collaborative, detail-oriented, and service-focused Administrative Specialist to support faculty development and advancement processes, employment administration, reporting, compliance, and process improvement activities. This position works closely with departments and College leadership to coordinate administrative processes, interpret University policies, maintain records, and support the College's academic and administrative mission. Contact Info Selin S. Oliver | Program Director, MED Administrative Services University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Starting salary: Low to mid $40,000\u2019s, commensurate with education and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is based in Tallahassee, FL and is eligible for a hybrid work schedule. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63762&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Clinical Finance Director | Florida Medical Practice Plan, Inc.", "description": "Clinical Finance Director | Florida Medical Practice Plan, Inc. Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63762 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department FSU College of Medicine | Florida Medical Practice Plan 1115 W Call St Tallahassee, FL 32304 Responsibilities The Clinical Finance Director serves as the critical bridge between FSU MED Finance & Administration, FMPP Clinical Operations, and FSU MED/FMPP Executive Leadership by directing the financial planning and analysis functions to support the strategic objectives of Florida Medical Practice Plan, Inc. Financial Planning/Budgeting/Forecasting: Direct the financial planning and analysis function for FMPP, Inc. clinical operations. Develop annual operating budgets and periodic financial forecasts for multiple practices and service lines. Evaluate revenue, expenses, profitability, provider productivity, and practice performance Strategic Financial Analysis/Decision Support: Provide executive clinical financial leadership using financial modeling, business case analyses. ROI studies, etc. Prepare executive reports, dashboards, presentations, & performance analyses that support data-engaged leadership decision-making Operational & Practice Performance Analytics: Lead the collection, validation, and analysis of operational and financial data to evaluate KPIs. Identify financial risks, operational inefficiencies, and emerging trends while recommending corrective actions and opportunities for performance improvement. Data Management, Reporting Systems and Business Intelligence: Oversee the development and maintenance of reporting tools, databases, dashboards, etc. for FMPP clinical operations. Ensure the integrity, accuracy, and consistency of financial and operational data utilized throughout FMPP. Utilize business intelligence platforms and reporting technologies to improve access to actionable information. Operational Improvement & Financial Stewardship: Serve as the financial planning resource for multiple medical practices. Lead process improvement initiatives, reporting automation efforts, and workflow assessments to enhance efficiency. Support audits, financial reviews, and compliance with organizational financial policies and standards. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and six years of experience related to budget, financial and/or accounting services; or a high school diploma/equivalent and experience equal to ten years. (Note: post-high school education can substitute for experience at the equivalent rate.) Preferred Qualifications Familiarity with Epic Electronic Health Records software platform. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Salary is commensurate with experience and education. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63765&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Executive Director for Election Law Center (12 Month Salaried)", "description": "Executive Director for Election Law Center (12 Month Salaried) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63765 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department College of Law Responsibilities The Executive Director of the College of Law Election Law Center provides overall strategic, operational, and institutional leadership for the Center. The Executive Director is responsible for directing the Center\u2019s administrative operations, expanding public programming, leading legislative and state agency engagement, managing budget resources, supporting scholarly and policy research, and driving comprehensive student advising, mentorship, and career placement initiatives. Institutional Leadership & Operational Management Oversee day-to-day operations, strategic planning, budgeting, and personnel management for the Center, including recruitment and supervision of staff attorneys, research fellows, and student workers. Lead strategic outreach to local, state, and national stakeholders to establish the Center as a premier, non-partisan institutional authority on election administration and constitutional law. Maintain active collaborations with key policy entities, academic networks, and professional associations across the country. Legislative Engagement & Policy Leadership Drive legislative and governmental affairs efforts to secure recurring public funding and fulfill legislative mandates in election administration. Work closely with university administration, legislative leaders, committee staff, and state agency officials to position the Center as a credible resource for lawmakers and policymakers. Direct specialized policy research initiatives, including the development of model statutes, statutory analysis, and legislative background reviews. Conferences, Teleforums & Public Programming Concept, fundraise for, and execute high-profile national conferences, symposia, and academic panels convening prominent judges, senior litigators, public officials, legal scholars, and journalists. Organize timely virtual programming, teleforums, and post-oral argument briefings covering major U.S. Supreme Court and state court election law cases. Serve as an institutional liaison to media outlets and legal reporters, facilitating commentary and expert references on election law and governance topics. Student Advising, Mentorship & Experiential Learning Provide individualized career counseling and mentorship to law students pursuing careers in election law, state government, litigation, and public policy. Serve as faculty advisor to legal student organizations, providing guidance on speaker recruitment, event execution, and leadership development. Cultivate and expand competitive internship, fellowship, and externship placements with key executive branch agencies, state election commissions, and private practice firms. Facilitate experiential learning opportunities by coordinating student involvement in high-level appellate research, amicus brief preparation, and major academic events. Engage with prospective, accepted, and alumni communities through specialized events, receptions, and targeted outreach. Qualifications A J.D. from an accredited law school is required. Minimum of 5\u20137 years of professional experience in election law, public policy, state government affairs, higher education administration, or appellate legal practice. Demonstrated track record of successful strategic leadership, stakeholder engagement, legislative advocacy, and event management. Preferred Qualifications Required Skills Strong leadership, managerial, and organizational abilities to direct complex projects under firm deadlines. Proven capacity to cultivate strategic relationships with government officials, university leadership, legal scholars, and donors. Exceptional written and oral communication skills for diverse audiences (academic, legal, media, and public). Demonstrated commitment to non-partisan, objective, and rigorous academic research and public service. Experience in student mentorship, career counseling, or law school student organization advising Contact Info Donna Chandler FSU College of Law HR Representative dchandler@law.fsu.edu 850-644-1063 University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Anticipated salary range: $140,000\u2013$165,000, negotiable depending on experience. This is a soft-money funded position, with renewal based on available funds and the needs of the College of Law and the University. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63763&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "OPS Administrative Assistant", "description": "OPS Administrative Assistant Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63763 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Dedman College of Hospitality Responsibilities The Administrative Assistant provides essential support to the Dedman College of Hospitality. Greet and assist visitors, students, faculty, and staff in a professional and welcoming manner, including validating parking for Dedman guests. Maintain, organize, and restock office supplies and ensure common areas remain clean, organized, and presentable. Coordinate and manage room reservations and scheduling requests. Receive, sort, and distribute incoming mail. Monitor and maintain office supply inventory, ensuring supplies are adequately stocked. Perform other related duties as assigned. Qualifications A high school diploma or equivalent. Ability to work effectively in a professional office setting. Excellent customer service and communication skills. Strong organizational and time management skills. Ability to work independently and as a part of a team. Proficiency in basic computer skills. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an OPS/temporary job. This is a part-time position requiring coverage on Tuesdays. Additional hours may be available Monday-Friday, between 8:00 AM and 5:00 PM, based on departmental needs and the availability of additional opportunities. Based on the duties, this position may require completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63764&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Program Associate - Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering Department", "description": "Program Associate - Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering Department Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63764 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Responsibilities Prepares & reviews correspondence, creates and formats presentation slides, and handouts for the Chair. Assists Chair in soliciting references and recommendation letters for employment, faculty promotions, tenure, and various awards. Drafts and distributes meeting agendas in advance, ensuring all relevant topics are included. Takes meeting minutes and ensures compliance with required specificity. Coordinates and schedules meetings and conference rooms. Proactively manages scheduling conflicts and prioritizes meetings based on the leadership\u2019s needs. Coordinates travel for Chair and Chair-led visits and assists the departmental travel rep with faculty/staff/student travel. Maintains front desk area, ensuring visitors have a positive experience. Greets visitors and answers phones, directing inquiries to the appropriate staff. Oversees and guides individuals tasked with front desk duties including OPS, student, or FWS workers. Assigns tasks, provides training and support, and ensures that front desk operations run smoothly and efficiently. Monitors office supply inventory, ensuring that it is stocked by preparing Spearmart carts for the departmental purchasing representative. Handles incoming and outgoing mail and packages. Submits work order requests and coordinates with Facilities. Requests keys and card swipe access. Assists Property Manager and Property Custodian with property inventory. Serves as the departmental Time and Leave Coordinator within FAMU and FSU systems. Coordinates time entry and approvals for staff and OPS, communicates discrepancies to the appropriate supervisor. Reviews biweekly payroll cost center reports, communicates concerns to the departmental Program Manager, and ensures retention of approved Payroll Certifications. Coordinates with the College of Engineering Dean\u2019s Office Central HR to ensure international hires and employees obtain and maintain work authorization and may begin work. Responsible for records retention, including faculty annual reviews, meeting minutes, and other departmental records, both physical and electronic. Responsible for records disposal in compliance with state and university. Records Retention Schedules. Ensures proper placement of employment posters Serves as FACET representative, distributing and ensuring FACET reports are completed in coordination with the COE HR team. Submits request to the College of Engineering Dean\u2019s Office for recruitment, job offers, reappointments and personnel actions, and monitors the progress of requested actions. Assists faculty with P&T binder submission and deadlines. Coordinates gathering, submitting, and approval of AOR\u2019s with Chair and faculty members. Assists with departmental events and special projects. Backup P Card Proxy for departmental Program Manager and travel/purchasing representative. Other office administrative duties as assigned. Qualifications High School diploma or equivalency and four years experience or a combination of post high school education and experience equal to four year University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select \u201cyes\u201d to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for Veterans\u2019 Preference eligibility requirements and Veterans\u2019 Preference required documentation (PDF) , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63689&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Program Associate - UBA/Center for Academic Retention & Enhancement (CARE)", "description": "Program Associate - UBA/Center for Academic Retention & Enhancement (CARE) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63689 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department University Business Administrators - Division of Undergraduate Studies - Center for Academic Retention & Enhancement (CARE) Responsibilities Responsible for performing administrative professional support services to the Center for Academic Retention & Enhancement (CARE). This includes administrative, operational, and fiscal activities with a focus on the Student Support Services (SSS), and local grant programs. Responsible for financial activities and administrative functions for CARE. Processes and reviews P-Card, Procurement, Scholarship, and Travel transactions. Serves as the primary fiscal support for the Student Support Services (SSS), and local grant programs. Ensures transactions are processed accurately, timely, and in compliance with University, State, and Federal policies and procedures. Serves as a P-Card proxy and as a backup for designated financial functions within the Division of Undergraduate Studies (UGS). Coordinates administrative functions related to CARE facilities and shared resources. Serves as the Property Custodian for CARE and the primary point of contact for room reservations and scheduling and manages reservations for department vans and golf carts. Assists program managers and coordinators with project and grant administrative needs related to CARE programs. Monitors grant expenditures and fund availability in accordance with reports provided by the Division of Undergraduate Studies (UGS) Business Manager, and assists with purchasing, travel, and other financial transactions associated with grant-funded activities. Provides administrative support for grant-related reporting, tracking, and compliance requirements. Provides departmental HR transactional support in coordination with the CARE HR Dept Rep and appropriate University HR offices. Assists with onboarding, required documentation, routine HR transactions, personnel actions, and grant participant stipends. Provides administrative support to CARE leadership, faculty, staff, and program personnel. Coordinates meetings, maintains records and calendars, prepares documents and correspondence, and supports department events, special projects, and operational initiatives. Assists with general office administration and coordinates with University offices and internal/external partners as needed. Qualifications High school diploma or equivalency and four years experience or a combination of post high school education and experience equal to four years. Preferred Qualifications The ideal candidate should possess the following skills and/or experience. Ability to communicate effectively with different groups and/or individuals verbally or in writing and in a calm, confident manner with complete objectivity. Experience with using the OMNI system, Microsoft Office applications, and Zoom. Experience handling multiple work assignments simultaneously and prioritizing based on departmental need. Ability to interpret and explain policies, procedures, goals, and objectives to students, parents, faculty, and staff. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with students, parents, supervisors, and interdepartmental personnel. Attention to detail with a high standard of integrity. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select \u201cyes\u201d to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for Veterans\u2019 Preference eligibility requirements and Veterans\u2019 Preference required documentation (PDF) , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63739&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Assistant Dean/Director, Office of Accessibility Services", "description": "Assistant Dean/Director, Office of Accessibility Services Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63739 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Student Support & Transition Office of Accessibility Services 874 Traditions Way, Suite 108 Student Services Bldg Tallahassee, Fl 32304 (850) 644-9566 oas@fsu.edu Responsibilities Oversee the implementation and development of initiatives and programs for students. Research and assist with the development of corresponding policies and procedures relating to the provision of accommodations, ADA/ADAAA compliance, academic testing procedures, and current and innovative technologies. Advises and trains University departments on accessibility issues. Promotes and monitors compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act, the Americans with Disabilities Amendments Act and the Rehabilitation Act of 1973 as amended. Communicates program services and maintains a high level of contact with students, faculty, staff, and internal/external University constituents. Attends corresponding community and state meetings. Directly oversees the Office of Accessibility Services Main Office which include the OAS Testing Center and the OAS Assistive Technology Center. Provides departmental direction and resolves issues that arise within the department. Identifies and evaluates departmental personnel issues, staffing needs, structure, and facility and space needs. Supervises and directs the work of USPS, A&P, and OPS employees and completes performance evaluations as required. Manages and monitors OAS budgets. Researches, secures, and administers program funding from local, state, and federal sources. Disperses and reports expenditures. Collaborates with campus partners to seek and secure outside funding sources. Works in conjunction with the Department of Student Support & Transitions to promote campus resources. Reviews documentation and collaborates with students to develop an academic accommodation plan. Assists in planning, developing and implementing services for students with all types of disabling conditions including learning, ADHD, mental health, medical, mobility, hearing, visual, and others. Serves as a liaison between faculty and students. Keeps current and detailed case notes within the OAS student data management system. Dean on Duty responsibilities on a rotational basis. Each Assistant and Associate Dean of Students is required to serve as the \"Dean on Duty\". During this time, the employee is responsible for managing all after hours crisis management situations, and triage emergency situations requiring a response from student affairs. These responses include acting independently and representing student affairs and, in some cases the entire University during very sensitive crisis situations. Maintains various scholarship resources offered through the OAS. Coordinates promotion, application process, chairs the scholarship committee and prepares required reports. Serves as the ADA Coordinator for Students. Investigates student grievances related to the ADA and advises University administration on application of federal law and emerging cases specifically related to provision of accommodations, testing center environments, and compliance with implementation technology. Coordinates University student accommodations (including academic, housing, dietary, and transportation) including the development, implementation, and monitoring of appropriate policies, procedures and practices to ensure compliance with the Americans with Disability Act, the Americans with Disabilities Amendments Qualifications Bachelor's degree in counseling or related field and four years' experience. Preferred Qualifications Master's degree preferred Contact Info Shelley Ducatt Student Support & Transition Office of Accessibility Services 874 Traditions Way, Suite 108 Student Services Bldg Tallahassee, Fl 32304 (850) 644-9566 oas@fsu.edu University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Anticipated salary will be between $74, 390 - $94,174, commensurate with education and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is open until filled Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=61635&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Carpenter (Open Rank Level)", "description": "Carpenter (Open Rank Level) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 61635 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Facilities - Maintenance Responsibilities Builds, erects, installs, and repairs forms, structures, and other fixtures made from wood and other materials as needed to assist with various types of construction projects. Installs and/or repairs kitchen cabinets, vanities, and shelving units along with other general carpentry duties. Repairs furniture tables, chairs, etc. Repairs and/or installs new doors and hardware. Utilizes various hand and power tools to securely build assigned projects. Assists other trades as needed, such as locksmiths, plasterers, and painters. Operates vehicles to carry supplies and travel campus wide to perform various skilled maintenance. Loads and unloads necessary equipment and materials. Review plans and work orders to ensure the correct completion of the scope of work. Documents work performed and orders materials on appropriate departmental forms. Follows established safety rules and regulations and maintains a safe and clean environment. Moves necessary materials around job site. Cleans up work site debris. Responsible for security, safety, and maintenance of all equipment, supplies, and vehicles. Maintains tools and equipment, ensuring all hand and power tools are in proper working condition, and reports maintenance problems to the supervisor. Organizes and cleans assigned shop areas. Prepares requests for materials and supplies. Performs additional maintenance and supervises helpers as required to include minor plaster, sheet rock repairs, and replacement of floor tiles, ceramic tiles, and damaged carpet campus wide. Qualifications High school diploma or equivalent and two years' experience, or a relevant Technical or vocational degree may substitute for experience. A valid State of Florida or Georgia Driver\u2019s License or the ability to obtain upon hire. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our interactive too l to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://jobs.fsu.edu. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select \u201cyes\u201d to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for eligibility information and required documentation , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . The work schedule is 8a to 4:30p with a 30-minute break. This position is being re-advertised. Previous applicants need not apply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63757&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Educational Talent Search - Assistant Director (Panama City Campus)", "description": "Educational Talent Search - Assistant Director (Panama City Campus) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63757 Location Panama City, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department PCC Sponsored Programs Florida State University is one of the nation\u2019s top public universities, and FSU Panama City amplifies the university\u2019s efforts to preserve, expand, and disseminate knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and human services professions. FSU Panama City is located 100 miles west of Tallahassee on the beautiful North St. Andrews Bay, and is only three miles from the beaches of the Emerald Coast. FSU PC currently houses 20 bachelor's programs, 9 master's programs, and 1 doctoral program, and boasts a small faculty-to-student ratio, which gives students a more personalized academic experience. Please visit https://pc.fsu.edu/promise for information about our FSU PC Promise to students and https://pc.fsu.edu/ for more information about our campus. FSU Panama City also recently opened a brand-new residential housing complex on campus, right on the water. This new apartment-style complex at FSU PC houses both undergraduate and graduate students. For more information about our on-campus housing, visit https://seminolelandingfsu.com/ . Responsibilities Student Recruitment, Services, Advising, and Data Management: Oversees and participates in the recruitment of pre-collegiate students to enhance academic enrichment and improve access to postsecondary opportunities for targeted middle and high school students. This includes organizing, implementing, and monitoring individual and group activities and services. Mentors and advises program participants regarding educational planning, career development, postsecondary pathways, and understanding federal financial aid. Additionally, monitors and maintains the electronic student database (BLUMEN) to ensure data integrity, accurate documentation of participant services, and timely updates. The Assistant Director will also assist in the progress monitoring of objectives directly tied to high school seniors. Participant Assessment, Progress Monitoring, and School Collaboration: Assesses the academic and personal needs of Talent Search participants to support achievement of Educational Talent Search (ETS) program objectives. Maintains and reviews student data in preparation for the Annual Performance Report (APR) through transcript evaluations, student interviews, academic progress monitoring, and regular participant check-ins. Collaborates with key personnel at target schools to develop and implement service plans responsive to participant needs while monitoring progress toward high school graduation and college readiness. This includes reviewing completion of college preparatory coursework and monitoring the submission of college admissions, financial aid, and scholarship applications. Responsible for Program Leadership, Staff Support, and Program Coordination: assists the TRIO ETS Director in the overall coordination and implementation of program services and objectives. Supervises and supports TRIO Talent Search staff in daily operations, program planning, service delivery, professional development, federal TRIO training, and team meetings. The Assistant Director serves as a key member of the senior leadership team and helps ensure consistent, high-quality programming across all service areas. Assists in developing and maintaining partnerships throughout the University in order to obtain Talent Search goals. Assists with grant-related administrative responsibilities, such as monitoring program activities and deliverables, supporting compliance, reviewing program data, assisting with federal reporting, and ensuring services are implemented in accordance with grant objectives. Responsibilities also include coordinating educational enrichment activities and program events, assisting with supervising and transporting program participants during approved activities, and performing other duties necessary to support program goals and objectives. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and four years experience related to academic and/or student services or a combination of post high school education and experience equal to eight years in the same. A valid State of Florida or Georgia Driver\u2019s License or the ability to obtain prior to hire. Preferred Qualifications Prior experience working with high school students. Prior experience supervising a team. Helpful The Assistant Director supports the implementation and delivery of Florida State University Panama City\u2019s TRIO Educational Talent Search (ETS) Program across eight designated target counties. The position requires regular travel to participating middle and high schools throughout Bay County and the surrounding areas to provide academic guidance, college and career-readiness services, and post-secondary planning support. The Assistant Director collaborates with students, families, school personnel, community partners, and program staff to promote academic success, high school graduation, and postsecondary enrollment among TRIO-eligible students. Responsibilities include monitoring participant progress, tracking high school seniors, and documenting postsecondary enrollment outcomes to support program objectives and federal reporting requirements. This position requires flexibility including attending monthly staff meetings, quarterly professional-development at FSU PC and FSU, work occasional evenings, weekends, as well as overnight, and out of area travel, to support program activities including, college visits, educational enrichment activities, professional development, student workshops, and other approved program events. Contact Info Melinda Jones University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Starting at $51,500, commensurate with education and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check , including a fingerprint-based screening via AHCA\u2019s Clearinghouse pursuant to Section 1012, Florida Statutes, for positions in a FSU Developmental Research School or Section 409.175, Florida Statutes, for positions in a Childcare or Summer Camp position. Visit the AHCA Clearinghouse Screenings webpage for more information. This position requires occasional travel to Tallahassee, FL. This position will begin in late Fall 2026. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63751&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Educational Talent Search, Program Associate (Tallahassee, FL)", "description": "Educational Talent Search, Program Associate (Tallahassee, FL) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63751 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department PCC Sponsored Programs Florida State University is one of the nation\u2019s top public universities, and FSU Panama City amplifies the university\u2019s efforts to preserve, expand, and disseminate knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and human services professions. FSU Panama City is located 100 miles west of Tallahassee on the beautiful North St. Andrews Bay, and is only three miles from the beaches of the Emerald Coast. FSU PC currently houses 20 bachelor's programs, 9 master's programs, and 1 doctoral program, and boasts a small faculty-to-student ratio, which gives students a more personalized academic experience. Please visit https://pc.fsu.edu/promise for information about our FSU PC Promise to students and https://pc.fsu.edu/ for more information about our campus. FSU Panama City also recently opened a brand-new residential housing complex on campus, right on the water. This new apartment-style complex at FSU PC houses both undergraduate and graduate students. For more information about our on-campus housing, visit https://seminolelandingfsu.com/ . Responsibilities Participant Records, Data & Program Compliance: Maintain participant files and databases; enter and verify demographic, eligibility, participation, academic, and service data; assist with documentation for the Annual Performance Report (APR); track missing records and forms; maintain confidentiality; and support accurate documentation of project services and outcomes. Recruitment, Enrollment & Participant Support: Assist coordinators with recruitment and outreach; process applications and eligibility documentation; communicate with students, families, and school partners; maintain recruitment and participation rosters; and support follow-up efforts to help the program meet funded participant targets. Assists with the planning, coordination, and implementation of Talent Search activities, including workshops, tutoring, and academic enrichment activities, college and career exploration, campus visits, enrichment experiences, and summer programming. Coordinates program logistics, including participant registration, permission forms, transportation arrangements, meals, program materials, and activity schedules. Helps communicate transportation schedules and other program information to students, families, schools, staff, and approved transportation providers. Provides on-site support for programming activities and helps maintain required participation and activity documentation. Communications & General Program Administration: Maintain calendars and program communications; prepare correspondence, reports, meeting materials, and program documents; assist with purchasing and supply tracking as assigned; participate in staff meetings and training; and perform other duties that support achievement of Talent Search objectives. Qualifications A high school diploma or equivalent and four years of experience. (Note: post high-school education and/or experience may substitute at a comparable rate.) A valid State of Florida or Georgia Driver\u2019s License or the ability to obtain prior to hire. Preferred Qualifications Prior experience working with high school students. Helpful The ETS Program Associate will provide administrative, operational, and programmatic support for the Federal TRIO Educational Talent Search (ETS) program by supporting the effective delivery of services to eligible middle and high school students by assisting with student recruitment and enrollment, maintaining accurate participant records, coordinating program activities and communications, and supporting data collection and documentation required for federal reporting and performance tracking. The program assistant may be required to collaborate with community partners to increase program awareness across the 8 target areas. The program associate may be required to work occasional evenings, weekends, some overnight, and out-of-area travel to support program activities, college visits, educational enrichment experiences, professional development, and other approved program events. Contact Info Melinda Jones University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Starting at $36,250, commensurate with education and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select \u201cyes\u201d to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for Veterans\u2019 Preference eligibility requirements and Veterans\u2019 Preference required documentation (PDF) , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check , including a fingerprint-based screening via AHCA\u2019s Clearinghouse pursuant to Section 1012, Florida Statutes, for positions in a FSU Developmental Research School or Section 409.175, Florida Statutes, for positions in a Childcare or Summer Camp position. Visit the AHCA Clearinghouse Screenings webpage for more information. This position will be primarily located in Tallahassee, FL and requires occasional travel to Panama City, FL. The position will begin in late Fall 2026. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63758&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Educational Talent Search, Student Program Coordinator (Gadsden County)", "description": "Educational Talent Search, Student Program Coordinator (Gadsden County) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63758 Location Quincy, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department PCC Sponsored Programs Florida State University is one of the nation\u2019s top public universities, and FSU Panama City amplifies the university\u2019s efforts to preserve, expand, and disseminate knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and human services professions. FSU Panama City is located 100 miles west of Tallahassee on the beautiful North St. Andrews Bay, and is only three miles from the beaches of the Emerald Coast. FSU PC currently houses 20 bachelor's programs, 9 master's programs, and 1 doctoral program, and boasts a small faculty-to-student ratio, which gives students a more personalized academic experience. Please visit https://pc.fsu.edu/promise for information about our FSU PC Promise to students and https://pc.fsu.edu/ for more information about our campus. FSU Panama City also recently opened a brand-new residential housing complex on campus, right on the water. This new apartment-style complex at FSU PC houses both undergraduate and graduate students. For more information about our on-campus housing, visit https://seminolelandingfsu.com/ . Responsibilities Oversees recruitment and provides direct services to program participants in alignment with federal TRIO Educational Talent Search (ETS) objectives. Provides middle and high school participants with academic enrichment, tutoring, mentoring, career exploration, college and post-secondary planning, financial aid information, and other college-readiness services through individual and group advising, workshops, student check-ins, and school-based events. Maintains regular communication with participants to encourage engagement and participation in program services. Plans, coordinates, and implements activities that support ETS program objectives, including academic and career workshops, test preparation, community service initiatives, college and career exposure, campus visits, and other educational enrichment experiences that promote high school completion and preparation for college, career, or trade/technical education. Participates in federal TRIO training and professional development provided by the university, department, and other approved organizations. Evaluates participants' academic and educational needs through transcript reviews, student check-ins, and collaboration with teachers, counselors, families, and other school personnel. Monitors participants\u2019 progress toward high school graduation and postsecondary readiness, including completion of college-preparatory coursework and applications for college admissions, financial aid, and scholarships. Collaborates with target school personnel and community partners to connect students and families with appropriate resources and provides guidance on college costs and financial aid. Responsibilities also include assisting with supervising and transporting program participants during approved program activities and performing other duties necessary to support program goals and objectives. Qualifications A Bachelor's degree and two years of experience; or a high school diploma or equivalent and six years of experience. (Note: a combination of post high school education and experience equal to six years.) A valid State of Florida or Georgia Driver\u2019s License or the ability to obtain prior to hire. Preferred Qualifications Prior experience working with high school students. Helpful The student program coordinator will travel to middle and high schools within the Gadsden County region to provide academic support to students. The coordinator will work with students, families, school personnel, community partners, and program staff to increase the number of TRIO-eligible students who graduate from high school and pursue postsecondary education. The coordinator will be required to attend monthly staff meetings and quarterly professional-development at FSU PC and FSU, work occasional evenings, weekends, some overnight, and out-of-area travel to support program activities, college visits, educational enrichment experiences, professional development, and other approved program events. Contact Info Melinda Jones University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Starting at $44,056, commensurate with education and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check , including a fingerprint-based screening via AHCA\u2019s Clearinghouse pursuant to Section 1012, Florida Statutes, for positions in a FSU Developmental Research School or Section 409.175, Florida Statutes, for positions in a Childcare or Summer Camp position. Visit the AHCA Clearinghouse Screenings webpage for more information. This position will be primarily located in Gadsden County and requires occasional travel to Panama City, FL and Tallahassee, FL. This position will begin in late Fall 2026. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63752&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Educational Talent Search, Student Program Coordinator - Gulf County", "description": "Educational Talent Search, Student Program Coordinator - Gulf County Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63752 Location Panama City, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favor