 both undergraduate and graduate students. For more information about our on-campus housing, visit https://seminolelandingfsu.com/ . Responsibilities Oversees recruitment and provides direct services to program participants in alignment with federal TRIO Educational Talent Search (ETS) objectives. Provides middle and high school participants with academic enrichment, tutoring, mentoring, career exploration, college and post-secondary planning, financial aid information, and other college-readiness services through individual and group advising, workshops, student check-ins, and school-based events. Maintains regular communication with participants to encourage engagement and participation in program services. Plans, coordinates, and implements activities that support ETS program objectives, including academic and career workshops, test preparation, community service initiatives, college and career exposure, campus visits, and other educational enrichment experiences that promote high school completion and preparation for college, career, or trade/technical education. Participates in federal TRIO training and professional development provided by the university, department, and other approved organizations. Evaluates participants' academic and educational needs through transcript reviews, student check-ins, and collaboration with teachers, counselors, families, and other school personnel. Monitors participants\u2019 progress toward high school graduation and postsecondary readiness, including completion of college-preparatory coursework and applications for college admissions, financial aid, and scholarships. Collaborates with target school personnel and community partners to connect students and families with appropriate resources and provides guidance on college costs and financial aid. Responsibilities also include assisting with supervising and transporting program participants during approved program activities and performing other duties necessary to support program goals and objectives. Qualifications A Bachelor's degree and two years of experience; or a high school diploma or equivalent and six years of experience. (Note: a combination of post high school education and experience equal to six years.) A valid State of Florida or Georgia Driver\u2019s License or the ability to obtain prior to hire. Preferred Qualifications Starting at $44,056, commensurate with education and experience. Helpful The student program coordinator will travel to middle and high schools within the Panhandle region, including Calhoun, Washington, Liberty, and Holmes counties, to provide academic support to students. The coordinator will work with students, families, school personnel, community partners, and program staff to increase the number of TRIO-eligible students who graduate from high school and pursue postsecondary education. The program coordinator will also collaborate with other program staff to connect program participants to other learning opportunities in other target areas. The coordinator will be required to attend monthly staff meetings, and quarterly professional-development at FSU PC and FSU, work occasional evenings, weekends, some overnight, and out-of-area travel to support program activities, college visits, educational enrichment experiences, professional development, and other approved program events. Contact Info Melinda Jones University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check , including a fingerprint-based screening via AHCA\u2019s Clearinghouse pursuant to Section 1012, Florida Statutes, for positions in a FSU Developmental Research School or Section 409.175, Florida Statutes, for positions in a Childcare or Summer Camp position. Visit the AHCA Clearinghouse Screenings webpage for more information. This position will be primarily located in the Panhandle Region and requires occasional travel to Panama City, FL and Tallahassee, FL. This position will begin in late Fall 2026. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63301&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "IT Support Specialist", "description": "IT Support Specialist Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63301 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department This position is within FSU\u2019s D epartment of Information Technology Services (ITS) This position will be located at the National High Magnetic Field Laboratory (NHMFL) . The NHMFL is the largest and highest-powered magnet laboratory in the world and is the only facility of its kind in the United States. The Computer Support Group (CSG) supports all aspects of IT at the Lab. Responsibilities This position provides specialized, scientific IT support to faculty and staff of the NHMFL. Set up and install various makes and models of networked servers, workstations, desktops, and laptop computers running different versions of Microsoft Windows and MacOS. Maintain Windows operating system imaging server for common desktop and laptop computers. Maintain SimpleMDM for Mac computers and tablets. Install and maintain networked printers, scanners and computer-connected scientific equipment. Create and administer user accounts for Microsoft Windows Active Directory and 0365 email services. Provide end user instruction in the use of various computer, tablet and mobile device operating systems and software applications, audio-visual equipment, and video-conferencing systems. Assist staff with computer hardware and software purchasing decisions and provide quotes. Work with NHMFL Cybersecurity expert on developing processes & procedures for CSG and NHMFL staff. Provide after-hours onsite support for mission-critical Microsoft Windows and Mac operations as needed. Qualifications Bachelor's degree or a high school diploma or equivalent and four years of experience. (Note: or a combination of post high school education and experience equal to four years.) Preferred Qualifications Experience in Microsoft Active Directory use is preferred. Microsoft Azure is a plus. Helpful A strong candidate would be someone with hands-on experience managing a Windows and macOS environment, Active Directory, and enterprise endpoint management. They should possess strong troubleshooting skills, a solid understanding of cybersecurity best practices, and experience supporting an IT infrastructure in a professional environment. The ideal candidate is customer-service oriented, communicates effectively with both technical and non-technical users, and can work independently while managing multiple priorities. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . After-hours onsite support as needed This position is being re-advertised. Previous applicants need not apply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63756&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Motor Pool Associate", "description": "Motor Pool Associate Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63756 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department FSU Facilities Waste Management Responsibilities Provides transportation and logistical support for Facilities fleet operations by moving vehicles, equipment, parts, and personnel to and from campus and off-campus locations. Coordinates vehicle pickups and deliveries to vendors, repair facilities, body shops, dealerships, and other service providers. Assists with locating, ordering, receiving, and procuring parts, supplies, tools, and equipment required for fleet maintenance activities. Communicates with vendors regarding pricing, availability, delivery schedules, and order status to ensure timely acquisition of materials necessary to maintain fleet operations. Operates university vehicles safely and performs basic vehicle condition inspections, reporting maintenance needs, operational deficiencies, safety concerns, vehicle damage, and unsafe conditions to appropriate personnel. Utilizes appropriate personal protective equipment (PPE) and follows established safety procedures while performing assigned duties. Provides administrative support for Motor Pool operations through the maintenance of records, processing of paperwork, and organization of fleet-related documentation. Assists with the preparation and processing of purchase orders, invoices, receiving documentation, and other financial transactions in accordance with university procedures. Utilizes university procurement systems and purchasing methods, including PCard transactions, to obtain parts, supplies, and operational materials. Maintains accurate procurement, maintenance, and fleet records to support operational accountability and compliance requirements. Assists in making recommendations on office operational needs to include equipment, workflow, and materials. Participates in required training, professional development activities, and administrative processes necessary to support departmental operations and compliance requirements. Supports Facilities' emergency response activities during weather events, disasters, utility interruptions, and other operational emergencies. Assists with coordinating and deploying fleet vehicles and equipment needed to support emergency operations and continuity of services. Carries out emergency assignments and special projects as directed by leadership and assists with the annual inventory, verification, and accountability of Facilities fleet vehicles and equipment. Performs additional duties in support of Facilities operations, emergency management activities, and departmental objectives as assigned. Assists supervisors and departmental leadership with fleet tracking, asset management, and vehicle utilization activities. Updates and maintains vehicle records, databases, maintenance schedules, registrations, inspections, and reporting systems. Supports vehicle lifecycle management by maintaining accurate information related to fleet assets and preparing reports used to monitor fleet performance, maintenance compliance, utilization, and operational readiness. Ensures records are maintained in accordance with university policies, fleet management requirements, and departmental procedures. Assists the Motor Pool Superintendent with tracking vehicles assigned to outside vendors for maintenance, warranty work, body repairs, and other services. Communicates with vendors regarding repair schedules, work progress, completion dates, and vehicle availability. Supports the intake, inspection, documentation, and processing of vehicles scheduled for maintenance and repair services. Ensures appropriate records and supporting documentation are maintained for outsourced repairs and vendor-provided services. Adheres to all Florida State University, Facilities, departmental, state, federal, and OSHA safety policies and procedures. Promotes a culture of safety and accountability by identifying and reporting hazards, supporting safe work practices, and ensuring compliance with applicable regulations and operational standards. Qualifications High school diploma or equivalency and four years experience or a combination of post high school education and experience equal to four years. A valid Florida or Georgia driver's license or the ability to obtain one prior to hire. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select \u201cyes\u201d to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for Veterans\u2019 Preference eligibility requirements and Veterans\u2019 Preference required documentation (PDF) , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63760&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Program Associate (Panama City Campus)", "description": "Program Associate (Panama City Campus) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63760 Location Panama City, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department PCC Finance & Administration Florida State University is one of the nation\u2019s top public universities, and FSU Panama City amplifies the university\u2019s efforts to preserve, expand, and disseminate knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and human services professions. FSU Panama City is located 100 miles west of Tallahassee on the beautiful North St. Andrews Bay and is only three miles from the beaches of the Emerald Coast. FSU PC currently houses 20 bachelor's programs, 9 master's programs, and 1 doctoral program, and boasts a small faculty-to-student ratio, which gives students a more personalized academic experience. Please visit https://pc.fsu.edu/promise for information about our FSU PC Promise to students and https://pc.fsu.edu/ for more information about our campus. FSU Panama City also recently opened a brand new, residential housing complex on campus and right on the water. This new apartment-style complex at FSU PC houses both undergraduate and graduate students. For more information about our on-campus housing, visit https://seminolelandingfsu.com/ . Responsibilities Supports PCC Finance & Administration, Police & Public Safety, and Facilities, Operations, and Maintenance. Enters facility-use requests and work orders; runs request and biweekly event-schedule queries; formats reports for the Director of F&A, Facility Use Coordinator, Maintenance Supervisor, and Switchboard. Manages the parking permit program. Enters requisitions as backup for Facilities, Operations, and Maintenance, and Police & Public Safety. Processes monthly P-Card reconciliations, certification reports, and department ledger reconciliations. Backs up card access, key requests, and deposit slips. Backs up travel for interviewees, guests, and employees: obtains Dean/Associate Dean approval, enters requests, books reservations, communicates policies and details, and submits expense reports. Processes contracts for departments; drafts contracts as needed. Coordinates and leads Panama City Campus training on contracts and travel. Backs up the campus Switchboard and Mail Center; assists with the Schedule of Classes; maintains flyers in elevators and on bulletin boards; represents F&A at SGC meetings and briefs the Director on relevant issues. Performs other duties as needed. Assists campus departments and maintains cross-training to cover absences or workflow surges. Supports payroll by reviewing timecards and verifying cost center reports. Qualifications A high school diploma or equivalent and four years of experience. (Note: post high-school education and/or experience may substitute at a comparable rate.) Preferred Qualifications Ability to establish effective working relationships with various departments in order to provide accurate documentation. Effective customer service skills are a must. Ability to prioritize tasks and meet deadlines. Strong attention to detail to ensure invoices, procurement-cards, and travel are processed correctly and on time. Ability to multitask. Helpful During the first two months, the Program Associate will receive structured, hands-on training to build familiarity with university policies and procedures. The selected candidate will work closely with their supervisor to: Participate in guided training sessions on university departments, purchasing, work orders, etc. Shadow experienced staff to learn daily workflows and deadlines. Gain an understanding of department responsibilities and requirements. Take on progressively more independent assignments with ongoing support and feedback. Establish strong working relationships with team members and campus partners. By the end of the first 60 days, the Program Associate is expected to be working independently with training as needed, being familiar with the campus departments, budgets, and policies and procedures, contributing independently to the department while continuing to develop advanced skills. Contact Info Jackie Brodie University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Starting at $36,250, commensurate with education and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select \u201cyes\u201d to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for Veterans\u2019 Preference eligibility requirements and Veterans\u2019 Preference required documentation (PDF) , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position will start in late Fall 2026. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63723&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Program Manager - The Graduate School", "description": "Program Manager - The Graduate School Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63723 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The Graduate School Responsibilities The program manager for the Graduate Student Resource Center (GSRC) is responsible for managing the administrative and programmatic functions of the GSRC travel grant program. Further, the program manager will lead marketing for academic and professional development programming to current FSU graduate students. The program manager will also assist the Director with the implementation of the Center\u2019s workshops and lead administrative support across the office. Manages the coordination of planning, and implementing for all GSRC marketing, media, and events, including the annual Graduate Student Resource Fair with GSRC staff and OPS staff. Liaises with other campus partners and supports campus partner events. Responsible for coordinating all GSRC event logistics, including room reservations, invitations, publicity, and materials preparation. Leads or assists in the creation of high-impact academic and professional development programming for doctoral student success. Leads or assists with colloquiums, workshops, or forums for graduate students. Works in close coordination with the GSRC\u2019s Director to lead the GSRC travel grant program. Reviews and evaluates travel grant materials, provides notice to recipients of travel grants, conducts budget reconciliation in consultation with the Associate Dean, assists in travel grant policy development, develops related publicity for the travel grant program. Assists the GSRC Director and Student Success Analyst in the development and administration of GRSC event feedback surveys. Collects and compiles data related to GSRC programs and services. Designs and writes the GSRC annual report and develops related charts and figures. Leads administrative operations, including clerical and facility duties, supplies/inventory, and assists in the supervision of OPS staff. Supports programmatic fundraising efforts. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and four years experience related to academic and/or student services or a combination of post high school education and experience equal to eight years in the same. Preferred Qualifications Ability to communicate effectively verbally and in writing. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships. Ability to perform basic mathematical calculations. Knowledge of and ability to interpret and apply related federal, state, and local laws, ordinances, rules and regulations. Knowledge of and ability to interpret and apply related University policies, procedures, principles, and practices. Knowledge of applicable computer applications and basic computer functions. Ability to maintain accurate records and retrieve files from active or archive sources. Basic filing practices; including numeric and alphabetic systems. Knowledge of office practices, procedures, and etiquette. Preferred Master's degree. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Mid to upper $40,000's, commensurate with education and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63753&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Real Time Crime Center Analyst", "description": "Real Time Crime Center Analyst Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63753 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Public Safety Responsibilities The Real Time Crime Center Analyst performs work receiving, abstracting, and summarizing data pertaining to criminal activities and involves the preparation of crime analysis information, criminal intelligence gathering, and real-time patrol support. Real-Time Crime Analysis specialization includes research, assembling, and presentation of information to provide investigative leads and functional patterns to be used as situational awareness in real time. Collect, evaluate, and summarize criminal intelligence data, determining its significance, completeness, and usefulness. Ensure the collection, integrity, accuracy, and timely updating of data from a variety of sources. Review daily bulletins (BOLOs, teletypes, etc.) and shift reports and maintain accurate records. Read and comprehend criminal justice laws, legal codes, court procedures, precedents, government regulations, executive orders, and agency policies and procedures. Analyze police data and provide strategic interpretation of information received through computer-aided dispatch (CAD), telephone, radio, and other communication systems. Request and receive confidential information, interpret maps to assist in locating geographic areas, and provide timely intelligence support during active calls for service and field operations. Communicate information clearly, concisely, and accurately. Adhere to the agency's core values and professionally represent the organization. Establish and maintain effective working relationships with partner agencies, organization members, and the public while providing professional customer service. Report to work reliably and on schedule, plan and coordinate work assignments, and communicate effectively both verbally and in writing. Perform all assigned duties safely and effectively without posing a direct threat to the health or safety of others in the workplace. Meet requirements and maintain required licensures and certifications, as well as successful completion of agency-required training. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and two years of experience related to criminal intelligence, crime analysis, or military intelligence, or similarly analytical in nature. Relevant experience can be substituted on a year-to-year basis for the required education. A valid State of Florida or Georgia Driver\u2019s License or the ability to obtain prior to hire. Contact Info Malia Brown - (850) 644-1239 University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select \u201cyes\u201d to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for Veterans\u2019 Preference eligibility requirements and Veterans\u2019 Preference required documentation (PDF) , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Real Time Crime Center Analysts work a 12-hour shift schedule that follows a rotating long-week/short-week format. Work hours may be adjusted during the training period. This position is located at the Real-Time Crime Center (RTCC) in Innovation Park. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63576&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Senior Administrative Specialist", "description": "Senior Administrative Specialist Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63576 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Dean\u2019s Office College of Criminology and Criminal Justice Responsibilities This is a professional position serving as a special assistant to the dean of the college. Responsible for managing the dean\u2019s office, coordinating meetings, communicating with university leadership, writing drafts, proofreading and editing documents, planning special events and other administrative functions. Assists the dean with development and fundraising. Serves as the subject matter expert for faculty administrative and HR matters. Assists with overall administrative matters. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and four years' experience or a high school diploma or equivalent and eight years of experience. (Note: or combination of post high school education and experience equal to eight years.) Preferred Qualifications Master\u2019s degree preferred, demonstrated ability to write, proofread, revise and make final edits for documents and/or presentations, FSU or other educational organizations work experience. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being re-advertised. Previous applicants need not apply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63748&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Social Sciences Librarian, 12 Month Salaried", "description": "Social Sciences Librarian, 12 Month Salaried Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63748 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Florida State University Libraries Responsibilities The Social Sciences Librarian serves as the library liaison for Public Administration & Policy, Political Science, and International Affairs providing research and instructional support to faculty and students. The position supports access to government publications, data, and information resources through FSU's participation in the Federal Depository Library Program and oversees the Libraries' government information collections and specialist staff. Working closely with fellow Social and Behavioral Sciences librarians and colleagues across the Libraries, the successful candidate will support research, teaching, and learning while contributing to the university's mission of research excellence and student success. Support Social Science Research Provide specialized research assistance and consultations involving social science research, government publications and data, legislative and regulatory materials, policy documents, and international information resources. Develop and assess social science collections in collaboration with other librarians to support research and teaching needs. Lead FSU Libraries' government documents program, overseeing federal depository and other government information collections, program compliance, and specialist staff. Advance Student Learning Design and deliver instructional sessions, workshops, and course-integrated instruction, including information literacy and AI literacy, in collaboration with fellow Social Science librarians. Develop and maintain instructional materials, research guides, tutorials, and other resources that support student learning and faculty research. Build Campus Partnerships Serve as the library liaison for Political Science, Public Administration & Policy, and International Affairs, including affiliated research centers and institutes. Develop and maintain relationships with faculty, students, and campus partners to promote library resources and services and support research and instructional needs. Contribute to Professional Excellence Engage in professional development, scholarship, and/or research appropriate to faculty rank and appointment. Participate in library and university committees, professional organizations, and service activities that support the Libraries' and university's missions. Perform other duties as assigned. Qualifications Master's degree from an ALA-accredited library and information science program; or master's degree in political science, public administration, international affairs, or a closely related social science field with relevant experience in academic libraries, research support, or government information services. Knowledge of the research practices, literature, and information sources in these disciplines, including government publications and data sources. Strong communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to provide research assistance, deliver instruction, and build collaborative relationships. Ability to coordinate projects, manage competing priorities, and work collaboratively with colleagues. Preferred Qualifications Three or more years of professional experience in an academic or research library, research support, or government information services, including providing research assistance, instruction, or liaison services. Experience with collection development or the management of specialized information resources. Experience using social science research databases, government data sources, or international statistical resources. Familiarity with the Federal Depository Library Program, government information classification systems, or government documents collection management. Knowledge of emerging trends and technologies relevant to academic librarianship, including information literacy, AI literacy, and scholarly communication. Demonstrated professional engagement through scholarship, presentations, professional organizations, or other contributions to the field. Experience supervising staff, coordinating workflows, or providing training and guidance to others. Helpful This position brings together social science librarianship and government information expertise, offering a varied portfolio of consultation, instruction, collection development, and program oversight. You will join a team of Social and Behavioral Sciences librarians while working with academic programs spanning public policy, political science, and international affairs. The role offers opportunities to apply your expertise across disciplines and support access to information for both the university and the broader community. Located within the Research & Learning Services division, this position offers an exciting opportunity to partner with faculty, graduate students, and undergraduates in the Askew School of Public Administration and Policy, the Department of Political Science, and the International Affairs Program (including Asian Studies, Latin American & Caribbean Studies, and Russian & East European Studies), along with their affiliated research centers and institutes within the College of Social Sciences and Public Policy. The position manages government information resources and expands access for the university and broader community. Contact Info Kyung Kim , Program Director for Social Sciences University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Starting at $60,000, commensurate with education and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63350&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Elevator Shop Manager", "description": "Elevator Shop Manager Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63350 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department FSU Facilities and Grounds Responsibilities Serves as a subject matter expert for vertical and horizontal transportation systems. Oversees compliance with Chapter 399, Florida Statutes, and Rule 61C-5, Florida Administrative Code. Serves as primary liaison with the Department of Business and Professional. Regulation (DBPR), Bureau of Elevator Safety. Provides direct supervision, leadership, and accountability for all Elevator Program support staff, including assigned coordinators, inspectors, and technical support personnel, ensuring effective day-to-day operations of the university elevator program. Manages campus-wide elevator maintenance control program including preventative maintenance, service interruptions, shutdowns, and return-to-service approvals. Responds to elevator entrapments and safety incidents, including after-hours emergencies. Maintains asset inventories, budgets, metrics, preventative maintenance records, and prepares reports for Facilities leadership. Coordinates inspections, permits, certificates of operation, corrective actions, and accident reporting. Oversees contracted elevator vendors, inspections, and documentation. Monitors performance, response times, safety practices, and contract compliance. Assists with procurement, renewals, invoicing, and amendments. Evaluate all FSU Facilities elevators to ensure equipment is being maintained to manufacture's specifications. Ensures safe and reliable elevator operation. Participates in elevator capital improvement planning. Coordinate with elevator vendor to evaluate campus conditions of equipment to identify if a modernization is required. Collaborate with Facilities PD&C to provide guidance and support when needed as the subject matter expert for elevator modernization. Contributes to the development of Capital Projects and Deferred Maintenance lists. Works closely with Facilities department reps, maintenance supervisors, and campus FLO personnel. Completes required safety training and complies with all safety standards including but not limited to lock out-tag out, confined space safety, safe handling of hazardous chemicals, participation in campus safety teams, and wearing required personal protective equipment (PPE). Reports complex and/or unusual problems to the Facilities Superintendent and coordinates with other Maintenance Supervisors and staff as required to complete complex tasks. Completes other relevant duties as assigned, operates university vehicles. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and four years experience related to facilities and/or grounds services or a high school diploma or equivalent and eight years of experience. (Note: or a combination of post high school education and experience equal to eight years.) A valid Florida or Georgia driver's license or the ability to obtain one upon hire University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position is being re-advertised. Previous applicants need not reapply. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63458&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Employee Labor Relations Analyst, Office of Human Resources (Multiple Vacancies)", "description": "Employee Labor Relations Analyst, Office of Human Resources (Multiple Vacancies) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63458 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Employee & Labor Relations | Office of Human Resources Florida State University, recognized as a Forbes Best-in-State Employer, is a place where purposeful work and public impact meet every day. The ELR Analyst I plays a central role in how FSU supports its workforce, manages complex employee matters, and strengthens the practices that allow the University to operate with stability, fairness, and sound judgment. This position helps shape the systems, partnerships, and decision-making that support FSU\u2019s mission at scale. You will advise leadership on sensitive issues, and contribute to a workplace where employees are supported and equipped to do their best work. Responsibilities About This Role Recently named a Forbes Best-in-State Employer, Florida State University is a place where public service, sound governance, and people-centered leadership come together every day. The ELR Analyst I plays a critical role in supporting that work by providing expert consultation on complex employee and labor relations matters that directly impact the University\u2019s ability to function effectively and responsibly. Serving as a trusted advisor within the Office of Human Resources, this position partners closely with university leadership and management to resolve sensitive workplace issues, protect institutional integrity, and promote effective people management practices across the institution. Why This Role Matters How an institution responds to employee concerns, performance issues, and labor relations challenges shapes trust, accountability, and organizational effectiveness. The ELR Analyst I helps ensure that workplace decisions are consistent, legally sound, and aligned with University policy and collective bargaining agreements. By guiding leaders through complex employee situations, conducting high-stakes investigations, and supporting labor relations processes, this role directly contributes to a stable, compliant, and well-managed work environment\u2014one that allows FSU\u2019s teaching, research, and public service mission to advance without disruption. What You\u2019ll Do As a member of the Employee & Labor Relations team, the ELR Analyst I provides high-level consultation, analysis, and project leadership across several core areas: Employee Relations Consultation & Case Management Provide guidance and coaching to managers at all levels on employee performance, conduct, and behavioral concerns. Conduct highly complex and sensitive employee relations investigations. Prepare thorough investigative reports and deliver sound, legally defensible recommendations for corrective action, up to and including termination. Analyze documentation and relevant data to support informed, compliant decision-making. Partner with leadership to mitigate organizational risk and resolve issues effectively. Labor Relations & Collective Bargaining Support Support the administration of collective bargaining agreements and labor relations activities. Assist with grievance processing, contract interpretation, and labor-management matters. Conduct research related to contract administration and ensure compliance with agreement-related initiatives and special projects. Employee Relations Programs & Training Assists with the University\u2019s employee performance evaluation processes. Develops and facilitates training on employee and labor relations topics, including workplace conduct, performance management, and disciplinary processes. Qualifications Education & Experience Bachelor\u2019s degree and two (2) years of experience in human resources, employee relations, or a related field or A high school diploma or equivalent, and the same experience totaling six (6) years Preferred Qualifications Demonstrated experience handling complex employee relations investigations, including performance issues, misconduct, and disciplinary actions in a higher education or large, decentralized organization. Working knowledge of collective bargaining agreements and experience supporting grievance processes or labor-management activities. Strong understanding of applicable federal and state employment laws and their practical application in an institutional setting. Experience advising leaders on risk mitigation and sensitive workplace decision-making. Proven ability to prepare clear, well-documented investigative reports and recommendations. Experience developing or delivering training related to employee relations, performance management, or workplace conduct. Ability to manage multiple high-priority matters with discretion, sound judgment, and attention to detail. Other Information Working at Florida State University Employees at Florida State University are part of a mission-driven academic and professional community where work has purpose and impact. Founded in 1851, FSU is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida and one of the nation\u2019s elite research universities. The work of Employee & Labor Relations helps sustain the organizational foundation that allows FSU\u2019s people\u2014faculty, staff, and administrators\u2014to do their best work in service of students and the public good. Love what YOU DO at FSU. Learn more and apply at jobs.fsu.edu Helpful What We\u2019re Looking For Who Thrives in This Role This role is ideal for an experienced employee and labor relations professional who exercises strong judgment, discretion, and critical thinking. You are confident navigating complex and sensitive matters, able to balance compliance requirements with thoughtful, people-centered solutions, and skilled at building trust with leaders and colleagues across the institution. Success in this role requires professionalism, emotional intelligence, attention to detail, and the ability to communicate clearly\u2014often in high-stakes situations\u2014while maintaining confidentiality and integrity. What a Typical Day Looks Like No two days are the same. One day may involve advising leadership on a difficult employee relations issue, reviewing investigative findings, or preparing disciplinary documentation. Another may focus on facilitating training, supporting the performance evaluation processes, or assisting with labor relations research. The work is dynamic, complex, and essential to maintaining a well-functioning University workplace. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range The salary is commensurate with experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Work Schedule: Monday through Friday, 8:00 am to 5:00 pm. This position is being re-advertised. Previous applicants need not reapply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63550&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "General Maintenance Technician (Open Rank)", "description": "General Maintenance Technician (Open Rank) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63550 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Facilities - Maintenance Responsibilities Performs preventive maintenance, troubleshooting and repairs to mechanical equipment, including, but not limited to: replacing/repairing belts, pulleys, actuators, valves, pneumatics, alignment, compressed air systems, fans, steam trap rebuilds, and pumps. Performs other preventative maintenance ir repairs for items such as hardware, door closures, etc. Performs preventive maintenance, troubleshooting, and repairs to electrical equipment including: repairing/replacing switches, outlets, breakers (limited), motor wiring, fixture replacement, ballasts, and re-lamping. Performs preventive maintenance, troubleshooting, and repairs to building control systems including: repairing/replacing actuators, sensors, variable speed drives, thermostats, terminal level devices (TEC/DXR), control wiring, UPS relays, and other control components as required. Perform preventive maintenance, troubleshooting, and repairs to plumbing systems. Duties include repairing faucets, valves, pipes, drains (including unclogging), toilets, and other plumbing-related items. Completes required safety training and complies with all safety standards including, but not limited to: lock out-tag out, safe handling of refrigerant, confined space safety, safe handling of hazardous chemicals, participation in campus safety teams, and wearing required personal protective equipment (PPE). Reports complex and/or unusual problems to the supervisor and coordinates with other Maintenance staff as required to complete complex tasks. Operates mobile equipment and/or campus vehicles including trucks, golf carts, personnel lifts, and forklifts. Maintains licensure and completes required training. Strives to provide excellent service to campus areas as measured by the 5-star program. Demonstrates proficient use of AiM mobile devices to complete work orders. Other duties as needed, including backup plant operator duties in Utilities, painting, sheetrock patching, and repairing door closures and hardware. Qualifications General Maintenance Technician Levels 1 - 2: High school diploma or equivalent and two years' experience, or a relevant Technical or vocational degree may substitute for experience General Maintenance Technician Level 3: High school diploma or equivalent and ten years of external professional experience. A valid State of Florida or Georgia Driver\u2019s License or the ability to obtain upon hire. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range The anticipated starting salary is $34,000, commensurate with experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select \u201cyes\u201d to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for Veterans\u2019 Preference eligibility requirements and Veterans\u2019 Preference required documentation (PDF) , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . The work schedule is from 8:00am to 4:30pm with a 30-minute break. This position i being re-advertised. Previous applicants need not apply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63077&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Overnight Museum Attendants (Part-Time/OPS)", "description": "Overnight Museum Attendants (Part-Time/OPS) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63077 Location Sarasota, FL Full/Part Time Part-Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The John & Mable Ringling Museum of Art is located in Sarasota, Florida, and is a department of Florida State University. Responsibilities Overnight Museum Attendants patrol The Ringling's 66-acre campus on foot and with golf carts. This role is responsible for: Conducting nightly inspections of assigned areas Assisting with urgent/emergency situations in a calm and timely manner. Protecting the collection, buildings, and grounds including guarding against theft, vandalism, other damage, and the safety of those on the property. Utilizing computers to write reports, check emails, send correspondences, and submit work orders as needed. Qualifications High school diploma or equivalent Valid Florida driver\u2019s license or the ability to obtain prior to hire. Ability to: Stand and walk for long periods Ascend/descend stairs Work in all types of weather conditions Preferred Qualifications Experience: Working in security Providing customer service Working in a museum or non-profit setting Ability to: Ability to promote a welcoming environment Contact Info For more information or technical assistance, please contact Ringling Human Resources via email or by calling 941-358-2771. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range $16.48 per hour (28 hours a week) How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an OPS/temporary job. Based on the duties, this position may require completion of a criminal history background check . Work Location: Sarasota, FL Employees are required to wear the standard-issue uniform while at work. This position is being readvertised. Previous applicants need not reapply. Working Hours Applicants must be available for the working hours as listed below. 10:15 PM to 6:45 AM Weekends, days, or holidays may be required based on the needs of The Ringling Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63567&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Program Associate, New Student & Family Program and Fraternity & Sorority Life - University Business Administrators", "description": "Program Associate, New Student & Family Program and Fraternity & Sorority Life - University Business Administrators Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63567 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department https://uba.fsu.edu/ - Division of Student Affairs - New Student & Family Program and Fraternity & Sorority Life Responsibilities Responsible for providing transactional financial and administrative support for the New Student and Family Program (NSFP) and Fraternity and Sorority Life (FSL). Provides fiscal support for both FSL & NSFP including entering requisitions, proxying purchasing cards, reviewing incoming invoices, and ensuring payment of all outstanding invoices. Assists the FSL & NSFP Business Manager in performing fiscal accounting for the Departments, including reconciling, and monitoring all FSL & NSFP budgets. Serves as PCard Proxy and completes weekly and monthly purchasing card reconciliation processes. Serves as both FSL & NSFP Contract Manager. Provides support and processes all contracts for both departments. Processes internal requisitions and purchase orders. Creates invoices for FSL & NSFP auxiliary budgets. Maintains FSL scholarship processes for Foundation projects. Coordinates departmental human resource functions for both FSL & NSFP Departments including hiring, personnel actions, terminations, and transfers. Ensures all hiring documents are complete and accurate. Responsible for reviewing and verifying active appointment reports, submitting cases to HR as needed, monitors time and leave for approvals, and payroll cost center reports. Serves as a FACET Rep. Oversees general office operations for NSFP including coordinating maintenance and repairs of space and equipment. Manages office supply inventory and orders supplies as needed. Serves as the departmental Property Custodian and Key Manager. Provides front desk coverage as needed. Provides recommendations on office operational needs to include equipment, workflow, staffing, and materials. Assists NSFP and FSL leadership with special projects as assigned. Serves as the Travel Representative for both FSL & NSFP Departments. Serves as travel delegate for Concur in preparing travel requests, expense reports, and may assist with travel arrangements. Qualifications A high school diploma or equivalent and four years of experience. (Note: post high-school education and/or experience may substitute at a comparable rate.) Preferred Qualifications The ideal candidate will possess excellent customer service skills, proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite, and experience working in a professional office environment. They will demonstrate strong communication and organizational abilities, attention to detail, and a professional approach to supporting daily operations. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Starting in the mid $30,000's to $40,000, commensurate with education and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select \u201cyes\u201d to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for Veterans\u2019 Preference eligibility requirements and Veterans\u2019 Preference required documentation (PDF) , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being re-advertised. Previous applicants need not reapply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63734&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Program Director & Open Rank Professor, 12 Month Salaried - TMH Cardiology Fellowship, College of Medicine", "description": "Program Director & Open Rank Professor, 12 Month Salaried - TMH Cardiology Fellowship, College of Medicine Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63734 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Florida State University (FSU) College of Medicine , in partnership with Tallahassee Memorial HealthCare (TMH), invites applications and nominations for the position of Program Director for the Founding Program Director for the Cardiovascular Disease Fellowship Program. Responsibilities ACGME Compliance & Program Administration Accreditation Leadership: Maintain full compliance with all ACGME Common Program Requirements and Specialty-Specific Requirements for Cardiovascular Disease. Institutional Collaboration: Partner closely with the FSU College of Medicine Graduate Medical Education (GME) leadership, the Designated Institutional Official (DIO), and the Program Director of the FSU-TMH Internal Medicine Residency to ensure seamless program integration. Curriculum Design: Oversee the development, implementation, and ongoing refinement of a comprehensive 36-month cardiology curriculum that ensures COCATS Level 2 training eligibility. Recruitment: Design and lead a mission-driven, holistic recruitment and selection process for incoming fellows via ERAS and the NRMP Match. Fellow Evaluation: Direct the Clinical Competency Committee (CCC) and Program Evaluation Committee (PEC); provide timely, constructive feedback and monitor fellow milestones. Teaching & Mentorship Academic Environment: Cultivate a culture of inquiry, psychological safety, and clinical excellence. Didactics & Conferences: Oversee core educational activities, including weekly grand rounds, journal clubs, board review sessions, and regular morbidity and mortality (M&M) conferences. Scholarly Activity: Mentor fellows in research, quality improvement (QI) initiatives, and clinical case presentations, ensuring compliance with ACGME requirements for scholarship. Clinical Practice & Hospital Leadership Clinical Presence: Maintain active clinical duties at TMH in general or subspecialty cardiology (inpatient attending, consult services, and outpatient clinics). Procedural Supervision: Provide direct supervision and hands-on teaching to fellows in TMH\u2019s advanced cardiac units, that may include the cardiac intensive care unit, echo, nuclear, catheterization, and electrophysiology labs, based on the candidate's specialty area. Qualifications Candidates must meet the strict program director criteria outlined by the ACGME: Degree: MD or DO from an accredited institution. Licensure: Eligible for an unrestricted Florida Medical License. Eligible for medical staff privileges at Tallahassee Memorial Healthcare (must be able to meet all credentialing requirements for appointment at TMH). Board Certification: Current board certification in Cardiovascular Disease by the American Board of Internal Medicine (ABIM) or the American Osteopathic Board of Internal Medicine (AOBIM). Experience: Minimum of three (3) years of documented educational and/or administrative experience as an active faculty member in an ACGME-accredited internal medicine residency or cardiovascular disease fellowship program. Scholarship: Evidence of ongoing, recent scholarly activity, including peer-reviewed publications, national presentations, or leadership roles in professional societies (e.g., ACC, AHA). Other Information FSU Health: The Evolution of Academic Healthcare FSU Health represents a bold, multi-billion-dollar transformation in healthcare delivery, clinical training, and biomedical research across North Florida. Anchored by a ultimate goal of a $1.7 billion partnership with Tallahassee Memorial Healthcare (TMH), FSU Health is transitioning the region\u2019s premier medical assets into a fully integrated, world-class academic health center. This expanding ecosystem actively bridges bench-to-bedside research with community-focused clinical care. Key components include: The FSU Health Research Center: A state-of-the-art, 140,000-square-foot facility opening on the TMH campus to serve as a hub for clinical trials, health equity studies, and translational science. Regional Network Expansion: Rapid development of advanced clinical hubs across the Florida Panhandle, including the development of a new 100-bed hospital campus in Panama City Beach operated by TMH. Precision & Specialized Medicine: Innovations like the new FSU Health Precision Pediatrics clinic and the Florida Institute for Pediatric Rare Diseases, which bring advanced diagnostics directly to the community. The Florida State University College of Medicine Established as the first U.S. medical school of the 21st century, the FSU College of Medicine has earned national recognition for its innovative, community-based educational model. Rather than isolating training within a single university hospital, FSU utilizes a highly successful distributed model, partnering with top-tier regional healthcare systems, community clinics, and over 3,000 physician faculty members across the state. Mission-Driven Excellence: The College\u2019s core mission focuses on developing exemplary, patient-centered physicians who are deeply responsive to community needs, with a proud legacy of excellence in training for primary care, elder care, and underserved populations. Robust GME Infrastructure: The FSU Graduate Medical Education (GME) footprint sponsors a rapidly expanding portfolio of ACGME-accredited residency and fellowship programs. GME programs under FSU sponsorship consistently achieve exceptional Match rates and board passage scores, backed by rigorous institutional oversight, a culture of psychological safety, and extensive administrative support. A Culture of Collaboration: Clinicians and program leaders at FSU enjoy access to robust academic resources, including medical informatics, instructional design experts, professional development pathways, and comprehensive research support through dedicated pre- and post-award grant infrastructure. Tallahassee Memorial HealthCare (TMH): A private, not-for-profit, 772-bed healthcare system serving a 17-county region in North Florida and South Georgia. TMH provides highly sophisticated tertiary and quaternary cardiovascular services, including structural heart interventions, advanced electrophysiology, and open-heart surgery. Southern Medical Group, P.A. (SMG) , a multi-specialty physician group providing services through a Professional Services Agreement (PSA) and Co-Management Agreement, has partnered with TMH to establish the Heart & Vascular Institute (HVI) . The HVI operates under a well-defined governance structure and strategic plan that aligns clinical, operational, and physician leadership to advance cardiovascular care across the region. Collectively, the HVI is home to one of the most advanced and highest-volume heart programs in the Southeast. Serving as a true regional epicenter for cardiovascular innovation, the HVI delivers an integrated, patient-centered cardiovascular program focused on expanding access, advancing quality, driving innovation, and improving outcomes throughout North Florida and South Georgia. The Heart & Vascular Institute features: Advanced Infrastructure: State-of-the-art hybrid cardiac/vascular suites, a dedicated biplane neurovascular suite, and a high-volume cardiac catheterization laboratory. Comprehensive Structural Heart & Electrophysiology: A highly robust structural heart program executing complex, minimally invasive interventions including TAVR, MitraClip, and Watchman implants, alongside cutting-edge heart failure neuromodulation therapies (e.g., Barostim). Top-Tier Accreditations: Recognized by the American College of Cardiology (ACC) as an Accredited Chest Pain Center with Primary PCI and Resuscitation\u2014the highest designation available\u2014with additional ACC certifications in Cardiac Catheterization and Transcatheter Valve procedures. National Recognition: 2026 Modern Healthcare top 50 Cardiovascular hospitals. Consistently ranked as a High-Performing Hospital by U.S. News & World Report in Heart Failure, Transcatheter Aortic Valve Replacement (TAVR), and Pacemaker Implantation. Helpful This is an exceptional leadership opportunity for a visionary cardiologist to build, shape, and direct a new ACGME-accredited 3-year General Cardiology Fellowship program. The position bridges clinical practice at TMH (a 772-bed regional medical center) with the robust educational resources and academic oversight of the FSU College of Medicine. Contact Info Heather Venclauskas Assistant Director of GME University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Negotiable based on qualifications and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Schedule: Monday - Friday, 8:00 am - 5:00 pm The role balance typically consists of 25% dedicated administrative/educational time and 75% clinical practice within TMH and Southern Medical Group. This is a clinical non-tenure earning position. This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63733&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Program Director & Open Rank Professor, 12 Month Salaried - TMH Pulmonary and Critical Care Fellowship, College of Medicine", "description": "Program Director & Open Rank Professor, 12 Month Salaried - TMH Pulmonary and Critical Care Fellowship, College of Medicine Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63733 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Florida State University (FSU) College of Medicine , in partnership with Tallahassee Memorial HealthCare (TMH), invites applications and nominations for the position of Program Director for the Pulmonary Critical Care Medicine Fellowship Program. Responsibilities ACGME Compliance & Program Administration Accreditation Leadership: Maintain full compliance with all ACGME Common Program Requirements, Institutional Requirements, and Specialty-Specific Requirements for Graduate Medical Education in Pulmonary Disease and Critical Care Medicine. Institutional Collaboration: Partner closely with the FSU College of Medicine Graduate Medical Education (GME) leadership, the Designated Institutional Official (DIO), GMEC, and the Program Director of the FSU-TMH Internal Medicine Residency to ensure seamless program integration and collaborative education. Curriculum Design & Maintenance: Oversee the development, implementation, and ongoing refinement of a comprehensive 36-month curriculum encompassing at least 18 months of clinical experience (9 months pulmonary, 9 months critical care including MICU/CICU and non-medical ICUs), 24 to 30 months of continuity ambulatory care clinic, and individualized learning tracks. Recruitment: Design and lead a mission-driven, holistic recruitment and selection process for incoming fellows via ERAS and the NRMP Match, ensuring compliance with institutional policies and ACGME eligibility criteria. Fellow Evaluation & Progression: Direct the Clinical Competency Committee (CCC) and Program Evaluation Committee (PEC); provide timely, constructive feedback; monitor fellow progress along subspecialty-specific milestones; and oversee remediation or grievance processes in accordance with Sponsoring Institution policies. Administrative Authority: Maintain authority and accountability for program operations, faculty appointment/removal regarding the educational program, fellow supervision, and accurate submission of all ACGME ADS data and documentation. Teaching, Mentorship & Scholarly Activity Academic Environment: Cultivate a culture of inquiry, psychological safety, professional well-being, and clinical excellence within the fellowship program. Didactics & Conferences: Oversee core educational activities, including protected didactic time, grand rounds, journal clubs, board review sessions, morbidity and mortality (M&M) conferences, and simulation-based training. Scholarly Activity Leadership: Mentor fellows in basic science, translational, clinical research, or quality improvement (QI) initiatives. Ensure fellow and core faculty engagement in annual scholarly activities and dissemination as required by ACGME standards. Procedural Supervision: Ensure direct supervision and structured evaluation of fellows in key diagnostic and therapeutic procedures until technical proficiency is documented (e.g., flexible fiber-optic bronchoscopy, endobronchial/transbronchial biopsies, thoracentesis, chest tube insertion, critical care ultrasound, advanced airway management, and hemodynamic monitoring). Clinical Practice & Hospital Leadership Clinical Presence: Maintain active clinical practice at TMH in pulmonary disease and critical care medicine (inpatient attending, consult services, MICU/ICU attending, and outpatient continuity/subspecialty clinics). Multidisciplinary Collaboration: Serve as a clinical expert and consultant, working collaboratively with thoracic surgery, interventional radiology, oncology, pathology, respiratory therapy, and critical care nursing teams across TMH. Quality & Patient Safety: Actively participate in hospital quality improvement, patient safety event reporting, and root cause analysis, incorporating quality metrics into clinical care and fellow education. Qualifications Candidates must meet the strict program director criteria outlined by the ACGME: Degree: MD or DO from an accredited institution. Licensure: Currently hold or be eligible for an unrestricted Florida Medical License. Eligible for medical staff privileges at Tallahassee Memorial Healthcare (must be able to meet all credentialing requirements for appointment at TMH). Board Certification: Current board certification in Pulmonary Disease and/or Critical Care Medicine by the American Board of Internal Medicine (ABIM) or the American Osteopathic Board of Internal Medicine (AOBIM). Experience: Minimum of three (3) years of documented educational and/or administrative experience as an active faculty member in an ACGME-accredited internal medicine residency or pulmonary disease and/or critical care medicine fellowship program. Scholarship: Evidence of ongoing, recent scholarly activity, including peer-reviewed publications, national presentations, grant leadership, or active involvement in professional societies (e.g., ATS, CHEST, SCCM). Leadership & Professionalism: Demonstrated exemplary professionalism, leadership capability, and dedication to medical education, faculty development, and fellow well-being. Other Information This is an exceptional leadership opportunity for a visionary pulmonary critical care physician to build, shape, and direct an ACGME-accredited 3-year Pulmonary Disease and Critical Care Medicine Fellowship program. The position bridges clinical practice at TMH (a 772-bed regional medical center) with the robust educational resources and academic oversight of the FSU College of Medicine. Helpful FSU Health: The Evolution of Academic Healthcare FSU Health represents a bold, multi-billion-dollar transformation in healthcare delivery, clinical training, and biomedical research across North Florida. Anchored by an ultimate goal of a $1.7 billion partnership with Tallahassee Memorial Healthcare (TMH), FSU Health is transitioning the region\u2019s premier medical assets into a fully integrated, world-class academic health center. This expanding ecosystem actively bridges bench-to-bedside research with community-focused clinical care. Key components include: The Florida State University College of Medicine Established as the first U.S. medical school of the 21st century, the FSU College of Medicine has earned national recognition for its innovative, community-based educational model. Rather than isolating training within a single university hospital, FSU utilizes a highly successful distributed model, partnering with top-tier regional healthcare systems, community clinics, and over 3,000 physician faculty members across the state. Mission-Driven Excellence: The College\u2019s core mission focuses on developing exemplary, patient-centered physicians who are deeply responsive to community needs, with a proud legacy of excellence in training for primary care, elder care, and underserved populations. Robust GME Infrastructure: The FSU Graduate Medical Education (GME) footprint sponsors a rapidly expanding portfolio of ACGME-accredited residency and fellowship programs. GME programs under FSU sponsorship consistently achieve exceptional Match rates and board passage scores, backed by rigorous institutional oversight, a culture of psychological safety, and extensive administrative support. A Culture of Collaboration: Clinicians and program leaders at FSU enjoy access to robust academic resources, including medical informatics, instructional design experts, professional development pathways, and comprehensive research support through dedicated pre- and post-award grant infrastructure. Contact Info Heather Venclauskas Assistant Director of GME University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Negotiable based on qualifications and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Schedule: Monday - Friday, 8:00 am - 5:00 pm. The role balance consists of 25% (0.25 FTE) dedicated administrative/educational time and 75% (0.75 FTE) clinical practice within TMH and associated clinical services. This is a clinical non-tenure earning position. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63655&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Research Coordinator, Scientific & Research Services (Remote-eligible) - Institute on Digital Health & Innovation (IDHI)", "description": "Research Coordinator, Scientific & Research Services (Remote-eligible) - Institute on Digital Health & Innovation (IDHI) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63655 Location Remote Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Florida State University College of Nursing I nstitute on Digital Health and Innovation (IDHI) Established in 2022, the Institute on Digital Health and Innovation (IDHI) within the Florida State University College of Nursing advances digital health science, technologies, and tools focused on solving real world needs of patients, providers, and populations through research, training, and innovation to maximize health. The mission of IDHI is to advance individual and public health through collaborative and synergistic partnerships focused on the development, evaluation, and dissemination of digital health tools, technologies, and innovations. IDHI co-leads the Adolescent Medicine Trials Network for HIV Interventions (ATN) \u2013 a multicenter research network conducting transformative research that addresses the HIV prevention and care continuum for adolescents and young adults in the US. The Statistical and Data Management Core (SDMC) within the ATN provides expertise in study design, statistical analysis, data collection, and data management to execute the ATN\u2019s research portfolio. Working in collaboration with Principal Investigators, Study Managers, site staff, and other key stakeholders, the SDMC provides comprehensive quantitative and qualitative data management and analyses for all network clinical studies; leadership; and services for regulatory aspects, biostatistics, study design analysis, interpretation, and publication or results. Responsibilities The Research Coordinator will operate as a member of the SDMC and IDHI teams by providing direct data-related support to the launch, implementation, and close-out of research projects. This position will assist with qualitative and quantitative data needs of the study teams. The range of responsibilities will include but are not limited to project planning, implementation, and monitoring of data collection activities; programming surveys and managing data from REDCap and/or Qualtrics; and overseeing qualitative data collection and analysis in NVivo and Dedoose. Other duties will include but are not limited to coordinating communication between research team members, participants and stakeholders; data/information quality control, cleaning, and analysis; identifying, evaluating, and modifying data collection methodologies; and assisting with the development of manuscripts, conference presentations, and research grant applications. Qualifications Bachelor\u2019s degree and two years of experience; or high school diploma/equivalent and experience equal to six years. (Note: post-high school education can substitute for experience at the equivalent rate.) Preferred Qualifications Master\u2019s degree in a related field and relevant experience. Interest in the development and evaluation of technology-based research interventions (e.g., the use of smartphone, social media, internet) to improve health and wellness. Experience reviewing and analyzing survey results, preparing recommendations, and reporting findings. Knowledge of research methodology and design. Knowledge of data collection and management principles, experience creating and maintaining data systems, and knowledge of effective data analysis and visualization strategies and trends. Proficiency working with data management systems (e.g., REDCap, Qualtrics, Stata, NVivo, Dedoose). Proficiency collecting qualitative data including, but not limited to: conducting in-depth interview and facilitating focus groups. Excellent interpersonal and communication skills, both oral and written, which are required for interacting with a wide range of stakeholders. Demonstrated ability to prioritize and complete assignments independently with excellent attention to detail. Proficient in the Microsoft Office Suite, specifically Outlook, Word, Excel, and Power Point. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position has been designated as eligible for remote work based on the current position/job functions. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63746&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Academic Advisor (Panama City Campus)", "description": "Academic Advisor (Panama City Campus) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63746 Location Panama City, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Chapman Center for Student Success and Advising Florida State University is one of the nation\u2019s top public universities, and FSU Panama City amplifies the university\u2019s efforts to preserve, expand, and disseminate knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and human services professions. FSU Panama City is located 100 miles west of Tallahassee on the beautiful North St. Andrews Bay and is only three miles from the beaches of the Emerald Coast. FSU PC currently houses 20 bachelor's programs, 9 master's programs, and 1 doctoral program, and boasts a small faculty-to-student ratio, which gives students a more personalized academic experience. Please visit https://pc.fsu.edu/promise for information about our FSU PC Promise to students and https://pc.fsu.edu/ for more information about our campus. FSU Panama City also recently opened a brand new residential housing complex on campus and right on the water. This new apartment-style complex at FSU PC houses both undergraduate and graduate students. For more information about our on-campus housing, visit https://seminolelandingfsu.com/ . Responsibilities Responsible for advising undergraduate students in the development of academic schedules appropriate for stated educational goals; takes a proactive approach in collaborating with faculty and staff for student advising purposes and provides advising services on request; interprets and recommends policies and procedures to the Director that will effectively deliver academic advisement to undergraduate students within established guidelines. Works closely with mapping coordinators within all university academic units represented on the FSU Panama City Campus in the evaluation of major-specific requirements for current and prospective students; takes a proactive approach in ensuring retention of students, student success, and timely completion of the degree. Works closely with FSU Panama City Admissions Officers to support and advise prospective transfer and first-year students. Collaborates with campus and university Admissions staff to coordinate academic advising events. Assists both on-campus and distance learning students in the enrollment and registration process; conducts follow-up with students to ensure proper course registration for timely completion of degree requirements. Assists the campus in the collection and reporting of data on all advising, retention, and student success initiatives on the Panama City campus, and any other duties assigned. Qualifications A Bachelor's degree and two years of experience; or a high school diploma or equivalent and six years of experience. (Note: a combination of post high school education and experience equal to six years.) Preferred Qualifications Ability to effectively communicate and demonstrate advanced interpersonal skills with students and coworkers. Experience successfully contributing to a team dynamic. Expertise in using Microsoft Office, OneDrive, Microsoft Teams, and Adobe PDF programs. Ability to compile and understand student academic data. Experience with computer-based student success/enrollment management platforms (e.g., EAB Campus Connect, PeopleSoft Student Central). Contact Info Dr. Tyler Towne University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position will begin in Fall 2026. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63735&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Administrative Specialist - UBA/CMPA", "description": "Administrative Specialist - UBA/CMPA Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63735 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department University Business Administrators | College of Motion Picture Arts Responsibilities Responsible for serving as the Department HR Representative for the CMPA, ensuring compliance with all HR policies and procedures. Interprets University policies and provides recommendations based on knowledge of the organization's business administrative objectives and activities. Serves as I-9 Coordinator and Notary Public for the CMPA. Oversees and coordinates vacancy postings and recruitment, and provides support to CMPA search committees in coordinating and conducting interviews and hires. Responsible for onboarding and day-to-day supervision of Federal Work Study students who manage the front desk reception area and visitor log. Provides administrative support for faculty affairs and faculty processes. Coordinates and completes personnel actions for all adjuncts, courtesy faculty, CMPA student drivers, interns, graduate assistants, and other OPS/salaried positions. Coordinates administrative processes related to faculty promotion. Provides support for residencies, including artist payments, visiting guest travel, and artist contracting. Serves as the primary administrative professional support for the Dean. Responsible for day-to-day administrative operations in the Dean's Office for the College of Motion Picture Arts (CMPA). Contributes to the team by scheduling meetings, talking minutes, setting agenda items. Works to fulfill the College's goals, deadlines, and objectives and assists with the implementation of approved College initiatives, projects, and administrative processes in collaboration with the Dean and Associate Deans. Serves as the first point of contact for the Dean and as a liaison to campus and community stakeholders to include university leaders, directors, faculty, staff, alumni, donors, and community partners. Exercises judgment in screening and referring visitors, phone calls, and inquiries. Reviews correspondence on behalf of the Dean for completeness and accuracy. Serves as CMPA Key Manager, Property Custodian, Security Coordinator, and coordinates facility maintenance and repair requests. Serves as the backup departmental representative for Travel and Purchasing during peak times. Provides support in planning and coordination of special events, such as awards ceremonies, conferences, annual and semesterly college retreats and meetings, graduation ceremonies, college project events, and other scholarly events. Qualifications A Bachelor's degree and two years of experience; or a high school diploma or equivalent and six years of experience. (Note: a combination of post high school education and experience equal to six years.) Preferred Qualifications Proficiency in performing accurately in a detail oriented environment. Ability to demonstrate quality customer service. Ability to communicate effectively verbally and in writing. Ability to multi-task and assess priorities. Ability to demonstrate critical thinking based upon data, information, and ethics. Ability to coordinate and manage calendars. Helpful The College of Motion Picture Arts is seeking a highly organized, proactive, and solutions-oriented professional to serve as the Dean's Executive Assistant and Department HR Representative. This pivotal role supports the daily operations of the Dean's Office while overseeing a broad range of human resources, administrative, faculty affairs, and special projects functions that are essential to the success of the College. The ideal candidate is a self-starter and critical thinker who takes initiative, anticipates needs, exercises sound judgment, and thrives in a fast-paced, collaborative environment. Working closely with the Dean, Associate Deans, faculty, staff, students, alumni, donors, and community partners, this individual will lead key administrative processes, coordinate strategic initiatives, manage executive communications and operations, and help advance the College's goals through exceptional organization, professionalism, and independent problem-solving. This position requires a confident professional who identifies opportunities, develops solutions, and serves as a trusted partner in supporting the mission and growth of the College of Motion Picture Arts. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63716&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Director of MFA Lighting Design / Open Rank Faculty, 9 Month Salaried - School of Theatre", "description": "Director of MFA Lighting Design / Open Rank Faculty, 9 Month Salaried - School of Theatre Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63716 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department School of Theatre Responsibilities Florida State University\u2019s School of Theatre invites applications for a 9 month tenure track faculty position in Lighting Design. We seek a dynamic and visionary artist-scholar to advance our graduate lighting design program, mentor students, and engage in creative and research activities that elevate the School of Theatre's profile. Teaching: Develop and teach courses in lighting design, covering introductory and advanced topics, production design, and related subjects. Participate in curriculum development and help integrate design technologies and digital media. Creative/Research Activity: Maintain an active schedule of creative work and/or research in lighting design. This may include professional design projects in theater, opera, film, television, or related fields; publications; conference presentations; and other scholarly outputs. Service: Engage in school, college, and university activities, including committee work, student advising, recruitment, and outreach. Actively support the School of Theatre\u2019s production season by serving as a lighting designer and mentor to graduate student designers. Collaboration: Collaborate with faculty and staff from both the school and the university on interdisciplinary projects and initiatives. Connect with industry professionals and maintain ties with the broader lighting design community. Qualifications MFA in Lighting Design or a closely related field by the time of appointment. Demonstrated excellence in teaching at the university level. A strong portfolio of professional lighting design work at a national level. Evidence of ongoing creative or scholarly activity. Experience with digital design technologies, including the use of computer-aided design to create lighting design paperwork, and 3D modeling A record of successful collaboration in academic or professional settings. Contact Info Search committee chair: Jesse Dreikosen , Professor University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Candidates should submit the following materials: A cover letter that outlines qualifications and experience. Curriculum Vitae. A digital portfolio showcasing recent work. A teaching philosophy statement. Three letters of recommendation. Please submit all application materials through the university\u2019s online application system. Incomplete applications will not be considered. Confidential Letters of Reference: This position requires that you have three confidential professional letters of recommendation submitted on your behalf. Follow the steps below to request these letters through our system: 1) After submitting your application, click the Explore Jobs link; 2) Click the My References link; 3) Click the Send/View Reference Request button next to the appropriate position; and 4) Follow the steps on that page to send your references a system generated email requesting they submit a letter of recommendation on your behalf. You may also return to the My References link and click on \"Send/View Reference Request\" to see if your references have responded, add additional references, or resend requests. Candidates who currently hold tenure and are seeking appointment with tenure at Florida State University will need to submit the materials for evaluation if selected. These materials are required to support the tenure review process at the time of hire. Finalists may be asked to provide the below additional documentation as part of the evaluation. Examples of excellence in research or creative activity or excellence in teaching. CV One-page statement of their accomplishments over the last five years. Discussion of their teaching, research and service (no longer than six pages). Three outside letters of recommendation directed specifically to Florida State University. No professional relationships should exist between the candidate and the external reviewer. Relationships include, but are not limited to, student- teacher (including dissertation committee chairs and members), colleagues in graduate school, former departmental colleagues, collaborators, and co-authors. These letters should be sent to Megan Mellino , Administrative Specialist, directly from the external reviewer. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled and will begin Fall 2027. Applicant Review will begin November 30, 2026, and continue until filled. The faculty rank associated with the appointment will be determined based on the selected candidate\u2019s qualifications and experience. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63184&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Groundskeeper - 7:00AM to 3:30PM", "description": "Groundskeeper - 7:00AM to 3:30PM Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63184 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department FSU Facilities - Grounds Department Responsibilities Responsible for groundskeeping maintenance tasks within zones on Florida State University properties as assigned to consistently maintain a safe, clean, sustainable, and attractively landscaped environment for the students, faculty, and staff of our institution. Performs groundskeeping tasks such as mowing, edging, raking, mulching, power blowing, weed eating, pulling weeds, light pruning, and watering plants. Responsible for debris removal, leaf removal, trash pickup and other tasks to keep grounds clean and presentable. Maintains areas by spreading landscape materials such as pine straw, bark, or rocks. Assists with landscaping tasks such as planting bushes, plants, shrubs, and trees. Assists in maintaining turf areas by utilizing push mowers to ensure an attractively landscaped environment on campus. Prepares landscaped areas with soil excavation, turf removal and re-sodding. Safely operates and maintains grounds equipment to ensure the health and appearance of university grounds. Ensures that all manual and power equipment is in proper working condition and reports maintenance problems to the supervisor. Performs other tasks as assigned by supervisor or higher authority. Qualifications Minimum of a 9th Grade Education Valid Florida or Georgia driver's license or the ability to obtain one upon hire University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select \u201cyes\u201d to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for Veterans\u2019 Preference eligibility requirements and Veterans\u2019 Preference required documentation (PDF) , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being re-advertised. Previous applicants need not apply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63687&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Open Publishing Specialist - University Libraries", "description": "Open Publishing Specialist - University Libraries Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63687 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department University Libraries Responsibilities The Open Publishing Specialist supports the day-to-day management of Florida State Open Publishing, including its publishing policies, platforms, and workflows. The position serves as managing editor of the Journal of Postsecondary Student Success (JPSS), coordinates journal and book production, supports the onboarding of new publications, and provides technical guidance to authors and editors. Working collaboratively with colleagues across FSU Libraries and university partners, the successful candidate will help strengthen FSOP's publishing services, promote best practices in scholarly communication, and expand access to research and scholarship. Coordinate Open Publishing Operations and Services Support the daily operations of Florida State Open Publishing in collaboration with the Digital Publishing Librarian. Coordinate the annual call for book proposals, onboarding of new journals, and ongoing management of FSOP's journal and book catalog. Consult with authors and editors to develop production plans, establish timelines, and support publication deadlines. Assist with the development and implementation of publishing policies, procedures, and workflows. Manage Journal Editorial and Production Workflows Serve as managing editor and technical editor of the Journal of Postsecondary Student Success , coordinating editorial and production activities to support its quarterly publication schedule. Work closely with editors, authors, and vendors to manage production timelines, address technical issues, and support timely publication. Maintain regular communication with journal editors regarding publishing policies, editorial workflows, and opportunities for improvement. Apply best practices in academic publishing to support consistent and effective editorial processes. Support Publishing Platforms and Technical Services Manage and support FSOP's publishing platforms, including Open Journal Systems (OJS) and Manifold. Provide technical assistance and guidance to faculty and student journal editors using FSOP's publishing platforms. Collaborate with the Florida Virtual Campus (FLVC) to address platform-level issues related to OJS. Develop and deliver training to support editors, authors, and readers in accessing and using FSOP's publishing platforms. Oversee Publication Production and Discoverability Coordinate the full publication production process for journal and book projects, including copyediting, graphic design, layout, and preparation of PDF, HTML, and EPUB formats. Manage publication-related web content, identifier registration (DOI, ISBN, and ISSN), and indexing in relevant discovery services. Coordinate with external vendors as needed and monitor production costs to support established project budgets. Develop promotional materials, press kits, and marketing strategies to increase the visibility and reach of new and forthcoming publications. Advance Accessibility and Publishing Best Practices Develop and maintain accessibility standards for FSOP's journal and book publications. Create and deliver training, including asynchronous resources, to help journal editors understand publishing requirements and accessibility best practices. Develop and maintain internal and external documentation for journal and book publishing workflows. Provide guidance to authors and editors on publishing standards, accessibility, and effective production practices. Qualifications A Bachelor's degree and two years of experience; or a high school diploma or equivalent and six years of experience. (Note: a combination of post high school education and experience equal to six years.) Preferred Qualifications Strong interest in academic publishing Strong communication and writing skills, including copyediting experience Strong interpersonal skills, including experience in providing instruction and guidance Proven organizational skills, including the ability to multitask, adapt to changing workflows and tools, and solve problems creatively Detail-oriented and process-driven, with the ability to both follow and create procedures Strong computer literacy, including fluency with common office tools (Microsoft Office and Google Workspace) Strong background in graphic design and production tools, including fluency with Adobe Creative Cloud (InDesign, Illustrator, Photoshop) Strong working knowledge of HTML and CSS Familiarity with open publishing platforms, including Open Journal Systems (OJS) and Manifold Web design experience, particularly with WordPress Knowledge of trends, issues, standards, and best practices in academic and digital publishing Willingness to learn new tools and technologies Other Information Located within FSU Libraries' Digital Research and Scholarship department, this position offers an exciting opportunity to contribute to open access scholarly publishing through the production and management of academic journals, books, and other scholarly publications. Working closely with the Digital Publishing Librarian, faculty editors, authors, and publishing partners, the Open Publishing Specialist helps ensure that FSOP's publications are professionally produced, accessible, and widely discoverable. Helpful Help expand access to scholarship through innovative, open publishing services. At University Libraries, you will have the opportunity to: Contribute to the growth of Florida State Open Publishing and its collection of open access journals, books, and scholarly publications. Collaborate with faculty, researchers, students, and publishing partners to bring scholarly work to a broader audience. Support innovative approaches to scholarly publishing, digital accessibility, and the discoverability of research. Develop expertise in publishing technologies, editorial workflows, and the production of accessible digital publications. Work in a collaborative environment that values creativity, innovation, continuous learning, and professional growth. Contact Info Landis Grenville , Digital Publishing Librarian University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Starting salary is $44,056, commensurate with education and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63738&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Open Rank Professor, 9 Month Salaried (The Department of Materials Science and Engineering in the FAMU-FSU College of Engineering- Multiple Openings)", "description": "Open Rank Professor, 9 Month Salaried (The Department of Materials Science and Engineering in the FAMU-FSU College of Engineering- Multiple Openings) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63738 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The Department of Materials Science and Engineering in the FAMU-FSU College of Engineering invites applications from highly qualified individuals for multiple faculty positions at all ranks in the city of Tallahassee, Florida. The department sits within the FAMU-FSU College of Engineering. Responsibilities Establish and maintain a robust, externally funded research program with international impact and a demonstrated track record of productive, high-quality research. Foster cross-campus, interdisciplinary collaborations to enhance university research initiatives. Deliver high-quality instruction primarily at the graduate level while maintaining a strong commitment to teaching excellence. Conduct targeted outreach to undergraduate students within FAMU and FSU science and engineering departments to foster interest and engagement in the discipline. Qualifications Candidates must possess an earned Ph.D. in Materials Science, Physics, Chemistry, Engineering or a closely related discipline. Successful candidates must have a demonstrated track record of productive high-quality research. Contact Info Any questions about the positions should be directed to Search Committee Co-Chairs, Dr. Tarik Dickens dickens@eng.famu.fsu.edu or Dr. Theo Siegrist siegrist@eng.famu.fsu.edu. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Please apply to each university with the following documents: A cover letter A full curriculum vitae A 3-page research statement A 1-page teaching statement An Equal Employment Opportunity Survey for Faculty Applicants Names and contact information of three professional references. To be considered for an appointment at the rank of Assistant Professor, three letters of recommendation must be submitted directly by the letter writers at the time of application. Documents should be named 'Candidate Last Name, First Name_MS&E' and must be on letterhead with the letter writers signature included.\u201d Faculty Information The FAMU-FSU College of Engineering is located in Innovation Park adjacent to the National High Magnetic Field Laboratory (NHMFL) which houses the world\u2019s highest field magnets and attracts well over 1000 world-wide users each year. The joint college is the nexus of two major public universities, each with a distinct mission but focused on world-class engineering education and research. Created by the Florida Legislature in 1982, the joint organization is the College of Engineering for both Florida A&M and Florida State Universities. Florida A&M is an 1890 Land Grant Institution. This unique partnership has created a truly innovative campus that leverages the benefits of the traditional HBCU with the innovations of an R-1 public research university. After completing pre-requisites at their home university, FAMU and FSU students learn, study and research together at the College campus with joint-appointed faculty and staff. Students graduate from their enrolling university AND from the FAMU-FSU College of Engineering. Both FAMU and FSU are part of the State University System of Florida. Additionally, all seven of the college\u2019s eligible undergraduate degree programs are accredited by the Engineering Accreditation Commission of ABET Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Full consideration will be given to applications received by December 1, 2026. Applications received after that date may be considered until positions are filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63741&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Program Coordinator (College of Arts and Sciences)", "description": "Program Coordinator (College of Arts and Sciences) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63741 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Florida State University College of Arts and Sciences Responsibilities The Program Coordinator is a member of the highly collaborative Business Operations Support Team (BOST) in the College of Arts & Sciences (CoAS). This position provides fiscal and administrative support to interdisciplinary programs within the CoAS. Working under the direction of the Associate Director, you'll work in collaboration with the Program Director and collaborate with faculty directors, staff, students, and university offices in support of accomplishing program goals. Responsibilities include: Coordinating and processing all travel, procurement, and HR actions for CoAS interdisciplinary programs including administrative, fiscal and operational activities. Serving as a primary point of contact for program participants, visitors, and stakeholders while supporting the implementation of program goals established by leadership. Coordinating logistics for lectures, workshops, conferences, committee meetings, and other special events. Serving as on-site support during events and assisting with event setup and breakdown, which may include events outside of normal business hours. Coordinating and attending routine committee meetings, preparing meeting minutes and tracking follow-up items. Assisting Program Director with program activities, events, communications, records management, faculty and student support, and routine financial and administrative processes. Reconciling financial transactions and gathering documentation for budget monitoring. Coordinating graduate and undergraduate fellowship and award paperwork and related documentation. Responding to inquiries related to fellowship application and disbursements. Qualifications A Bachelor's degree and two years of experience; or a high school diploma or equivalent and six years of experience. (Note: post-high school education may substitute for experience at the equivalent rate.) Preferred Qualifications An individual who thrives in a collaborative environment while possessing a high degree of self-motivation and ownership. Previous experience with FSU's administrative processes and systems is a plus! Other Information The Business Operations Support Team in the College of Arts & Sciences works to ensure continuity of business operations during unexpected challenges and staffing vacancies by providing fiscal and administrative support to the departments, programs, institutes, and centers across our college. By partnering directly with units, we deliver tailored temporary operational support, comprehensive systems analysis and process implementation, and targeted training services. Our approach focuses on collaboration, customization and excellence. To learn more, please visit our website . Helpful The College of Arts and Sciences is the largest and most academically comprehensive at FSU, encompassing 200-plus major programs of study and approximately 11,000 students. Every day, an outstanding team of more than 2,200 faculty and staff members in the College of Arts and Sciences work together to deliver exceptional academic programming to our students, conduct groundbreaking research, and provide research and administrative support across nearly three dozen departments, programs, centers and institutes. A career in the College of Arts & Sciences has global reach and meaningful impact, contributing directly to the success of the research and academic teaching efforts at Florida State University! University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63726&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Program Director & Open Rank Professor, 12 Month Salaried - Obstetrics and Gynecology Residency Program - Sarasota Memorial Health Care System, College of Medicine", "description": "Program Director & Open Rank Professor, 12 Month Salaried - Obstetrics and Gynecology Residency Program - Sarasota Memorial Health Care System, College of Medicine Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63726 Location Sarasota, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The Florida State University College of Medicine , in partnership with Sarasota Memorial Health Care System, seeks a visionary and accomplished academic leader to serve as the Founding Program Director (PD) for the Obstetrics and Gynecology Residency Program. Responsibilities The Program Director holds authority, accountability, and operational responsibility for all aspects of the residency program, including the integration of clinical education, resident well-being, faculty development, and strict adherence to the Accreditation Council for Graduate Medical Education (ACGME) Institutional and Program Requirements. This position balances dedicated administrative and educational leadership with ongoing clinical practice within the high-volume, high-acuity environment of Sarasota Memorial Hospital Care System. Key Responsibilities & ACGME Core Mandates 1. Program Administration & Compliance Maintain oversight and ultimate accountability for the operation of the residency program across all clinical environments. Administer and maintain an educational environment conducive to teaching and training residents in each of the six ACGME core competency areas. Ensure accurate, complete, and timely updates of all required program information in the ACGME Accreditation Data System (ADS). Implement and enforce institutional and program-specific policies regarding resident selection, evaluation, promotion, discipline, grievance, and due process. 2. Curriculum & Clinical Oversight Design, implement, and continuously improve a robust educational curriculum that reflects current trends and standards in OB/GYN education, including advanced surgical and simulation modalities. Approve the selection, continued participation, and evaluation of all core and subspecialty program faculty at participating clinical sites. Identify and collaborate with qualified Subspecialty Faculty Educators across the mandatory domains: Maternal-Fetal Medicine (MFM), Gynecologic Oncology, Female Pelvic Medicine and Reconstructive Surgery (FPMRS), and Reproductive Endocrinology and Infertility (REI). Ensure rigorous monitoring of resident supervision, appropriate clinical and educational work hours (including moonlighting policies), and safe transitions of care. 3. Resident Evaluation & Tracking Oversee the Clinical Competency Committee (CCC) to ensure objective, milestone-based evaluations of resident progression. Maintain meticulous tracking of resident operative and clinical volumes via the ACGME Case Log System, ensuring each resident comfortably achieves required procedural minimums. Provide verified, documented evidence of completion and competency for all graduating residents or those transferring laterally out of the program. 4. Academic Environment & Quality Improvement Lead the Program Evaluation Committee (PEC) in conducting the Annual Program Evaluation (APE) to assess curriculum, faculty performance, and program efficacy. Foster a robust environment of scientific inquiry, mentoring residents in quality improvement (QI) projects, patient safety initiatives, and peer-reviewed research or scholarly activities. Qualifications Education: Medical Degree (MD or DO) from an accredited institution. Certification: Current, active board certification in Obstetrics and Gynecology by the American Board of Obstetrics and Gynecology (ABOG) or the American Osteopathic Board of Obstetrics and Gynecology (AOBOG). Licensure: Eligible for or currently holding an unrestricted medical license in the State of Florida. Eligible for appropriate medical staff appointments at Sarasota Memorial Healthcare (must be able to meet all credentialing requirements). Clinical Experience: A minimum of five (5) years of clinical experience in obstetrics and gynecology following completion of an OB/GYN residency. GME Experience: Minimum of three (3) years of documented educational and/or administrative experience as an active faculty member in an ACGME-accredited obstetrics and gynecology residency program. Aptitude: Demonstrated expertise in medical education pedagogy, familiarity with modern GME residency management platforms (e.g., New Innovations, Thalamus, ERAS), and an adaptive leadership approach to managing high-performing teams in high-stress clinical environments. Preferred Qualifications Leadership Track Record: Documented educational and/or administrative experience in an ACGME-accredited residency program (e.g., as an Associate Program Director, Core Faculty member, or Clerkship Director) is highly preferred. Other Information Established as the first U.S. medical school of the 21st century, the FSU College of Medicine has earned national recognition for its innovative, community-based educational model. Rather than isolating training within a single university hospital, FSU utilizes a highly successful distributed model, partnering with top-tier regional healthcare systems, community clinics, and over 3,000 physician faculty members across the state. Mission-Driven Excellence: The College\u2019s core mission focuses on developing exemplary, patient-centered physicians who are deeply responsive to community needs, with a proud legacy of excellence in training for primary care, elder care, and underserved populations. Robust GME Infrastructure: The FSU Graduate Medical Education (GME) footprint sponsors a rapidly expanding portfolio of ACGME-accredited residency and fellowship programs. GME programs under FSU sponsorship consistently achieve exceptional Match rates and board passage scores, backed by rigorous institutional oversight, a culture of psychological safety, and extensive administrative support. A Culture of Collaboration: Clinicians and program leaders at FSU enjoy access to robust academic resources, including medical informatics, instructional design experts, professional development pathways, and comprehensive research support through dedicated pre- and post-award grant infrastructure. About Sarasota Memorial Health Care System Founded in 1925, Sarasota Memorial Health Care System (SMHCS) is a highly decorated full-service public health system, a regional medical center and the largest employer in Sarasota County. Anchored by its flagship 897-bed acute-care campus in Sarasota, Florida, the health system spans a comprehensive network of care that includes a second full-service hospital in Venice, the newly opened Milman-Kover Cancer Outpatient Pavilion (part of the Brian D. Jellison Cancer Institute), freestanding emergency rooms, and a dedicated behavioral health hospital. Across its expansive network, SMH supports approximately 11,000 employees, 2,500 medical staff members, and manages more than 2 million patient visits annually. For an incoming OB/GYN Residency Program Director, SMH offers an exceptionally robust clinical training ground. The health system manages nearly 5,000 births per year, supported by a state-of-the-art Level III Neonatal Intensive Care Unit (NICU), comprehensive maternal-fetal medicine oversight, and specialized subspecialty clinics. National Recognitions & Quality Benchmarks Sarasota Memorial is internationally recognized for its uncompromising commitment to patient safety, clinical outcomes, and nursing excellence: The CMS \"Gold Standard\": SMH is the only hospital in the state of Florida\u2014and one of fewer than a dozen nationwide\u2014to earn the prestigious 5-Star Quality Rating from the U.S. Centers for Medicare & Medicaid Services (CMS) every single year since the federal rating program's inception in 2016. Top 15 Health System: Named one of the nation's 15 Top Health Systems by Modern Healthcare and Premier Inc., placing it in the highest tier of high-performing U.S. healthcare delivery organizations. Magnet\u00ae Recognition: Holds over 20 consecutive years of Magnet Designation for Nursing Excellence from the American Nurses Credentialing Center, a distinction shared by less than 2% of hospitals nationwide. Safety & Specialty Accolades: Consistently achieves \"Straight A\" safety ratings from The Leapfrog Group and is repeatedly named among America's Best Hospitals by U.S. News & World Report, Newsweek, and Forbes. Designated as a Baby-Friendly Hospital in 2017 and successfully re-designated in 2023. SMH-Sarasota was the first, and remains the only hospital in southwest Florida to earn the designation from Baby-Friendly USA Inc. The organization is part of a global initiative by World Health Organization and United Nations Children's Fund to promote mother-baby bonding, successful breastfeeding and best practices in maternity care. Level III Maternal Care Verification from the Joint Commission, in collaboration with the American College of Obstetrics in 2023. Sarasota Memorial received the Level III verification for providing advanced care to low and moderate-risk pregnancies, as well as to high-risk patients, including subspecialty care for more complex maternal medical conditions, obstetric complications and fetal conditions. As an elite clinical partner to the Florida State University College of Medicine, Sarasota Memorial Health Care System provides residents and faculty with the resource-rich, high-volume environment of a premier regional powerhouse, coupled with the deeply mission-driven culture of a true community asset. Contact Info R. Bubba Hamilton Director of GME University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Negotiable, based on qualifications and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Schedule: Monday - Friday, 8:00 am - 5:00 pm Required Protected Time & Support: Administrative Allocation: In strict compliance with ACGME requirements, the Sponsoring Institution guarantees no less than 20 hours per week (0.50 FTE) of protected, non-clinical professional effort dedicated entirely to the administrative, educational, and academic activities of the Obstetrics and Gynecology program. This is a clinical non-tenure earning position. This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63541&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Receptionist (OPS) FSU Health Lifestyle Medicine Clinic (College of Nursing)", "description": "Receptionist (OPS) FSU Health Lifestyle Medicine Clinic (College of Nursing) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63541 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The FSU Health Lifestyle Medicine Clinic at the College of Nursing is seeking a professional, dependable, and patient-focused Medical Office Receptionist to provide front-office support and help ensure an efficient and welcoming experience for our patients. Responsibilities Greet and check patients in and out in a professional and courteous manner. Answer incoming telephone calls, route messages, and respond to routine patient questions within the scope of the position. Schedule, reschedule, and confirm patient appointments. Maintain accurate patient demographic, contact, and insurance information. Assist with patient registration and completion of required forms. Verify that necessary documentation is available prior to patient appointments. Collect applicable copayments or patient payments and provide appropriate documentation. Monitor provider schedules and communicate scheduling concerns or changes to appropriate clinic staff. Assist patients with general questions regarding appointments, clinic procedures, referrals, and medical record requests. Communicate patient messages to providers and clinical staff in a timely and accurate manner. Maintain patient confidentiality and comply with HIPAA and applicable FSU Health policies and procedures. Maintain an organized and professional reception and waiting area. Assist with scanning, filing, faxing, medical records, and other general administrative duties. Coordinate with medical assistants and providers to support efficient patient flow throughout the clinic. When the Medical Assistant is unavailable, assist with obtaining non-invasive vital signs, such as blood pressure, when appropriately trained and authorized to do so. Perform other duties as assigned to support clinic operations. Qualifications High school diploma or equivalent. Strong customer service and interpersonal skills. Excellent verbal and written communication skills. Ability to communicate professionally with patients, providers, coworkers, and outside organizations. Strong attention to detail and ability to maintain accurate records. Ability to maintain confidentiality and appropriately handle protected health information. Ability to manage multiple responsibilities and prioritize tasks in a busy medical office environment. Basic computer proficiency, including experience with Microsoft Office and the ability to learn electronic health record and scheduling systems. Dependable attendance and punctuality. Ability to work effectively both independently and as part of a healthcare team. Preferred Qualifications Previous experience working in a medical office, physician practice, outpatient clinic, or other healthcare setting. Experience with electronic health record (EHR) or practice-management systems. Experience scheduling medical appointments and communicating with patients by telephone and electronic messaging. Knowledge of basic medical terminology. Experience with health insurance verification, patient registration, and medical records. Experience obtaining blood pressure and other basic vital signs. CPR/BLS certification or willingness to obtain certification, if required by the clinic. Experience working with multidisciplinary healthcare teams. The successful candidate should demonstrate: A patient-centered and service-oriented approach. Professionalism, discretion, and sound judgment. Ability to remain calm and courteous when assisting patients with questions or concerns. Strong organizational and time-management skills. Ability to recognize when a patient concern should be immediately referred to clinical staff. Ability to follow established clinic policies, procedures, and workflows. Willingness to cross-train in additional front-office functions as needed. Ability to adapt to changes in clinic schedules and operational needs. Helpful The ideal candidate will have previous medical office experience, excellent communication and organizational skills, and the ability to work effectively in a fast-paced clinical environment. This position serves as a primary point of contact for patients and works closely with providers, medical assistants, and clinic leadership to support daily clinic operations. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an OPS/temporary job. This position is being readvertised. Previous applicants need not reapply. Based on the duties, this position may require completion of a criminal history background check . Full-time/40 hours per week. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63551&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Senior Academic Innovation Learning Specialist", "description": "Senior Academic Innovation Learning Specialist Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63551 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Florida Institute for Child Welfare Responsibilities The Senior Academic Innovation Learning Specialist coordinates and facilitates simulation-based learning, faculty development, and experiential learning initiatives that prepare students and faculty to engage effectively with Florida\u2019s child welfare system. Key responsibilities include: Planning and coordinating simulation experiences in the Experiential Learning Lab and at university locations throughout Florida, including scheduling, logistics, university partner coordination, actor recruitment and preparation, resource management, and participant evaluation. Facilitating simulations, structured debriefs, faculty development workshops, simulation training, communities of practice, and faculty workgroups focused on experiential learning and child welfare education. Collaborating with Institute programs to pilot and implement innovative educational tools, simulations, coaching resources, and faculty and student initiatives, while serving as a backup facilitator for Institute learning events as needed. Providing child welfare subject matter expertise to support curriculum implementation, faculty consultation, simulation development, conference presentations, webinars, and educational outreach. Strengthening relationships with universities and faculty across Florida and expanding the Institute\u2019s capacity to deliver consistent, high-quality experiential learning opportunities statewide. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and four years' experience related to health and human services or a high school diploma or equivalent and eight years of experience. (Note: or a combination of post high school education and experience equal to eight years.) Preferred Qualifications Master\u2019s degree in social work, education, instructional design, child and family studies, public administration, or a related field. Direct experience working in Florida\u2019s child welfare system or supporting Florida\u2019s child welfare workforce. Experience facilitating simulation-based learning, experiential learning, role-play activities, or case-based instruction. Experience designing or implementing simulations, including scenario preparation, actor coordination, facilitation, and participant debriefing. Experience working with institutions of higher education, university faculty, or students. Experience facilitating faculty development workshops, communities of practice, or collaborative workgroups. Experience providing child welfare subject matter expertise for curriculum development or implementation. Experience piloting or implementing innovative learning tools, educational technologies, or interdisciplinary learning initiatives. Experience delivering presentations, webinars, or conference sessions to professional audiences. Knowledge of evaluation methods used to assess participant learning and program outcomes. Helpful The Florida Institute for Child Welfare is housed at the Florida State University College of Social Work. The purpose of the institute is to advance the well-being of children and families by improving the performance of child protection and child welfare services through research, policy analysis, evaluation, and leadership development. Suggested to visit The Florida Institute for Child Welfare for more information. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Anticipated salary between low to mid $60,000's, commensurate with education and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being re-advertised. Previous applicant need not apply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63073&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "1st Shift Museum Attendants (Part-Time/OPS)", "description": "1st Shift Museum Attendants (Part-Time/OPS) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63073 Location Sarasota, FL Full/Part Time Part-Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The John & Mable Ringling Museum of Art is located in Sarasota, Florida, and is a department of Florida State University . Responsibilities Primary responsibilities include: Patrols The Ringling's 66 acres of buildings, galleries, and grounds as assigned. Monitor visitor activity to ensure: Safety of staff and visitors Adherence to all policies/procedures Protection of the collection, buildings, and grounds while guarding against theft, vandalism, and other damage Briefly answers guest questions with a focus on customer service and creating a welcoming environment for our visitor population. Conducts daily inspections of assigned areas and reports: Safety issues Damages or necessary repairs Water intrusion or leaks As needed: Assists with emergency situations by communicating with the appropriate point of contact. Escorting staff and guests as assigned. Qualifications High school diploma or equivalent Valid Florida driver's license or the ability to obtain one prior to hire. Preferred Qualifications Experience with: Customer service and creating a welcoming environment Museums or similar non-profit organizations Ability to: Respond calmly to urgent/emergency situations Effectively communicate with the public Pay attention to surroundings and report issues Contact Info For more information or technical assistance, please contact Ringling Human Resources via email or by calling 941-358-2771. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range $15.45 (28 hours a week) This role is eligible for a $5 per hour pay additive for working eligible assigned special events. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an OPS/temporary job. Based on the duties, this position may require completion of a criminal history background check . Work Location: Sarasota, FL Employees are required to wear the standard-issue uniform while at work. This position is being readvertised. Previous applicants need not reapply. Working Hours This role has a set bi-weekly schedule. Applicants must be available for the schedule as listed below. Week 1: Saturday, Sunday, Tuesday, and Wednesday from 9:30 AM to 5:00 PM. Week 2: Friday and Monday from 9:30 AM to 5:00 PM, and Thursday from 9:30 AM to 8:00 PM. Weekends, evenings, and holidays may be required per the needs of the Ringling. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63715&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Deputy Building Official", "description": "Deputy Building Official Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63715 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department FSU Facilities Environmental Health and Safety Department Responsibilities Conduct review of construction documents and construction inspections of University Building Projects for Compliance with Florida Building Code. Act as assistant to the University's Building Official in the accomplishment of the mission of the Building Code Administration section to ensure that construction and maintenance activities on University facilities comply with the appropriate regulations. Perform supervisory activities of BCA sections staff to include coordination of daily work efforts, educational opportunities and requirements. Interact with all construction project team members (University Project Manager, Design Professionals and Contractor and Sub-Contractor personnel) to ensure compliance with Florida Building Code is maintained. Assist in the development and implementation of policies and procedures associated with the activities of the Building & Fire Safety sections. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and three years' experience or a high school diploma or equivalent and seven years of experience. (Note: or a combination of post high school education and experience equal to seven years) Possess or obtain within 120 days of employment standard or provisional FL license as plans reviewer & inspector in two disciplines (Building, Mechanical, Plumbing, Electrical, Fire) in accordance with FS 468. Possess or obtain within one year of employment FL Building Code Administrative license. A valid Florida or Georgia driver's license or the ability to obtain one upon hire. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63713&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Director of MFA Costume Design / Open Rank Faculty, 9 Month Salaried - School of Theatre", "description": "Director of MFA Costume Design / Open Rank Faculty, 9 Month Salaried - School of Theatre Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63713 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department School of Theatre Responsibilities The School of Theatre at Florida State University seeks a full-time nine-month, tenure-track open rank faculty position in Costume Design. We seek a dynamic and visionary artist-scholar to advance our graduate costume design program, mentor students, and engage in creative and research activities that elevate the School of Theatre's profile. Teaching : Responsibilities include teaching three courses per semester, which may include costume design, costume rendering, and costume history. Creative/Research Activity: Maintain an active schedule of creative work and/or research in costume design. Service : This position requires active*departmental participation, including curriculum development, recruitment, student advising, and season planning. Collaboration : Collaborate with faculty and staff from both the school and the university on interdisciplinary projects and initiatives. Connect with industry professionals and maintain ties with the broader costume design community. Communication : The applicant must be able to communicate effectively with costume graduate and undergraduate students and collaborate successfully with directors, faculty, and staff. Qualifications MFA in Costume Design or a closely related field by the time of appointment. Advanced expertise in rendering, costume design, and computer rendering Knowledge of historical period costume Experience in millinery construction, fabric modification, and costume crafts Demonstrated excellence in teaching at the university level. A strong portfolio of professional costume design work at a national level. Evidence of ongoing creative or scholarly activity. A record of successful collaboration in academic or professional settings. Contact Info Search committee chair: Jacki Armit , Associate Professor University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Candidates should submit the following materials: A cover letter that outlines qualifications and experience. Curriculum Vitae. A digital portfolio or website showcasing recent work. A teaching philosophy statement. Three letters of recommendation. Please submit all application materials through the university\u2019s online application system. Incomplete applications will not be considered. Confidential Letters of Reference: This position requires that you have three confidential professional letters of recommendation submitted on your behalf. Follow the steps below to request these letters through our system: 1. After submitting your application, click the Explore Jobs link; 2. Click the My References link; 3. Click the Send/View Reference Request button next to the appropriate position; and 4. Follow the steps on that page to send your references a system generated email requesting they submit a letter of recommendation on your behalf. You may also return to the My References link and click on \"Send/View Reference Request\" to see if your references have responded, add additional references, or resend requests. Candidates who currently hold tenure and are seeking appointment with tenure at Florida State University will need to submit the materials for evaluation if selected. These materials are required to support the tenure review process at the time of hire. Finalists may be asked to provide the below additional documentation as part of the evaluation. Examples of excellence in research or creative activity or excellence in teaching. CV One-page statement of their accomplishments over the last five years. Discussion of their teaching, research and service (no longer than six pages). Three outside letters of recommendation directed specifically to Florida State University. No professional relationships should exist between the candidate and the external reviewer. Relationships include, but are not limited to, student- teacher (including dissertation committee chairs and members), colleagues in graduate school, former departmental colleagues, collaborators, and co-authors. These letters should be sent to Megan Mellino , Administrative Specialist, directly from the external reviewer. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled and will begin Fall 2027. Applicant Review will begin November 30, 2026, and continue until filled. The faculty rank associated with the appointment will be determined based on the selected candidate\u2019s qualifications and experience. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=62108&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Finishes Technician (Facilities Maintenance - Levels 1-2 Multiple Vacancies)", "description": "Finishes Technician (Facilities Maintenance - Levels 1-2 Multiple Vacancies) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 62108 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Facilities - Maintenance Responsibilities Responsible for performing repairs and replacements of floor tiles, ceramic tiles, and damaged carpet campus-wide. Performs minor plaster and sheet rock repairs, which may include minor carpentry maintenance. Utilizes various hand and power tools to securely build assigned projects. Assists other trades as needed, such as painting, carpentry, and locksmiths. Operates vehicles to carry supplies and travel campus-wide to perform various skilled maintenance tasks. Loads and unloads necessary equipment and materials. Review plans and work orders to ensure correct completion of the scope of work. Documents work performed and orders materials on appropriate departmental forms. Follows established safety rules and regulations and maintains a safe and clean environment. Moves necessary materials around the job site. Cleans up work site debris. Responsible for security, safety, and maintenance of all equipment, supplies, and vehicles. Maintains tools and equipment, ensuring all hand and power tools are in proper working condition, and reports maintenance problems to the supervisor. Organizes and cleans assigned shop areas. Prepares requests for materials and supplies. Performs additional maintenance and supervises helpers as required to include general trades, minor carpentry tasks, painting, and lock hardware. Qualifications High school diploma or equivalent and two years' experience, or a relevant Technical or vocational degree may substitute for experience. A valid State of Florida or Georgia Driver\u2019s License or ability to obtain upon hire. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. Anticipated Salary Range The anticipated starting salary is $34,000, commensurate with experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our interactive too l to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://jobs.fsu.edu. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select \u201cyes\u201d to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for eligibility information and required documentation , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . The work schedule is 8:00am to 4:30pm with a 30-minute break. This position is being re-advertised. Previous applicants need not apply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63663&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Grants Administrator for Research & Science - College of Nursing, Office for Research & Scholarship", "description": "Grants Administrator for Research & Science - College of Nursing, Office for Research & Scholarship Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63663 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Florida State University College of Nursing Office for Research & Scholarship (ORS) Responsibilities Reports directly to the Assistant Director for the College of Nursing (CON) Office of Research. Will support the college\u2019s research team, but will be primarily responsible for development, implementation, and monitoring of the administration of contract/grant activity for an assigned portfolio. Processes and provides guidance on sponsored project HR, Purchasing and Travel transactions. Responsible for oversight of the post-award contract/grant activities. Responsible for developing and preparing financial reports, tracking salary commitments, identifying and resolving funding and compliance issues, coordinating close-outs; documents organization and storage. Advises and assists faculty, staff, and principal investigators in all areas of contracts/grant pre-award activities. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and four years of experience; or high school diploma/equivalent and experience equal to eight years. This position requires successful completion of the eSPEAR Certification , or ability to obtain the certification within 6 months of hire. Preferred Qualifications The preferred candidate will have experience in research administration, grants and contracts management, financial reporting, and sponsored project compliance, preferably within a higher education or a research institution. Candidates should demonstrate the ability to manage pre-award and post-award activities, including preparing and reviewing grant proposals, developing budgets, tracking salary commitments, reconciling financial data, monitoring expenditures, resolving funding discrepancies, and coordinating project closeouts. Familiarity with federal, state, and private funding sources, including National Institutes of Health (NIH) guidelines and other sponsor requirements, is preferred. The ideal candidate will possess strong analytical and organizational skills, with the ability to interpret and apply institutional policies, sponsor regulations, and compliance requirements to ensure accurate and timely submissions and reporting. Experience developing financial reports, analyzing project spending, projecting salary allocations, identifying funding opportunities, and supporting strategic planning initiatives is highly desirable. Candidates should also demonstrate proficiency in developing administrative procedures, establishing departmental deadlines, maintaining organized documentation, and managing multiple projects simultaneously. Strong written and verbal communication skills are essential, as the position requires collaboration with faculty, principal investigators, departmental leadership, funding agencies, the Research Foundation, and other sponsored research stakeholders. The ability to build effective working relationships, provide guidance on sponsored project administration, and support staff through training and mentoring is also preferred. A bachelor's degree and four years of relevant experience, or an equivalent combination of postsecondary education and experience. Familiarity with financial management systems, budgeting practices, contract administration, and applicable computer applications is highly desirable. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=62737&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Maintenance Support Worker (Panama City Campus)", "description": "Maintenance Support Worker (Panama City Campus) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 62737 Location Panama City, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department PCC Finance and Administration Department About Us | FSU Panama City Florida State University is one of the nation\u2019s top public universities, and FSU Panama City amplifies the university\u2019s efforts to preserve, expand, and disseminate knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and human services professions. FSU Panama City is located 100 miles west of Tallahassee on the beautiful North St. Andrews Bay is only three miles from the beaches of the Emerald Coast. FSU PC currently houses 20 bachelor's programs, 9 master's programs, and 1 doctoral program, and boasts a small faculty-to-student ratio, which gives students a more personalized academic experience. Please visit https://pc.fsu.edu/promise for information about our FSU PC Promise to students and https://pc.fsu.edu/ for more information about our campus. FSU Panama City also recently opened a brand new, residential housing complex on campus and right on the water. This new apartment-style complex at FSU PC houses both undergraduate and graduate students. For more information about our on-campus housing, visit https://seminolelandingfsu.com/ . Responsibilities Assists with maintenance of buildings, including windows, doors, furnishings, drywall, painting, construction, trash and debris removal, and cleaning of all areas; provides set-ups for special functions both on and off campus. Performs general cleaning and grounds maintenance around buildings, parking areas, drives, and other campus areas; operates mowers, edgers, fertilizer spreaders, spray rig, tractor, and weed trimmer as necessary to maintain law areas; plants trees, maintains roadways, parking areas, and fencing. Maintains exterior sprinkler systems, makes repairs to water pipes and sprinkler heads. Performs routine maintenance of all groundskeeping equipment, mowers, tractors, edgers, other lawn equipment, and tools. Assists in HVAC routine preventive maintenance, special projects, emergency repairs, cleaning, adjusting of machinery, cleaning equipment rooms; assists in repair of piping for water and sewer systems; assists in other duties as directed by supervisor. Qualifications Completion of 9th grade. A valid State of Florida or Georgia Driver\u2019s License or the ability to obtain prior to hire. Preferred Qualifications Knowledge of general safety practices (OSHA awareness). OSHA 10 or 30 certification. Trade-related certifications (entry-level HVAC, electrical, or plumbing). Helpful During the first three months, the Maintenance Support Worker will receive structured, hands-on training to build familiarity with campus systems, tools, and safety procedures. The selected candidate will work closely with their supervisor and department head to: Participate in guided training sessions on university equipment, facilities, and standard operating procedures. Shadow experienced staff to learn daily workflows and preventative maintenance practices. Gain an understanding of department safety protocols and compliance requirements. Take on progressively more independent assignments with ongoing support and feedback. Establish strong working relationships with team members and campus partners. By the end of the first 90 days, the Maintenance Support Worker is expected to be confident in navigating campus facilities, performing routine maintenance tasks, and contributing independently to the department's work while continuing to develop advanced skills. Contact Info Inquiries should be directed to David Gary at dgary@fsu.edu f or more information regarding this position. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our interactive too l to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://jobs.fsu.edu. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select \u201cyes\u201d to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for eligibility information and required documentation , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is a Full-time USPS position. This position requires the successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position qualifies for on-call and shift differential pay. This position is being re-advertised. Previous applicants need not reapply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63727&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "OPS Full time- Program Assistant (CIVICS Seal of Excellence Project)", "description": "OPS Full time- Program Assistant (CIVICS Seal of Excellence Project) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63727 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The Learning Systems Institute Responsibilities \u2022 Data entry, filing, and record keeping \u2022 Track suppliers and payments \u2022 Manage large quantities of data in Excel \u2022 Organize and maintain office supplies and clean workspace \u2022 Other related duties as assigned by the supervisor Qualifications High school diploma or equivalency. Must be able to work in office in Tallahassee, Florida. Preferred Qualifications \u2022 Familiarity with OMNI and Payment Works. \u2022 Experience with Microsoft Office, particularly Microsoft Word, and/or Excel is strongly preferred Contact Info Marissa Love mlove@lsi.fsu.edu University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Rate: $20.00 per hour. This position is full-time at 40 hours per week. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an OPS/temporary job. Based on the duties, this position may require completion of a criminal history background check . This position does not begin until JANUARY 2027. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63725&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Resource Sharing Assistant \u2013 FSU Libraries (Part-time, OPS)", "description": "Resource Sharing Assistant \u2013 FSU Libraries (Part-time, OPS) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63725 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Part-Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department FSU Libraries Responsibilities FSU Libraries is seeking a dependable, detail-oriented OPS Resource Sharing Assistant to support the daily operations of the Resource Sharing department at Strozier Library. This position plays an important role in helping students, faculty, and researchers access library materials and scholarly resources through interlibrary loan, document delivery, and related services. Working as part of a collaborative team, the OPS Resource Sharing Assistant will help process requests, retrieve and scan library materials, prepare shipments, and maintain accurate records. This position offers an opportunity to gain hands-on experience with academic library operations, resource sharing services, and specialized library systems while developing valuable skills in organization, communication, technology, and customer service. Key responsibilities include: Process resource sharing requests and materials using library systems and established workflows, including ILLiad, UBorrow+, and document delivery services. Retrieve requested materials from library collections and conduct shelf searches for requested, missing, or overdue items. Scan articles and book chapters to fulfill Resource Sharing and Library Express Delivery Service (LEDS) requests. Process incoming and outgoing departmental mail, including preparing library materials for shipment and return through USPS and FedEx. Assist with returns and routine circulation and Resource Sharing transactions. Maintain accurate transaction records and departmental statistics. Communicate professionally with library staff, users, and partner libraries in person and through electronic communication. Support other departmental workflows, special projects, and related duties as assigned. Qualifications Ability to learn and accurately follow established procedures and workflows. Strong organizational skills and attention to detail. Ability to manage multiple tasks, prioritize responsibilities, and maintain accurate records. Strong written and verbal communication skills and a commitment to providing helpful, professional customer service. Ability to learn and use multiple computer applications and web-based systems. Ability to work independently after training and collaboratively as part of a team. Dependability and ability to maintain a consistent work schedule. Ability to perform duties involving prolonged sitting; regular standing, walking, bending, and reaching; and lifting and moving library materials, tubs, and boxes weighing up to 30 pounds, with or without reasonable accommodation. Preferred Qualifications Previous experience in a library, shipping and receiving, scanning or document processing, office administration, or customer service environment. Contact Info Darrell Collier , UBorrow Coordinator Timothy Kanke , Interlibrary Loan Lending Supervisor University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range $15 per hour How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an OPS/temporary job. Based on the duties, this position may require completion of a criminal history background check . The schedule is 10 hours per week, Monday through Friday, between 8:00 a.m. and 4:00 p.m. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63247&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Technical Research Designer, Level I (Control Room - National High Magnetic Field Laboratory)", "description": "Technical Research Designer, Level I (Control Room - National High Magnetic Field Laboratory) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63247 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department National High Magnetic Field Laboratory Join the world-renowned National High Magnetic Field Laboratory at Florida State University (FSU) and support groundbreaking scientific discovery in a collaborative, high-tech environment. FSU was recently recognized as one of America\u2019s Best-in-State Employers for its strong workplace culture and employee-centered values. Responsibilities Operate and maintain facility equipment and systems in support of the National High Magnetic Field Laboratory\u2019s DC high magnetic field user program. Interact with and assist users, research faculty, technicians and other National High Magnetic Field Laboratory staff on the operation and maintenance of the facility. Facility Operations & System Monitoring Monitor and safely operate facility equipment and systems. Coordinate with the City of Tallahassee\u2019s Electrical Distribution Control Room with regards to facility operations and power levels. Take the proper corrective actions in response to alarms or other indications of abnormal equipment operation. Exercise skilled independent judgement in handling facility operations as well as unexpected or emergency situations. Distributed Control System (DCS) Engineering Perform engineering functions on the National High Magnetic Field Laboratory Distributed Control System (DCS) such as graphic, trend group and control group building, logic development and troubleshooting, field device integration. Use knowledge of the DCS to perform troubleshooting between the DCS and field devices. Safety & Compliance Coordinate, prepare and issue Lock, Tag, Verify procedures for facility maintenance, troubleshooting and repair in accordance with National High Magnetic Field Laboratory safety policies and procedures. Work with other National High Magnetic Field Laboratory personnel in the evaluation and development of safety policies and procedures. Take a proactive attitude and make solution-oriented contributions to the National High Magnetic Field Laboratory safety program. Maintenance & System Performance Assist Facility engineers, staff and scientists with the development of preventative maintenance programs and procedures. Assist Facility engineers and staff in tracking the performance and characteristics of the water-cooled magnets. Contribute to equipment and system characterization, troubleshooting, repairs, maintenance, installation, integration and commissioning. Training & User Support Provide training to users and staff on safe magnet operations, safe overhead crane operations and other safety procedures as necessary. Engineering Support & Projects In consultation with supervisor(s) and design engineers, assist with determining changes in design and operation of plant and power equipment to improve operations, capabilities, reliability and uptime. Contribute to facility projects. Giving tours. Qualifications High school diploma/equivalent and four years of experience. (Note: post-high school education can substitute for experience at the equivalent rate.) Helpful What You Gain at FSU Opportunity to work at a world-renowned national research laboratory. Meaningful contributions to scientific discovery and student learning. A collaborative environment that values your expertise and invests in your growth. Contact Info For additional information, please contact Kayla West . University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Minimum salary of $47,660, commensurate with education and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select \u201cyes\u201d to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for Veterans\u2019 Preference eligibility requirements and Veterans\u2019 Preference required documentation (PDF) , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Participate in on-call duties. This position is being re-advertised. Previous applicants need not reapply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63731&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Analytics Architect", "description": "Analytics Architect Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63731 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department This position is within FSU\u2019s Department of Information Technology Services (ITS) The Data & Analytics team at Florida State University connects, manages, and delivers data that powers decision-making across campus. We build the pipelines, reporting, predictive models and analytics that help leaders understand student success, operations, and institutional performance, and we\u2019re advancing AI-enabled tools to make that insight easier to use. Responsibilities Analytics Architects use critical thinking skills and exercise their judgment to discover the patterns and information found in vast amounts of data using analytics predictive models and machine learning. The incumbent makes sense of these patterns and signals to help the university make better decisions which will lead to better service for our students, faculty, community partners, and staff. An effective analytics architect will also be adept at providing an explanatory narrative that a non-expert can follow and understand. Responsible for supporting the University's data and analytic needs across multiple sources of data. Designs, develops, analyses, and supports the creation of information products in alignment with functional and technical system requirements. Develops programming code and scripting using appropriate language and tools to provide problem resolutions and new functionality in complex analytical systems. Responsible for reviewing and capturing business requirements needed for a new design, development, and maintenance of analytical models, and process modifications, and performing the technical development based on these requirements. Will also provide recommendations and narratives explaining the value of the models. Responsible for conducting testing scenarios to ensure the integrity of analytical products and processes and validation of all applications, Provides recommendations for enhancements to existing systems. Responsible for the creation and maintenance of system specifications and documented requirements pertaining to analytical products, models, and processes. Performs duties in compliance with ITS policies, guidelines, and processes pertaining to support requests, work orders, project management, change management, and incident management. Appropriately utilizes associated tools in accordance with ITS standards. Qualifications Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, MIS, or other appropriate degree and three years' experience or a high school diploma or equivalent and seven years of experience. (Note: or an equivalent combination of education and experience.) Preferred Qualifications Prior experience with Microsoft Power BI or similar visualization tool and Snowflake. Practical experience with SQL including CTEs and ranking/partition functions. Helpful Who is an ideal candidate for this position? Someone who enjoys dealing directly with stakeholders to capture requirements and collaborating with colleagues. What is a typical day in this position? A typical day may involve building an information or data product from scratch or reengineering a legacy dashboard or logical view. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63704&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Associate Vice Provost, Academic Policy and Faculty Affairs (Open Rank Professor, 12-Month Salaried)", "description": "Associate Vice Provost, Academic Policy and Faculty Affairs (Open Rank Professor, 12-Month Salaried) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63704 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Office of Faculty Development & Advancement Responsibilities The Associate Vice Provost for Academic Policy and Faculty Affairs provides university-wide leadership for academic policy administration, curriculum governance and the fair and consistent resolution of academic matters. Working across colleges and administrative units, the position oversees critical academic systems and regulatory processes; promotes institutional compliance with university, Board of Governors, and state requirements; and serves as a central liaison on curriculum, syllabi, student conduct, appeals, and academic integrity. The role also supervises designated staff and supports data-informed decision-making that advances faculty effectiveness and the university\u2019s academic mission. Responsibilities of the Position: Provide strategic and operational oversight of Coursedog, the university\u2019s curriculum management platform, ensuring alignment with institutional curriculum policies. Serve as the principal Faculty Development and Advancement liaison to department chairs, deans, and college curriculum leaders regarding course proposals, approval pathways, and policy implementation. Collaborate with the Office of Digital Learning to oversee the institutional implementation and administration of Simple Syllabus, including governance, adoption, and compliance with university and Board of Governors syllabus requirements. Work closely with college leadership on institutional compliance with Board of Governors Regulation 8.003, including coordination and monitoring and reporting of faculty attestations every semester. Administer and ensure university compliance with Florida\u2019s Statewide Articulation Framework under section 1007.23, Florida Statutes, and the Common Prerequisite Manual, coordinating policy interpretation and implementation across academic units. Serve as the primary Faculty Development and Advancement liaison to the Division of Student Affairs and serve as the office\u2019s representative on the Behavioral Intervention Team, facilitating coordinated responses to complex student matters with academic implications. Serve as the primary Faculty Development and Advancement liaison to the Student Ombuds, coordinating consultation and follow-up on academic concerns that require central administrative review. Supervise the Academic Affairs Administrator responsible for administration of the Academic Honor Policy, ensuring consistent procedures, timely case management, effective training and guidance, and compliance with university requirements. Supervise the Academic Affairs Administrator responsible for administration and fiscal operations of the Faculty Senate and Faculty Senate Steering Committee. Provide central review and guidance for general academic appeals that remain unresolved at the instructor, department, or college level, ensuring fair, timely, and policy-consistent resolution. Coordinate Faculty Development and Advancement review of grade appeals elevated to the Student Academic Relations Committee, while supporting consistent application of university policy. Evaluate academic policies and processes and propose changes to enhance effectiveness. This also includes the approval or denial of requests for exceptions to academic rules submitted to Faculty Development and Advancement for consideration. These decisions should be documented and applied consistently according to university standards. Represent Faculty Development and Advancement as an ex officio member of the University Curriculum Committee. Assist in leadership development programming related to the areas of responsibility outlined in this job description. Qualifications The successful candidate must have a doctoral degree (or terminal degree for the field). Preference will be given to faculty who are tenured and at the highest rank for their position. The successful candidate will have at least three years of experience in an administrative role in an academic unit (e.g., department, school) or at the college level. Experience in supervising staff is highly valued as is direct experience with the creation and implementation of academic policies at the unit and/or college level. The successful candidate will have the following characteristics: Highly organized and efficient in managing complex processes Excellent communications skills (written and oral) Curiosity about academic affairs processes and systems at the university level Self-starter who can perform independently but seeks advice appropriately Motivated to develop a deep understanding of academic affairs policies and procedures Appreciation for technology that is used in administering academic affairs policies and procedures Fair minded and able to listen to multiple viewpoints while also applying academic policies and guidelines consistently Ability to work effectively with multiple stakeholder offices (e.g., colleges; Division of Student Affairs; Institutional Research) Collaborative and able to work with a wide array of people in various positions (students, staff, faculty, department chairs, associate deans, deans, and senior leadership) Strong instincts for tracking down answers and identifying relevant policies to resolve academic affairs issues Strong interest in advancing the academic excellence of the university Contact Info For inquiries regarding the application and search process, please contact Craig Stanley, chair of the Search Advisory Committee. Email: cstanley@fsu.edu Phone: 850-644-6876 University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information and include education details. Applicants must submit a letter of interest in the position and curriculum vitae. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}, "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63495&PostingSeq=1": {"title": "Research Coordinator (OPS, Remote), Institute on Digital Health and Innovation (IDHI)", "description": "Research Coordinator (OPS, Remote), Institute on Digital Health and Innovation (IDHI) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63495 Location Remote Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Florida State University College of Nursing Institute on Digital Health and Innovation (IDHI) Responsibilities Established in 2022, the Institute on Digital Health and Innovation (IDHI) within the Florida State University College of Nursing advances digital health science, technologies, and tools focused on solving real world needs of patients, providers, and populations through research, training, and innovation to maximize health. The mission of IDHI is to advance individual and public health through collaborative and synergistic partnerships focused on the development, evaluation, and dissemination of digital health tools, technologies, and innovations. IDHI is now home to the Teen Health Lab, which focuses on developing, implementing, and evaluating digital interventions to improve communication skills and promote adolescent sexual health. As a newly created lab, faculty and staff will be launching new research studies and analyzing previously collected data in order to best develop cutting edge research interventions. Additionally, IDHI co-leads the Adolescent Medicine Trials Network for HIV Interventions (ATN) \u2013 a multicenter research network conducting transformative research that addresses the HIV prevention and care continuum for adolescents and young adults in the US. The Scientific Leadership Center (SLC) within the ATN is responsible for the overall scientific leadership and governance of the network and its activities by managing multiple interdependent functional components and research activities. The Research Coordinator serves as a member of IDHI\u2019s Teen Health Lab team and the ATN SLC team, providing operational support for the design, launch, and implementation of multiple multi-site health behavior research studies across the IDHI and ATN portfolios. This position is responsible for coordinating day-to-day administrative, fiscal, and operational research activities, including project planning, protocol development, collaboration with research partners, monitoring study activation timelines, and invoice reconciliation. Qualifications Bachelor\u2019s degree and one year of relevant experience; or a combination of post high school education and experience equal to five years. This position requires successful completion of the eSPEAR Certification , or ability to obtain the certification within 6 months of hire. Preferred Qualifications Experience coordinating study start-up activities. Possess research project management experience. Excellent interpersonal and communication skills, both oral and written, which are required for interacting with a wide range of stakeholders and collaborators. Experience with qualitative data collection and analysis. Ability to follow regulatory, good clinical practice, and human subjects research protections guidelines. Demonstrated ability to prioritize and complete assignments independently with excellent attention to detail. Proficient in the Microsoft Office Suite, specifically Outlook, Word, Excel, and Power Point. Master\u2019s degree in a related field. Bilingual proficiency in English and Spanish, with the ability to support translation and adaptation of study materials. Interest in the development and evaluation of technology-based research interventions (e.g., the use of smartphone, social media, internet) to improve health and wellness. Background in health-related research. Experience using SPSS, Stata, or other similar statistical software. Experience using REDCap. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there\u2019s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow\u2019s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range $28.85 per hour, commensurate with experience/education. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an OPS/temporary full-time job. Based on the duties, this position may require completion of a criminal history background check . This role has been designated as eligible for remote work based on the job functions. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"}}, "rows": {"https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=62375&PostingSeq=1": {"school_id": 261, "posting_url": "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRA